    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41386&lang=en": {
      "title": "Leukemia/Lymphoma Physician Scientist - Open Rank",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 12, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: SOM-PEDS Hematology-Onc-GenOps Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Department: Pediatrics – Hematology/Oncology Job Title: Leukemia/Lymphoma Physician Scientist Position #: 00722321 – Requisition #:41386 Job Summary: The Section of Pediatric Hematology/Oncology seeks an innovative physician-scientist to establish and lead an independent laboratory-based research program focused on pediatric leukemia and/or lymphoma. This position is intended for an early- or mid-career investigator with a strong commitment to basic or translational research that advances understanding of leukemia/lymphoma biology and accelerates development of novel therapeutic approaches. The successful candidate will devote approximately 80% effort to research and 20% effort to clinical care. As an integral member of the Leukemia/Lymphoma Program, the faculty member will serve as a critical bridge between clinical and laboratory research initiatives, translating clinically relevant questions into impactful scientific investigations while advancing discoveries toward improved outcomes for children and adolescents with leukemia and lymphoma. The successful candidate will join a nationally recognized pediatric Leukemia/Lymphoma program with a robust clinical research footprint including substantial participation and leadership in Children's Oncology Group (COG) and Therapeutic Advances in Childhood Leukemia (TACL) clinical trials. The position provides opportunities for collaboration with established investigators across leukemia biology, cellular therapy, immunotherapy, precision medicine, and regenerative medicine programs. Key Responsibilities: Research Responsibilities (80%) Develop and lead an independent, innovative, and externally funded laboratory-based research program focused on pediatric leukemia and/or lymphoma. Conduct basic and/or translational research related to leukemia biology, disease progression, therapeutic resistance, or novel treatment development. Pursue and secure extramural funding through federal agencies, foundations, industry partnerships, and philanthropic support. Publish research findings in high-impact, peer-reviewed scientific journals. Present research at regional, national, and international scientific meetings. Establish productive collaborations with investigators across the University Cancer Center, the Gates Institute, and other campus research initiatives. Contribute to the development of institutional leukemia research priorities and strategic initiatives. Mentor graduate students, postdoctoral fellows, trainees, residents, fellows, and junior faculty members. Participate in departmental, divisional, institutional, and national academic activities as appropriate. Clinical Responsibilities (20%) Provide approximately four weeks of inpatient oncology service annually, including chemotherapy service and shared call coverage. Maintain an outpatient leukemia clinic practice averaging approximately one clinic session every other week. Participate in procedure clinics as needed. Contribute to multidisciplinary patient care conferences and leukemia/lymphoma disease-specific initiatives. Support clinical and translational research activities through collaboration with clinical trial and disease-focused teams. Evidence of successful grant funding or strong potential to obtain independent extramural funding. Experience leading or contributing to translational research studies that bridge laboratory discovery and clinical application. Demonstrated commitment to mentorship, education, and trainee development. Experience collaborating across disciplines within academic research environments. Interest in leveraging institutional strengths in immunotherapy, cellular therapeutics, regenerative medicine, and precision oncology. Work Location: Onsite – this role is expected to work onsite and is located in Aurora, CO at the Anschutz Medical Campus. Why Join Us: The Center for Cancer and Blood Disorders at Children’s Hospital Colorado is one of the leading pediatric oncology, hematology, blood and marrow transplant and cellular therapy programs in the country. Our center is consistently ranked among the top pediatric hospitals in the nation by U.S. News & World Report and the Department of Pediatrics, was ranked No. 7 in the nation for “Best Medical Schools – Pediatrics” in U.S. News & World Report’s 2022 rankings. Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year (based on percentage of time) Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 11/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. This is an open rank position and could be categorized as Assistant Professor or Associate Professor based on experience and qualifications as indicated below: Assistant Professor ● MD, DO, MD/PhD, or equivalent medical degree. ● Completion of an accredited Pediatric Hematology/Oncology fellowship. ● Board certified or board eligible in Pediatric Hematology/Oncology. ● Eligible for Colorado medical licensure and DEA registration. ● Demonstrated record of scholarly achievement, including peer-reviewed publications in pediatric leukemia, lymphoma, cancer biology, immunology, cellular therapy, or a related field. ● Demonstrated experience conducting basic, translational, or laboratory-based research. Associate Professor ● Current or prior federal peer-reviewed funding or major foundation support. ● An established independent research program with evidence of sustained scholarly productivity and extramural funding. ● Leadership roles in cooperative groups, multicenter research initiatives, disease-specific programs, or national scientific organizations. ● Demonstrated success translating laboratory discoveries into clinically impactful applications. ● Track record of sustained mentorship of fellows, graduate students, postdoctoral fellows, and junior faculty. ● Experience leading interdisciplinary research teams and contributing to institutional strategic initiatives. ● Established collaborations within cancer centers, translational science institutes, cellular therapy programs, or transplantation programs. Condition of Employment: ● Must successfully pass a drug test through Children’s Hospital Colorado ● Must be willing and able to pass a national criminal background check *For questions regarding Children’s Hospital drug testing requirements, please contact Children’s Human Resources at 720-777-8598. Some positions may require testing if access to Children’s Hospital or their systems is needed at any time during employment with the University. If drug testing is required, it will be listed in the job posting. Preferred Qualifications: Assistant Professor ● Advanced research training through a postdoctoral fellowship, physician-scientist training program, K-award, institutional career development program, or equivalent protected research experience. ● Demonstrate strong potential to establish an independent research program. ● Prior success obtaining pilot, foundation, society, institutional, industry-sponsored, or federal research funding. ● Evidence of translational research that bridges laboratory discovery and clinical application. ● Experience mentoring students, residents, fellows, or research trainees. ● Demonstrated collaborative work with multidisciplinary research teams. ● Interest in developing innovative research programs aligned with institutional strengths Associate Professor ● Current or prior federal peer-reviewed funding or major foundation support. ● An established independent research program with evidence of sustained scholarly productivity and extramural funding. ● Leadership roles in cooperative groups, multicenter research initiatives, disease-specific programs, or national scientific organizations. ● Demonstrated success translating laboratory discoveries into clinically impactful applications. ● Track record of sustained mentorship of fellows, graduate students, postdoctoral fellows, and junior faculty. ● Experience leading interdisciplinary research teams and contributing to institutional strategic initiatives. ● Established collaborations within cancer centers, translational science institutes, cellular therapy programs, or transplantation programs. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Demonstrated knowledge of pediatric hematology/oncology, leukemia biology, cancer genetics, immunology, and translational research methodologies. Ability to develop, lead, and sustain an independent laboratory-based research program focused on leukemia and related hematologic malignancies. Strong scientific writing and communication skills, including the ability to prepare peer-reviewed publications, grant applications, presentations, and other scholarly works. Ability to secure and manage extramural funding from federal agencies, foundations, industry, and philanthropic sources. Expertise in experimental design, data analysis, scientific rigor, and the conduct of high-quality laboratory and translational research. Ability to translate clinically relevant questions into innovative research studies that advance scientific knowledge and patient care. Demonstrated ability to establish productive interdisciplinary collaborations with clinical, translational, and basic science investigators. Effective mentoring, teaching, and leadership skills with the ability to support the professional development of trainees, fellows, students, and junior faculty. Strong organizational, project management, and problem-solving skills, with the ability to balance research, clinical, educational, and administrative responsibilities. Commitment to fostering a collaborative and high-performing academic environment while contributing to the strategic growth and national visibility of the Leukemia/Lymphoma Program and Cancer Center. Evidence of potential to establish an independent, externally funded research program. Ability to work effectively within multidisciplinary academic and clinical teams. Expertise in pediatric leukemia biology, lymphoma biology, leukemia genomics, immunotherapy, cellular therapy, immune-oncology, precision medicine, or related disciplines. How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): 1. A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position 2. Curriculum vitae / Resume 3. Five professional references including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers . Questions should be directed to: Staci Ertzberger staci.ertzberger@childrenscolorado.org Screening of Applications Begins: Immediately and continues until position is filled. For best consideration, apply by 12/1/2026. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as HIRING RANGE: Assistant Professor: $191,400 to $ 223,000 Associate Professor: $233,800 to $282,000 The above hiring range represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation unless it is non-exempt. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: The University of Colorado (CU) is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@ucdenver.edu ​. Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41382&lang=en": {
      "title": "Certified Medical Assistant - Float Pool (PRN)",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 12, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: SOM-DEAN DO COMM PRC COV POOL Schedule: Part-time University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus Department: Community Practice Job Title: Certified Medical Assistant - Float Pool (PRN) Position #: 00853888 – Requisition #: 41382 Job Summary: The Float Pool Certified Medical Assistant (CMA) is responsible for providing patient care under the direction of a physician or another healthcare provider across all Community Practice clinics, specialties, and care teams based on patient care and operational needs of the CU School of Medicine Community Practice Department. The Float Pool CMA adapts to varying clinic environments, patient populations, and workflows while working to facilitate clinic workflow, assist patients, and ensure safe, seamless delivery of care for each patient. Key Responsibilities: Accurately rooms patients, obtains and records vital signs, patient history, and reason for seeking care. Accurately processes and records telephone messages in patient medical records and according to policy. Assists in preparing prescription refills for providers according to policy. Maintains patient confidentiality, written and verbal. Communicates effectively and in an attentive manner with every patient encounter. Verifies the patient’s understanding of the purpose of the visit. Accurately documents all care provided and procedures performed within the patient’s medical record. Work Location: Onsite – this role is expected to work onsite and is located in Denver Metro , CO. Why Join Us: Community Practice Medicine, housed within the School of Medicine at the University of Colorado, is seeking trained medical professionals to join our growing team. With clinics spanning from Longmont to Castle Rock, we offer a wide variety of opportunities. Specialty areas include, but are not limited to: Orthopedics, Vascular Surgery, OBGYN, Internal Medicine, Urology, Psychiatry, and many more! The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is a public education, clinical and research facility serving 4,500 students and a world-class medical destination at the forefront of life-changing science, medicine, and healthcare. CU Anschutz offers more than 42 highly rated degree programs through 6 schools and colleges and receives over $500 million in research awards each year. We are the single largest health professions education provider in Colorado, awarding nearly 1,450 degrees annually. Powered by our award-winning faculty, renowned researchers, and a reputation for academic excellence, the CU Anschutz Medical Campus drives innovation from the classroom to the laboratory to the delivery of unparalleled patient care. Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation, and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package, including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accrues over the year Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 15/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced-rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Completion of an accredited medical assistant program. One year of medical assistant work experience. Current CMA certification (i.e., AAMA, NCCT). Substitution: A combination of education and related technical/paraprofessional experience may be substituted on a year-for-year basis. Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Preferred Qualifications: Experience with MS Office. Experience with EPIC. Experience with Kronos. Experience with HealthStream. Conditions of Employment: Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without requiring sponsorship. We are unable to provide work visa sponsorship or employment authorization for this position now or in the future. Current Basic Life Support (BLS) for Healthcare Providers issued by the American Heart Association or the American Red Cross healthcare provider-level CPR certification. Maintains all required licensure and certifications for the position. Must be able to work in-person. Must be able to travel to alternate locations as assigned. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Strong organizational and personal skills. Strong medical terminology knowledge and skills. Strong knowledge of CPT & ICD-10 procedures. Strong knowledge of value-based care and risk-based coding procedures in Primary Care. Strong knowledge of medication and injection procedures. Ability to safely administer a variety of treatments and medications as directed. Ability to use various types of equipment for examination and treatment procedures. Ability to accurately take and record vital signs. Ability to accurately reconcile patient medications. Ability to maintain quality control standards. Ability to identify problems and recommend solutions. How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position Curriculum vitae / Resume Three to five professional references, including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Questions should be directed to: Erin McKitrick, Erin.McKitrick@cuanschutz.edu , and Trisha Ward, Trisha.Ward@cuanschutz.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Immediately and continues until the position is filled. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as $22.98 to $26.84 per hour. The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position may be eligible for overtime compensation, depending on the level. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans, and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@cuanschutz.edu . Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students, and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine-preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety-sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41380&lang=en": {
      "title": "Patient Services Representative I-II – Float Pool",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 12, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: SOM-DEAN DO COMM PRC COV POOL Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus Department: Community Practice Job Title: Patient Services Representative I-II – Float Pool Position #: 00853887 – Requisition #: 41380 Job Summary: Float Pool Patient Service Representatives provide flexible administrative coverage across all Community Practice clinics, specialties, and care teams based on patient schedules and operational needs of the CU School of Medicine Community Practice Department. Staff in this role must adapt to varying clinic environments, patient populations, and workflows and are responsible for providing efficient, effective, quality customer service through a variety of duties including, but not limited to, patient check-in, registration, scheduling, exam preparation, outbound calling, and some referral management. Complies with established company policies and procedures, HIPAA Privacy Rules and University of Colorado School of Medicine Confidentiality Policy. Ensures clear and timely communication including patient appointment status to clinical department(s). Key Responsibilities: Acknowledges and welcomes patients and visitors; sets the tone for a positive experience Checks patients in and out for appointments; schedules follow-up appointments at the time of discharge Verifies patient and insurance information, while accurately documenting necessary modifications in the Electronic Health Record (EPIC) Answers multiple phone lines to fulfill patient needs over the phone Monitors provider schedules daily to ensure that all open appointment slots are filled on the same day and schedules are free of roadblocks Reviews the Daily Appointment Report three to five days in advance for patient appointments to ensure referral accuracy Collects patient copays and balances the drawer daily Work Location: Onsite – this role is expected to work onsite and is located in Denver Metro, CO. Why Join Us: Community Practice Medicine, housed within the School of Medicine at the University of Colorado, is seeking trained medical professionals to join our growing team. With clinics spanning from Longmont to Castle Rock, we offer a wide variety of opportunities. Specialty areas include, but are not limited to: Orthopedics, Vascular Surgery, OBGYN, Internal Medicine, Urology, Psychiatry, and many more! The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is a public education, clinical, and research facility serving 4,500 students and a world-class medical destination at the forefront of life-changing science, medicine, and healthcare. CU Anschutz offers more than 42 highly rated degree programs through 6 schools and colleges and receives over $500 million in research awards each year. We are the single largest health professions education provider in Colorado, awarding nearly 1,450 degrees annually. Powered by our award-winning faculty, renowned researchers, and a reputation for academic excellence, the CU Anschutz Medical Campus drives innovation from the classroom to the laboratory to the delivery of unparalleled patient care. Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation, and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package, including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 15/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced-rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Patient Services Representative I: High school diploma or GED One or more (1+) years of patient/client-facing experience Patient Services Representative II: High school diploma or GED Two or more (2+) years of patient/client-facing experience Substitution (All Levels): A combination of education and related technical/military/paraprofessional experience may be substituted for a bachelor’s degree on a year-for-year basis. Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Preferred Qualifications (All Ranks): College graduate Medical office experience EPIC experience MS Office experience Bilingual, Spanish-speaking Conditions of Employment: Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without requiring sponsorship. We are unable to provide work visa sponsorship or employment authorization for this position now or in the future. Comply with the applicable University of Colorado School of Medicine, Community Practice mandatory education and training Must be able to work in person Must be able to travel to alternate locations as assigned Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Strong organizational and personal skills; must have strong work ethic Strong communication skills, both written and verbal Ability to maintain a positive attitude with clients, employees, and management Ability to work quickly – individually and as part of a team Ability to read, analyze, and interpret policies, documents, and regulations Must be detail-oriented and maintain excellent organizational skills Must be tech-savvy (ability to understand, apply, and benefit from technology) How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to the listed job qualifications and interest in the position Curriculum vitae / Resume Three to five professional references, including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Questions should be directed to: Erin McKitrick, Erin.McKitrick@cuanschutz.edu , and Trisha Ward, Trisha.Ward@cuanschutz.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Immediately and continues until the position is filled. For best consideration, apply within one month of the posting date. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as: Patient Services Representative I: $40,000 to $46,720 Patient Services Representative II: $43,700 to $51,042 The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position may be eligible for overtime compensation, depending on the level. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans, and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@cuanschutz.edu . Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students, and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine-preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety-sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=40319&lang=en": {
      "title": "Women’s Health Primary Care Fellowship (Instructor)",
      "description": "Closing Date: 10/17/2026 Posted Date: Oct 12, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: SOM-MED-GIM Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Department: Medicine, General Internal Medicine Job Title: Women’s Health Primary Care Fellowship (Instructor) Position #00603913 – Requisition #40319 Job Summary: This unique, one-year, ambulatory-based fellowship position is designed to train internal medicine graduates to provide broad-spectrum women’s health primary care to women of all ages. In addition, participants will undergo a supportive transition to independent primary care practice, gain dedicated women’s health procedural experience, develop an understanding of both academic and community-based medical settings, and develop leadership skills in education, quality improvement, and clinic administration. This fellowship offers a unique blend of independent patient care, leadership experiences, and focused women’s health clinical knowledge and skill acquisition. The Division of General Internal Medicine’s goal is to train capable, experienced women’s health internists who wish to be leaders in women’s health in their future careers. Key Responsibilities : Build and maintain own primary care panel at the Women’s Integrated Services in Health clinic and see other clinic patients as needed, 5 half days per week, which includes 1 half day precepting an LIC students Work with Women’s Health Fellowship Director to arrange clinical sessions with subspecialty physicians at University of Colorado in target women’s health subspecialties Core subspecialty clinical content areas include gynecology, urogynecology, endocrinology, and breast health. Other possible rotations include cardiology, sports medicine, psychiatry, fertility clinic, and others depending on fellow interest and faculty availability Design and complete a mentored scholarly project by the end of the year. Present didactic presentation on women’s health topic to WISH faculty and staff four times annually. Present once a year at GIM Grand Rounds and/or WISH Rounds on topic of choice Partner with WISH Medical Director in an apprentice model to get on-the-job training for a future career in educational or administrative clinician leadership. Work Location: Onsite – This role is expected to work onsite and is located in the Denver Metro area. Why Join Us: The Division of General Internal Medicine (GIM), established at the University of Colorado in 1977, was one of the first GIM divisions established within the United States. Building on a rich history and tradition, our GIM Division has undergone significant change and evolution to maintain our goal of being a national leader in patient care, medical education and health services research. We take our three-part mission of patient care, medical education, and research​ seriously. Each of our affiliated institutions has its own unique medical care programs. These programs, when taken together, provide a wide breadth and depth of clinical experiences that allows our trainees to experience virtually all aspects of inpatient and ambulatory medical care. Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 10/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. MD or DO degree Completion of Internal Medicine residency Board certified or board eligible in Internal Medicine Active medical license in Colorado Preferred Qualifications: Experience caring for women in primary care setting Experience caring for underserved or diverse patient populations Experience with EPIC or similar EHR system Prior research and/or teaching experiences Commitment to academic leadership and advocacy Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Understanding how biological sex and gender identity influence disease presentation, treatment response, and health outcomes. Interest in reproductive health topics, including contraception, menopause, abnormal uterine bleeding, and fertility counseling. Familiarity with conditions commonly affecting female populations, including autoimmune disorders, cardiovascular disease, endocrinopathies, and osteoporosis. Awareness of systemic barriers affecting care for marginalized groups, including racial/ethnic minorities and LGBTQIA+ individuals. Knowledge of how trauma impacts physical and mental health, especially in women with histories of interpersonal violence. Ability to collaborate as part of a multi-disciplinary team with subspecialties, such as OB/GYN, psychiatry, endocrinology, and social services to deliver holistic care. Adaptable in dynamic clinical environments and responsive to evolving patient needs and healthcare systems. How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position Curriculum vitae / Resume Three to five professional references, including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers . Questions should be directed to: Patricia Colella, GIM HR, patricia.colella@cuanschutz.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Immediately and continues until position is filled. For best consideration, apply by December 1, 2026. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as HIRING RANGE: $115,000 The above salary represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position may be eligible for overtime compensation, depending on the level. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@cuanschutz.edu ​. Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41384&lang=en": {
      "title": "Instructor - Clinical Scholar",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 12, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: SOM-MED-HSPMED GEN OPERATIONS Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Department: Medicine-Division of Hospital Medicine Job Title: Instructor - Clinical Scholar Position #00853831 – Requisition #41384 Job Summary: The Division of Hospital Medicine, Department of Medicine at the University of Colorado School of Medicine, Anschutz Medical Campus seeks hospitalists at the Instructor level to join our vibrant hospitalist group practicing and teaching Hospital Medicine in 1-year intensive faculty development program. The participants of this program will work part-time as hospital medicine faculty, attending on resident and advanced practice provider teaching services. The remainder of time is dedicated to the advancement of skills in reasoning, critical appraisal, and Point-of-Care ultrasonography (POCUS). Key Responsibilities : Develop expertise in POCUS under guided mentorship. Build advanced clinical decision-making skills, founded in biostatistics and evidence-based medicine. Enhance critical appraisal skills and develop expertise in nuanced interpretation of variety of study designs such as observational study, randomized clinical trial, adaptive randomizations, Bayesian analysis of randomized trials, conventional meta-analysis, meta-regression, and network meta-analysis. Develop as an educator by taking an active teaching role in POCUS and EBM curriculums for internal medicine residency program and for hospital medicine faculty development. ( optional ) Build specific skills pertinent to hospital medicine practice, such as quality and patient safety, addiction medicine, clinical operations, and leadership. Apply advanced clinical decision-making and bedside ultrasonography skills to patient care under guided mentorship. Develop an area of interest and produce a scholarship in that area by the end of the academic year (curriculum development for students or faculty is a form of scholarship). Work Location: Onsite – this role is expected to work onsite and is located in Aurora, Colorado. Why Join Us: The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is a public education, clinical and research facility and a world-class medical destination at the forefront of life-changing science, medicine, and healthcare. We are the single largest health professions education provider in Colorado. Powered by our award-winning faculty, renowned researchers and a reputation for academic excellence, the CU Anschutz Medical Campus drives innovation from the classroom to the laboratory to the delivery of unparalleled patient care. Read CU Anschutz Quick Facts here Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 10/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Must have medical degree MD/DO Completion of 3-year ACGME-accredited internal medicine residency program (or other programs that involve training in internal medicine, such as Medicine/Pediatrics joint residency) Open Track: To support the growth of our faculty, selected candidates will be offered the opportunity to choose a track that corresponds to their area of excellence. Learn more about faculty tracks at the Office for Faculty Affairs. How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): 1. A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position 2. Curriculum vitae / Resume 3. Five professional references including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers . Questions should be directed to: Lauren Sutherland Lauren.Sutherland@cuanschutz.edu or Amiran Baduashvili amiran.baduashvili@cuanschutz.edu Screening of Applications Begins: This position may be seeking multiple candidates. Positions will remain open until filled. Applications will be reviewed as they are received, and candidates may be contacted for interviews throughout the posting period. Upon candidate(s) selection, the posting will be closed, and no further applications will be accepted. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as HIRING RANGE: $130,156 - $160,192 depending on Clinical FTE (cFTE). Clinical Scholars can choose the amount of clinical time they wish to work. Compensation will vary based on this choice – see options below. 0.65 cFTE - $130,156 0.70 cFTE - $140,168 0.75 cFTE - $150,180 0.80 cFTE - $160,192 The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation unless it is non-exempt. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: The University of Colorado (CU) is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@ucdenver.edu ​. Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41378&lang=en": {
      "title": "Registered Nurse – Float Pool",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 9, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: SOM-DEAN DO COMM PRC COV POOL Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Department: Community Practice Job Title: Registered Nurse – Float Pool Position #: 00853886 – Requisition #: 41378 Job Summary: The Ambulatory Clinic Registered Nurse Float Pool position provides flexible nursing coverage across all Community Practice clinics, specialties, and care teams based on patient care and operational needs. Functions include patient assessment, triage, care coordination, patient education, medication administration, clinical procedures, documentation, and follow-up care. Float Pool Registered Nurses adapt to varying clinical environments, patient populations, and workflows while applying established nursing standards, organizational policies, and regulatory requirements. Registered Nurses exercise independent clinical judgment, critical thinking, accountability, and prioritization within the RN scope of practice while collaborating with providers and the interdisciplinary care team to ensure safe, effective, and patient-centered care. Key Responsibilities: Escorts patients to and from exam rooms and readies them for physicians. Performs telephone triage, patient education, handling of physician phone calls, and pharmacy calls. Takes vital signs, records medical history/symptoms, and ensures medical chart/lab test results are available and complete. Administers immunizations and minor treatments as prescribed. Responds to patient questions and concerns as a liaison between physician and patient. Reports all test results to the patient as directed by the physician. Work Location: Onsite – this role is expected to work onsite and is located in Denver Metro, CO . Why Join Us: Community Practice Medicine, housed within the School of Medicine at the University of Colorado, is seeking trained medical professionals to join our growing team. With clinics spanning from Longmont to Castle Rock, we offer a wide variety of opportunities. Specialty areas include, but are not limited to: Orthopedics, Vascular Surgery, OBGYN, Internal Medicine, Urology, Psychiatry, and many more! The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is a public education, clinical, and research facility serving 4,500 students and a world-class medical destination at the forefront of life-changing science, medicine, and healthcare. CU Anschutz offers more than 42 highly rated degree programs through 6 schools and colleges and receives over $500 million in research awards each year. We are the single largest health professions education provider in Colorado, awarding nearly 1,450 degrees annually. Powered by our award-winning faculty, renowned researchers, and a reputation for academic excellence, the CU Anschutz Medical Campus drives innovation from the classroom to the laboratory to the delivery of unparalleled patient care. Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation, and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package, including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 15/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced-rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Entry Level: Graduate of an accredited Nursing program through the Accreditation Commission for Education in Nursing (ACEN) or American Nursing Credentialing Center (ANCC). Intermediate Level: Graduate of an accredited Nursing program through the Accreditation Commission for Education in Nursing (ACEN) or American Nursing Credentialing Center (ANCC). Two (2) years of nursing experience. Senior Level: Graduate of an accredited Nursing program through the Accreditation Commission for Education in Nursing (ACEN) or American Nursing Credentialing Center (ANCC). Four (4) years of nursing experience. Substitution (All Levels): A combination of education and related technical/military/paraprofessional experience may be substituted for a bachelor’s degree on a year-for-year basis. Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Preferred Qualifications (All Levels): Bachelor of Science in Nursing (BSN). One to two (1-2) or more years of job-related/clinic experience. Bilingual, Spanish-speaking. Nursing certification (ANCC) in specialty area. Epic, Kronos, and HealthStream experience. Conditions of Employment (All Levels): Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without requiring sponsorship. We are unable to provide work visa sponsorship or employment authorization for this position now or in the future. Current Basic Life Support (BLS) for Healthcare Providers issued by the American Heart Association or the American Red Cross healthcare provider-level CPR certification. Registered Nurse (RN), State of Colorado. Maintains all required licensure and certifications for the position. Maintains all required continuing education requirements. Must be able to work in person. Must be able to travel to alternate locations as assigned. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities (All Levels): Strong organizational and communication skills. Ability to effectively communicate at all levels, to include physicians, leadership, and staff within the various affiliate organizations (UCH, Children’s Colorado, CU Medicine, CU SOM). Ability to work within large, complex healthcare systems. Ability to analyze and interpret data. Ability to compile complex reports and develop presentations. Ability to compose letters and memorandums. Ability to deal calmly and courteously with people. Ability to deal with stressful situations. Ability to finish tasks in a timely manner. How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to the listed job qualifications and interest in the position Curriculum vitae / Resume Three to five professional references, including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Questions should be directed to: Erin McKitrick, Erin.McKitrick@cuanschutz.edu , and Trisha Ward, Trisha.Ward@cuanschutz.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Immediately and continues until the position is filled. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as: Entry Level: $69,160 to $80,226 Intermediate Level: $74,347 to $86,243 Senior Level: $79,534 to $93,850 The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position may be eligible for overtime compensation, depending on the level. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans, and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@cuanschutz.edu . Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students, and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine-preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety-sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41377&lang=en": {
      "title": "Payroll Shared Services Specialist (Entry to Intermediate)",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 9, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: SOM-DEAN DO Shared Srvc-HR Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus Department: Office of the Dean Collective HR Units Job Title: Payroll Shared Services Specialist (Entry to Intermediate) Position #: 00853883 – Requisition #: 41377 Job Summary: The Payroll Shared Services Specialist, under the direction of the Payroll Shared Services Program Manager, provides day-to-day payroll support for participating and assigned units at the University of Colorado, Anschutz Medical Campus, School of Medicine. Functions of the Payroll Specialist include monthly and bi-weekly payroll processing for all university employee groups, hospital payment entries, funding distribution and allocation Updates, and FAMLI/FMLA coordination and entry. In addition, the Payroll Shared Services Specialist provides guidance and interpretation of Federal, State, University, and School of Medicine laws, rules, regulations, policies, and procedures, assuring compliance in a variety of payroll areas. Key Responsibilities: Process monthly payroll for all university employment groups. Process bi-weekly payroll for participating university employment groups. Ensure accurate calculation of wages earned. Verify timekeeping records and resolve discrepancies. Accurately enter hospital payments (UPI & UOC) for affected faculty Accurately enter and update funding and allocations for all university employment groups. Coordinate, enter, and track FAMLI and FMLA in conjunction with the CU Leave Office. Process off-cycle payroll, terminations, and final checks when necessary. Address employee payroll inquiries regarding paychecks, deductions, and tax withholdings. Investigate and resolve payroll discrepancies in a timely manner. Provide guidance on direct deposit setup and payroll self-service portals. Enter and update employee payroll data in payroll software or HRIS systems. Work closely with HR and Finance to ensure payroll accuracy. Assist with payroll system upgrades and process improvements. Maintain knowledge of relevant policies, procedures, laws, and regulations and provide updates and training to the Payroll Shared Services team as needed. Maintain accurate, timely, and complete records, ensuring compliance with Federal, State, and University laws, regulations, policies, and procedures. Serve as a resource on HR policies and procedures. Support departments as needed and/or in the absence of Payroll Specialists. Perform other duties, tasks, and projects assigned. Work Location: Hybrid – this role is eligible for a hybrid schedule of three (3) days per week on campus and as needed for in-person meetings. Why Join Us: This is an exciting opportunity to join the HR Collective Units team at the University of Colorado | School of Medicine. The Payroll Shared Services team (PRSS) manages and streamlines payroll processing and functions for participating departments in the School of Medicine on the Anschutz Medical Campus. The Anschutz Medical Campus fosters collaboration among students, researchers, and clinicians in one of the largest academic health centers in the nation. Innovative architecture fosters collaboration among students, researchers, and clinicians and extends to two world-class campus hospitals: UCHealth and Children’s Hospital Colorado. The School of Medicine continues to rank among the top 10 medical schools in the country for primary care, according to numbers released by the U.S. News and World Report. Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation, and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 15/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced-rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Entry Level: A bachelor’s degree in Human Resources, Business, Public Administration, Healthcare Administration, Accounting, Finance, or a related field from an accredited college or university. Substitution: A combination of education and related technical/paraprofessional experience may be substituted for the bachelor’s degree on a year-for-year basis. Intermediate Level: A bachelor’s degree in Human Resources, Business, Public Administration, Healthcare Administration, Accounting, Finance, or a related field from an accredited college or university. Substitution: A combination of education and related technical/paraprofessional experience may be substituted for the bachelor’s degree on a year-for-year basis. One (1) year of experience performing Human Resources functions with an emphasis on payroll functions. Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Preferred Qualifications: Experience working in an academic medical center. Experience working with PeopleSoft Human Capital Management. Conditions of Employment: Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without requiring sponsorship. We are unable to provide work visa sponsorship or employment authorization for this position now or in the future. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Strong independent judgment and critical thinking skills. Self-directed. Excellent communication and interpersonal skills. Ability to work collaboratively with people from all levels within an organization. Ability to independently establish work priorities, follow through, and meet established deadlines. Advanced Microsoft Office skills, including Word, Excel, and Outlook. Ability to maintain a high level of confidentiality while working with sensitive information. Strong analytical and problem-solving skills. Ability to actively listen and share relevant information, anticipate problems, and establish and maintain effective working relationships. Knowledge of professional standards, concepts and practices related to Human Resources. Ability to analyze, interpret, and evaluate a broad range of laws, rules, and regulations in order to exercise good judgment in applying them to human resources challenges. Knowledge of applicable Federal and State laws and regulations. How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): Curriculum vitae / Resume Three to five professional references, including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Questions should be directed to: Melia Blair at Melia.Blair@cuanschutz.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Immediately and continues until the position is filled. For best consideration , apply within ten (10) days of the posting date. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as: Entry Level: $48,512 to $65,006 Intermediate Level: $52,793 to $70,742 The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position may be eligible for overtime compensation, depending on the level. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans, and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@cuanschutz.edu . Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students, and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine-preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety-sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=39083&lang=en": {
      "title": "Post-Doctoral Fellow",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 9, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: SOM-OB/GYN RS GENERAL OPS Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus Department: Obstetrics and Gynecology Working Title: Post Doctoral Fellow Position #: 00845409 – Requisition #: 39083 Job Summary: We are searching for a qualified post-doctoral fellow to join our growing laboratory, whose principal investigator is an NIH-funded scientist. Postdoctoral fellow’s main focus in the Kumar Lab is to study functional analysis of gonadotropin biosynthesis, secretion and action in gonads and bone and adipose tissues using multiple in vivo and in vitro approaches. These include transgenic, cell culture, molecular biological, genetics, biochemical and other physiological approaches . Successful applicants will need to demonstrate a strong work ethic, to have the ability to work both independently and collaboratively, to exhibit excellent skills in scientific writing, and to display meticulous, detail-oriented technical skills and record-keeping. Key Responsibilities: Research 90%: Work under supervision of Dr. Kumar on research projects including performing experiments Interpretation of experimental results, data and statistical analyses. Collaborate with mentor and other Professional Research Services professionals/students in the lab. Assist in maintaining lab equipment and laboratory maintenance. · Mentorship 10% Teach/supervise students and/or research assistants. Work Location: Onsite – this role is expected to work onsite and is located in Aurora, CO. Why Join Us: The Department of Obstetrics and Gynecology at the University of Colorado is a world-class research enterprise, ranked 17th in the nation by the Blue Ridge Institute for federal funding. The Department currently has an impressive research portfolio of $32M in existing federal and foundation grants and contracts through the lifetime of the projects, increasing in budget annually by $9M. Departmental faculty provide a full-spectrum of clinical care for women of all ages, participate in research, and provide education to students and residents. Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package including: · Medical: Multiple plan options · Dental: Multiple plan options · Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision · FMLA Medical leave · Tax deferred annuity savings option plans (401k, 403B, 457) · Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses · ECO Pass: Reduced rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: · PhD in relevant scientific area such as Biochemistry, Cell Biology, Molecular Biology, or Reproductive Biology · Relevant previous post-doctoral experience (for applicants with a previous postdoctoral fellowship) · Relevant technical skills, including experience with primary cell isolation, cell culture, and routine laboratory experiments such as performance and analysis of real-time PCR, western blotting, biochemical assays, immunohistochemistry, immunofluorescence, EIAs, gene transfection/transduction studies, generation of viral constructs, iPSC technology · Experience in handling mice Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Preferred Qualifications: · PhD in reproductive biology/endocrinology/mouse genetics Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: · Excellent communication and organizational skills · Excellent skills in scientific writing · Ability to work independently yet collaboratively · A strong work ethic and a commitment to being a team player in the lab and advancing knowledge in the field · Meticulous record-keeping of experiments and laboratory operations How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): 1. A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position 2. Curriculum vitae / Resume 3. Three to five professional references, including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Questions should be directed to: Olivia Castillo at Olivia.Castillo@cuanschutz.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Immediately and continues until position is filled. For best consideration, apply by November 15th, 2026. Anticipated Pay Range: HIRING RANGE : Salaries commensurate with experience according to NIH Kirschstein-NRSA guidelines which are $62,232 – $75,564 The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation unless it is non-exempt. Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: The University of Colorado (CU) is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@ucdenver.edu ​. Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41373&lang=en": {
      "title": "Business Operations Professional",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 9, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: SOP-Center Substance AbusePrev Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus Department: Skaggs School of Pharmacy and Pharmaceutical Sciences – Colorado Consortium for Prescription Drug Misuse Prevention Job Title: Business Operations Professional Position #: 00799058 – Requisition #: 41373 Job Summary: The Center for Prescription Drug Misuse Prevention coordinates Colorado’s response to the misuse of medications such as opioids, stimulants, and sedatives. The Center’s mission is to reduce prescription drug misuse in Colorado by developing policies, programs, and partnerships with the state agencies, nonprofit organizations, and community coalitions to address one of Colorado’s major public health crises. The Colorado Consortium for Prescription Drug Misuse Prevention (Consortium) is the community engagement core of the Center. The Center is supported by and located at the University of Colorado Skaggs School of Pharmacy and Pharmaceutical Sciences at the CU Anschutz Medical Campus. The Business Operations Professional provides comprehensive operational, financial, and administrative support for the Center for Prescription Drug Misuse Prevention. This position is responsible for coordinating procurement and vendor activities, monitoring grant and program deliverables, tracking expenditures, preparing reports, supporting recruitment and onboarding activities, and coordinating events and special projects. The role ensures efficient business operations, compliance with funding and procurement requirements, and effective support of the Center’s public health programs and strategic initiatives. Key Responsibilities: Coordinate and support the day-to-day operations of the Center, including planning, organizing, and implementing administrative and programmatic activities in partnership with Center leadership. Manage procurement and financial processes, including purchase orders, honoraria payments, vendor payments, sponsorships, invoices, expense reimbursements, and related financial documentation. Evaluate vendor proposals, recommend vendor selections, and assist with negotiating pricing, services, and contract terms to support Center projects and initiatives. Administer grant and program activities by tracking deliverables, expenditures, timelines, and outcomes, and preparing regular progress and financial reports for leadership and funding requirements. Support grant application and project administration processes, including coordinating requests for applications, organizing review activities, and maintaining accurate program records and documentation. Provide administrative support for recruitment, onboarding, and employee transitions, including scheduling interviews, coordinating orientation activities, and ensuring staff have the resources necessary to perform their roles. Coordinate Center-sponsored meetings, trainings, and special events; manage travel and expense processes; and identify opportunities to improve operational efficiency, service delivery, and organizational effectiveness. Work Location: Remote – this role is eligible to work remotely, but the employee must be in the United States. There is an expectation for the candidate to be on campus 1-2 times a year. Why Join Us: The Skaggs School of Pharmacy and Pharmaceutical Sciences, located at the Anschutz Medical Campus, is an internationally renowned School of Pharmacy and a top-tier research school ranked in the top 10% of more than 140 schools in the country for research grant funding. At the Skaggs School of Pharmacy and Pharmaceutical Sciences, we are committed to excellence and innovation in professional, graduate, and post-graduate education; scholarship and research; patient-centered care; public health advocacy; and societal leadership and engagement. Together, our innovation, discoveries, and engagement with our communities improve the health and well-being of society. Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation, and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 15/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree in business, business administration, finance, accounting, education, social services, healthcare administration, public administration, public health, or a directly related field from an accredited institution. Substitution : A combination of education and related technical/military/paraprofessional experience may be substituted for a bachelor’s degree on a year for year basis. One (1) year of professional level experience with business administration or operations. Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Preferred Qualifications: Working knowledge of University of Colorado procurement process and marketplace. At least one (1) year of professional level work with budgets, financial reports, or grants. Conditions of Employment: Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without requiring sponsorship. We are unable to provide work visa sponsorship or employment authorization for this position now or in the future. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Ability to communicate effectively, both in writing and orally. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with employees at all levels throughout the organization. Outstanding customer service skills. Strong problem-solving and analytical skills. Strong administrative skills with the ability to set priorities and manage multiple tasks. Proficient with technology, especially Microsoft Office applications. How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position. Curriculum vitae / Resume Three to five professional references, including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address. Questions should be directed to: Jennifer Place, jennifer.place@cuanschutz.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Screening begins 10/23/2026. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as $56,995 – $76,374 . The above salary range (or hiring range) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position may be eligible for overtime compensation, depending on the level. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@cuanschutz.edu . Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41371&lang=en": {
      "title": "Research Services Principal Professional (Post Award Specialist)",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 9, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: SOM-EM MED CLINICAL Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus Department: Emergency Medicine Job Title: Research Services Principal Professional (Post Award Specialist) Position #: 00853862 – Requisition #: 41371 Job Summary: The University of Colorado Denver | Anschutz Medical Campus is currently seeking applications for a Research Services Principal Professional - Post-Award Specialist. This is a full-time University Staff (non-classified) position, will be responsible for managing the administration of grants for the Department of Emergency Medicine. Using available resources, this position will investigate discrepancies and incorporate feedback to ensure accurate financial reporting on grants. This position will also verify transactions and details posted to the General Ledger (GL), handle payroll changes and transfers related to grants, as well as conduct other budget proposals and analyses as requested. This position will be faced with multiple priorities, as well as difficult situations, and will be required to be flexible, adaptive, and able to articulate thoughts and explanations to those with varying levels of understanding in finance and budgeting. This position will work independently, as well as interact with a diverse group of professionals and research faculty in an evolving professional environment to effectively contribute to the growth and accomplishment of departmental goals. It is expected that these duties and responsibilities are performed at an intermediate and advanced level, and that this position has complete responsibility and accountability for all departmental processes that involve post-award grant management, as well as Payroll/Human Resource functions Key Responsibilities: Assist with grant and contract management in the Department of Emergency Medicine. Serve as a backup for developing and submitting grant applications, contributing to both pre- and post-award processes. Review grant notices of award and granting agencies’ policies to identify specific policies, rules, and deadlines. Establish correct funding and personnel effort for each sponsored project and manage subcontracts, independent contractors, and purchase orders as needed. Analyze cash balances, reconcile expenditures, assist in subrecipient monitoring, prepare journal entries and process payroll expense transfers and funding distribution updates for all sponsored projects. Initiate preaward speedtypes and manage re-budgeting requests for awarded grants. Prepare prior approval and carry-forward requests, amendments, and no cost extensions. Collaborate with OGC during closeout process and assists with preparing financial reports. Promptly notify Grants Manager of contractual issues and potential problems; propose viable solutions. Review, analyze and report monthly accounting activity on sponsored project accounts ensuring compliance to internal and external policies. Engage in strategic collaboration with Grants Manager to customize monthly reports, concisely itemizing, interpreting, and comparing expenditures to budget. Run payroll and financial detail reports to confirm funding distributions are posting correctly; investigate and resolve errors as needed. Develop and maintain accurate budget projections and prepare comprehensive budget/reporting/forecasting tools for internal and external stakeholders. Actively participate in budget preparation and analysis and prepare financial statements and monthly projections for PIs. Complete all pertinent forms and request to sponsor and Office of Grants and Contracts, facilitating the timely closure of grant accounts. Act as custodian for PI gift card programs and complete quarterly reconciliations. Assist faculty in keeping their Other Support records up to date. Review and process payments for subcontractor and other vendor invoices. Reconcile study subject visit payments and work with sponsor to resolve any payment discrepancies. Independently track all clinical research revenue and ensures a 100% collection of all clinical trials and generates processes and systems to identify if/when clinical trial revenue is late or uncollected. Recommend process and procedure updates to improve workflow. Understand and interpret complex guidelines and regulations for salary caps, facilities and administrative cost calculations, and funding restrictions on sponsored projects. Interpret and implement complex layers of policy. Assist with other Postaward duties as needed by the department. This description is a summary only and describes the general level of work being performed, it is not intended to be all-inclusive. The duties of this position may change from time to time and/or based on business need. We reserve the right to add or delete duties and responsibilities at the discretion of the supervisor and/or hiring authority. Work Location: Hybrid/Remote – In-State Candidates: this role is eligible for a hybrid schedule of 3 days per week on campus in Aurora, CO and as needed for in-person meetings. We will also consider fully remote applicants located within the United States. Why Join Us: The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is a public education, clinical and research facility serving 4,500 students, and a world-class medical destination at the forefront of life-changing science, medicine, and healthcare. CU Anschutz offers more than 42 highly rated degree programs through 6 schools and colleges, and receives over $500 million in research awards each year. We are the single largest health professions education provider in Colorado, awarding nearly 1,450 degrees annually. Powered by our award-winning faculty, renowned researchers and a reputation for academic excellence, the CU Anschutz Medical Campus drives innovation from the classroom to the laboratory to the delivery of unparalleled patient care. Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 10/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree with an emphasis in Accounting, Finance or Business-related major. A combination of education and related technical/paraprofessional experience may be substituted for the bachelor’s degree on a year for year basis. 3-5 years of professional grant and contract experience. Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Preferred Qualifications: Experience with Info Ed Proposal Development System or similar grant submission software. Experience with CU Data, A2E, HCM and CU Marketplace. Experience working in an academic environment or medical center. Experience with PeopleSoft (HRMS &/or Finance). Proficient with Excel Grant and/or contract experience both pre and post. Research administration experience. Master’s degree from an accredited college or university in a related field. Conditions of Employment: Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without requiring sponsorship. We are unable to provide work visa sponsorship or employment authorization for this position now or in the future. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Ability to communicate effectively, both in writing and orally. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with employees at all levels throughout the institution. Outstanding customer service skills. Excellent attention to detail. Ability to prioritize and handle multiple competing deadlines in a fast-paced environment. Ability to maintain a high level of confidentiality with sensitive information. Demonstrated ability to use spreadsheets, word processing, email and calendar software. Ability to tolerate a high degree of ambiguity yet work effectively to fulfill the mission, goals and objectives of the department. Ability to understand and interpret complex guidelines and regulations for salary caps, facilities and administrative cost calculations, funding restrictions. How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position Curriculum vitae / Resume Three to five professional references, including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Questions should be directed to: EMED HR, emed.humanresources@cudenver.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Immediately and continues until position is filled, preferred apply by date of 10/15. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as HIRING RANGE $67,864 – 90,937 . The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position may be eligible for overtime compensation, depending on the level. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@cuanschutz.edu ​. Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41368&lang=en": {
      "title": "Float New Patient and Surgery Scheduler",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 9, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: SOM-OB/GYN CHAIR GENERAL OPS Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Department: Obstetrics and Gynecology Job Title: Float New Patient and Surgery Scheduler Position #: 00853816 – Requisition #:41368 Job Summary: In the Department of Obstetrics and Gynecology, as part of the larger University of Colorado Anschutz School of Medicine, we have access to an intensive care unit, cutting-edge equipment, and multiple teams of subspecialists in female health. This allows us to address even the most complex medical problems. We also provide a wide array of reconstructive surgical options, including minimally invasive and robotic surgery. The individual in this position will function as the liaison between the patient and the providers for all non-clinical issues, including scheduling office visits and procedures within the clinics, scheduling surgeries, communicating pre-appointment instructions and appointment confirmations, insurance verifications, and/or pre-authorizations as necessary. The Float New Patient and Surgery Scheduler will NOT disseminate any clinical information such as diagnosis, test results or post care instructions. They must be able to analyze the faculty’s availability when scheduling patients for new patient visits and surgeries. Must understand the length of time needed for a particular visit type and schedule patient appropriately. They must be able to identify conflicts in these schedules, review them with the appropriate physician and resolve them in a timely manner. This position interacts with patients, faculty, scheduling staff, research staff, clinic staff, hospital and department administration, and insurance representatives daily in providing support for scheduling appointments and surgeries. As a float position, this individual will be trained on and support scheduling across multiple divisions in the OBGYN department. This position may also support some administrative needs of assigned providers. This position will work under the direction of the Clinical Operations Program Manager for the Department. Key Responsibilities: Scheduling Support: Assist and act in patient scheduling issues, training, education, communication and problem solving. Develop and maintain training and workflow documents for Surgery scheduling. Schedule operative cases across multiple locations of care and different health systems as directed by supervisor, clinical providers and nursing staff. Obtain surgery insurance authorizations. Coordinate, track, and generate reports on OR block time, including all related communication with the hospitals Assist with new patient visit scheduling and procure new patient medical records in a timely manner as needed. Route correspondence to referring physicians and other appropriate care providers. Share in answering incoming telephone calls from patients and referring physicians. Serve as a liaison between patients and physicians for all non-clinical issues. Complete referral and authorization checks. Participate in staff meetings and trainings as required. Generate patient quotes for procedures and surgeries. Display a willingness to work collaboratively, timely and cooperatively with all members of the Department team. Establishes and maintains effective working relationships with leadership, physicians, colleagues and patients, addresses concerns in a forthright manner. Administrative Support Provide administrative support to Department faculty as needed. Perform broad range of high-level administrative duties as requested. Work Location: Hybrid – this role is eligible for a hybrid schedule of 3 days per week on campus and as needed for in-person meetings. Why Join Us: Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 15/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: High school diploma or GED Two (2) years of patient registration and insurance processes. Substitution : A combination of related education and/or relevant experience in an occupation related to the work assigned equal to two (2) years. Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Preferred Qualifications: Bilingual, Spanish-speaking. Customer service or general administrative experience. Experience with appointment scheduling and insurance verification. EPIC experience. MS Office experience. Two (2) years or more of Surgical Scheduling experience. Surgical Scheduling training experience within EPIC. Four (4) years or more of administrative experience in a health-care setting. Conditions of Employment: Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without requiring sponsorship. We are unable to provide work visa sponsorship or employment authorization for this position now or in the future. Competencies: Ability to communicate effectively, both in writing and orally. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with employees at all levels throughout the institution. Ability to multitask efficiently and effectively while maintaining quality control standards. Ability to maintain accuracy, consistency, and confidentiality. Outstanding customer service skills. Understanding of HIPAA practices and patient confidentiality. Ability to maintain a positive attitude with clients, employees, and management. Ability to work quickly – individually and as part of a team. Ability to read, analyze, and interpret policies, documents, and regulations. Must be detail-orientated and maintain excellent organizational skills. Must be tech savvy (ability to understand, apply, and benefit from technology). Ability to effectively communicate at all levels, including physicians, leadership, and staff. Ability to work within large, complex healthcare systems. Ability to attest to computer proficiency and learn new computer applications. Ability to keyboard/type, write legibly, and accurately record information. Ability to analyze and interpret data. Ability to organize workflow with particular focus on tracking patient care and improving patient flow. Effectively copes with fast-paced environment and typical job stressors. Ability to deal calmly and courteously with people. Ability to follow oral and written instructions and established procedures. Ability to multitask efficiently and effectively while maintaining quality control standards. Ability to maintain accuracy, consistency, and confidentiality. Demonstrates personal integrity, honesty, and sincerity at all times. Ability to perform basic filing, office procedures and word processing. Ability to adhere to all policies and procedures, including but not limited to standards for safety, attendance, punctuality, and personal appearance. How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position Curriculum vitae / Resume Three to five professional references, including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Questions should be directed to: Amrita Shetty, Amrita.Shetty@cuanschutz.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Applications will be accepted until finalists are identified, but preference will be given to complete applications received by October 31 st . Those who do not apply by this date may or may not be considered. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as $43,700 - $52,877. The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position may be eligible for overtime compensation, depending on the level. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@cuanschutz.edu ​. Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41366&lang=en": {
      "title": "Anatomic Pathology (AP) Business Support Office Manager",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 9, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: SOM-Pathology Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Department of Pathology Anatomic Pathology (AP) Business Support Office Manager Position #:00853859 – Requisition #: 41366 Job Summary: The CU Anschutz, Department of Pathology is excited to recruit a full-time Anatomic Pathology (AP) Business Support Office Manager. This position will provide high-level administrative support to the Surgical Pathology Laboratory, a CLIA and CAP approved clinical laboratory and the Anatomic Pathology Leadership. The AP Business Support Office Manager directly supervises a team of eight (8) full-time members and is responsible for the day-to-day operations of the Anatomic Pathology Business Support Office and personnel performance and management. The AP Business Support Office Manager will work closely with pathologists and Department administration to create efficiencies and support of general, indirect patient care operations and management of healthcare services. Key Responsibilities: 40% - Performs and coordinates specimen activities, including specimen accessioning, filling testing and IHC requests for send outs to various outside institutions and labs on the AMC, case preparation for clinical conferences, tumor boards, and consultations, procurement of patient slides, blocks and reports, and data entry into clinical reports. 10% - Prepares staff schedules to ensure coverage for smooth service operations and provides back-up coverage to any role within the Front Office. 5% - Develops and implements written policies, protocols, and practices for each task performed by the Front Office staff. Maintains document control of the AP Front Office Manual in Media Lab (cloud-based document control application). 5% - Ensures staff receives CU required inline training and assigns additional training courses, as relevant to the employee roles. Provides direct, on-the-job training of personnel and functional cross-training of staff. Develops and conducts performing employees’ competency checks, per CAP requirements. 10% - Engages in Quality Control and Quality Assurance activities. Prepares quarterly QA reports for the Lab Director/ Quality Director, and the Operations Director, including accessioning productivity, send-out statistics, percent clerical error rate, safety audits, and various special QI assignments, as needed. 5% - Resolves technical problems, investigates errors, conducts root-cause analysis, and trouble shoot processes towards continuous quality improvement. Takes actions required to close any performance gaps. 5% - Regularly holds staff feedback forums, coaching sessions, safety huddles, and educational in-services. Assesses and communicates progress towards work goals and objectives. Takes action that results in a high level of morale and motivation among team members. 5% - Engages in two-way conversations throughout the year that ensure an up-to-date understanding of expectations, standards, and provides ongoing feedback and support as employees strive to achieve expectations. Completes annual staff performance evaluations. Guards against burnout and implements a system for employee development, and recognition, as well as a timely disciplinary action. 10% - Takes initiative to address new and longstanding issues in a timely and proactive manner with appropriate written documentation (written job expectation standards and periodic employee-in-person coaching. Handles sensitive or difficult issues with grace and confidence. Manages personnel issues with sound judgement, fairness, and clear-headed focus. 5% - Participates in the departmental administration and management meetings, educational, and professional development activities, as well as teaching activities related to laboratory administration, professionalism, and quality management in anatomic pathology laboratory. Work Location: Onsite – this role is expected to work onsite and is located in Aurora, CO. Why Join Us: Welcome to the Department of Pathology of the University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus. The Department has grown substantially in the past 15 years, from 40 to 120 faculty in parallel with the remarkable growth of our hospital-based affiliates as well as the city and county of Denver. Our work is value driven and focused on scientific investigation, lifelong learning and a balance of personal and professional values. In addition to a vibrant and highly competitive residency program with 25 positions, we offer 9 fellowships and participate in numerous graduate school and the MD/PhD program of the CU School of Medicine. Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 15/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree in biological science, nutrition, nursing, health, human services, psychology, counseling, social work, or a directly related field from an accredited institution 4-6 years of professional experience in medical office/personnel management, which includes 3-5 years in a supervisory/ managerial role Substitution : An advanced degree (Masters or Doctorate) may be substituted for experience on a year for year basis if the degree is in a field of study directly related to the work assignment. Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Preferred Qualifications: Experience calculating lab results and data using math and analytical skills. Professional experience in management, in a teaching hospital setting Previous experience in a leadership role within a pathology department Experience with day-to-day transcriptionist services operations/functions. Experience entering data into an electronic system. Experience with medical terminology, human anatomy and physiology. Conditions of Employment: Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without requiring sponsorship. We are unable to provide work visa sponsorship or employment authorization for this position now or in the future. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Advanced computer skills (including proficiency in the use of MS Office and AI tools). Familiarity with HIPAA and security compliance requirements. Highly motivated individual looking to pursue a long-term career in hospital management A bility to communicate effectively, both in writing and orally. Self-starter that demonstrates the ability to work individually with minimal supervision as well as part of a team, and to maintain effective working relationships with employees at all levels throughout the institution. Demeanor of professionalism, helpfulness, and dedication to providing excellent customer service to the internal and external clients of Anatomic Pathology. Outstanding interpersonal and customer service skills with focus on patient care. Solid organizational skills: ability to handle multiple assignments and priorities yet still fulfill all commitments. Ability to take direction and use independent judgment to coordinate and meet multiple deadlines. Ability to interpret complex rules, regulations, policies, procedures, and guidelines. Ability to work effectively under pressure and handle sensitive or difficult issues with grace and confidence. Personal integrity and proven sound judgment and problem-solving skills. Credibility, accountability, and outstanding work ethics. How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): Curriculum vitae / Resume Three to five professional references, including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Questions should be directed to: PathHR@cuanschutz.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Applications will be accepted until finalists are identified, but preference will be given to complete applications received by 10/31/2026. Those who do not apply by this date may or may not be considered. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as $85,068 to $113,992. The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position may be eligible for overtime compensation, depending on the level. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@cuanschutz.edu ​. Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41363&lang=en": {
      "title": "Post Award Finance Int – Principal Specialist",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 9, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: SOM-SRG-CH GENERAL OPERATIONS Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Department: Surgery Job Title: Post Award Finance Int – Principal Specialist Position #: 00773174 - Requisition #:41363 Job Summary: This position serves a key role in the fiscal management and oversight of grant and clinical trial post-award activities within the Department of Surgery (DOS). The position applies professional knowledge of research administration, financial management, and sponsored project compliance to support the financial administration of grants and clinical trials. Responsibilities include preparing and analyzing financial reports, monitoring project expenditures, reconciling accounts, and providing guidance to Principal Investigators (PIs) and designated research personnel regarding post-award financial activities. Key Responsibilities: Financial Reporting (33%): Develop and maintain reporting tools to forecast funding and spending per PI, lab or other cohort. Deliver monthly financial reporting and projections to PIs. Host regular meetings with PIs to advise spending trends and strategic planning Confirm accuracy of budgets against award documents. Confirm accuracy of collected revenues against invoices. Provide expense documentation as required by award to OGC. Maintain reconciliation processes and communicate findings to the PIs/ Run payroll reports to confirm funding and distribution; investigate and resolve errors by working with Payroll and Benefits. Financial Transactions (33%): Prepare and submit payroll expense transfers (PET), payroll expense transfers benefits only (PETb), and personnel funding entries (FE) as needed. Review clinical trial coordinator time reporting with Clinical Research Manager, and make funding updates accordingly. Prepare and submit journal entries to distribute funds and to transfer expenditures. Prepare and submit purchase orders for external institutions serving as subrecipients to CU. Review and submit subrecipient invoices. Assist faculty with electronic Personal Effort Report (ePERS) certification for time-reporting spent on research grants and clinical trials. Award Management (34%): Extract data using InfoED to collect and store proposal and award documentation. Prepare Other Support documentation (AKA Current and Pending Support) for project personnel, build budget revisions, and create budget justifications as needed. Request PreAward speedtypes for incoming awards. Review award documents with the PI, making note of any special restrictions. Develop and maintain a comprehensive calendar that includes all award start, end and renewal dates, as well as progress report and final report submission deadlines. Interface with OnCore to track patient visits, medical procedures, and other recurring administrative fees for invoicing purposes. Prepare and submit requests for award no-cost extensions, revised budgets, key personnel changes, change of scope, and financial reporting directly to sponsors or through OGC. Prepare and submit financial invoices to industry sponsored clinical trials per terms of individual contracts and track clinical trial payments. Process close-out paperwork for grants and clinical trials. Principal Professional : In addition to the duties above… Serve as a research administration subject matter expert for the DOS. Manage multiple large and small federal and non-federal grants, contracts and clinical trials using Uniform Guidance CFR 200. This description is a summary only and describes the general level of work being performed, it is not intended to be all-inclusive. The duties of this position may change from time to time and/or based on business need. We reserve the right to add or delete duties and responsibilities at the discretion of the supervisor and/or hiring authority. Work Location: Hybrid – this role is eligible for a hybrid schedule of 3 days per week on campus and as needed for in-person meetings. Why Join Us: Welcome to the Department of Surgery. Our mission is to make a positive contribution to each person’s life. Through care, curing, compassion, and hope, we strive to improve the lives of our patients, their families, those we work with, our community, and the world. Our department consists of surgeons and researchers who are known for their work nationally and internationally. Alongside these individuals works a support system of administrative personnel who are unmatched in their efforts as we all dare to be exceptional. Through our collective work, we are innovating surgical care, finding cures through discovery, and educating the world’s future surgical leaders. Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 15/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Intermediate: Bachelor’s degree in finance, accounting, business administration, business, or a directly related field from an accredited institution. Substitution : A combination of education and related technical/military/paraprofessional experience may be substituted for a bachelor’s degree on a year for year basis. One (1) year professional level experience in sponsored project administration or related finance administration Senior: Bachelor’s degree in finance, accounting, business administration, business, or a directly related field from an accredited institution. Substitution : A combination of education and related technical/military/paraprofessional experience may be substituted for a bachelor’s degree on a year for year basis. Two (2) years professional level experience in sponsored project administration or related finance administration Principal: Bachelor’s degree in finance, accounting, business administration, business, or a directly related field from an accredited institution. Substitution : A combination of education and related technical/military/paraprofessional experience may be substituted for a bachelor’s degree on a year for year basis. Five (5) years professional level experience in sponsored project administration or related finance administration For all levels, applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Preferred Qualifications (All Levels): Experience working with the Uniform Guidance Code of Federal Regulations (CFR 200) and NIH GPS. Experience managing the administrative tasks of clinical trials and research grants. Experience using integrated accounting, purchasing and payroll system. Experience operating University of Colorado systems: Peoplesoft, HCM, M-fin reporting, CU Marketplace, InfoED, redCAP, Smartsheet. Senior : Three (3) years of professional level experience in sponsored project administration or related finance administration. Principal: Experience operating as a subject matter expert of CFR 200. Conditions of Employment: Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without requiring sponsorship. We are unable to provide work visa sponsorship or employment authorization for this position now or in the future. Competencies, Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Ability to communicate effectively, both in writing and orally. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with employees at all levels throughout the institution. Outstanding customer service skills. Elevated and/or advanced understanding of Microsoft Office, especially excel Demonstrated ability to use spreadsheets, word processing, email and calendar software. Ability to work fully independently ( Senior & Principal Levels). How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position Curriculum vitae / Resume Three to five professional references, including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Questions should be directed to: SurgeryFinance@cuanschutz.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Applications will be accepted until finalists are identified, but preference will be given to complete applications received by October 22, 2026. Those who do not apply by this date may or may not be considered. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as HIRING RANGE Intermediate: $54,586 to $73,145 Senior: $59,012 to $79,076 Principal: $67,864 to $90,937 The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position may be eligible for overtime compensation, depending on the level. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@cuanschutz.edu ​. Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41361&lang=en": {
      "title": "Events & Marketing Professional",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 8, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: SOM-OB/GYN CHAIR GENERAL OPS Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Department: Obstetrics and Gynecology Job Title: Events & Marketing Professional Position #: 00853585 – Requisition #:41361 Job Summary: The Department of Obstetrics and Gynecology is recruiting an Events and Marketing Professional who will assist with planning and overseeing both department and divisional events, event marketing, and social media for the department in partnership with the Events and Marketing Core team. This includes a variety of Continuing Medical Education (CME) courses, including larger events throughout the year at offsite locations, such as the Department’s Annual Vail OB-GYN Conference. This position will work in a collaborative, close relationship with the department’s Events and Marketing Core Team, which includes the Director of Operations, Events and Marketing Coordinator, Department CME & Education Coordinator, and the Web Development and Marketing Professional. This individual will partner with this team to establish the schedules and work processes that contribute to the ongoing development, analysis and evaluations of existing and proposed events, and marketing within the department. This position is responsible for representing the department in the utmost professional manner to attendees, exhibitors, faculty, and community members. In addition to event planning, this position will partner with the Events and Marketing Professional to complete social media updates, write content, update the website, and advertise events for the department. This individual will also create print and digital marketing materials and signage for department events including ordering promotional materials and swag. This individual is also responsible for planning, producing, and analyzing the effectiveness of digital communications for the Department of OB-GYN's education and clinical groups alongside the Events and Marketing Core team. This work also happens across a variety of platforms including email, event registration and websites. This position will work with clinical faculty and staff to create creative content for various department and divisional marketing efforts including visual, copywriting, story creation, and video editing (as needed). Key Responsibilities: Facilitates national and local conferences and meetings for departmental and divisional leadership. This includes the scheduling and coordination for national, regional, and local speakers, sponsors and guests as needed by the various events. Tracks budgets for events and marketing. Coordinates procurement for travel logistics and events related to speakers. Provide event-related support for regular and annual educational activities with our faculty and staff. Assists with Community Engagement events and provide support to divisional community events. Building and maintaining relationships with local organizations that support and engage women Produces and maintains social media editorial content for department and divisional social media accounts. Develop content and creative storytelling for social media targeted at engaging specific audiences including community members, donors, alumni, potential trainees, conference attendees, etc. Produce multimedia content such as Instagram reels, quality photography, and quality infographics. Creates digital and print materials for event marketing and educational seminars. Manage social media communities – monitoring, listening, recording and responding appropriately. Work Location: Hybrid – this role is eligible for a hybrid schedule of 3 days per week on campus and as needed for in-person meetings. Why Join Us: Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 15/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree in marketing, journalism, public relations, communications, business administration, business, or a directly related field from an accredited institution. Substitution : A combination of education and related technical/military/paraprofessional experience may be substituted for a bachelor’s degree on a year for year basis . 2 years of professional experience directly related to event planning and marketing. Substitution: An advanced degree (Masters or Doctorate) may be substituted for experience on a year-for-year basis if the degree is in a field of study directly related to the work assignment. Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Preferred Qualifications: 3-5 years of professional experience directly related to event planning and marketing. Experience working with Outlook, Excel, Word, and PowerPoint. Experience working with University of Colorado procurement systems (i.e. Concur, Marketplace, Cvent etc.). Experience booking travel arrangements (airfare, hotel, rental cars, etc.). Experience with multimedia production (photography and videography) and Adobe Creative Suite. Experience working in Canva. Experience working in Sitefinity (website platform). Meeting and event planning experience, including contract negotiation, exhibitor management, and catering. Experience working within branding guidelines Conditions of Employment: Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without requiring sponsorship. We are unable to provide work visa sponsorship or employment authorization for this position now or in the future. May occasionally need to work evenings and weekends for events Competencies/Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Expertise in contract negotiation, exhibitor management, and catering selection. Knowledge of social media standard processes and community management for platforms including, but not limited to Facebook, Instagram, X (formerly Twitter), LinkedIn and TikTok. Ability to communicate effectively, both in writing and orally. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with employees at all levels throughout the institution. Outstanding customer service skills. Ability to develop and manage budgets and carry out the fiscal responsibilities of the position. Ability to manage projects in an efficient and effective manner. Ability to establish priorities and meet competing deadlines. How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position. Curriculum vitae / Resume Three to five professional references, including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Questions should be directed to: Amrita Shetty, Amrita.Shetty@cuanschutz.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Applications will be accepted until finalists are identified, but preference will be given to complete applications received by October 16 th . Those who do not apply by this date may or may not be considered. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as $56,787 - $76,095. The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position may be eligible for overtime compensation, depending on the level. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@cuanschutz.edu ​. Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41357&lang=en": {
      "title": "Senior Clinical Research Coordinator",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 8, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: SOM-MED-Gastroenterology Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus Department: Medicine – Division of Gastroenterology & Hepatology Job Title: Senior Clinical Research Coordinator Position #: 00845344 – Requisition #: 41357 Job Summary: The Senior Clinical Research Coordinator is part of a team that includes supportive research personnel (regulatory, budget, coordinators) and medical personnel all led by the principal investigator and the GI division research leadership. This position will participate in clinical research projects including studies examining pancreatitis and therapeutic endoscopy. This position requires an ability to work independently, but collaboratively, attention to detail, and the ability to maintain organized protocol documentation and data. The studies we conduct require in-person and telephone interactions with participants/patients/staff. Key Responsibilities: Assist with developing or developing protocol-specific systems and documents including process flows, training manuals, Standard Operating Procedures (SOPs) and Case Report Forms (CRFs). Maintains subject level documentation and prepares documents, equipment and/or supplies Assist with identifying issues related to operational efficiency and shares results with leadership Collect information to determine feasibility, recruitment and retention strategies. Employ, evaluate and assist with the implementation of innovative solutions to maximize recruitment and retention Serve as a resource and participate in study initiation and close out duties Other duties as assigned. Work Location: Hybrid – this role is eligible for a hybrid schedule of 3-4 days per week on campus and as needed for in-person meetings. Why Join Us: The University of Colorado’s Division of Gastroenterology and Hepatology in the Department of Medicine, located at the Anschutz Medical Campus, is an internationally renowned program that provides comprehensive resources for the diagnosis and therapy of diseases of the digestive tract, pancreas, and liver. The Division of Gastroenterology and Hepatology has faculty and staff making contributions to translational research, clinical trials, and nationally recognized patient care. By joining our division, you would be joining a rapidly growing team, with clinical practices throughout the state of Colorado and over 80 researchers, physicians, and staff, all working toward its vision to prevent and treat diseases while being a global model for patient care delivery, interdisciplinary research, and training. Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation, and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 15/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree in any field. A combination of education and related technical/military/paraprofessional experience may be substituted for a bachelor’s degree on a year for year basis. Two (2) years’ clinical research or related experience. Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Preferred Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree in science or health related field. Three (3) years of clinical research or related experience. Experience with electronic data capture systems (e.g. EMR or EHR and data management systems), preferably Epic and/or CPRS. Experience with data capture and management tools, such as REDCap. Conditions of Employment: Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without requiring sponsorship. We are unable to provide work visa sponsorship or employment authorization for this position now or in the future. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Knowledge and understanding of federal regulations and Good Clinical Practice (GCP). Ability to communicate effectively, both in writing and orally. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with employees at all levels throughout the institution. Outstanding customer service skills. Knowledge of basic human anatomy, physiology medical terminology. Ability to interpret and master complex research protocol information. Proficiency with Microsoft Office products and functionality, specifically Excel, Word, and PowerPoint. Knowledge and experience with IRB policies and procedures. How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position. Curriculum vitae / Resume Three to five professional references, including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address. Questions should be directed to: Ingeborg Cuba, Ingeborg.cuba@cuanschutz.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Immediately and continue until position is filled. For best consideration, apply by November 1 st , 2026 . Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as $58,705 – $78,665 . The above salary range (or hiring range) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position may be eligible for overtime compensation, depending on the level. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@cuanschutz.edu . Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41341&lang=en": {
      "title": "Post-Award Admin Professional (Part-Time, Non-Benefits Eligible)",
      "description": "Closing Date: 10/19/2026 Posted Date: Oct 8, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: SOM-PM&R GENERAL OPERATIONS Schedule: Part-time University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus | Department: Physical Medicine and Rehabilitation Job Title: Post-Award Admin Professional (Part-Time, Non-Benefits Eligible) Position #: 00853808 | Requisition #: 41341 Job Summary: The Department of Physical Medicine and Rehabilitation is seeking a collaborative professional to provide comprehensive support to post-award research administration, sponsored projects, procurement and administrative operations. The position works with faculty, staff, department leadership, Principal Investigators, research teams, hospital affiliates, and central campus partners to coordinate complex operational and sponsored-project activities while maintaining confidentiality, accuracy, and compliance. The role combines day-to-day departmental support with post-award research administration, procurement and travel. Key Responsibilities: Process grant-related invoices through CU Marketplace and coordinate payment of expenditures funded by Children's Hospital Colorado (CHCO). Support sponsored project administration by tracking expenditures, maintaining documentation, and assisting faculty and research staff with financial and operational processes. Reconcile purchases against financial detail reports to ensure accuracy and appropriateness Provide travel coordination and reimbursement support for faculty and research personnel in compliance with University and sponsor requirements. Procure research equipment, supplies, and services, ensuring costs are allowable and compliant with grant and institutional guidelines. Liaison for research groups within Department and Procurement Service Center Work Location: Remote given small FTE. However, if the FTE increases at any point, the department will reassess the hybrid workspace. Why Join Us: Thank you for considering joining our team. The field of rehabilitation believes in using your whole body to improve your human performance. The department of Physical Medicine and Rehabilitation at the University of Colorado (which we affectionately call \"CU PM&R\") is at the forefront of using team science, regenerative medicine, and exercise treatments. It is uniquely situated in the state-of-the-art CU Anschutz Medical Campus, the first campus in the nation to be built from the ground up to bring research, education, and patient care into one visionary collaboration. Like the Rocky Mountains that provide a backdrop of our institutions, CU PM&R is on the rise! We combine the disciplines of rehabilitation medicine, physical therapy, psychology, speech/language therapy, and rehabilitation sciences into a singular department. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's degree from an accredited institution in business, business administration, public administration, healthcare administration, research administration, finance, accounting, communications, education, or a directly related field. Substitution : A combination of education and related technical/military/paraprofessional experience may be substituted for a bachelor’s degree on a year for year basis. One (1) year of professional experience with sponsored research, pre-/post-award, financial management or other related research experience. Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Preferred Qualifications: Experience with post-award research administration, sponsored-project financial management, budgeting, forecasting, reconciliation, invoicing, or financial reporting. Experience working in a large, complex organization, higher education, academic medicine, healthcare, or a health sciences environment. Experience providing administrative support to senior or executive-level leaders. Condition of Employment Must be willing and able to work part-time, with sporadic work schedules, as well as non-guaranteed work hours Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without requiring sponsorship. We are unable to provide work visa sponsorship or employment authorization for this position now or in the future. Competencies: Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities (KSAs): Advanced proficiency with Microsoft Excel and experience maintaining spreadsheets, databases, dashboards, and tracking tools Proficiency with Microsoft Office and the ability to learn new systems and technology. Ability to maintain effective working relationships and confidentiality across a complex environment. Ability to interpret and apply policies, procedures, sponsor requirements, and established business practices. Working knowledge of budgeting, financial reconciliation, sponsored-project administration, and compliance principles. Independent judgment, analytical problem-solving, accuracy, and accountability. Strong organization, prioritization, project coordination, and time-management skills. Clear and professional oral and written communication. Conditions of Employment: Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without requiring sponsorship. We are unable to provide work visa sponsorship or employment authorization for this position now or in the future. How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): A letter of interest describing relevant experience as it relates to the listed qualifications and interest in the position Curriculum vitae / Resume Three to five professional references, if required by the hiring unit Questions should be directed to: Sydney Sanders, Sydney.sanders@cuanschutz.edu , HR Program Manager Screening of Applications Begins: Immediately and continue until 5 days after posting. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting hiring range for this hourly position has been established as: $26.24 - $35.16/hour The above salary range represents the University's good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. Overtime eligibility will be determined based on the approved classification. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans, and retirement contributions. Use the current required compensation and benefits language at the time of posting. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@cuanschutz.edu ​. Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41356&lang=en": {
      "title": "Advanced Practice Provider (APP)/(NP/PA)/ Department of Family Medicine/ Adjoint Senior Instructor/ Whole Person Pain Service",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 8, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: SOM-FM GENERAL OPERATIONS Schedule: Part-time University of Colorado Anschutz Department of Family Medicine Advanced Practice Provider (APP)/(NP/PA)/ Department of Family Medicine/ Adjoint Senior Instructor/ Whole Person Pain Service Position #:00853323 - Requisition #: 41356 Job Summary: The Advanced Practice Provider (APP) in this position will provide care within the Department of Family Medicine, serving the Whole Person Pain Service (WPPS) as a 0.25 cFTE . The Whole Person Pain Service (WPPS) will provide holistic chronic pain care for primary care patients established in the department of family medicine. The service will be 100% virtual and will serve as the chronic pain hub for patients in the department who are currently prescribed chronic opioid medications. The APP in this role will be responsible for two main functions: chronic pain patient care and care coordination. TOTAL FTE COMMITMENT : 0.25 cFTE ( 8 hours of appointable clinic hours per week and 2 hours per week of clinical administrative time (paperwork, documentation, required meetings, required trainings, etc.). Examples of Work Performed The duties and responsibilities of the position include, but are not limited to: Clinical Care · Provide patient care to patients with chronic pain in a virtual setting. · Perform intake, routine follow-up, and group visits for patients on chronic opioids. · Participate as needed in chart review and clinical coding compliance activities. · Collaborate as appropriate with medical staff in the care of complex patients. · Interact with other health professionals to create guidelines and coordinate patient care. · Triage the WPPS inbasket and telephone line and support patients as needed. · Using opioid registries, proactively outreach patients and/or PCPs who may benefit from the WPPS. · Using opioid registries determine the highest risk patients in need to be discussed at collaborative care conferences. Administrative/Professional Development · Maintain eligibility for School of Medicine Faculty. · ­Keep abreast of the latest developments in field, both academically and through applied skills. · Attend and present at conferences, meetings and trainings to maintain certification and enhance professional skills; participates in faculty development activities. · Accept other responsibilities assigned by the Medical Director Quality · Develops, implements, and evaluates the strategy for quality improvement. Why Join Us: Among these is the Department of Family Medicine (DFM) which is dedicated to “helping people be healthier\" by educating, nurturing, fostering, and enhancing those in the field of family medicine and the communities we live in and serve. The Department of Family Medicine has five (5) focus areas, each with specific goals: · Patient Care: Provide outstanding Family Medicine to every patient. · Research: Create and disseminate new knowledge. · Training: Train integrated future Family Medicine workforce. · Community Engagement: Achieve health equity with community engagement and advocacy. · Our People: Nurture a thriving, diverse and equitable department culture Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. · Masters/Doctor of Nursing practice degree or graduation from an NCCPA-approved physician assistant program. · Licensed as a Registered Nurse and Nurse Practitioner or Physician Assistant in the State of Colorado. · Completion of required 1,000 hours (provisional prescription authority/mentorship) or other minimum as defined by State of Colorado in order to obtain full prescriptive authority and DEA registration. · Medicare/Medicaid credentials. · Unrestricted DEA license and current CPR license. · National certification by ANCC or AANP as family or adult nurse practitioner (if FNP). Preferred Qualifications · Minimum 3+ years (full time) of FNP/PA experience working in a Patient Centered Medical Home/Ambulatory Family Medicine practice · Experience working with Epic or another EHR. · Knowledge and skills necessary to provide care appropriate to the age of the patients served; the ability to assess data reflective of the patient’s status and interpret the appropriate information needed to identify each patient’s requirements relative to their age-specific needs, and to provide the care needed as described in the office’s policies and procedures. · Demonstrates cultural humility and commitment to minimizing implicit bias in clinical care Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities To be successful in this position, candidates will need the following: · Ability to consult with supervisory physicians on patient care and administrative issues. · Able to document history, physical examinations, assessments and treatment plans for each patient by using the electronic medical record and enter follow-up diagnostic testing and laboratory studies that have been ordered. · Able to discuss and promote wellness for all patients. · Knows when and how to refer patients to other health care professionals when the care that needs to be provided is beyond their scope of practice. · Proven effectiveness in working with individuals from diverse ethnic, cultural, and socio-economic backgrounds · Working knowledge of HIPAA. · Ability to prioritize and respond to emergencies in a calm manner. · Ability to verbalize information/directions clearly and concisely. · Ability to administer patient medications properly. · Ability to maintain confidentiality of sensitive information. · Conflict resolution skills. · Excellent communication skills, both oral and written. · Ability to analyze, prioritize, and resolve patient and office problems. · Ability to participate effectively as a member of a team. · Ability to simultaneously perform multiple tasks and complete administrative duties correctly and on time. How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): 1. A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position 2. Curriculum vitae / Resume 3. Five professional references including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers . Questions should be directed to: Lydia Lyon Lydia.lyon@cuanschutz.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Screening begins Immediately and continues until position is filled. For best consideration apply by November 15 th , 2026. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as HIRING RANGE: Adjoint Senior Instructor Hiring Range: $26,296.50 - $35,578.50 The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty and training. The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation unless it is non-exempt. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: The University of Colorado (CU) is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state and local laws governing non-discrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@ucdenver.edu ​. Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41352&lang=en": {
      "title": "Medical Renal Pathologist – Open Rank-Assistant or Associate Professor",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 8, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: SOM-Pathology Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Department: Pathology Job Title: Medical Renal Pathologist – Open Rank-Assistant or Associate Professor Position #00853635: – Requisition # 41352 : Job Summary: The Department of Pathology of the University of Colorado School of Medicine, Anschutz Medical Campus seeks a full-time Faculty member (Assistant or Associate Professor) with medical renal pathology subspecialty training. The recruit will serve as an attending pathologist and educate others in medical renal pathology including native and transplant kidney biopsies and in the frozen section assessment of potential donor kidney biopsies. The attending pathologist will be part of a multidisciplinary team, including a team of senior pathologists as well as other subspecialty trained physicians; thus, strong verbal and written communication and professionalism skills are expected. This position is an academic post; hence, scholarly activity and teaching of pathology residents is expected and time for these activities will be provided. The general responsibilities and expectations of this position mirror the missions of the Departments and affiliated systems, including excellence in clinical care, medical undergraduate and graduate education, and scholarship. Those with interest and expertise/experience in other pathology subspecialties are encouraged to apply. There is currently a particular need for additional expertise in cardiovascular/transplant pathology and head and neck pathology. The successful applicant will join a group of three dozen subspecialty surgical pathologists, who currently contribute to the practice of multi-disciplinary team-based subspecialty pathology practice at the University of Colorado Hospital. The position may include general intraoperative frozen section work as well as minor general anatomic pathology on call responsibilities. Key Responsibilities: · Promote quality patient care through the sign out of routine and complex medical renal cases from UCH and affiliated clinics as well as consulting institutions, pathologists, and patients. · Adherence to the quality standards and regulatory requirements associated with the anatomic pathology laboratories, as well as UCH and affiliated clinics · Ensure timely completion and accurate reporting of pathology tests associated with your practice, consultations, or translational research. · Consult with peer pathologists on cases as requested or required by policy. · Participate in the education of pathologists and affiliated non-pathologist providers through consultations, including at multidisciplinary clinics, and the application and education associated with test interpretation. · Train and supervise pathology and non-pathology students, residents, and fellows. · Engage in scholarly activities as broadly defined by the School of Medicine, including the scholarship of application, teaching, integration, and discovery. · Maintain exemplary professionalism and continue to develop collaborative relationships with the pathology community and non-pathology providers. Work Location: Onsite – this role is expected to work onsite and is located in Aurora, CO. Why Join Us: Welcome to the Department of Pathology of the CU Anschutz, School of Medicine. The Department has grown substantially in the past 15 years, from 40 to 120 faculty in parallel with the remarkable growth of our hospital-based affiliates as well as the city and county of Denver. Our work is value driven and focused on scientific investigation, lifelong learning, and a balance of personal and professional values. In addition to a vibrant and highly competitive residency program with 25 positions, we offer 9 fellowships and participate in numerous graduate schools and the MD/PhD program of the CU Anschutz School of Medicine. Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year (based on percentage of time) Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 11/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. This is an open rank position and could be categorized Assistant Professor or Associate Professor based on experience and qualifications as indicated below: Open Rank: Rank at the time of appointment will be based on the candidate’s demonstrated contributions and experience in teaching, clinical, research, and/or service to the field. We welcome applicants with a range of backgrounds and accomplishments and encourage individuals to highlight the breadth and depth of their professional impact. Learn more about faculty tracks at the Office for Faculty Affairs . Assistant Professor: · MD, DO, or equivalent · Graduation from an accredited Anatomic Pathology Residency Program · Board certified in Anatomic Pathology and the credentials to obtain medical licensure in Colorado, followed by a University appointment at the rank of Assistant Professor · Completion of fellowship(s) in medical renal pathology or extensive relevant experience · Demonstrated excellence in teaching and scholarship · 0-5 years of experience Associate Professor: · MD, DO, or equivalent · Graduation from an accredited Anatomic Pathology Residency Program · Board certified in Anatomic Pathology and the credentials to obtain medical licensure in Colorado, followed by a University appointment at the rank of Associate Professor · Completion of fellowship(s) in medical renal pathology or extensive relevant experience · Demonstrated excellence in teaching and scholarship · 5-10 years of experience Conditions of Employment: · Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without requiring sponsorship. We are unable to provide work visa sponsorship or employment authorization for this position now or in the future. How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): 1. A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position 2. Curriculum vitae / Resume 3. Five professional references including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers . Questions should be directed to Dr. Scott Lucia at Scott.Lucia@cuanschutz.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Immediately and continues until position is filled. For best consideration, apply by October 31, 2026. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as HIRING RANGE: Assistant Professor: $230,000 to $265,000 Associate Professor: $260,000 to $315,000 The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation unless it is non-exempt. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: The University of Colorado (CU) is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@ucdenver.edu ​. Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41354&lang=en": {
      "title": "Family Physician – Whole Person Pain Service – Open Rank: Adjoint Senior Instructor- Adjoint Professor",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 8, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: SOM-FM GENERAL OPERATIONS Schedule: Part-time University of Colorado Anschutz Department of Family Medicine Job Title: Family Physician – Whole Person Pain Service – Open Rank: Adjoint Senior Instructor- Adjoint Professor Position#: 00853324 - Requisition #: 41354 Job Summary: The clinician (MD or DO) in this position will provide care within the Department of Family Medicine, serving the Whole Person Pain Service (WPPS) as a 0.25 cFTE . The Whole Person Pain Service (WPPS) will provide holistic chronic pain care for primary care patients established in the department of family medicine. The service will be 100% virtual and will serve as the chronic pain hub for patients in the department who are currently prescribed chronic opioid medications. The Physician in this role will be responsible for two main functions: chronic pain patient care and care coordination. Examples of Work Performed The duties and responsibilities of the position include, but are not limited to: Clinical Care · Provide patient care to patients with chronic pain in a virtual setting. · Perform intake, routine follow-up, and group visits for patients on chronic opioids. · Participate as needed in chart review and clinical coding compliance activities. · Collaborate as appropriate with medical staff in the care of complex patients. · Interact with other health professionals to create guidelines and coordinate patient care. · Triage the WPPS inbasket and telephone line and support patients as needed. · Using opioid registries, proactively outreach patients and/or PCPs who may benefit from the WPPS. · Using opioid registries determine the highest risk patients in need to be discussed at collaborative care conferences. Administrative/Professional Development · Maintain eligibility for School of Medicine Faculty. · ­Keep abreast of the latest developments in field, both academically and through applied skills. · Attend and present at conferences, meetings and trainings to maintain certification and enhance professional skills; participates in faculty development activities. · Accept other responsibilities assigned by the Medical Director Quality · Develops, implements, and evaluates the strategy for quality improvement. Work Location: Hybrid – candidates must live in Colorado upon hire. Why Join Us: The Department of Family Medicine (DFM) is dedicated to “helping people be healthier\" by educating, nurturing, fostering, and enhancing those in the field of family medicine and the communities we live in and serve. The Department of Family Medicine has five (5) focus areas, each with specific goals: · Patient Care: Provide outstanding Family Medicine to every patient. · Research: Create and disseminate new knowledge. · Training: Train integrated future Family Medicine workforce. · Community Engagement: Achieve health equity with community engagement and advocacy. · Our People: Nurture a thriving, diverse and equitable department culture Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Open Rank: Rank at the time of appointment will be based on the candidate’s demonstrated contributions and experience in teaching, clinical, research, and/or service to the field. We welcome applicants with a range of backgrounds and accomplishments and encourage individuals to highlight the breadth and depth of their professional impact. Learn more about faculty tracks at the Office for Faculty Affairs . Adjoint Senior Instructor · Education: Terminal degree in Medicine or Osteopathy (MD or DO). Board Certified in Family Medicine. · Experience: Graduation from an accredited Family Medicine Residency program. · Special Skills: Ability to obtain Colorado Medical License and possession of a current DEA Certificate. Ability to be fully credentialed with the UCH system and UPI Managed Care. Adjoint Assistant Professor · Education: Terminal degree in Medicine or Osteopathy (MD or DO). Board Certified in Family Medicine. · Experience: Graduation from an accredited Family Medicine Residency program. · Special Skills: Ability to obtain Colorado Medical License and possession of a current DEA Certificate. Ability to be fully credentialed with the UCH system and UPI Managed Care. Adjoint Associate Professor · Education: Terminal degree in Medicine or Osteopathy (MD or DO). Board Certified in Family Medicine. · Experience: Graduation from an accredited Family Medicine Residency program and 7+ years’ experience working in primary care. · Special Skills: Ability to obtain Colorado Medical License and possession of a current DEA Certificate. Ability to be fully credentialed with the UCH system and UPI Managed Care. Ability to meet the School of Medicine’s criteria for associate professor. Adjoint Professor · Education: Terminal degree in Medicine or Osteopathy (MD or DO). Board Certified in Family Medicine. · Experience: Graduation from an accredited Family Medicine Residency program and 10+ years’ experience working in primary care. · Special Skills: Ability to obtain Colorado Medical License and possession of a current DEA Certificate. Ability to be fully credentialed with the UCH system and UPI Managed Care. Ability to meet the School of Medicine’s criteria for full professor. Preferred Qualifications · Experience working in a Patient Centered Medical Home/Ambulatory Family Medicine and/or Adult Medicine practice. or interest in education and research and faculty development. · Experience with using an electronic health record system, preferably Epic · Experience with providing Telehealth/virtual visits · Licensed MAT provider Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities To be successful in this position, candidates will need the following: · Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with clinic and Department of Family Medicine faculty and staff. · Ability to work effectively on multiple tasks and maintain a well-organized work environment. · Ability to maintain confidentiality. · Ability to work effectively as part of a team and independently. · Capacity for flexibility and adaptability in different work situations. · Experience training and developing staff. · Ability to meet clinic-specific competencies and expectations. How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): 1. A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position 2. Curriculum vitae / Resume 3. Five professional references including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers . Questions should be directed to: Lydia Lyon Lydia.lyon@cuanschutz.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Screening begins immediately and continues until 11/01/2026 . Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as HIRING RANGE: Adjoint Senior Instructor Hiring Range: $48,750–$60,500 for 0.25 cFTE, plus the possibility of incentives based on clinical FTE. Adjoint Assistant Professor Hiring Range: $48,750–$60,500 for 0.25 cFTE, plus the possibility of incentives based on clinical FTE. Adjoint Associate Professor Hiring Range: $50,250–$62,000 for 0.25 cFTE, plus the possibility of incentives based on clinical FTE. Adjoint Professor Hiring Range: $51,750–$63,500 for 0.25 cFTE, plus the possibility of incentives based on clinical FTE. The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty and training. The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation unless it is non-exempt. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: The University of Colorado (CU) is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state and local laws governing non-discrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@ucdenver.edu ​. Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=40588&lang=en": {
      "title": "Director, Pediatric Division, Barbara Davis Center for Diabetes",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 8, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: SOM-BDC Pediatric Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Department: Barbara Davis Center for Diabetes, Pediatric Diabetes Division Job Title: Director, Pediatric Division, Barbara Davis Center for Diabetes Position #00656433 – Requisition #40588 Job Summary: The Barbara Davis Center for Diabetes (BDC) at the University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus seeks an accomplished clinician-scientist and leader for an open rank faculty position at the Associate or Professor rank. This position includes an administrative appointment as Pediatric Diabetes Director and represents a unique opportunity to lead the nation’s premier pediatric diabetes programs within one of the largest diabetes-focused institute in the world. The successful candidate will be a nationally recognized leader in pediatric diabetes care, research, and program development with a demonstrated commitment to advancing clinical excellence, innovation, education, and discovery. The Pediatric Diabetes Director will provide strategic and operational leadership for the BDC Pediatric Diabetes Division, overseeing clinical care delivery, faculty and staff development, research growth, and educational programs while fostering a collaborative culture focused on improving outcomes for children and adolescents with diabetes. The Pediatric Diabetes Director will serve as the primary leader for pediatric diabetes programs at the Barbara Davis Center, guiding the continued growth of a nationally recognized clinical and academic enterprise. This leader will work closely with faculty, trainees, BDC leadership, hospital leadership, and community partners to advance innovative models of care, expand clinical and translational research, strengthen educational programs, and enhance the national reputation of the Barbara Davis Center. The Barbara Davis Center is internationally recognized for excellence in type 1 diabetes research and care. More than 220 clinicians, scientists, and staff work together to advance prevention, treatment, and cures for diabetes through groundbreaking research, comprehensive clinical care, and world-class education. This position offers an exceptional opportunity for a visionary physician leader to shape the future of pediatric diabetes care and research while building upon the Center’s longstanding legacy of innovation and impact. Key Responsibilities : Provide strategic leadership and oversight for the Pediatric Diabetes Division’s clinical, research, educational, and community outreach missions. Develop and implement a long-term vision that advance the Division’s national leadership in pediatric diabetes care, research, and innovation. Recruit, mentor, retain, and develop outstanding faculty, advanced practice providers, and staff while fostering a culture of collaboration, accountability, professionalism, and inclusion. Supervise faculty, clinical, educational, and administrative personnel. Serve as the primary liaison for diabetes care between Children’s Hospital Colorado and the Barbara Davis Center (20% effort). Partner with BDC, University of Colorado School of Medicine, and Children’s Hospital Colorado leadership to align priorities and achieve strategic goals. Direct the organization, quality, and delivery of outpatient pediatric diabetes care at the BDC. Advance innovative models of care that improve patient outcomes, access, efficiency, patient experience, and population health. Foster growth of clinical, translational, and investigator-initiated diabetes research programs. Support faculty in obtaining and sustaining extramural funding and developing collaborative research initiatives. Provide leadership for pediatric diabetes education programs and participate in oversight of the jointly funded Pediatric Endocrinology Fellowship Program. Serve as the ambassador for the Barbara Davis Center and University of Colorado nationally and internationally. Cultivate productive relationships with philanthropic partners, advocacy organizations, and community stakeholders. Provides oversight to Division’s Clinical and Research Directors. Work Location: Onsite – this role is expected to work onsite and is located in Aurora, Colorado. Why Join Us: The BDC is one of the largest diabetes institute in the world specializing in type 1 diabetes research and care for children and adults. Over 220 clinicians, clinical researchers, basic biomedical scientists and supporting staff work at the BDC to find the most effective treatment, prevention, and cure for type 1 diabetes. The Center provides state-of-the-art diabetes care to over 8,000 children and adults with diabetes as well as inpatient care at the Children’s Hospital Colorado. The dedicated Children’s Diabetes Foundation has generously supported the BDC mission since 1977. The BDC Pediatric Diabetes Division provides families and patients with an understanding of type 1 diabetes and encourages their confidence in its day-to-day management. Present evidence strongly suggests that consistent blood sugar control greatly diminishes the chances of long-term eye and kidney complications. The Pediatric Clinic offers complete education and support for children and adolescents with type 1 diabetes. The expectation is that by the time patients are ready to leave home for college or the workforce, they will have the ability to manage their own blood sugars. Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Optional 457(b) and 403(b) retirement programs Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year (based on percentage of time) Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 11/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced rate RTD Bus and light rail service Malpractice coverage through group provider Professional development supplement annually Incentive plan that rewards clinical service in research grant funding There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. This is an open rank , open track position and could be categorized as Associate Professor or Professor based on experience and qualifications as indicated below: Associate Professor: MD or MD/PhD degree Board Certification in Pediatrics and Pediatric Endocrinology Eligible for medical licensure in Colorado. Record of scholarly achievement consistent with appointment at the Associate Professor rank. Demonstrated success in clinical program development, quality improvement, and leadership of multidisciplinary teams Evidence of peer-reviewed scholarship and sustained research productivity. Experience mentoring faculty, trainees, and junior investigators. Professor: MD or MD/PhD degree Board Certification in Pediatrics and Pediatric Endocrinology Eligible for medical licensure in Colorado. Record of scholarly achievement consistent with appointment at the Associate Professor rank. Demonstrated success in clinical program development, quality improvement, and leadership of multidisciplinary teams Evidence of peer-reviewed scholarship and sustained research productivity. Experience mentoring faculty, trainees, and junior investigators. National or international reputation in pediatric diabetes care, research, or education. Sustained record of extramural funding, scholarly impact, and academic leadership Demonstrated success leading complex clinical and academic programs. Proven track record in faculty recruitment, retention, and development. Experience developing strategic initiatives that expand clinical, research, and educational programs. Preferred Qualifications: Experience directing a pediatric diabetes program, division, center, or clinical service. Success leading multicenter clinical trials or large collaborative research initiatives. Experience managing budgets and operational performance Demonstrated engagement with philanthropy, donor relations, or institutional advancement activities. Experience partnering effectively with hospital and health-system leadership. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Exceptional interpersonal communication and relationship-building skills. Demonstrated skill in leading organizational change, managing competing priorities, and achieving results in a dynamic and evolving healthcare environment. Ability to promote a culture of professionalism, accountability, innovation, inclusion, and patient-centered care. Strong presentation and advocacy skills Ability to maintain confidentiality Ability to work effectively as part of a team and independently. Capacity for flexibility and adaptability in different work situations. Ability to work well with diverse populations How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): 1. A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position 2. Curriculum vitae / Resume 3. Five professional references including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers . Questions should be directed to: Robby Rigby, BDCHR@cuanschutz.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Applications will be accepted until finalists are identified, but preference will be given to complete applications received by November 30, 2026. Those who do not apply by this date may or may not be considered. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as: Associate Professor: $200,000 - $225,000 Professor: $225,000 - $275,000 Pediatric Division Director Stipend: $50,000 The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation unless it is non-exempt. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: The University of Colorado (CU) is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@ucdenver.edu ​. Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=40938&lang=en": {
      "title": "Finance & Accounting Senior Manager",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 8, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: SOM-EM MED CLINICAL Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Department: Emergency Medicine Job Title: Finance & Accounting Senior Manager Position # 00852607: – Requisition #: 40938 Job Summary: The Finance & Accounting Senior Manager se rves as a high level financial leader for the Department of Emergency Medicine and is responsible for the strategic oversight of financial planning, forecasting, business analytics, financial modeling, budgeting, and operational decision support. This position partners closely with departmental leadership (Vice Chair of Finance and Administration, Vice Chair of Research, and Vice Chair of Clinical Operations) to develop data-driven strategies that support the department's clinical, research, educational, and administrative missions. The Finance & Accounting Senior Manager is responsible for developing sophisticated financial models, forecasting tools, and executive dashboards in collaboration with the analytics team that inform strategic planning, resource allocation, program growth, and operational performance improvement. The position provides leadership for data analytics initiatives and promotes the use of emerging technologies, including artificial intelligence, to enhance financial analysis, reporting efficiency, and business intelligence capabilities. This position oversees the day-to-day operations of the finance, analytics, procurement, and contract management functions and serves as a trusted advisor to department leadership regarding financial risks, opportunities, and long-term strategic investments. Key Responsibilities: Financial and Budget Management 70%: Provides leadership and supervision for finance, analytics, procurement, and contract management staff. Serves as the department's senior financial strategist and trusted advisor to the Chair, Vice Chair for Administration and Finance, and executive leadership team. Establishes performance expectations and fosters a culture of accountability, innovation, collaboration, and continuous improvement. Mentors staff in advanced financial analysis, data analytics, forecasting, and business intelligence methodologies. Promotes adoption of emerging analytics technologies and AI-enabled solutions to improve departmental performance. Leads strategic initiatives focused on process automation, data governance, and analytical capability development. Oversees management of departmental funds including state, grant, clinical, gift, endowment, auxiliary, and contract funding. Designs, develops, and maintains sophisticated financial models to evaluate new programs, faculty recruitment, compensation plans, clinical initiatives, research investments, and strategic partnerships. Leads the development of executive dashboards and financial scorecards. Utilizes advanced Excel modeling techniques, data visualization tools, and AI-enabled technologies to improve forecasting accuracy and operational efficiency. Identifies emerging trends, financial risks, and growth opportunities through advanced analytics and benchmarking. Ensures departmental compliance with applicable procurement policies and procedures. Prepares cost studies for all service center accounts and conducts cost-benefit analysis to determine the best allocation methodology for overhead costs. Leads development of long-range financial strategies that support departmental growth, sustainability, and operational excellence. Reconciles and consolidates financial information from multiple entities including University, CU Medicine, hospital, research, and affiliated organizations. Monitors departmental financial performance and proactively identifies budget variances, operational risks, and opportunities for improvement. Directs all departmental budgeting, forecasting, and financial planning activities. Oversees development of annual operating budgets, multi-year financial plans, and periodic forecast updates. Ensures compliance with University, School of Medicine, CU Medicine, hospital, state, and federal financial policies and regulations. Establishes and maintains internal controls to ensure responsible stewardship of departmental resources Procurement and Contract Management: 30% Serves as the departmental Approving Official (AO) for procurement activities. Ensures the propriety of all transactions in accordance with State, University, CU Medicine and UCH rules and regulations. Implements and oversees execution of procurement policies and procedures related to all facets of the University and CU Medicine procurement systems (CU Marketplace, Concur, Travel, etc.), including, electronic and paper approval and submission (Pos, SPOs, Payment Vouchers, Travel Reconciliation, Employee Reimbursements, CU Medicine Travel and accounts payable) Sets reimbursement policy for the department faculty and staff. Oversees and manages reimbursement requests for all faculty/staff and develops training program to best inform faculty/staff. Manages all procurement and travel card transaction activity. Develops, implements and educates others about the departmental policy on the use of university credit cards. Provides financial guidance and support for contract negotiations and business agreements. Study the legalities of contracts and help to negotiate terms and conditions with faculty and third parties, before drafting agreements to outline terms of service and project deliverables. Provide contract analysis and summaries, and ensure contract execution accomplished in accordance with company policy Drives current contract processes and provides improvement initiative direction including scrutiny and evaluation of best practices and lessons learned Manage all service agreements in the department. Reviews agreements for cost effectiveness and develops budgets to ensure cost reimbursement exceeds costs for all agreement. Negotiates with sponsors for budget consideration. Develops departmental tax allocation process on all clinical and contract income. Serves as the subject-matter expert for Scope of Work transactions and acts as a work lead for all department personnel under the Chair and DFA. Performs other duties as assigned. Work Location: Hybrid – this role is eligible for a hybrid schedule of 3 days per week on campus and as needed for in-person meetings. Why Join Us: The Department of Emergency Medicine at the University of Colorado School of Medicine is dedicated to delivering superlative patient care, providing an environment where training and education thrive and innovation and discovery are fostered. The Department of Emergency Medicine is based at the Anschutz Medical Campus in Aurora Colorado. The campus is a state of the art medical campus home to the University of Colorado Schools of Medicine, Nursing, Dentistry, Pharmacy, the Colorado School of Public Health; as well as the University of Colorado Hospital and Children's Hospital Colorado both of which serve as major training sites for the Denver Health Residency in Emergency Medicine Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 10/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree in business administration, business, finance, accounting, or a directly related field from an accredited institution and 5-7 years of professional experience related to finance and accounting management. A combination of education and related technical/military/paraprofessional experience may be substituted for a bachelor’s degree on a year for year basis. Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Preferred Qualifications: Master’s degree in Finance, Accounting or a related field from an accredited college or university. Experience with fund accounting. Experience working with standard accounting policies and procedures. Higher education accounting experience. Higher education budget management, modeling and forecasting experience. Experience with contract and grant administration. Experience working with clinical data. Conditions of Employment: Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without requiring sponsorship. We are unable to provide work visa sponsorship or employment authorization for this position now or in the future. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Proficiency working with Microsoft Word, Access, PowerPoint and Outlook. Advanced knowledge of Excel. Ability to work with a diverse group and competing interests. Ability to tolerate a high degree of ambiguity yet work effectively to fulfill the mission, goals and objectives of the department. Knowledge of standard accounting practices. Knowledge of fund accounting. Ability to work independently, exercise sound judgment, identify and set priorities for self and others, and meet deadlines in a fast-paced work environment. Excellent time management and organization skills. Ability to effectively explain processes and procedures. Strong analytical skills. Excellent attention to detail. Strong commitment to the team approach. Ability to understand complex systems and guide other personnel with regard to their use. Strong financial management and the ability to manage funds from a variety of sources. Solid understanding of budget development and management. Ability to evaluate, analyze and interpret vast amounts of data, recommend solutions and implement the preferred course of action. High degree of technical skills in fiscal management, and knowledge of accounting and business practices, including accounting software packages. Ability to communicate effectively, both in writing and orally. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with employees at all levels throughout the institution. Outstanding customer service skills. How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position Curriculum vitae / Resume Three to five professional references, including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Questions should be directed to: EMED Human Resources at emed.humanresources@ucdenver.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Immediately and continues until position is filled. For best consideration, apply by September 8. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as ($79,990-107,187). The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position may be eligible for overtime compensation, depending on the level. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@cuanschutz.edu ​. Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41350&lang=en": {
      "title": "Open Rank Assistant to Associate Professor – Orthopedic Trauma Surgeon – HRH",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 8, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: SOM-ORTHO GENERAL OPERATIONS Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Department: Orthopedics Job Title: Open Rank Assistant to Associate Professor – Orthopedic Trauma Surgeon – HRH Position #00853709 – Requisition #41350 Job Summary: The Department of Orthopedic Surgery at the University of Colorado is seeking a board certified/board eligible Orthopedic Trauma Surgeon to be based at the Highlands Ranch Hospital. This newly created position will play a key role in expanding orthopedic trauma services within a growing community-based practice and supporting the continued development of trauma care at Highlands Ranch Hospital. All candidates must have completed a 5-year residency and a one-year orthopedic trauma fellowship and possess a demonstrated interest in developing a robust clinical practice within a growing community-based hospital setting. This person will serve as the orthopedic trauma liaison for Highlands Ranch Hospital, will work collaboratively to support the development and growth of the hospital’s trauma program and advancement toward Level II Trauma Center designation. This candidate should have an interest in developing a clinical practice, interest in research endeavors, and participate in our resident/fellowship education program. The primary responsibility will be as an Orthopedic Trauma Surgeon. Clinical responsibilities include actively participating in the continued growth of the Trauma Surgery program at the University of Colorado. The candidate will provide services in both inpatient and outpatient environments. Teaching responsibilities include participating in the education of Orthopedic fellows, residents, and medical students. As an academic institution with a promotional track, candidates will have to display a record of active research endeavors. Research Responsibilities integral to this position include active participation in research activities within the Trauma program, and the personal development of focused clinical and/or basic science research activities parallel to their clinical practice. The applicant must be self-directed, detail-oriented, and adaptable in a high-intensity environment. Alternatively, the candidate may choose a clinical track. This track does not have a research requirement but is not tenure eligible. All other rights and privileges are the same in both tracks. Academic rank and salary will be commensurate with the level of expertise and academic credentials and will be closely linked with income generated. Key Responsibilities : Obtains detailed history and performs physical examinations on assigned patients; assesses and treats acute/chronic medical problems and provides direct patient care to a specified patient population. Writes prescriptions for medications, PT, OT, imaging studies, and DME as needed. Complete FMLA and other forms and school notes as needed. Provides pre-op, intra-op and post-op care; writes appropriate orders, including those for narcotics and other scheduled drugs. Duties may include inpatient care, consultation and coverage in the emergency room. Practices safety, environmental, and/or infection control methods. Coordinates the activities of patient care and support staff within the clinic. Work with the team to ensure smooth operation of the clinic. Writes progress notes on patients' office and hospital charts in a timely fashion indicating patient status and treatment procedures performed; maintains other records as required. Participates in on-call coverage of Highlands Ranch Hospital for orthopedic surgery as part of the orthopedic group practice. This will include jointly covering all on-call days as needed with the group practice, emergent treatment as appropriate and admitting/temporizing patients as medically appropriate. Provides health education to patients and families; may train and supervise medical students, residents, fellows, mid-level students and other health professional students engaged in specific clinical activities. Enhances professional growth and development through participation in educational programs, current literature, in-service meetings and workshops. Participate (attend, give talks, help organize) in educational programs including weekly academic conferences, journal clubs, etc. Will assist in community outreach events including giving educational talks, organizing, planning, and attending. Develop written educational materials and treatment protocols for specific conditions and post-operative care. Gives power point and poster presentations for educational purposes at institutional, local and national meetings. Proficient in documentation and use of the current electronic medical record programs and maintains timely documentation at or above hospital set standards. Work Location: Onsite - this role is expected to work onsite and is in the South metro area; primarily Highlands Ranch Hospital (HRH). Why Join Us: We are a nationally ranked Orthopedic department with a mission to provide the highest quality patient care and advance the field of orthopedics through innovation in research and education. We are dedicated to fostering an environment where new ideas lead to breakthrough changes in healthcare. We actively champion a diverse, equitable and inclusive environment, empowering unique perspectives and cultivating spaces where everyone belongs. Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year (based on percentage of time) Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 11/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Open Rank: Rank at the time of appointment will be based on the candidate’s demonstrated contributions and experience in teaching, clinical, research, and/or service to the field. We welcome applicants with a range of backgrounds and accomplishments and encourage individuals to highlight the breadth and depth of their professional impact. Learn more about faculty tracks at the Office for Faculty Affairs . This is an open rank position and could be categorized as an Assistant Professor or Associate Professor based on experience and qualifications as indicated below: Assistant Professor Board certified/board eligible Orthopedic Surgeon Completion of an Orthopedic trauma fellowship Current Medical License CPR certified Associate Professor Board certified/board eligible Orthopedic Surgeon Completion of an Orthopedic trauma fellowship Current Medical License CPR certified 5 years’ experience directly related to the duties and responsibilities specified Preferred Qualifications: Interest in developing a clinical practice and working together as an orthopedic group in a hybrid academic-private practice setting. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Flexibility to handle unforeseen challenges during surgery and make real-time decisions for the patient's well-being. Ability to explain complex medical conditions in a way that patients and their families can understand. Compassion and patience to support patients through their medical journey, providing emotional support and guidance. How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): 1. A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position. 2. Curriculum vitae / Resume 3. Five professional references including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address. Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers . Questions should be directed to: Lindsey Renn, lindsey.renn@cuanschutz.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Immediately and continue until filled. Full consideration for applications received by December 1, 2026. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as HIRING RANGE: Assistant Professor: $417,742 - $590,374 Associate Professor: $530,909 - $790,759 The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation unless it is non-exempt. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: The University of Colorado (CU) is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodation to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@ucdenver.edu ​. Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41347&lang=en": {
      "title": "Post-Doctoral Fellow",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 7, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: SOM-DERM GATES CENTER Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Department: Department of Dermatology Job Title: Post-Doctoral Fellow Position #00853156: – Requisition #: 41347 Job Summary: A postdoctoral position is available in the Fan Laboratory in the Department of Dermatology at the University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus. The Fan Laboratory investigates the molecular and cellular mechanisms underlying cancer immunoediting in skin cancer. Current research focuses on understanding the role of natural killer (NK) cells in shaping tumor evolution and controlling cutaneous squamous cell carcinoma (cSCC) progression using molecular, cellular, genomic, and animal model approaches. This full-time postdoctoral position will support NIH-funded and foundation-funded research projects with the potential to be funded through NIH-T32. The successful candidate will be mentored by Dr. Xiying Fan and work closely with other research assistants in the lab. The postdoctoral fellow will have the opportunity to work independently and propose studies that complement ongoing and expand upon projects in the lab. Key Responsibilities: · Design and carry out cell culture and rodent-based research projects · Develop and troubleshoot experimental protocols · Perform molecular and cellular assays including PCR, qRT-PCR, Western blotting, flow cytometry, immunohistochemistry, immunofluorescence microscopy, and gene expression analyses. · Help train laboratory personnel in experimental techniques. · Present research findings at laboratory meetings, institutional seminars, and research conferences. · Prepare manuscripts for publication and assist with the development of grant applications and research reports. · Prepare grant applications · Perform all research compliance activities required by the University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus. Work Location: Onsite – this role is expected to work onsite and is located in Aurora, CO Why Join Us: Why work for the University? The University of Colorado offers a comprehensive benefits package. To see what benefits are available for Post-Doctoral Fellows, please visit: · Payroll & Benefits Orientation for Post-Doctoral Fellows | University of Colorado (cu.edu) · benefits guide cover-post-doc-2024 (cu.edu) Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: · PhD in Immunology, Cancer Biology, Molecular Biology, Cell Biology, or a related biomedical discipline. · Experience with mammalian cell culture and experimental design. · Only U.S. citizens, non-citizen nationals, and permanent U.S. residents. Preferred Qualifications: · Demonstrated expertise in molecular and cellular biology techniques. · Background in cancer immunology. · Previous experience in some or all the following laboratory techniques is preferred: experience designing and conducting experiments with rodents, flow cytometry acquisition and analysis, immunohistochemistry, fluorescence microscopy, and molecular biology (RNA/protein extraction, RT-PCR, enzyme-linked immune-sorbent assay (ELISA), western blotting) Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: · Strong written and oral communication skills. · Ability to work independently while contributing to a collaborative research environment. · Strong organizational, analytical, and problem solving skills Conditions of Employment: Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without requiring sponsorship. We are unable to provide work visa sponsorship or employment authorization for this position now or in the future. How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): 1. A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position 2. Curriculum vitae / Resume 3. Five professional references including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers . Questions should be directed to: Jennifer Nevener at Jennifer.Nevener@cuanschutz.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Applications will be accepted until finalists are identified, but preference will be given to complete applications received by October 15. Those who do not apply by this date may or may not be considered. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as HIRING RANGE: $63,480 to $64,380 The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation unless it is non-exempt. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: The University of Colorado (CU) is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@ucdenver.edu ​. Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41343&lang=en": {
      "title": "Research Services Clinical Sciences Program Manager",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 7, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: SOM-EM MED CLINICAL Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus Department: Emergency Medicine Job Title: Research Services Clinical Sciences Program Manager Position #: 00853817 – Requisition #: 41343 Job Summary: The University of Colorado, Anschutz Medical Campus, Department of Emergency Medicine is currently seeking applications for a Research Services Clinical Sciences Program Manager. This is a full-time, University Staff (non-classified) position for the Airway, Trauma, Lung injury, and Sepsis (ATLAS) Research Program. Research Services Clinical Sciences Program Managers perform clinical and research-related functions which may include patient-oriented research or research conducted with human subjects. Patient-oriented research includes mechanisms of human disease, therapeutic interventions, clinical trials, or development of new technologies. Research Services Clinical Sciences Program Managers independently manage clinical research programs, perform clinical research project management functions and/or supervise clinical research teams of 2 or more FTE. This position will work closely with lead project coordinators, Principal Investigators (PIs), and ATLAS Leadership. Key Responsibilities: Supervise research staff and coordinators. Provide leadership, direction, coaching, and performance management to professional staff. Develop protocol-specific systems and documents including process flows, training manuals, Standard Operating Procedures (SOPs) and Case Report Forms (CRFs). Maintains subject level documentation and prepares documents, equipment and/or supplies May perform supervision and management responsibilities for a team of 2 or more professionals. Duties include, but are not limited to, recruitment, supervision, and performance management responsibilities Manage project timelines, deliverables, and resources. Develop program/project goals and communicate goals and outcomes with a variety of stakeholders Participate in tactical and strategic program/project development and planning Coordinate site visits and other meetings with key stakeholders Develop and implement community outreach and engagement initiatives Assist with and oversee the day-to-day operations of clinical trials and studies, when needed May perform duties and responsibilities of Clinic Research Professionals when necessary Ensure compliance with FDA, IRB, and institutional requirements. Develop, review, maintain regulatory and other program/project documentation Ensure program/project compliance with Food and Drug Administration (FDA) and other regulatory bodies Support study activation, implementation, and closeout activities. Liaise and coordinate with a variety of program/project stakeholders including, but not limited to, program/project sponsors, regulatory agents, pharmaceutical representatives, and clinic/hospital staff Develop and maintain a variety of reports and communicate and present data to stakeholders This description is a summary only and describes the general level of work being performed, it is not intended to be all-inclusive. The duties of this position may change from time to time and/or based on business needs. We reserve the right to add or delete duties and responsibilities at the discretion of the supervisor and/or hiring authority. Work Location: Hybrid – this role is eligible for a hybrid schedule of 4 days per week on campus and as needed for in-person meetings. Why Join Us: This is an in-person position within the ATLAS Research Program, which offers a unique career and growth opportunity to serve as an integral member of a highly productive, collaborative, and vibrant research group conducting impactful health research in the care of acutely ill and injured patients. The diverse and complex patient population provides a rich learning environment and opportunities to expand the candidate's skillset across several research projects (including clinical trials and observational trials). The candidate will also be exposed to a like-minded research community to help enrich skills and enhance career growth. The ATLAS Research Program aims to advance solutions to the greatest challenges in acute care by leading transformative clinical trials. We are interested in candidates that have/want a direct connection to advancing medical knowledge and evidence-based care that can impact the lives of patients. Outside the ATLAS Research Program environment, the candidate will be part of the larger University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus community. CU Anschutz is a prestigious public education, clinical and research academic institution serving 4,500 students, and a world-class medical destination at the forefront of life-changing science, medicine, and healthcare. The campus encompasses the University of Colorado health professional schools, more than 60 centers and institutes, and two nationally ranked independent hospitals - UCHealth University of Colorado Hospital and Children's Hospital Colorado - that treat more than two million adult and pediatric patients each year. CU Anschutz offers more than 42 highly rated degree programs through 6 schools and colleges, and receives over $650 million in research awards each year. We are the single largest health professions education provider in Colorado, awarding nearly 1,450 degrees annually. Powered by our award-winning faculty, renowned researchers and a reputation for academic excellence, the CU Anschutz Medical Campus drives innovation from the classroom to the laboratory to the delivery of unparalleled patient care. The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus seeks individuals with demonstrated commitment to creating an inclusive learning and working environment. We value the ability to engage effectively with students, faculty, and staff of diverse backgrounds. The University offers a comprehensive benefits package that includes health insurance, life insurance, retirement plans, tuition benefits, ECO pass, paid time off – vacation, sick, and holidays and more. To see what benefits are available, please visit: https://www.cu.edu/employee-services/benefits-wellness . Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 10/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications (pre-clinical/wet lab experience does not ap ply) : Bachelor’s degree in any field Four (4) years clinical research or related experience Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Preferred Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree in science or health related field 2+ years of supervisory and team leadership Five (5) years clinical research or related experience Prior experience providing program and/or project management duties in a clinical research setting Experience with electronic data capture systems (e.g. EMR or EHR and data management systems) Experience developing and managing documents for Institutional Review Board (IRB) submissions Experience with Department of War Office of Human Research Oversight (OHRO) and National Institutes of Health (NIH) regulatory requirements and reporting Conditions of Employment: Must be willing to provide leadership support through participation in a rotating on-call schedule to address time-sensitive operational and staff needs outside of standard business hours. Must demonstrate the flexibility and commitment required to work extended hours, including evenings and weekends, to support critical research, regulatory, and programmatic initiatives. Must be able to work a hybrid schedule, with a minimum of four (4) days per week on-site at the University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus in Aurora, Colorado. Must be legally authorized to work in the United States and able to maintain work authorization throughout employment without employer sponsorship now or in the future. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Strong project management skills and experience within a complex and diverse environment Advanced knowledge and understanding of federal regulations and Good Clinical Practice (GCP) Demonstration of strong analytical and problem-solving skills Ability to communicate effectively, both in writing and orally Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with employees at all levels throughout the institution Outstanding customer service skills Knowledge of basic human anatomy, physiology medical terminology Ability to interpret and master complex research protocol information How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position Curriculum vitae / Resume Three to five professional references, including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Questions should be directed to: Carolyn Hamburg, emed.humanresources@ucdenver.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Immediately and continues until position is filled. For best consideration, apply by November 1, 2026. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as HIRING RANGE ($70,446-$94,398). The above salary range ($70,446-$94,398) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position may be eligible for overtime compensation, depending on the level. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@cuanschutz.edu ​. Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41084&lang=en": {
      "title": "Neuroimaging Research Data Analyst",
      "description": "Closing Date: 10/13/2026 Posted Date: Oct 7, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: SOM-PSYCH-OTHR CLIN SVS-GEN OP Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Department: Psychiatry Job Title: Neuroimaging Research Data Analyst Position #:00852958 – Requisition #: 41084 Job Summary: The Neuromoimaging Research Data Analyst will provide quantitative, computational, and data management support for a multidisciplinary neuromodulation research program within the Department of Psychiatry at the University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus. The research program uses advanced neuroscience methods, including functional and structural magnetic resonance imaging (fMRI/MRI), transcranial magnetic stimulation (TMS), neuronavigation, clinical assessments, behavioral measures, and other multimodal approaches to investigate brain circuitry and develop and evaluate neuromodulation interventions for psychiatric and related conditions. Working as part of Neuromodulation Research, the Research Data Analyst will work under the Neuromodulation Chair, and in collaboration with faculty investigators, research professionals, clinicians, statisticians, data scientists, and trainees. The position will support the organization, processing, quality control, analysis, integration, visualization, and reporting of complex neuroimaging research datasets. Responsibilities will include implementation of established computational workflows, development and maintenance of research datasets and code, statistical and neuroimaging analyses, data quality assurance, preparation of research results, and support for manuscripts, presentations, and grant applications. The position will apply established quantitative methods while developing increasing independence and expertise in neuroimaging, neuromodulation, and reproducible research practices. Key Responsibilities: 25% – Research Data Processing and Quantitative Analysis Process and analyze neuroimaging, neuromodulation, behavioral, clinical, and other research datasets using established quantitative and computational methods. Implement statistical analyses under the guidance of senior scientific personnel and investigators. Apply established analysis pipelines to functional and structural MRI data and other neuroscience datasets. Generate summary statistics, derived variables, quantitative measures, and analytic datasets for research projects. Assist with integration of imaging, TMS, neuronavigation, clinical, behavioral, and other multimodal research data. 20% – Neuroimaging and Neuromodulation Data Analysis Perform preprocessing and quality assessment of functional and structural MRI data using established software and analysis pipelines. Assist with analyses of brain structure, function, connectivity, and other imaging-derived measures relevant to neuromodulation research. Support processing and analysis of data used for MRI-informed TMS targeting and neuronavigation. Assist with quantitative evaluation of relationships among stimulation targets, imaging measures, treatment parameters, and clinical or behavioral outcomes. Identify data quality issues and consult with senior scientific personnel regarding appropriate resolution or exclusion procedures. 15% – Research Data Management and Quality Assurance Organize, maintain, and document research datasets according to program standards and approved research protocols. Perform routine data quality checks to identify missing, inconsistent, duplicated, out-of-range, or otherwise problematic data. Assist with development and maintenance of data dictionaries, variable definitions, file structures, metadata, and other research documentation. Reconcile information across research data sources and work with study personnel to resolve discrepancies. Support preparation of analysis-ready datasets while maintaining appropriate participant confidentiality and data security. 15% – Computational Workflows and Reproducible Research Implement, maintain, and troubleshoot established computational workflows for research data processing and analysis. Write, modify, test, and document code and scripts using programming and scientific computing tools such as Python, R, MATLAB, shell scripting, or related platforms. Use version-control and code-management practices to support reproducibility and collaboration. Assist with automation of repetitive data processing, quality-control, and reporting tasks. Maintain clear documentation of analytical procedures, software versions, processing parameters, and data transformations. 10% – Statistical Analysis and Data Visualization Conduct descriptive and inferential statistical analyses under the direction of investigators and senior quantitative personnel. Create tables, figures, dashboards, and other visualizations to communicate research findings and data quality metrics. Assist with interpretation of statistical and quantitative results in collaboration with the Neuromodulation Research Lead Scientist and study investigators. Support exploratory analyses and feasibility assessments for new research questions and grant applications. 5% – Scientific Dissemination Prepare figures, tables, data summaries, methods documentation, and other quantitative materials for manuscripts, abstracts, presentations, grant applications, progress reports, and scientific meetings. Assist investigators and senior scientific personnel with responding to data and analysis questions arising during manuscript and grant preparation. Maintain sufficient documentation to support verification and reproducibility of reported research findings. 5% – Research Collaboration and Technical Support Participate in Neuromodulation Research, research program, and individual study meetings as appropriate. Work collaboratively with investigators and research personnel to understand project requirements and translate research questions into defined data and analysis tasks. Provide technical assistance to research team members regarding established data management, processing, analysis, and visualization procedures. Coordinate with research informatics, information technology, imaging, and other institutional resources as needed to resolve routine data or computational issues. 5% – Research Compliance and Professional Development Conduct research data activities in accordance with approved protocols, data use requirements, institutional policies, and applicable human-subjects research requirements. Maintain appropriate protections for confidential and sensitive research information. Complete required institutional research, information security, human-subjects protection, MRI safety, and other applicable training. Maintain knowledge of evolving methods, software, and best practices relevant to neuroimaging, neuromodulation, quantitative neuroscience, and reproducible research. Perform other research data and quantitative support duties as assigned. Work Location: Onsite – this role is expected to work onsite and is located in Aurora, CO . This position is expected to work at the University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus, with hybrid work eligibility determined by the needs of the Department of Psychiatry, Neuromodulation Research Program, and Neuromodulation Research. Why Join Us: The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus Department of Psychiatry is home to one of the most comprehensive neuromodulation programs in the country. Clinically, the department provides a full continuum of evidence-based treatments, including transcranial magnetic stimulation (TMS), Deep Brain Stimulation (DBS) for obsessive-compulsive disorder, Tourette Syndrome, depression, and chronic pain, Electroconvulsive Therapy (ECT), and esketamine. This robust clinical infrastructure creates unparalleled opportunities for translational research directly tied to patient care. Our neuromodulation research portfolio is rapidly expanding, with active studies in TMS, DBS, and low-intensity focused ultrasound, alongside initiatives in adaptive/closed-loop stimulation and biomarker discovery. Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 15/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree in social/behavioral sciences, physical sciences, public health, healthcare, or a directly related field from an accredited institution. 2 years of professional experience in research data analysis, quantitative research, neuroimaging, neuroscience research, biomedical data analysis, statistics, data science, scientific computing, or a closely related area relevant to the work assignment. A combination of education and related technical, military, or paraprofessional experience may be substituted for a bachelor’s degree on a year-for-year basis. An advanced degree (Master’s or Doctorate) may be substituted for experience on a year-for-year basis if the degree is in a field of study directly related to the work assignment. Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Preferred Qualifications: Experience analyzing human neuroscience, neuroimaging, clinical research, behavioral, or other complex biomedical research data. Experience with functional and/or structural MRI data processing and analysis and commonly used neuroimaging software or computational workflows. Experience using one or more programming or statistical languages such as Python, R, MATLAB, or related scientific computing tools. Experience with research data management, quality assurance, reproducible analysis workflows, and version-control tools such as Git. Experience working in a multidisciplinary academic research environment and contributing quantitative analyses, figures, or other materials to scientific manuscripts, presentations, or grant applications. Conditions of Employment: This position is expected to work at the University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus, with hybrid work eligibility determined by the needs of the Department of Psychiatry, Neuromodulation Research Program, and Neuromodulation Research. The position may require work in or around MRI, TMS, computational research, and clinical research environments. Must complete and maintain applicable institutional human-subjects protection, information security, research compliance, MRI safety, and other required training. Must adhere to institutional requirements for access, storage, analysis, transmission, and protection of confidential and sensitive research data. Occasional schedule flexibility may be required to support research deadlines, data acquisition, grant submissions, or scientific activities. Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without requiring sponsorship. We are unable to provide work visa sponsorship or employment authorization for this position now or in the future. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Quantitative and analytical skills: Knowledge of quantitative research methods and ability to organize, process, analyze, interpret, and visualize complex research data using appropriate statistical and computational methods. Computational skills: Ability to use programming, statistical, and/or scientific computing tools to implement data-processing and analysis workflows and to learn new analytical tools and methods as research needs evolve. Data quality and reproducibility: Ability to identify and resolve data quality issues, maintain accurate research documentation, and follow reproducible data management and analytical practices. Problem-solving and attention to detail: Strong analytical reasoning and attention to detail, with the ability to troubleshoot routine data and computational problems and recognize when issues require consultation or escalation. Communication: Ability to communicate effectively, both in writing and orally, and to explain data, analytical methods, and results to colleagues with varying levels of quantitative expertise. Collaboration and customer service: Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with faculty, scientists, clinicians, research staff, trainees, and employees at all levels throughout the institution, with outstanding customer service skills. Organization and professional accountability: Ability to manage multiple research assignments, meet project deadlines, maintain confidential information, and exercise appropriate discretion and personal accountability in a collaborative research environment. How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): Curriculum vitae / Resume Three to five professional references, including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Questions should be directed to: Samantha Martin, Samantha.2.martin@cuanschutz.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Immediately and continues until October 12, 2026. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as $63,096 - $80,258 The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position may be eligible for overtime compensation, depending on the level. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@cuanschutz.edu ​. Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=38321&lang=en": {
      "title": "Open Rank-Instructor, Senior Instructor",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 7, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: SOM-EM MED CLINICAL Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus Department: Emergency Medicine Job Title: Open Rank – Instructor, Senior Instructor Position #00841930: – Requisition #38321: Job Summary: The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus seeks individuals with demonstrated commitment to creating an comprehensive learning and working environment. We value the ability to engage effectively with students, faculty and staff of different backgrounds. The Department of Emergency Medicine at the University of Colorado School of Medicine is currently recruiting emergency medicine physicians in the clinical series. This position will work as a full-time faculty position at the rank of Instructor/Senior Instructor in the Department of Emergency Medicine at any UCHealth site of practice, which may include virtual platforms of care. The successful candidate will be an excellent clinician who collaborates well within teams to deliver the highest quality of emergency care to every patient, every time. Key Responsibilities : · Serve as an attending in the emergency department at one of the approved sites, including: any affiliated free-standing emergency department, virtual health care, Broomfield Hospital, Highlands Ranch Hospital, or the University of Colorado Hospital. · Actively participate in efforts to improve patient safety, clinical quality and patient experience and provide leadership of at least one project annually, if requested by the Chair or designee. · Participate in the rotating sick call coverage schedule per departmental or practice site guidelines, if applicable. · Complete necessary CME per departmental and/or practice site guidelines. · Serve as a committee member as needed by the Department or practice site on an ad hoc basis. Work Location: Onsite – this role is expected to work onsite and is located in Denver, CO metropolitan area. Why Join Us: The Department of Emergency Medicine at the University of Colorado School of Medicine is dedicated to delivering superlative patient care, providing an environment where training and education thrive and innovation and discovery are fostered. The Department of Emergency Medicine is based at the Anschutz Medical Campus in Aurora, Colorado. The campus is a state-of-the-art medical campus home to the University of Colorado Schools of Medicine, Nursing, Dentistry, Pharmacy, the Colorado School of Public Health; as well as the University of Colorado Hospital and Children's Hospital Colorado both of which serve as major training sites for the Denver Health Residency in Emergency Medicine. Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package including: · Medical: Multiple plan options · Dental: Multiple plan options · Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision · Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay · Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year · Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) · Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) · Holiday Days: 10/year · Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses · ECO Pass: Reduced rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Instructor · Current Colorado Medical License, or ability to obtain prior to start date · Completion of an emergency medicine residency · Board prepared or certified by the American Board of Emergency Medicine Senior Instructor · Current Colorado Medical License, or ability to obtain prior to start date · Completion of an emergency medicine residency · Board prepared or certified by the American Board of Emergency Medicine · Completion of fellowship training in Emergency Medicine Preferred Qualifications: · A track record of excellence in clinical performance Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: · It is expected the employee will be competent to interpret age specific developmental, physiological and unique care needs by assessment and by observation of care delivery. Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without requiring sponsorship. We are unable to provide work visa sponsorship or employment authorization for this position now or in the future. How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): 1. A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position 2. Curriculum vitae / Resume 3. Five professional references including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers . Questions should be directed to: Emergency Medicine Human Resources, emed.humanresources@ucdenver.edu Screening of Applications Begins: This position may be seeking multiple candidates. Positions will remain open until filled. Applications will be reviewed as they are received, and candidates may be contacted for interviews throughout the posting period. Upon candidate(s) selection, the posting will be closed, and no further applications will be accepted. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as HIRING RANGE: Instructor $271,703 Senior Instructor $271,703 The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation unless it is non-exempt. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: The University of Colorado (CU) is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@ucdenver.edu ​. Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=40973&lang=en": {
      "title": "COMBAT Open Rank-Research Scientist, Senior Research Scientist",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 7, 2026 Job category: Research Faculty Department: SOM-EM MED CLINICAL Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Department: Emergency Medicine Job Title: COMBAT Open Rank-Research Scientist, Senior Research Scientist Position #00820553: – Requisition #: 40973 Job Summary: The incumbent filling this position will serve at the rank of Research Scientist or Senior Research Scientist, have significant experience as a Project Management Professional (PMP), and will lead day-to-day operations of a large, translational research program spanning preclinical and clinical research activities. This is a full-time (1.0 FTE) faculty position in a fast-paced environment supported by federal funding. Work will occur primarily on campus (in-person). The incumbent will work alongside a highly collaborative multi-disciplinary team of clinician-investigators, preclinical researchers, regulatory experts, analysts and programmers, professional research assistants, and other research staff. The incumbent will be a full-time member of the Department of Emergency Medicine and will support research and development related to hemorrhage and resuscitation. The incumbent will work under supervision of the COMBAT Medicine Research Center (COMBAT) Senior Director/Program Principal Investigator (PI). COMBAT focuses on creating and executing acute care research to fulfill the needs of the U.S. military and our Colorado communities. COMBAT facilitates the execution of collaborative combat and deployment-relevant research by fostering relationships among military scientists, clinical investigators, combat leaders, and field operators to produce successful innovations, materiel solutions, and knowledge products of high impact to the warfighter and the medics. The successful candidate will have demonstrated expertise in program management and relevant expertise in translational science, public health, epidemiology, health-related science, or a related field. They will have a passion for collaborative research (team science), will be detail oriented, and contribute to development of detailed research plans and interpretation of data. In addition, the candidate should be able to work independently and manage a portfolio of concurrent projects, with excellent written and oral communication skills to contribute to program reports, presentations, and scientific writing. The job requires in-person duties and will be performed on the University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus in Aurora, CO. Domestic travel may be intermittently required to attend domestic scientific conferences/meetings or to present to stakeholder groups. This role is contingent on award funding. Key Responsibilities: · Translate high-level research program objectives into detailed plans and timelines to align to funding sponsor goals · Facilitate collaboration across multidisciplinary research teams and leadership, ensuring program activities are executed in accordance with timelines and budgets · Identify internal and external risks to research program success, including internal and external factors, and develop mitigation strategies · Communicate with external stakeholders including federal sponsors, regulatory bodies, and other academic/industry partners · Support development and execution of agreements with program associated partners · Work with department and program finance teams to track and project costs · Ensure appropriate milestone documentation is complete · Manage reporting requirements · Assist data collection, analysis, and reporting Compared to the Research Scientist, the Senior Research Scientist will: · Exercise more autonomy in duties · Assume larger managerial roles in overall program execution · Undertake a larger role in directly interfacing with program funding sponsor and other external stakeholders and representing the program at high level engagements · Assume a larger role in execution of research activities The duties of this position may change from time to time and/or based on business needs. We reserve the right to add or delete duties and responsibilities at the discretion of the supervisor and/or hiring authority. Work Location: Hybrid – this role is expected to work onsite 3 days per week and is located in Aurora, Colorado. Why Join Us: The Department of Emergency Medicine conducts ground-breaking research into areas such as trauma, injury prevention, global health, opioid misuse, critical care, mental health, pharmacogenomics, toxicology, and healthcare policy. The Department values team members who are eager to pursue further training and exciting career growth as a researcher and professional. Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package including: · Medical: Multiple plan options · Dental: Multiple plan options · Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision · Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay · Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year (based on percentage of time) · Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) · Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) · Holiday Days: 11/year · Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses · ECO Pass: Reduced rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. This is an open rank position and could be categorized as Research Scientist or Senior Research Scientist based on experience and qualifications as indicated below: Open Rank: Rank at the time of appointment will be based on the candidate’s demonstrated contributions and experience in teaching, clinical, research, and/or service to the field. We welcome applicants with a range of backgrounds and accomplishments and encourage individuals to highlight the breadth and depth of their professional impact. Learn more about faculty tracks at the Office for Faculty Affairs . Research Scientist: · Masters degree in translational research, public health, project management, or related field · At least two years of experience working in project management role at an academic medical or research, biotechnology research and development, or contract research organization setting Senior Research Scientist: · Doctoral Degree in translational science, public health, epidemiology, health-related science, or related field. · At least four years of experience working in project management role at an academic medical or research, biotechnology research and development, or contract research organization setting Preferred Qualifications: · Project Management Professional certification · Experience working on translational research projects from · Demonstrated proficiency with at least one project management software application (e.g., MS Project, Smartsheet) · At least seven years of experience working in an academic medical or research setting such as biotechnology R&D or contract research organization · Demonstrated ability to develop and manage timelines for multiple research projects simultaneously · Experience in presenting at seminars and scientific meetings · Equivalent combination of education, training, and experience that provides the individual with the required knowledge, skills and abilities Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: · Highly self-motivated · Strong written and oral communication skills · Proactive communicator · Strong organizational skills · Good interpersonal skills · Ability to think creatively and work independently · Effective team player · Positive attitude · Ability to solve complex problems · Effective project management and time management skills with ability to manage multiple projects or requests simultaneously · Strong knowledge of basic statistical principles relevant in medical research · An innate desire to learn Conditions of Employment: · Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without requiring sponsorship. We are unable to provide work visa sponsorship or employment authorization for this position now or in the future. · This role is contingent on award funding. How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): 1. A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position 2. Curriculum vitae / Resume 3. Five professional references including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers . Questions should be directed to: EMED Human Resources at emed.humanresources@ucdenver.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Immediately and continues until position is filled. For best consideration, apply by 10/30/2026. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as: Research Scientist: starts at $90,000 and goes up from there based on years of experience. Research Senior Scientist: starts at $100,000 and goes up from there based on years of experience. The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation unless it is non-exempt. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: The University of Colorado (CU) is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@ucdenver.edu ​. Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41340&lang=en": {
      "title": "Registered Nurse - Family Medicine, Landmark",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 7, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: SOM-DEAN DO CPD - PRIM CARE Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Department: Community Practice Job Title: Registered Nurse - Family Medicine, Landmark Position #: 00853812 – Requisition #: 41340 Job Summary: The Registered Nurse (RN) provides high-quality support to physicians and advanced practice providers (APPs) in meeting the operational needs of the practice and the medical needs of the patient. The RN assesses and evaluates patient conditions, and then plans, implements, provides, and documents patient care in a manner that follows professional nursing standards and outlined practices. Key Responsibilities: Escorts patients to and from exam rooms and readies them for physicians. Performs telephone triage, patient education, handling of physician phone calls, and pharmacy calls. Takes vital signs, records medical history/symptoms, and ensures medical chart/lab test results are available and complete. Administers immunizations and minor treatments as prescribed. Responds to patient questions and concerns as a liaison between physician and patient. Reports all test results to the patient as directed by the physician. Work Location: Onsite – this role is expected to work onsite and is located in Landmark, CO . Why Join Us: Community Practice Medicine, housed within the School of Medicine at the University of Colorado, is seeking trained medical professionals to join our growing team. With clinics spanning from Longmont to Castle Rock, we offer a wide variety of opportunities. Specialty areas include, but are not limited to: Orthopedics, Vascular Surgery, OBGYN, Internal Medicine, Urology, Psychiatry, and many more! The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is a public education, clinical, and research facility serving 4,500 students and a world-class medical destination at the forefront of life-changing science, medicine, and healthcare. CU Anschutz offers more than 42 highly rated degree programs through 6 schools and colleges and receives over $500 million in research awards each year. We are the single largest health professions education provider in Colorado, awarding nearly 1,450 degrees annually. Powered by our award-winning faculty, renowned researchers, and a reputation for academic excellence, the CU Anschutz Medical Campus drives innovation from the classroom to the laboratory to the delivery of unparalleled patient care. Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation, and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package, including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 15/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced-rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Entry Level: Graduate of an accredited Nursing program through the Accreditation Commission for Education in Nursing (ACEN) or American Nursing Credentialing Center (ANCC). Intermediate Level: Graduate of an accredited Nursing program through the Accreditation Commission for Education in Nursing (ACEN) or American Nursing Credentialing Center (ANCC). Two (2) years of nursing experience. Senior Level: Graduate of an accredited Nursing program through the Accreditation Commission for Education in Nursing (ACEN) or American Nursing Credentialing Center (ANCC). Four (4) years of nursing experience. Substitution (All Levels): A combination of education and related technical/military/paraprofessional experience may be substituted for a bachelor’s degree on a year-for-year basis. Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Preferred Qualifications (All Levels): Bachelor of Science in Nursing (BSN). One to two (1-2) or more years of job-related/clinic experience. Bilingual, Spanish-speaking. Nursing certification (ANCC) in specialty area. Epic, Kronos, and HealthStream experience. Conditions of Employment (All Levels): Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without requiring sponsorship. We are unable to provide work visa sponsorship or employment authorization for this position now or in the future. Current Basic Life Support (BLS) for Healthcare Providers issued by the American Heart Association or the American Red Cross healthcare provider-level CPR certification. Registered Nurse (RN), State of Colorado. Maintains all required licensure and certifications for the position. Maintains all required continuing education requirements. Must be able to work in person. Must be able to travel to alternate locations as assigned. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities (All Levels): Strong organizational and communication skills. Ability to effectively communicate at all levels, to include physicians, leadership, and staff within the various affiliate organizations (UCH, Children’s Colorado, CU Medicine, CU SOM). Ability to work within large, complex healthcare systems. Ability to analyze and interpret data. Ability to compile complex reports and develop presentations. Ability to compose letters and memorandums. Ability to deal calmly and courteously with people. Ability to deal with stressful situations. Ability to finish tasks in a timely manner. How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to the listed job qualifications and interest in the position Curriculum vitae / Resume Three to five professional references, including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Questions should be directed to: Cristine Gentert, cristine.gentert@cuanschutz.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Immediately and continues until the position is filled. Best consideration will be given to those who apply by 11/7/2026 . Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as: Entry Level: $69,160 to $80,226 Intermediate Level: $74,347 to $86,243 Senior Level: $79,534 to $93,850 The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position may be eligible for overtime compensation, depending on the level. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans, and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@cuanschutz.edu . Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students, and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine-preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety-sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41339&lang=en": {
      "title": "Open Rank Laboratory Sciences Professional",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 7, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: SOM-PEDS Critical Care-GenOps Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Department: Pediatrics, Section of Critical Care Job Title: Open Rank Laboratory Sciences Professional Position #: 00853810 – Requisition #: 41339 Job Summary: The Department of Pediatrics, Section of Pediatric Critical Care is seeking a full-time Research Services Professional or Research Services Senior Professional to join a research program investigating the mechanistic drivers of pulmonary hypertension (PH) across the lifespan. The successful candidate will contribute to two related lines of investigation: (1) macrophage–extracellular matrix interactions that govern vascular remodeling in PH, and (2) maternal stress signaling pathways that predispose offspring to pulmonary vascular disease. This position offers the opportunity to work across in vivo mouse models, cell/tissue-based assays, and advanced molecular techniques (e.g., flow cytometry, spatial transcriptomics, single-cell sequencing) within a collaborative, translationally oriented lab environment. Responsibilities include performing experiments using mouse models of PH and primary cell culture, as well as flow cytometry, ELISA, Western blot, immunohistochemistry, and microscopic analysis. The role also involves maintaining an accurate database, participating in data analysis, and managing project records and protocol organization. Additional responsibilities include developing new lab protocols and, potentially, supervising trainees (students) and training new lab personnel. The ideal candidate is reliable, personable, highly motivated, and organized, with a demonstrated ability to work independently when appropriate. This is an excellent opportunity to join a fast-paced, diverse, and productive research group. The position is based in the Research Complex 2 building on the Anschutz Medical Campus. Key Responsibilities: Intermediate Level: Collaborate with and support Principal Investigators (PI) and other stakeholders with laboratory and research functions Utilize a variety of laboratory techniques required for research projects Perform experiments and tabulate and analyze research data Support the analytical testing process using standard lab support knowledge in the collection and review of conditions, including preserving samples, completing sample preparation, documenting and communicating results Perform pre-analytical, analytical, and post-analytical test processes and evaluate results produced Prepare lab for daily operations, including stocking materials, equipment, safety, cleanliness, and related areas Provide animal care related to research studies, as necessary Pick up, transport, and maintain results, samples, documents, materials, and other items as needed Dispose of laboratory materials and samples using well-established guidelines and instructions Review, complete, and process logs, documents, databases, and related materials and information Provide support researching issues and developing recommendations to resolve process, unit and related issues Assist in the review and implementation of lab support policies, practices, and programs to meet organizational, operations, and management needs Assist with ensuring compliance with applicable laws, rules and regulations; receive guidance and direction or escalate when required Independently and creatively identify laboratory solutions Independently Review, develop, and implement new or modified laboratory techniques required for research projects Assist Team Leads, Supervisors and/or management with creation and implementation of processes and procedures and quality improvement initiatives Assist and train junior team members Senior Level, all above and: Assist with developing or develop protocol-specific systems and documents including process flows, training manuals, and Standard Operating Procedures (SOPs). Maintains subject-level documentation and prepares documents, equipment, and/or supplies Assist with identifying issues related to operational efficiency and share results with leadership Provide laboratory science expertise and leadership in study design, study oversight, data management, data analysis and manuscript preparation to assist all levels of investigators, researchers and clinicians on new research activities across a wide range of disciplines Serve as a resource to PIs and other stakeholders Additional Duties & Responsibilities: Conduct bench work including: Perform basic laboratory studies, including: Molecular and Biochemical research; cell culture, transfections, ELISA, Western blot, immunohistochemistry, molecular biology, flow cytometry, biochemical assays, microscopic analysis, small rodent (mouse) work excluding genotyping and colony management Train/supervise junior lab members in bench work Lab management including: Contributing to organization and overall maintenance of lab Organization of data Overseeing maintenance of lab equipment Maintaining lab protocols Training new lab personnel as appropriate This description is a summary only and describes the general level of work being performed; it is not intended to be all-inclusive. The duties of this position may change from time to time and/or based on business need. We reserve the right to add or delete duties and responsibilities at the discretion of the supervisor and/or hiring authority. Work Location: Onsite – this role is expected to work onsite and is located in Aurora, CO . Why Join Us: The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is a public education, clinical, and research facility serving 4,500 students and is a world-class medical destination at the forefront of life-changing science, medicine, and healthcare. CU Anschutz offers more than 42 highly rated degree programs through 6 schools and colleges and receives over $500 million in research awards each year. We are the single largest health professions education provider in Colorado, awarding nearly 1,450 degrees annually. Powered by our award-winning faculty, renowned researchers, and a reputation for academic excellence, the CU Anschutz Medical Campus drives innovation from the classroom to the laboratory to the delivery of unparalleled patient care. Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation, and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package, including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 15/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced-rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Intermediate Level: Bachelor’s degree in biology, molecular biology, chemistry, genetics, or related field Substitution: A combination of education and related technical/paraprofessional experience may be substituted for the bachelor’s degree on a year-for-year basis One (1) year of professional-level research experience Senior Level: Bachelor’s degree in biology, molecular biology, chemistry, genetics, or related field Substitution: A combination of education and related technical/paraprofessional experience may be substituted for the bachelor’s degree on a year-for-year basis Two (2) years of professional-level research experience Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Preferred Qualifications: Intermediate Level: Master’s degree in biology, molecular biology, chemistry, genetics, or related field Two (2) years of experience in an experimental or wet laboratory Senior Level: Master’s degree in biology, molecular biology, chemistry, genetics, or a related field Three (3) years of experience in an experimental or wet laboratory Conditions of Employment: Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without requiring sponsorship. We are unable to provide work visa sponsorship or employment authorization for this position now or in the future. Must be willing and able to pass national criminal and sex offender background checks Must successfully pass a 10-panel drug screen through Children’s Hospital Colorado *For questions regarding Children’s Hospital drug testing requirements, please contact Children’s Human Resources at 720-777-8598. Some positions may require testing if access to Children’s Hospital or its systems is needed at any time during employment with the University. If drug testing is required, it will be listed in the job posting. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Intermediate Level: Proficient knowledge of basic laboratory techniques, including safety procedures and techniques Ability to communicate effectively, both in writing and orally Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with employees at all levels throughout the institution Outstanding customer service skills Demonstrated commitment and leadership ability to advance diversity and inclusion Knowledge of basic human anatomy, physiology, and medical terminology Ability to interpret and master complex research protocol information Experience with models of lung disease Experience with flow cytometry and/or advanced molecular techniques Experience developing and troubleshooting new laboratory protocols Experience maintaining a database and organizing a lab as lab manager Experience training students and fellows Senior Level: Advanced knowledge of laboratory techniques, including safety procedures and techniques Ability to communicate effectively, both in writing and orally Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with employees at all levels throughout the institution Outstanding customer service skills Demonstrated commitment and leadership ability to advance diversity and inclusion Knowledge of basic human anatomy, physiology, and medical terminology Experience with models of lung disease Experience with flow cytometry and/or advanced molecular techniques Experience developing and troubleshooting new laboratory protocols Experience maintaining a database and organizing a lab as lab manager Experience training students and fellows How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to the listed job qualifications and interest in the position Curriculum vitae / Resume Three to five professional references, including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Questions should be directed to: Caitlin Lewis, Caitlin.V.Lewis@cuanschutz.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Immediately and continues until the position is filled. For best consideration, apply by October 31, 2026 . Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as: Intermediate Level: $52,030 to $69,720 Senior Level: $56,249 to $75,373 The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position may be eligible for overtime compensation, depending on the level. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans, and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@cuanschutz.edu . Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students, and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine-preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety-sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
