    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41316&lang=en": {
      "title": "Open Rank: Instructor, Sr. Instructor, Assistant, Associate Professor",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 3, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: SOM-OB/GYN CMED GENERAL OPS Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Department: Obstetrics and Gynecology Job Title: Open Rank: Instructor, Sr. Instructor, Assistant, Associate Professor Position #00853651: – Requisition #: 41316 Job Summary: The Department of Obstetrics and Gynecology, Division of Community Practice, is excited to announce an opening for a full-time Instructor or above to join our Community Practice Division. We are seeking a skilled generalist to provide comprehensive clinical care in both obstetrics and gynecology, including inpatient and outpatient services, as well as surgery. As a member of the Community Practice Division, you will collaborate with a team of providers, sharing service coverage, including night and weekend call at UCHealth Highlands Ranch Hospital. While the position is primarily clinical, you will have opportunities to contribute to the education of medical residents and students, supporting the next generation of clinicians. Key Responsibilities: · Provide high-quality, patient-centered obstetrics and gynecology care across outpatient, inpatient, and surgical settings. · Participate in shared call coverage, including night and weekend calls. · Collaborate with physicians, advanced practice providers, nurses, and staff to support efficient, coordinated care across the practice. · Supervise and teach medical students and residents in clinical and procedural settings. · Maintain accurate, timely, and complete medical documentation and required training. · Engage in quality improvement initiatives that support patient safety, care quality, and clinical outcomes. · Contribute to community outreach and patient education efforts that advance the health and well-being of the communities we serve. Work Location: Onsite – this role is expected to work onsite in Highlands Ranch, CO. Why Join Us: This is an ideal opportunity for clinicians who want the variety and fulfillment of a generalist practice while staying connected to an academic institution that fosters professional growth, collaboration, and excellence in patient care. You will join a community-focused team that values work-life balance, high-quality care, and a modern, patient-centered facility designed to make both providers and patients feel at home. Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation, and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package including: · Medical: Multiple plan options · Dental: Multiple plan options · Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision · Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay · Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year (based on percentage of time) · Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) · Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) · Holiday Days: 11/year · Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses · ECO Pass: Reduced rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. This is an open rank position and could be categorized as Instructor, Senior Instructor, Assistant Professor, or Associate Professor based on experience and qualifications as indicated below: Open Track: To support the growth of our faculty, selected candidates will be offered the opportunity to choose a track that corresponds to their area of excellence. Learn more about faculty tracks at the Office for Faculty Affairs . Open Rank: Rank at the time of appointment will be based on the candidate’s demonstrated contributions and experience in teaching, clinical, research, and/or service to the field. We welcome applicants with a range of backgrounds and accomplishments and encourage individuals to highlight the breadth and depth of their professional impact. Learn more about faculty tracks at the Office for Faculty Affairs . Instructor: · MD or DO degree from an accredited institution · Board certified or board eligible in Obstetrics & Gynecology · Newly graduated physicians who meet licensure and board eligibility requirements are encouraged to apply. · Active , unrestricted Colorado medical license · Current BLS certification Sr. Instructor: · MD or DO degree from an accredited institution · Board certified or board eligible in Obstetrics & Gynecology · Active , unrestricted Colorado medical license · Current BLS certification · Four (4) years of post-residency clinical experience in Obstetrics and Gynecology, with demonstrated commitment to high-quality patient care, collaboration, and clinical excellence Assistant Professor: · MD or DO degree from an accredited institution · Board certified in Obstetrics & Gynecology · Active , unrestricted Colorado medical license · Current BLS certification · Six (6) years of post-residency clinical experience in Obstetrics and Gynecology, with demonstrated commitment to high-quality patient care, collaboration, and clinical excellence Associate Professor: · MD or DO degree from an accredited institution · Board certified in Obstetrics & Gynecology · Active , unrestricted Colorado medical license · Current BLS certification · Seven (7) years of post-residency clinical experience in Obstetrics and Gynecology, with demonstrated commitment to high-quality patient care, collaboration, and clinical excellence Preferred Qualifications: · Experience in high-volume and/or high-risk obstetrics · Experience supporting clinical education · Knowledge of Epic electronic medical record systems Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: · Labor management, including knowledge of normal and high-risk labor progression · Fetal heart rate monitoring and interpretation · Knowledge of gynecologic evaluation and management · Experience with contraception counseling and procedures, including LARC placement and removal · Ability to perform routine gynecologic surgeries · Clear, effective communication and clinical documentation · Demonstrated professionalism, compassion, and a patient-centered approach to care across diverse populations Conditions of Employment: · Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without requiring sponsorship. We are unable to provide work visa sponsorship or employment authorization for this position now or in the future. How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): 1. A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position 2. Curriculum vitae / Resume 3. Five professional references including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers . Questions should be directed to: Tammy Orton, tammy.orton@cuanschutz.edu Screening of Applications Begins: This position may be seeking multiple candidates. Positions will remain open until filled. Applications will be reviewed as they are received, and candidates may be contacted for interviews throughout the posting period. Upon candidate(s) selection, the posting will be closed, and no further applications will be accepted. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as Instructor: $295,000 to $300,000 Sr. Instructor: $301,000 to $325,000 Assistant Professor: $325,000 to $335,000 Associate Professor: $335,000 to $360,000 **This position is eligible for participation in a metric-based incentive following the first 12 months of employment. The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation unless it is non-exempt. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: The University of Colorado (CU) is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@ucdenver.edu ​. Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41312&lang=en": {
      "title": "Head and Neck Pathologist (Assistant or Associate Professor)",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 3, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: SOM-Pathology Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Department of Pathology Head and Neck Pathologist (Assistant or Associate Professor) Position #: 00853667 – Requisition #:41312 Job Summary: The Department of Pathology of the University of Colorado School of Medicine, Anschutz Medical Campus seeks a full-time Faculty member (Assistant or Associate Professor) with head and neck surgical pathology subspecialty training. The recruit will serve as an attending pathologist and educate others in head and neck surgical pathology. The attending pathologist will be part of a multidisciplinary team, inclusive of a team of senior pathologists as well as other subspecialty trained physicians; thus, strong verbal and written communication and professionalism skills are expected. This position is an academic post; hence, scholarly activity and teaching of pathology residents is expected and time for these activities will be provided. The general responsibilities and expectations of this position mirror the missions of the Departments and affiliated systems, including: excellence in clinical care, medical undergraduate and graduate education, and scholarship. The successful applicant will join a group of three dozen subspecialty surgical pathologists, including 3 head and neck pathologists, who contribute to the practice of multi-disciplinary team based subspecialty pathology practice at the University of Colorado Hospital. Applicants with interest and expertise in pathology subspecialties in addition to head and neck surgical pathology are encouraged to apply. The position includes regularly scheduled clinical and intraoperative frozen section work as well as minor general anatomic pathology on call responsibilities. Key Responsibilities: · Promote quality patient care through the sign out of routine and complex head and neck cases from UCH and affiliated clinics as well as consulting institutions, pathologists, and patients. · Adherence to the quality standards and regulatory requirements associated with the anatomic pathology laboratories, as well as UCH and affiliated clinics · Ensure timely completion and accurate reporting of pathology tests associated with your practice, consultations, or translational research. · Consult with peer pathologists on cases as requested or required by policy. · Participate in the education of pathologists and affiliated non-pathologist providers through consultations, including at multidisciplinary clinics, and the application and education associated with test interpretation. · Train and supervise pathology and non-pathology students, residents, and fellows. · Engage in scholarly activities as broadly defined by the School of Medicine, inclusive of the scholarship of application, teaching, integration, and discovery. · Maintain exemplary professionalism and continue to develop collaborative relationships with the pathology community and non-pathology providers. Work Location: Onsite – this role is expected to work onsite and is located in Aurora, CO. Why Join Us: Welcome to the Department of Pathology of the CU Anschutz, School of Medicine. The Department has grown substantially in the past 15 years, from 40 to 120 faculty in parallel with the remarkable growth of our hospital-based affiliates as well as the city and county of Denver. Our work is value driven and focused on scientific investigation, lifelong learning, and a balance of personal and professional values. In addition to a vibrant and highly competitive residency program with 25 positions, we offer 9 fellowships and participate in numerous graduate schools and the MD/PhD program of the CU Anschutz School of Medicine. Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package including: · Medical: Multiple plan options · Dental: Multiple plan options · Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision · Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay · Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year (based on percentage of time) · Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) · Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) · Holiday Days: 11/year · Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses · ECO Pass: Reduced rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. This is an open rank position and could be categorized Assistant Professor or Associate Professor based on experience and qualifications as indicated below: To support the growth of our faculty, selected candidates will be offered the opportunity to choose a track that corresponds to their area of excellence. Learn more about faculty tracks at the Office for Faculty Affairs . Rank at the time of appointment will be based on the candidate’s demonstrated contributions and experience in teaching, clinical, research, and/or service to the field. We welcome applicants with a range of backgrounds and accomplishments and encourage individuals to highlight the breadth and depth of their professional impact. Learn more about faculty tracks at the Office for Faculty Affairs . Assistant Professor: · MD, DO, or equivalent · Graduation from an accredited Anatomic Pathology Residency Program · Board certified in Anatomic Pathology and the credentials to obtain medical licensure in Colorado, followed by a University appointment at the rank of Assistant Professor · Completion of a head and neck pathology fellowship or extensive relevant experience · Demonstrated excellence in teaching and scholarship · 0-5 years of experience Associate Professor: · MD, DO, or equivalent · Graduation from an accredited Anatomic Pathology Residency Program · Board certified in Anatomic Pathology and the credentials to obtain medical licensure in Colorado, followed by a University appointment at the rank of Associate Professor · Completion of a head and neck pathology fellowship or extensive relevant experience · Demonstrated excellence in teaching and scholarship · Generally 5-10 years of experience Conditions of Employment: · Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without requiring sponsorship. We are unable to provide work visa sponsorship or employment authorization for this position now or in the future. How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): 1. A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position 2. Curriculum vitae / Resume 3. Five professional references including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers . Questions should be directed to Dr. Jeffrey Kaplan at Jeffrey.Kaplan@cuanschutz.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Immediately and continues until position is filled. For best consideration, apply by October 31, 2026. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as: Assistant Professor: $230,000 to $265,000 Associate Professor: $260,000 to $315,000 The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation unless it is non-exempt. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: The University of Colorado (CU) is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@ucdenver.edu ​. Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41311&lang=en": {
      "title": "Gastrointestinal and Liver Pathologist (Assistant or Associate Professor)",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 3, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: SOM-Pathology Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anaschutz Department of Pathology Gastrointestinal and Liver Pathologist (Assistant or Associate Professor) Position #: 00853674 – Requisition #: 41311 Job Summary: The Department of Pathology of the CU Anschutz, School of Medicine seeks a full-time junior to senior faculty member with expertise in gastrointestinal, hepatic, and pancreaticobiliary (GI/liver) surgical pathology at the rank of Assistant Professor or Associate Professor. The successful candidate will join a team of eight academic GI/liver surgical pathologists based at the affiliated 925 bed University of Colorado Hospital (UCH) located in metro Denver. GI/liver pathology fellowship training or extensive relevant experience in GI/liver surgical pathology is required. The Department of Pathology provides professional and technical anatomic pathology services to the UCH and affiliated clinics using a subspecialty sign out model. The GI/liver service reports on approximately 22,000 cases per year, inclusive of advanced endoscopic interventions, complex oncologic resections, and transplantations. While the primary clinical focus of this position is in GI/liver surgical pathology, secondary clinical interests in other areas of anatomic pathology will be accommodated. Faculty engage in scholarship, through collaborative scientific investigations and/or through the development of their own research programs. Faculty teach in the 25 seat Combined Anatomic Pathology and Clinical Pathology Residency Program, 11 pathology fellowship programs (including a 2 seat GI/Liver Pathology Fellowship Program), affiliated clinical residency and fellowship programs, medical school, and other graduate health programs. Faculty are part of a multidisciplinary team, inclusive of other pathologists, technical staff, and non-pathologist providers; thus, strong communication and professionalism skills are necessary. The successful applicant will join a group of three dozen subspecialty surgical pathologists who currently contribute to the practice of multi-disciplinary team based subspecialty pathology practice at the University of Colorado Hospital. The position includes regularly scheduled clinical and GI/liver subspecialty intraoperative frozen section work as well as minor general anatomic pathology on call responsibilities. Key Responsibilities: · Promote quality patient care through the sign out of routine and complex GI/liver cases from UCH and affiliated clinics as well as consulting institutions, pathologists, and patients. · Adherence to the quality standards and regulatory requirements associated with the anatomic pathology laboratories, as well as UCH and affiliated clinics · Ensure timely completion and accurate reporting of pathology tests associated with your practice, consultations, or translational research. o Consult with peer pathologists on cases as requested or required by policy. · Participate in the education of pathologists and affiliated non-pathologist providers through consultations, including at multidisciplinary clinics, and the application and education associated with test interpretation. · Train and supervise pathology and non-pathology students, residents, and fellows. · Engage in scholarly activities as broadly defined by the School of Medicine, inclusive of the scholarship of application, teaching, integration, and discovery. · Maintain exemplary professionalism and continue to develop collaborative relationships with the pathology community and non-pathology providers. Work Location: Onsite – this role is expected to work onsite and is located in Aurora, CO. Why Join Us: Welcome to the Department of Pathology of the CU Anschutz, School of Medicine. The Department has grown substantially in the past 15 years, from 40 to 120 faculty in parallel with the remarkable growth of our hospital-based affiliates as well as the city and county of Denver. Our work is value driven and focused on scientific investigation, lifelong learning, and a balance of personal and professional values. In addition to a vibrant and highly competitive residency program with 25 positions, we offer 9 fellowships and participate in numerous graduate schools and the MD/PhD program of the CU Anschutz School of Medicine. Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package including: · Medical: Multiple plan options · Dental: Multiple plan options · Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision · Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay · Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year (based on percentage of time) · Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) · Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) · Holiday Days: 11/year · Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses · ECO Pass: Reduced rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. This is an open rank position and could be categorized as Instructor, Senior Instructor, Assistant Professor, Associate Professor or Professor based on experience and qualifications as indicated below: To support the growth of our faculty, selected candidates will be offered the opportunity to choose a track that corresponds to their area of excellence. Learn more about faculty tracks at the Office for Faculty Affairs . Rank at the time of appointment will be based on the candidate’s demonstrated contributions and experience in teaching, clinical, research, and/or service to the field. We welcome applicants with a range of backgrounds and accomplishments and encourage individuals to highlight the breadth and depth of their professional impact. Learn more about faculty tracks at the Office for Faculty Affairs . Assistant Professor: · MD, DO, or equivalent · Graduation from an accredited Anatomic Pathology Residency Program · Board certified in Anatomic Pathology and the credentials to obtain medical licensure in Colorado, followed by a University appointment at the rank of Assistant Professor · Completion of a fellowship in GI/Liver pathology or extensive relevant experience · Demonstrated excellence in teaching and scholarship · 0-5 years of experience Associate Professor: · MD, DO, or equivalent · Graduation from an accredited Anatomic Pathology Residency Program · Board certified in Anatomic Pathology and the credentials to obtain medical licensure in Colorado, followed by a University appointment at the rank of Associate Professor · Completion of a fellowship in GI/Liver pathology or extensive relevant experience · Demonstrated excellence in teaching and scholarship · 5-10 years of experience Conditions of Employment: · Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without requiring sponsorship. We are unable to provide work visa sponsorship or employment authorization for this position now or in the future. How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): 1. A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position 2. Curriculum vitae / Resume 3. Five professional references including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers . Questions should be directed to Dr. Jeffrey Kaplan at Jeffrey.Kaplan@cuanschutz.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Immediately and continues until position is filled. For best consideration, apply by October 31, 2026. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as: Assistant: $230,000 – $265,000 Associate Professor: $260,000 – $315,000 The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation unless it is non-exempt. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: The University of Colorado (CU) is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@ucdenver.edu ​. Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41307&lang=en": {
      "title": "Advanced Practice Provider (APP) (PA/NP/APRN) Pediatrics- -Instructor",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 2, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: SOM-PEDS General Peds-GenOps Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Department: Pediatrics, Section of General Pediatrics Job Title: (SCC-Outpatient) Advanced Practice Provider - Instructor (APP) (PA/NP/APRN) Position #: 00602123 – Requisition #:41307 Job Summary: The Special Care Clinic (SCC) serves as a medical home and consultative base for over 3,000 children in our region who are medically complex, in addition to their well siblings. The outpatient Advanced Practice Provider (physician assistant or nurse practitioner) of Clinical Practice will serve as a primary care provider for these patients. They will be responsible for managing their well visits, follow up visits, care coordination, chronic illness management, and treatment of minor and acute illness. As a 1.0 cFTE, the clinical expectation is 6 clinic sessions/week, with an additional 1-2 clinics/month. Each clinic session is four hours in length and this equates to 294 sessions/year. Program leadership holds the right to determine when the admin session can be taken based on clinic need. This is a clinical position, involving clinical work in an outpatient setting, which can include teaching responsibilities for clinical trainees. The position primarily works daytime hours, Monday - Friday. Key Responsibilities: · Providing direct clinical care to patients in our region who are medically complex · Engaging in teaching of trainees when needed · Participating regularly in joint faculty/staff meetings · Participating in the on-call rotation · Participating in the provider of the day rotation Work Location: Onsite – this role is expected to work onsite and is located in Aurora, CO. Why Join Us: Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year (based on percentage of time) Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 11/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. ● Physician Assistant (PA) or Nurse Practitioner license required (FNP or PNP) ● Clinical experience required as a PA, FNP or PNP Condition of Employment: ● Must successfully pass a drug test through Children’s Hospital Colorado ● Must be willing and able to pass a national criminal background check *For questions regarding Children’s Hospital drug testing requirements, please contact Children’s Human Resources at 720-777-8598. Some positions may require testing if access to Children’s Hospital or their systems is needed at any time during employment with the University. If drug testing is required, it will be listed in the job posting. Preferred Qualifications: ● Clinical experience with children who have complex needs. ● Clinical experience in a pediatric outpatient environment. ● Clinical experience in a pediatric primary care location. ● Clinical experience in an academic setting. ● Spanish speaking preferred but not required. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: ● Strong time management as the provider will be managing multiple patients at a time. ● Strong communication and teamwork skills. ● Adaptability and flexibility. ● We are looking for an energetic, open-minded provider who enjoys working with a diverse and complex population. How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): 1. A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position 2. Curriculum vitae / Resume 3. Five professional references including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers . Questions should be directed to: Rebecca Barlow rebecca.barlow@childrenscolorado.org Screening of Applications Begins: Immediately and continues until position is filled. For best consideration, apply by Nov. 1, 2026 Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range (or hiring range) for this position has been established as HIRING RANGE: $103,000 - $119,000 The above salary range (or hiring range) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation unless it is non-exempt. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Equal Opportunity Statement: The University of Colorado (CU) is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@ucdenver.edu ​. Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41304&lang=en": {
      "title": "Patient Services Representative I-II – Family Medicine, Landmark",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 2, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: SOM-DEAN DO CPD - PRIM CARE Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus Department: Community Practice Job Title: Patient Services Representative I-II – Family Medicine, Landmark Position #: 00853707 – Requisition #: 41304 Job Summary: Attention customer service experts with a passion for team-centric care coordination in an outpatient setting. We need your caring and compassionate expertise to continue providing our patients with top-notch quality care. The Patient Services Representative is responsible for providing efficient, effective, quality customer service through a variety of duties, including, but not limited to, patient check-in, registration, scheduling, exam preparation, outbound calling, and some referral management. They comply with established company policies and procedures, HIPAA Privacy Rules, and the University of Colorado School of Medicine Confidentiality Policy. The Patient Services Representative ensures clear and timely communication, including patient appointment status, to clinical department(s). Key Responsibilities: Acknowledges and welcomes patients and visitors; sets the tone for a positive experience Checks patients in and out for appointments; schedules follow-up appointments at the time of discharge Verifies patient and insurance information, while accurately documenting necessary modifications in the Electronic Health Record (EPIC) Answers multiple phone lines to fulfill patient needs over the phone Monitors provider schedules daily to ensure that all open appointment slots are filled on the same day and schedules are free of roadblocks Reviews the Daily Appointment Report three to five days in advance for patient appointments to ensure referral accuracy Collects patient copays and balances the drawer daily Work Location: Onsite – this role is expected to work onsite and is located in Landmark, CO. Why Join Us: Community Practice Medicine, housed within the School of Medicine at the University of Colorado, is seeking trained medical professionals to join our growing team. With clinics spanning from Longmont to Castle Rock, we offer a wide variety of opportunities. Specialty areas include, but are not limited to: Orthopedics, Vascular Surgery, OBGYN, Internal Medicine, Urology, Psychiatry, and many more! The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is a public education, clinical, and research facility serving 4,500 students and a world-class medical destination at the forefront of life-changing science, medicine, and healthcare. CU Anschutz offers more than 42 highly rated degree programs through 6 schools and colleges and receives over $500 million in research awards each year. We are the single largest health professions education provider in Colorado, awarding nearly 1,450 degrees annually. Powered by our award-winning faculty, renowned researchers, and a reputation for academic excellence, the CU Anschutz Medical Campus drives innovation from the classroom to the laboratory to the delivery of unparalleled patient care. Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation, and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package, including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 15/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced-rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Patient Services Representative I: High school diploma or GED One or more (1+) years of patient/client-facing experience Patient Services Representative II: High school diploma or GED Two or more (2+) years of patient/client-facing experience Substitution (All Levels): A combination of education and related technical/military/paraprofessional experience may be substituted for a bachelor’s degree on a year-for-year basis. Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Preferred Qualifications (All Ranks): College graduate Medical office experience EPIC experience MS Office experience Bilingual, Spanish-speaking Conditions of Employment: Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without requiring sponsorship. We are unable to provide work visa sponsorship or employment authorization for this position now or in the future. Comply with the applicable University of Colorado School of Medicine, Community Practice mandatory education and training Must be able to work in person Must be able to travel to alternate locations as assigned Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Strong organizational and personal skills; must have strong work ethic Strong communication skills, both written and verbal Ability to maintain a positive attitude with clients, employees, and management Ability to work quickly – individually and as part of a team Ability to read, analyze, and interpret policies, documents, and regulations Must be detail-oriented and maintain excellent organizational skills Must be tech-savvy (ability to understand, apply, and benefit from technology) How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to the listed job qualifications and interest in the position Curriculum vitae / Resume Three to five professional references, including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Questions should be directed to: Cristine Gentert, cristine.gentert@cuanschutz.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Immediately and continues until the position is filled. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as: Patient Services Representative I: $40,000 to $46,720 Patient Services Representative II: $43,700 to $51,042 The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position may be eligible for overtime compensation, depending on the level. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans, and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@cuanschutz.edu . Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students, and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine-preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety-sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=40651&lang=en": {
      "title": "Research Services Clinical Sciences Professional OPEN RANK (Entry – Senior) Onsite",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 2, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: SOM-PM&R GENERAL OPERATIONS Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus Department: Department of Physical Medicine and Rehabilitation Job Title: Research Services Clinical Sciences Professional OPEN RANK (Entry – Senior) Onsite Position #:00851340 – Requisition #: 40651 Job Summary: The B4 Health Lab is looking for sharp, curious, and driven researchers to join our team full-time. Our work sits at the intersection of the Brain, Body, Biome, and Behavior — exploring how these systems connect to advance both physical and mental health. This is not a passive role. You'll be actively engaged with many, if not all, aspects of human subjects clinical research across multiple studies. This is a role for those that thrive in a fast-paced and detail-driven environment. You will not be bored! This is not a wet lab or bench science position. What You'll Do You'll actively engage in the day-to-day operations of human clinical trials and research studies from start to finish. That means you'll be the person participants trust, the one ensuring protocols are followed precisely, and the contributor who keeps studies running smoothly and compliantly. Specifically, you will. Serve as Coordinator on multiple human subject research studies, mastering protocols and study documents and ensuring every procedure meets regulatory standards Drive participant recruitment — from pre-screening and phone contacts to in-person interviews and eligibility confirmation Guide participants through the informed consent process and coordinate all scheduling logistics, including clinical resources such as nursing, laboratory, radiology, and pharmacy Collect, code, and analyze study data with precision, maintaining records in compliance with FDA requirements, IRB standards, and applicable SOPs Contribute to process improvement by supporting the development of SOPs and quality assurance initiatives that make the whole team better Perform data entry and quality reviews in REDCap and Excel Duties and responsibilities expand and increase with each successive level or rank. This description is a summary only and is describing the general level of work being performed, it is not intended to be all-inclusive. The duties of this position may change from time to time and/or based on business need. We reserve the right to add or delete duties and responsibilities at the discretion of the supervisor and/or hiring authority. Work Location: Onsite – this role is expected to work onsite five (5) days per week and is in Aurora, Colorado. Why Join Us: The University of Colorado (CU) is one of the nation’s premier educational and research institutions and is ideally suited to carry out this project. Built as state-of-the-art, the Anschutz Medical Campus (AMC) consists of three zones: an education zone with facilities for training in the medical and health-related fields, a research zone that houses the various graduate programs, and a clinical care zone with the University of Colorado Hospital (UCH) and the Children's Hospital, the CU AMC's primary adult and pediatric hospital partners, nearby. The university is considered by the Carnegie Classification of Institutions of Higher Education to have \"very high research activity\" with a basic classification of Research Universities. UCH, a teaching hospital affiliated with the CU Denver, has a $644 million, 820,000-square-foot facility at the AMC. The Children's Hospital, with 1,400,000 square feet, opened in 2007 to the south of the campus. CU is one of 34 public universities to be a member of the prestigious Association of American Universities. The CU AMC campus is located adjacent to the newly constructed Rocky Mountain Regional VA Medical Center. Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 10/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Entry Level Bachelor's degree U.S. Citizenship or Permanent Resident status (required due to funding restrictions) Intermediate Level Bachelor's degree in a related field (or equivalent professional experience, year for year) At least one (1) year of human clinical research administration experience, including familiarity with research methods, protocols, data collection, and analysis U.S. Citizenship or Permanent Resident status (required due to funding restrictions) Senior Level Bachelor's degree in a related field (or equivalent professional experience, year for year) At least two (2) years of human clinical research administration experience, including familiarity with research methods, protocols, data collection, and analysis U.S. Citizenship or Permanent Resident status (required due to funding restrictions) Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Preferred Qualifications: Entry Level One (1) year of research administration experience, including fundamental knowledge of research methods, protocols, data collection, and analysis. Intermediate Level Master’s degree in science or health related field Two (2) years of research administration experience, including skilled knowledge of research methods, protocols, data collection, and analysis. Experience in REDCap surveys and data entry Strong working knowledge of Good Clinical Practice, Institutional Review Board, Veterans Administration, and Food and Drug Administration regulations Senior Level Master’s degree in science or health related field Four (4) years of research administration experience, including advanced knowledge of research methods, protocols, data collection, and analysis. Proficient experience in REDCap surveys and data entry Related professional experience as manager, supervisor, work leader, staff authority or project/program administrator. You'll Thrive Here If You: Can juggle multiple projects without losing your attention to detail Communicate clearly and confidently with participants, clinical staff, and research teams alike Take personal accountability seriously and enjoy working with a high degree of independence in a fast-paced environment Bring genuine curiosity to your work and care about the science behind what you're doing Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Knowledge and understanding of federal regulations and Good Clinical Practice (GCP) Ability to communicate effectively, both in writing and orally Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with employees at all levels throughout the institution Outstanding customer service skills Ability to interpret and master complex research protocol information Conditions of Employment: Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without requiring sponsorship. We are unable to provide work visa sponsorship or employment authorization for this position now or in the future. How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit all the following document(s): A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position Curriculum vitae / Resume Three to five professional references, including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers . Applications sent via email will not be considered. Questions should be directed to: angel.garcia@cuanschutz.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Screening begins immediately and continues until position is filled. For the best consideration, apply by August 10, 2026. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as Entry Level: $49,899 - $66,865 Intermediate Level: $54,302 - $72,765 Senior Level: $58,705 - $78,665 The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position may be eligible for overtime compensation, depending on the level. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@cuanschutz.edu ​. Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41301&lang=en": {
      "title": "Registered Nurse - Internal Medicine, Cherry Creek",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 1, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: SOM-DEAN DO CPD - PRIM CARE Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Department: Community Practice Job Title: Registered Nurse - Internal Medicine, Cherry Creek Position #: 00853704 – Requisition #:41301 Job Summary: The Registered Nurse (RN) provides high-quality support to physicians and advanced practice providers (APPs) in meeting the operational needs of the practice and the medical needs of the patient. The RN assesses and evaluates patient conditions, and then plans, implements, provides, and documents patient care in a manner that follows professional nursing standards and outlined practices. Key Responsibilities: Escorts patients to and from exam rooms and readies them for physicians. Performs telephone triage, patient education, handling of physician phone calls, and pharmacy calls. Takes vital signs, records medical history/symptoms, and ensures medical chart/lab test results are available and complete. Administers immunizations and minor treatments as prescribed. Responds to patient questions and concerns as a liaison between physician and patient. Reports all test results to the patient as directed by the physician. Work Location: Onsite – this role is expected to work onsite and is located in Cherry Creek, CO . Why Join Us: Community Practice Medicine, housed within the School of Medicine at the University of Colorado, is seeking trained medical professionals to join our growing team. With clinics spanning from Longmont to Castle Rock, we offer a wide variety of opportunities. Specialty areas include, but are not limited to: Orthopedics, Vascular Surgery, OBGYN, Internal Medicine, Urology, Psychiatry, and many more! The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is a public education, clinical, and research facility serving 4,500 students and a world-class medical destination at the forefront of life-changing science, medicine, and healthcare. CU Anschutz offers more than 42 highly rated degree programs through 6 schools and colleges and receives over $500 million in research awards each year. We are the single largest health professions education provider in Colorado, awarding nearly 1,450 degrees annually. Powered by our award-winning faculty, renowned researchers, and a reputation for academic excellence, the CU Anschutz Medical Campus drives innovation from the classroom to the laboratory to the delivery of unparalleled patient care. Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation, and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package, including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 15/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced-rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Entry Level: Graduate of an accredited Nursing program through the Accreditation Commission for Education in Nursing (ACEN) or American Nursing Credentialing Center (ANCC). Intermediate Level: Graduate of an accredited Nursing program through the Accreditation Commission for Education in Nursing (ACEN) or American Nursing Credentialing Center (ANCC). Two (2) years of nursing experience. Senior Level: Graduate of an accredited Nursing program through the Accreditation Commission for Education in Nursing (ACEN) or American Nursing Credentialing Center (ANCC). Four (4) years of nursing experience. Substitution (All Levels): A combination of education and related technical/military/paraprofessional experience may be substituted for a bachelor’s degree on a year-for-year basis. Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Preferred Qualifications (All Levels): Bachelor of Science in Nursing (BSN). One to two (1-2) or more years of job-related/clinic experience. Bilingual, Spanish-speaking. Nursing certification (ANCC) in specialty area. Epic, Kronos, and HealthStream experience. Conditions of Employment (All Levels): Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without requiring sponsorship. We are unable to provide work visa sponsorship or employment authorization for this position now or in the future. Current Basic Life Support (BLS) for Healthcare Providers issued by the American Heart Association or the American Red Cross healthcare provider-level CPR certification. Registered Nurse (RN), State of Colorado. Maintains all required licensure and certifications for the position. Maintains all required continuing education requirements. Must be able to work in person. Must be able to travel to alternate locations as assigned. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities (All Levels): Strong organizational and communication skills. Ability to effectively communicate at all levels, to include physicians, leadership, and staff within the various affiliate organizations (UCH, Children’s Colorado, CU Medicine, CU SOM). Ability to work within large, complex healthcare systems. Ability to analyze and interpret data. Ability to compile complex reports and develop presentations. Ability to compose letters and memorandums. Ability to deal calmly and courteously with people. Ability to deal with stressful situations. Ability to finish tasks in a timely manner. How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to the listed job qualifications and interest in the position Curriculum vitae / Resume Three to five professional references, including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Questions should be directed to: Cristine Gentert, cristine.gentert@cuanschutz.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Immediately and continues until the position is filled. Best consideration will be given to those who apply within one (1) month of the posting date. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as: Entry Level: $69,160 to $80,226 Intermediate Level: $74,347 to $86,243 Senior Level: $79,534 to $93,850 The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position may be eligible for overtime compensation, depending on the level. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans, and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@cuanschutz.edu . Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students, and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine-preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety-sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41300&lang=en": {
      "title": "Medication Dispensing Nurse, LPN I",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 2, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: SOM-PSYCH-ARTS SP/G Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Department: School of Medicine – Department of Psychiatry Job Title: Medication Dispensing Nurse, LPN I Position # 00853700: – Requisition #: 41300 Job Summary: The Medication Dispensing Nurse, LPN I is responsible for performing work related to assessing a patient’s physical and/or mental state, assessing if a patient presents in a state appropriate for substance use disorder (SUD) treatment and/or Medication Assisted Treatment (MAT), as well as dispensing medications, drawing blood from patients, keeping accurate, timely, and clear patient health records, storing controlled substances, and other duties as assigned. This position will require working hours ranging from 5:00am to 5:30pm Monday to Saturday, based on the needs of the agency and not to exceed 40 hours per week. This position will also be required to deliver medication to off-site locations in the greater Metro Denver area. The Medication Dispensing Nurse, LPN I will be assigned to ARTS Adult Outpatient Program clinic locations (or Opioid Treatment Programs), located in Aurora, Arvada, Denver and Sheridan, and may be required to periodically work on the Medication Mobile Unit (MMU), which will operate and provide substance use disorder services in the greater Metro Denver area. This position will report to the Nursing Program Manager of Medication Assisted Treatment and Nursing Programs. Administer medication such as: Methadone, Suboxone, Naltrexone, Antabuse, and extended-release injectable naltrexone to patients. Transport narcotic medication in a manner consistent with DEA, State, and Federal, rules and regulations, while abiding by ARTS policies and procedures to include but not limited to using a lock box. Delivery locations will include correctional facilities, rehabilitation centers, inpatient treatment facilities, or any location deemed appropriate by ARTS. Monitor each patient’s vital signs and health condition. Draw blood for analysis/labs, obtain test results and Administer TB tests. Assess adverse reactions to medications, and issues relating to drug overdose, HIV, and/or HCV and report to the team lead. Handle infectious materials, human blood, or other body fluids according to applicable policy and procedures. Perform other duties as assigned by ARTS AOP Nursing Manager. Key Responsibilities (100%): Administer medication such as: Methadone, Suboxone, Naltrexone, Antabuse, and extended-release injectable naltrexone to patients. Transport narcotic medication in a manner consistent with DEA, State, and Federal, rules and regulations, while abiding by ARTS policies and procedures to include but not limited to using a lock box. Delivery locations will include correctional facilities, rehabilitation centers, inpatient treatment facilities, or any location deemed appropriate by ARTS. Monitor each patient’s vital signs and health condition. Draw blood for analysis/labs, obtain test results and Administer TB tests. Assess adverse reactions to medications, and issues relating to drug overdose, HIV, and/or HCV and report to the team lead. Handle infectious materials, human blood, or other body fluids according to applicable policy and procedures. Perform other duties as assigned by ARTS AOP Nursing Manager. Work Location: Onsite – this role is expected to work onsite and is located in Aurora, Denver, Sheridan, Colorado.. Why Join Us: This position at the University of Colorado/ Addiction Research and Treatment Services (ARTS) provides a unique opportunity for individuals with lived experience and recovery from SUDs to use, in turn, their specialized knowledge and experience to provide care, assistance and support of individuals currently living with SUD. The individual in this position, through their words and actions, will have a direct influence on helping others with SUD to set themselves on a path to recovery and make healthy lifestyle choices. In addition, by joining ARTS, employees will be actively engaged in a supportive, professional, and nurturing environment where individuals with various backgrounds and experiences converge and collaborate to provide an evidence-based, multi-faceted approach to provide the best treatment and care to every patient who comes into care at ARTS clinics. Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 15/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: High school diploma or GED. Must possess and maintain a valid, Licensed Practical Nurse (LPN) or Registered Nurse (RN) license with the Colorado Department of Regulatory Agencies (DORA). Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Preferred Qualifications: Prior work experience with medication assisted treatment. Prior work experience with patients in substance use disorder treatment. Possess and maintain in good standing a valid intravenous (IV) certification. Experience observing, monitoring, and intervening in drug/alcohol treatment. Experience working with patients who are involved with probation, human services, and/or other referral sources. Experience using an electronic patient health record system. Conditions of Employment: Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without requiring sponsorship. We are unable to provide work visa sponsorship or employment authorization for this position now or in the future. Must possess and maintain a valid Colorado Driver's License or be able to obtain one within 30 days of hire. Must agree to, and successfully pass, a fingerprint and criminal background check. ( Note : Required background checks include a review with the Colorado Bureau of Investigation, and the Federal Bureau of Investigation). May be subject to pre-employment, post-accident, post-incident or reasonable suspicion drug and alcohol testing per University Addiction Research and Treatment Services Department Policies. This position may require working on Mondays – Saturdays ranging from 5:00am to 5:30pm, not to exceed 40 hours per week. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Excellent communication and interpersonal skills. Excellent written communication skills, which includes the ability to check for typographical, grammatical, and spelling errors. Ability to effectively manage difficult behaviors. Ability to engage patients in treatment for substance use disorder treatment. Ability to comply with established rules, policies and procedures and meet deadlines. Ability to be open-minded and nonjudgmental. Ability to develop healthy relationships with clients. Ability to establish boundaries with clients. Ability to exercise patient confidentiality. Working knowledge of Clinical Laboratory Improvement Amendments (CLIA) and Health Information Portability and Accountability Act (HIPAA). Ability to establish and maintain effective relationships with patients as well as with employees at all levels throughout the institution. Outstanding customer service skills. Ability to develop rapport with patients in a caring and nurturing manner. Ability to problem-solve and make appropriate decisions, and work under pressure and meet deadlines. How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position Curriculum vitae / Resume Three to five professional references, including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Questions should be directed to: Heidi McKinnon at heidi.mckinnon@cuanschutz.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Applications will be accepted until finalists are identified, but preference will be given to complete applications received by December 30, 2026 . Those who do not apply by this date may or may not be considered. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range (or hiring range) for this position has been established as $42,153 - $50,577. The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position may be eligible for overtime compensation, depending on the level. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@cuanschutz.edu ​. Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41296&lang=en": {
      "title": "Director of Development, Foundation Relations (Principal Professional)",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 1, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: ADM-CHAN Advancement Anschutz Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Department: Office of Advancement Job Title: Director of Development, Foundation Relations (Principal Professional) Position #: 00001243 – Requisition #: 41296 Job Summary: Reporting to the Executive Strategist for Major and Principal Gifts and working in close collaboration with the Office of Grants and Contracts (OGC) and the Office of Research Development and Strategy (ORDS), this full-time, University Staff (non-classified) Director of Development for Foundation Relations serves as the primary strategist, relationship manager, and hands-on fundraiser for a portfolio of foundation partners. The position personally drives and executes all aspects of foundation relations activity, including prospect identification, relationship cultivation, proposal development, solicitation strategy, stewardship, and funder engagement. Operating as the primary owner of foundation fundraising efforts, this role translates institutional priorities into compelling funding opportunities while building sustainable partnerships that increase philanthropic investment in support of CU Anschutz priorities. Supervision Received: Executive Strategist for Major and Principal Gits (pos. 00781435) Supervision Exercised: No direct reports Key Responsibilities: Partnership Development and Strategy – 40% Serve as the primary relationship manager and strategic contact for a portfolio of significant local and regional foundations, personally cultivating, stewarding, and advancing relationships to maximize philanthropic investment. Independently develop and execute comprehensive engagement plans that build robust partnerships with major foundation funders while expanding and diversifying institutional revenue opportunities. Develop and implement comprehensive, tailored strategies for cultivation, solicitation, and long-term stewardship. Develop and maintain a deep understanding and awareness of funding opportunities, institutional priorities, academic programs, and centers of excellence in order to translate these assets into compelling funding opportunities and align them with funders’ interests. Personally conduct high-impact relationship-building activities through calls, visits, presentations, and strategic engagements that lead to strong, sustained partner relationships and proposal invitations. Serve as a primary point of contact (and primary relationship manager) for organizations that wish to partner with CU Anschutz in meaningful ways, facilitating appropriate introductions and exchange of ideas and information that serve to advance campus priorities, as well as the interests of the prospective funder. Partner with stewardship coordinators, faculty, OGC and ORDS staff and others, as necessary, to ensure timely and appropriate stewardship of current and previous institutional funders, consistent with the terms and reporting requirements of grant agreements as well as best practices. Proposal Development, Strategic Writing, and Execution- 60% Serve as the lead architect, writer, and project manager for significant foundation proposals, personally driving the development and submission of high-quality funding requests. Independently develop, write and refine letters of intent, concept papers, proposals, and related fundraising materials, ensuring alignment with university polices and funder interests. Maintain primary ownership and accountability for the timely and accurate completion of proposals, gift and grant agreements, stewardship, and report requirements. Maintain accurate records in the university’s database, ensuring timely contact reports and entity updates. Collaborate with OGC and ORDS on funder strategy, faculty engagement, proposal development, award negotiation, and compliance. Personally identify, assess, and advance institutional funding opportunities by working closely with faculty, hospital relations staff, and campus leaders to align foundation interests with high-priority programs and initiatives. Assist with other duties as assigned to support the team and institutional goals. Work Location: Hybrid – this role is eligible for a hybrid schedule of 3 days per week on campus and as needed for in-person meetings. Why Join Us: Philanthropy brings people together; it’s a driving force in accelerating the pace of discovery, attracting and retaining excellent students and faculty, and delivering world-class prevention and care. At the Office of Advancement at the University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus, we put our passions to work. We have the privilege to collaborate with people who want to make a difference in the world – people who want to make an impact on humanity that may be felt long after they have passed. Our office exists to ensure stakeholders within and outside the university know, value, and support the important work being done on this academic medical campus. Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 15/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree from an accredited institution Minimum of 3 years of professional fundraising experience or experience in related fields like nonprofit administration, public affairs, or business development, including managing funding relationships with individuals, corporations or foundations. A combination of education and related technical/military/paraprofessional experience may be substituted for a bachelor’s degree on a year for year basis. Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Preferred Qualifications: Extensive experience soliciting major gifts of at least $50,000 from foundation funders. Experience coordinating large-scale projects that involve multiple partners and interests. Demonstrated experience in securing 6-7 figure awards in both philanthropy and sponsored research Seven (7) years of successful professional fundraising experience, or experience in related fields. Project Management - Personal computer proficiency required, especially as related to Microsoft Office Products; MS Word, Excel, and PowerPoint; and donor tracking software. Experience working in a higher education and/or medical campus environment and/or relevant experience working in a nonprofit environment as a fundraiser. Conditions of Employment: Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without requiring sponsorship. We are unable to provide work visa sponsorship or employment authorization for this position now or in the future. National travel may be required for partnership development, fundraising events, and conferences. This position requires flexibility in hours, including evenings and weekends for events and meetings. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Demonstrated ability to think strategically while personally executing operational and fundraising activities from concept through completion. Proven success functioning as the primary owner of complex fundraising initiatives with minimal reliance on staff oversight or administrative delegation. Strong project management skills with the ability to independently drive multiple priorities, deadlines, stakeholder relationships, and deliverables simultaneously. Demonstrated ability to translate institutional priorities into actionable fundraising strategies and personally execute those strategies to achieve measurable outcomes. Expert knowledge of foundation relationship building and gift management, including cultivation, stewardship, and solicitation. Expert ability to communicate verbally and in writing and develop and maintain interpersonal relationships. Strong ability to analyze information/situations and solve problems. Solid knowledge of the funding landscape and giving climate for foundation partners. Expert ability to organize and manage multiple projects/tasks simultaneously Must have ability to work independently and collaboratively and adapt to changing priorities. Solid experience in grant writing. Proven ability to foster and build relationships internally and externally. How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position (only use if a cover letter is necessary) Curriculum vitae / Resume Three to five professional references, including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Questions should be directed to: Shannon Palombi – Shannon.Palombi@cuanschutz.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Applications will be accepted until finalists are identified, but preference will be given to complete applications received by October 14, 2026. Those who do not apply by this date may or may not be considered. Hiring department will need to notify their Talent Acquisition Consultant when they want to have the advertisements removed for the posting. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as $103,497 - $108,000 The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position may be eligible for overtime compensation, depending on the level. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@cuanschutz.edu ​. Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41286&lang=en": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Fellow",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 1, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: SOM-MED-ONC GENERAL OPERATIONS Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Department: Medical Oncology Job Title: Postdoctoral Fellow Position #00853634 – Requisition #41286 Job Summary: The Division of Medical Oncology at the University of Colorado School of Medicine invites applications for a Postdoctoral Fellowship in Oncology Research in the Davila Laboratory. The overarching goal of this fellowship is to prepare outstanding trainees for independent research careers, with a focus on developing next-generation cellular therapies for cancer. The fellowship consists of two integrated components: scholarly research (85%) and education/training (15%). The postdoctoral fellow will play a central role in experimental design, execution, data analysis, and interpretation, and will present findings regularly in one-on-one meetings, laboratory meetings, and multidisciplinary research forums. This position reports to Eduardo Davila, PhD, Professor in the Division of Medical Oncology and a member of the Comprehensive Cancer Center. Administrative and human resources support are provided by the Division of Medical Oncology. Key Responsibilities : 75% – Primary Research Design, initiate, and execute independent and collaborative research projects Perform rigorous literature review, data analysis, and interpretation with guidance from the PI Develop and validate TCR-T or Tumor Infiltrating Lymphocyte cellular therapy Conduct in vitro and in vivo studies, including mouse models Collaborate closely with lab members and local, national, and international collaborators Maintain clear, transparent, and reproducible documentation of all research activities, including well-annotated and shareable code where applicable 10% – Communication and Dissemination Present research progress at lab meetings, project meetings, and individual PI meetings Prepare abstracts and present findings at local, national, and international scientific conferences Write and publish manuscripts as first or co-author in peer-reviewed journals Actively pursue individual fellowship and career development awards 5% – Training and Mentorship Develop and document experimental workflows and protocols Train and mentor graduate students and research staff in relevant techniques 5% – Career Development Participate in career development seminars, workshops, and networking opportunities Develop and review an Individual Development Plan (IDP) annually with the PI 5% – Patient and Community Engagement Communicate research progress to patient advocacy groups in accessible formats Participate, when appropriate, in public-facing educational or outreach efforts Work Location: Onsite – this role is expected to work onsite and is located in Aurora, CO. Why Join Us: CU Anschutz is an academic medical campus at the forefront of transformative education, science, medicine, and healthcare. From heart disease to cancer, Alzheimer’s to COVID-19, our campus and collaborative partnerships advance the life-changing discoveries of tomorrow. We educate 4,500 degree-seeking future health professionals and see over 2 million patient visits annually with $757 million in annual research grants. In the Department of Medicine alone, we have more than 1,000 faculty, 192 residents and 200 fellows distributed in 14 divisions, our clinical, research and academic programs attract the best providers, investigators, staff, and students from around the world who are transforming the future of health care. In Medical Oncology, our faculty are acknowledged both nationally and internationally for their innovative work in cancer research, resulting in regular collaborations with a variety of institutions globally in addition to collaborations with colleagues within our own division and institution. The focus of our researchers is centered around the development and application of experimental therapeutics and targeted agents for future cancer patient treatment as well as advancing patient-centered care for those facing cancer. Innovative strides continue to be made in cancer research each day because of the continued passion and dedication by our faculty in the fight against cancer. Why work for the University? The University of Colorado offers a comprehensive benefits package. To see what benefits are available for Post-Doctoral Fellows, please visit: · Payroll & Benefits Orientation for Post-Doctoral Fellows | University of Colorado (cu.edu) · benefits guide cover-post-doc-2024 (cu.edu) Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. PhD in biological sciences or a related field, with emphasis on cancer biology and/or cellular therapy Demonstrated proficiency in scientific communication, including at least one first-author peer-reviewed publication and oral presentations at scientific meetings Preferred Qualifications: Experience with R, Python, or similar programming languages Experience in flow cytometry Prior work in translational or immuno-oncology research Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Experience developing and executing in vitro and in vivo models of cellular therapies Experience designing, cloning, and validating cellular therapy constructs Proficiency with high-parameter flow cytometry Familiarity with bioinformatics workflows (e.g., single-cell RNA-seq analysis) Strong background in cell culture, molecular cloning, viral transduction, and molecular biology (western blot, PCR, imaging, immunoprecipitation) Strong interest in cancer cell therapeutics How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): 1. A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position 2. Curriculum vitae / Resume 3. Three professional references including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers . Questions should be directed to: Stephanie Fields, stephanie.n.fields@cuanschutz.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Applications will be accepted until finalists are identified, but preference will be given to complete applications received by October 15, 2026 . Those who do not apply by this date may or may not be considered. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as HIRING RANGE: $ 63,480 - $66,000 The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation unless it is non-exempt. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: The University of Colorado (CU) is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@ucdenver.edu ​. Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=40563&lang=en": {
      "title": "Pediatric Nurse Practitioner (PNP) Open Rank-Instructor, Sr. Instructor, Assistant, Associate, Professor",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 1, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: CON-DEAN ADMINISTRATION Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Department: College of Nursing Job Title: Pediatric Nurse Practitioner (PNP) Open Rank-Instructor, Sr. Instructor, Assistant, Associate, Professor Position #: 00811620 – Requisition #: 40563 Job Summary: The University of Colorado, College of Nursing, is seeking a Pediatric Nurse Practitioner (PNP) for a full-time (0.90 FTE) benefitted position at CU Sheridan Health Services (SHS), a Federally Qualified Health Center (FQHC) located in southwest Denver, CO (zip code: 80236). This position will primarily provide integrated primary care in the pediatrics department with potential clinical coverage at one of our community partner practice sites. This position is clinic based as a health care provider and is hired at the level of Instructor / Senior Instructor / Assistant Professor of Clinical Practice (Open Rank) in the Clinical Practice Faculty Series within the College of Nursing. Clinic Description: SHS is a nurse-managed FQHC, funded through the Health Resources and Services Administration Bureau of Primary Healthcare; and is a collaborative effort between the College of Nursing and the Sheridan School District. The clinic serves community health needs primarily for residents of Arapahoe, Denver, Adams, and Jefferson counties. Sheridan Health Services is located in southwest Denver on the Fort Logan campus and provides services to adults and children, 65% of whom identify as Latinx, and 42% of whom are best served in another language, with Spanish being the predominant second language. Services offered include primary care across the lifespan; perinatal, gynecology, dentistry, pharmacy, behavioral health, and outpatient substance use disorder treatment. Sheridan Health Services is a Patient-Centered Medical Home and upholds a model of care that places the patient at the center, incorporating the values and beliefs of the patient in all decision-making. We extend the reach of the clinic by providing services to our community partners in the Sheridan School District and Urban Peak. For more information, please visit https://nursing.cuanschutz.edu/patient-care/sheridan-health-services Supervision Received: Work is performed independently under the supervision of the APN Clinical Lead for Pediatrics. Supervision Exercised: Student supervision is required during clinical placements. Examples of Work Performed: Provides acute and chronic primary care for the clinic’s pediatric populations Performs the full scope of Nurse Practitioner duties, to include comprehensive physical examination, diagnosis, evaluation & treatment of both chronic and acute illness. Refers to specialists when indicated. Provides culturally & linguistically appropriate services to patients from diverse backgrounds in an underserved, resource-limited setting Coordinates patient care needs with other care team members, including RN Case Managers, Referral Coordinators, Behavioral Health Team members and Pharmacy Team members. Provides individualized client teaching and counseling utilizing current, evidence-based guidelines. Provides health education to patients, students, families, and/or community health partners Collaborates on quality improvement Initiatives under the direction of the Pediatric Clinical Lead and/or Clinical Director Improves and supports care delivery both within the service line and clinic-wide, by participating in programmatic planning, team-based huddles and integrated or all-staff meetings as requested by the Pediatric Clinical Lead and/or Clinical Director Implements and upholds evidence-based policies & procedures Functions as a clinical preceptor and/or clinical instructor for health professions students. Participates in after-hours call in rotation with the other providers on the team Uphold compliance with university and professional policies/procedures. Maintains electronic health record documentation in compliance with accepted standards, in keeping with the policies & procedures of the clinic. Meet rigorous standards for documentation, and complete notes, referrals and follow-ups in a timely manner. Performs other duties as assigned. Maintains all necessary licenses, certifications, credentialing materials and other required documents as outlined by the Office of Clinical and Community Affairs at the College of Nursing. Work Location: Onsite – this role is expected to work onsite and located in southwest Denver, Colorado. Why Join Us: CU Nursing is an amazing place to be. We have the distinct advantage of being a part of a huge medical campus with three incredible hospitals – the VA, the nationally ranked University of Colorado Hospital, and the Children’s Hospital Colorado where our nursing students and faculty learn every day. From our beginning 125 years ago as part of the School of Medicine at CU Boulder to our current home at the Anschutz Medical Campus, the college has been a recognized leader in nursing education (ranked #10 in online MS graduate programs by U.S. News & World Report 2023). Our faculty, students and staff have been instrumental in shaping the profession of nursing and teaching the next generation of nurses while treating patients in our own nurse-led clinics. Be a part of an innovative, dynamic, diverse, and exciting workplace -- helping make great things happen. Join us in our quest to boldly transform health together. The University of Colorado offers a comprehensive benefits package that includes health insurance, life insurance, retirement plans, tuition benefits, ECO pass, paid time off – vacation, sick, holiday and more. To see what benefits are available, please visit: https://nursing.cuanschutz.edu/about/careers/benefits . Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package including: · Medical: Multiple plan options · Dental: Multiple plan options · Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision · Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay · Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year (based on percentage of time) · Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) · Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) · Holiday Days: 11/year · Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses · ECO Pass: Reduced rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. This is an open rank position and could be categorized as Instructor, Senior Instructor, or Assistant Professor based on experience and qualifications as indicated below: Instructor: · Graduate degree in nursing from an accredited institution · Current board certification as a PNP · Current RN, RXN, and APN licensures in good standing (any state) o Must have CO licensures by date of hire. Could be working toward CO clinical licenses during application process and registered with DORA-Department of Regulatory Agencies. o Please review DORA’s Nursing Licensing Guide for detailed requirements: https://drive.google.com/file/d/1XUWVoJSKm06kbhiH-WBNJ8OqolFRmXwD/view Senior Instructor: · Graduate degree in nursing from an accredited institution · Current board certification as a PNP · Current RN, RXN, and APN licensures in good standing (any state) o Must have CO licensures by date of hire. Could be working toward CO clinical licenses during application process and registered with DORA-Department of Regulatory Agencies. o Please review DORA’s Nursing Licensing Guide for detailed requirements: https://drive.google.com/file/d/1XUWVoJSKm06kbhiH-WBNJ8OqolFRmXwD/view · Demonstrated leadership in area of practice. · Demonstrated experience collaborating with academic colleagues and students in practice activities. Assistant Professor: · Doctoral degree in nursing from an accredited institution · Current board certification as a PNP · Current RN, RXN, and APN licensures in good standing (any state) o Must have CO licensures by date of hire. Could be working toward CO clinical licenses during application process and registered with DORA-Department of Regulatory Agencies. o Please review DORA’s Nursing Licensing Guide for detailed requirements: https://drive.google.com/file/d/1XUWVoJSKm06kbhiH-WBNJ8OqolFRmXwD/view · Demonstrated leadership in area of practice. · Demonstrated experience collaborating with academic colleagues and students in practice activities. Preferred Qualifications: · Experience utilizing bilingual skills (Spanish/English) at a conversation level in a clinical setting · Current DEA licenses and full prescriptive authority · Experience working with population-based outcomes · Experienced clinical preceptor · Experience working with marginalized populations · One or more years of advanced practice experience Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: · Considerable degree of independent judgment and autonomy in practice. · Clinical expertise in pediatric primary care · Willingness and ability to work in an integrated care setting, with a high degree of teamwork and collaboration · Ability to use computer and clinic software, and to document in the Electronic Health Record (EHR) with thoroughness and accuracy. · Exceptional interpersonal and communication skills to work effectively with patients, their families, and other members of the health care team · Excellent knowledge of and ability to perform clinical teaching · Ability to remain credentialed by the health plans and ensure credentialing materials stay current. · Ability to effectively develop and promote practice through participation in marketing and patient recruitment · Ability to take one week-at-a-time on-call in a rotation schedule. · Availability of working evenings and weekends as needed. · Ability to handle average nurse practitioner caseload How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): 1. A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position 2. Curriculum vitae / Resume 3. Five professional references including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers . Questions should be directed to: CON.HR@UCDenver.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Applications will be accepted until finalists are identified, but preference will be given to complete applications received by October 14th, 2026 . Those who do not apply by this date may or may not be considered. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as: Clinical Instructor - $43.46 to $48.90/Hour Clinical Sr. Instructor - $43.90 - $49.39/Hour Assistant Professor - $44.33 - $49.87/Hour The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation unless it is non-exempt. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: The University of Colorado (CU) is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@ucdenver.edu ​. Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41290&lang=en": {
      "title": "Manager of Planning and Facilities",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 2, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: SOM-DEAN DO ADMINISTRATION Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Department: School of Medicine, Dean’s Office Job Title: Manager of Planning and Facilities Position #: 00698756 – Requisition #: 41290 Job Summary: The Manager of Planning & Facilities for the School of Medicine (School) at CU Anschutz will be assigned projects on the CU Anschutz campus, acting as a resource and subject matter expert for all departments, divisions, sections, Centers, and Programs within the School of Medicine. The Manager is typically assigned a project at conception and will manage coordination of the project through all phases of planning, design, construction, close-out, and occupancy. Project management may be executed independently or in collaboration with the Facilities Management team(s). The Manager may manage several projects at various stages of the project life-cycle depending on project type, volume, and needs. Throughout the course of a project, the Manager will work with internal University clients, departments, stakeholders, Facilities Building Maintenance and Operations, and University Service Providers, such as the Office of Institutional Planning, EH&S, Office of Information Technology, University Police, Electronic Security, and Grants and Contracts, as appropriate. The position will develop strong internal relationships with CU Anschutz Facilities Management departments, including Projects, Construction Services, and Fire and Life Safety, and strong external relationships with architectural and engineering firms, consultants, and contractors. This position will have opportunities to serve on project oversight committees, design team and contractor selection committees, and internal department committees. This position will also assist with special projects related to large renovation and construction projects, space utilization, and efficiency. In conjunction with the SOM Director of Facilities and Planning and the Senior Director for the Office of Research, this position will be responsible for the development, implementation, and management of the budget for the Office of Research. Key Responsibilities: Planning, Projects, and Space Management (40%) Provide project oversight and management for SOM Dean’s Office-managed or funded projects, including attending meetings, reviewing drawings, participating in consultant selection committees, and budget review. Design and manage small project renovations and test fits, monitor schedules, and manage contractors or consultants as necessary to deliver project(s) on time. Create graphic documents and floor plans in programs like Photoshop, PowerPoint, and AutoCAD. Assist with space utilization projects including managing data, compiling data, and strategic planning based on findings. Act as badging and access approver for the SOM Dean’s Office. Approve and track key requests for the SOM Dean’s Office. Manage planning, design, construction, and close-out phases of assigned projects. Coordinate with contractors, consultants, and stakeholders. Review project scopes, drawings, budgets, and schedules. Support space request and reassignment processes. Strategic Planning and Reporting (30%) Support strategic space and facilities planning through data collection, analysis, and reporting. Collaborate with SOM units, programs, and centers to collect, update, and review data in campus space tracking programs like WebSpace and Archibus, annually and in real time. Act as a SOM point of contact and liaison for all SOM reservable spaces in EMS for the Office of Information Technology Scheduling Services team. Assist with space utilization metrics and reporting processes. Cross-Functional Engagement and Operations (20%) Act as a subject matter expert and resource for School of Medicine units related to projects and planning, Work Order processes, design and construction resources, move coordination, and furniture procurement processes. Act as a subject matter expert and resource for School of Medicine units related to facilities and maintenance, including custodial services and security/access. Coordinate moves, furniture procurement, and workspace setup. Act as liaison with campus service providers. Financial and Administrative Support (10%) Oversee the review and approval process (when needed) for all School of Medicine Work Order requests for scope, standards, and fiscal responsibility. Negotiate costs of services with facilities, consultants, contractors, and/or suppliers. Assist with budget tracking and project costs. Support procurement and contract coordination. Work Location: Hybrid – this role is eligible for a hybrid schedule of three (3) days per week on campus and as needed for in-person meetings. Why Join Us: The University of Colorado School of Medicine offers comprehensive, lifelong, interdisciplinary learning for health care professionals. With state-of-the-art laboratories for discovery and innovation, a commitment to decreasing health disparities and increasing health equity, and faculty who provide world-class clinical care, the CU School of Medicine is transforming the health care landscape. Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation, and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package, including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 15/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced-rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: A bachelor’s degree in business, architecture or engineering, management, project management, communications, information systems, or a directly related field from an accredited institution. Substitution: A combination of education and related technical/paraprofessional experience may be substituted for the bachelor’s degree on a year-for-year basis. Three to five (3-5) years of professional and progressive facilities planning, space management, or facilities operations experience. Two (2) years of supervisory experience required, with a demonstrated ability to lead and develop staff. Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Preferred Qualifications: Five or more (5+) years of progressive facilities planning, space management, or facilities operations experience. Experience working with floor plans, space planning, and AutoCAD. Experience in an academic medical center, healthcare, research, or higher education environment preferred. Experience developing budgets and managing project finances. Conditions of Employment: Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without requiring sponsorship. We are unable to provide work visa sponsorship or employment authorization for this position now or in the future. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Proven ability to manage multiple competing priorities in a complex, fast-paced environment. Strong analytical, organizational, communication, and stakeholder management skills. Knowledge of building codes, ADA requirements, and facilities-related regulatory standards preferred. Knowledge of facilities management and construction processes. Knowledge of business and administration processes. Strong project management and organizational skills. Ability to analyze data and interpret floor plans and architectural drawings. Proficiency with space systems and design tools. Strong communication and interpersonal skills. Strong organizational skills with the ability to manage complex projects. How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position Curriculum vitae / Resume Three to five professional references, including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Questions should be directed to: Vanessa Valesquez, VANESSA.VALESQUEZ@CUANSCHUTZ.EDU Screening of Applications Begins: Immediately and continues until 10/15 from the posting date. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as $82,867 to $111,041. The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position may be eligible for overtime compensation, depending on the level. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans, and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@cuanschutz.edu . Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students, and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine-preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety-sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41285&lang=en": {
      "title": "Accounting Operations Lead or Accounting Operations Program Manager",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 1, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: ADM AVCFC Administratn Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Department: Financial Services, Finance Office Job Title: Accounting Operations Lead or Accounting Operations Program Manager Position #: 673907 – Requisition #: 41285 Job Summary: The Finance Office is seeking a collaborative, analytical, and customer-focused accounting professional to join our team. This position provides advanced technical accounting leadership and professionally oversees key accounting operations within the Finance Office. At the principal level, this role will act as a subject matter expert for the Department and lead campus accounting support functions, including chartfield oversight; reviewing and approving complex accounting transactions; overseeing selected financial reporting, reconciliations, and close activities; and ensuring compliance with generally accepted accounting principles, Governmental Accounting Standards Board requirements, university policies, and internal controls. This role serves as a trusted advisor to campus departments, strengthens service delivery through training and process improvement, and supervises one Finance and Accounting Professional. At the program manager level, this role will manage the day-to-day accounting functions and operations of the Finance Office. This includes managing chartfield governance, developing and implementing operational workflows, policies and processes, and independently supervising the accounting operations team. In collaboration with the Assistant Director, this role will make informed recommendations to leadership and effectively translate Departmental strategy into relevant long and short-term objectives for accounting operations . Key Responsibilities: Lead and oversee the campus accounting support function, serving as the primary resource for accounting guidance, issue resolution, stakeholder consultation, and service delivery. Review and approve complex accounting transactions, journal entries, chartfield requests, and organizational structure changes to ensure compliance with GAAP, GASB requirements, university policies, and internal controls. Manage financial reporting, reconciliations, and analysis activities by investigating discrepancies, resolving complex accounting issues, monitoring financial activity, and ensuring the accuracy of financial records. Coordinate and perform month-end, quarter-end, and fiscal year-end close activities, including account analysis, accrual review, financial reporting, sales tax reporting, and resolution of outstanding items. Provide technical accounting expertise and consultative support to campus departments by interpreting accounting requirements, advising on financial matters, and delivering training on accounting policies and procedures. Supervise and develop accounting staff through coaching, work prioritization, performance management, quality review, and professional development support. Identify and implement opportunities to improve accounting processes, strengthen financial controls, enhance reporting capabilities, and leverage technology and automation to increase operational efficiency and service excellence. Work Location: Hybrid – this role is eligible for a hybrid schedule of 2 days per week on campus and as needed for in-person meetings. Why Join Us: The Finance Office offers an opportunity to make a meaningful impact in a collaborative, mission-driven environment. As an Accounting Operations Professional, you'll work on complex accounting and financial management activities, partner with stakeholders across campus, and help shape processes that support effective decision-making and responsible stewardship of university resources. Join a team that values expertise, innovation, and continuous improvement while providing opportunities to expand your technical accounting knowledge, develop leadership skills, and contribute to initiatives that enhance financial operations across the university. Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 15/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Principal Professional Level (Lead): Bachelor’s degree in accounting or a directly related field from an accredited institution. Substitution : A combination of education and related technical/military/paraprofessional experience may be substituted for a bachelor’s degree on a year for year basis. Three (3) years of professional accounting experience which includes financial reconciliations, financial analysis and reporting, journal-entry review, and month-end and fiscal year-end close activities. Program Manager Level: Bachelor’s degree in accounting or a directly related field from an accredited institution. Substitution : A combination of education and related technical/military/paraprofessional experience may be substituted for a bachelor’s degree on a year for year basis. Five (5) years of professional accounting experience including financial reconciliations, financial analysis and reporting, journal-entry review, complex problem resolution, and month-end and fiscal year-end close activities. One (1) year of professional experience supervising employees, including assigning and reviewing work, coaching staff, and supporting performance and professional development. Applicants for both levels must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Preferred Qualifications : Professional accounting experience in higher education, government, the public sector, or another complex organization. Experience with an enterprise resource planning system such as PeopleSoft, Workday, Oracle, SAP, or a comparable financial system. Experience using financial reporting, business intelligence, or data analytics tools. Experience identifying and implementing process improvements, strengthened controls, or workflow automation. Experience providing consultative financial guidance and customer support to diverse stakeholder groups. Prior experience or familiarity with University of Colorado financial systems, reporting tools, and administrative policies. Conditions of Employment: Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without requiring sponsorship. We are unable to provide work visa sponsorship or employment authorization for this position now or in the future. Knowledge, Skills, and Competencies: Advanced Microsoft Excel skills, including PivotTables, lookup functions, data analysis, and reporting. Familiarity with University of Colorado financial systems, reporting tools, and administrative policies. Advanced knowledge of generally accepted accounting principles, fund accounting, Governmental Accounting Standards Board requirements, financial reporting, and internal controls. Strong analytical and critical-thinking skills, including the ability to identify trends, investigate discrepancies, assess risk, and resolve complex financial issues. Ability to communicate complex financial information clearly and effectively in writing and verbally to financial and non-financial audiences. Ability to build collaborative working relationships with employees and stakeholders at all levels of the institution. Responsive, solutions-oriented customer service that balances stakeholder needs with accounting standards, university policy, and internal-control requirements. Sound judgment, discretion, accountability, and the ability to make well-supported decisions in areas of technical complexity. Strong organizational skills, attention to detail, and the ability to prioritize competing responsibilities and meet deadlines. Ability to learn and effectively use new software, systems, reporting tools, and business processes. Commitment to continuous improvement, responsible use of technology, and an inclusive, collaborative, and respectful workplace. How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position. Curriculum vitae / Resume Three to five professional references, including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Questions should be directed to: Melodie Proffitt, melodie.proffitt@cuanschutz.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Applications will be accepted until finalists are identified, but preference will be given to complete applications received by 10/15/26. Those who do not apply by this date may or may not be considered. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as: Accounting Operations Lead (Principal Professional ): $64,336 - $78,000 Accounting Operations Program Manager : $67,133 - $78,000 The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position may be eligible for overtime compensation, depending on the level. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@cuanschutz.edu ​. Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41291&lang=en": {
      "title": "Instructor - Genetic Counselor",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 1, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: SOM-PEDS Genetics & Metabolism Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Department of Pediatrics | Section of Genetics & Metabolism Job Title: Instructor – Genetic Counselor Position #: 00826660 – Requisition #:41291 Job Summary: This position provides genetic counseling services for clinical patients with genetic and metabolic diseases to the population of the States of Colorado. It is associated with Children's Hospital Colorado but also serves the University of Colorado Hospital on the Anschutz Medical Campus, as well as several affiliated community hospitals throughout the State. The individual hired in this position will have an academic home in the Section of Genetics and Metabolism but will work primarily in the clinical operations of the Section of Developmental Pediatrics. They will report to both Section Heads, with administrative supervision provided by Genetics & Metabolism and clinical (and if pertinent, research) supervision from the Head of the Section of Developmental Pediatrics or their delegate. The individual will work collaboratively with other faculty and care team members. The successful candidate will join a group of approximately 30 genetic counselors who work with both medical genetics and specialists in other areas, including regional satellite clinics. Key Responsibilities: The duties and responsibilities of the position include, but are not limited to: Participation in funded research activities. Provide outpatient and, potentially, inpatient genetic counseling for known or suspected genetic disorders. Share on-call responsibilities with the other GC faculty in their clinical group. Participate in the education of genetic counseling graduate students, residents, medical students, and fellows. Genetic counseling support of various specialty clinics. · Work Location: Onsite – this role is expected to work onsite and is located in Aurora, CO Why Join Us: The University of Colorado Anschutz is a public education, clinical, and research facility serving 4,500 students and is a world-class medical destination at the forefront of life-changing science, medicine, and healthcare. CU Anschutz offers more than 42 highly rated degree programs through 6 schools and colleges and receives over $757 million in research awards each year. We are the single largest health professions education provider in Colorado, awarding nearly 1,450 degrees annually. Powered by our award-winning faculty, renowned researchers, and a reputation for academic excellence, the CU Anschutz Medical Campus drives innovation from the classroom to the laboratory to the delivery of unparalleled patient care. Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year (based on percentage of time) Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 11/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. · Graduated from an accredited genetic counseling program · ABGC board certified or Board eligible with board certification attained within 10 months of graduation Condition of Employment: · Must successfully pass a drug test through Children’s Hospital Colorado · Must be willing and able to pass a national criminal background check *For questions regarding Children’s Hospital drug testing requirements, please contact Children’s Human Resources at 720-777-8598. Some positions may require testing if access to Children’s Hospital or their systems is needed at any time during employment with the University. If drug testing is required, it will be listed in the job posting. Preferred Qualifications: · ABGC Board Certified with one-year relevant experience · Pediatric practice experience · 1 year experience involved in Human Subjects Research · Certification of training for Human Subjects Research (CITI, or equivalent) · Experience working with patients and families with genetic causes of autism, epilepsy, and/or developmental disabilities Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: · Knowledge of standard inpatient and outpatient clinical operations and procedures. · Ability to develop and present educational information to patients as well as to professionals. · Ability to provide genetic counseling, and technical information in a comprehensive, understandable, nondirective manner to patients and families. · Ability to work independently as well as serving as a team member. · Ability to gather data and prepare reports. · Skilled in communication, both oral and written. · Skilled in establishing priorities. · Requires ability to travel via car to outreach clinics. · Ability to develop collaborative or independent How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): 1. A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position 2. Curriculum vitae / Resume 3. Five professional references including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers . Questions should be directed to: katherine.2.copeland@cuanschutz.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Immediately and continues until position is filled. For best consideration, apply by December 15, 2026. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as HIRING RANGE: $80,000 - $94,000 The above hiring range represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation unless it is non-exempt. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: The University of Colorado (CU) is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@ucdenver.edu ​. Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41284&lang=en": {
      "title": "Registered Nurse - Oncology, Highlands Ranch (Part-time, 0.8 FTE)",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 1, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: SOM-DEAN DO CPD - MEDICINE Schedule: Part-time University of Colorado Anschutz Department: Community Practice Job Title: Registered Nurse - Oncology, Highlands Ranch (Part-time, 0.8 FTE) Position #: 00853682 – Requisition #: 41284 Job Summary: The Registered Nurse (RN) provides high-quality support to physicians and advanced practice providers (APPs) in meeting the operational needs of the practice and the medical needs of the patient. The RN assesses and evaluates patient conditions, and then plans, implements, provides, and documents patient care in a manner that follows professional nursing standards and outlined practices. Key Responsibilities: Escorts patients to and from exam rooms and readies them for physicians. Performs telephone triage, patient education, handling of physician phone calls, and pharmacy calls. Takes vital signs, records medical history/symptoms, and ensures medical chart/lab test results are available and complete. Administers immunizations and minor treatments as prescribed. Responds to patient questions and concerns as a liaison between physician and patient. Reports all test results to the patient as directed by the physician. Work Location: Onsite – this role is expected to work onsite and is located in Highlands Ranch, CO. Why Join Us: Community Practice Medicine, housed within the School of Medicine at the University of Colorado, is seeking trained medical professionals to join our growing team. With clinics spanning from Longmont to Castle Rock, we offer a wide variety of opportunities. Specialty areas include, but are not limited to: Orthopedics, Vascular Surgery, OBGYN, Internal Medicine, Urology, Psychiatry, and many more! The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is a public education, clinical, and research facility serving 4,500 students and a world-class medical destination at the forefront of life-changing science, medicine, and healthcare. CU Anschutz offers more than 42 highly rated degree programs through 6 schools and colleges and receives over $500 million in research awards each year. We are the single largest health professions education provider in Colorado, awarding nearly 1,450 degrees annually. Powered by our award-winning faculty, renowned researchers, and a reputation for academic excellence, the CU Anschutz Medical Campus drives innovation from the classroom to the laboratory to the delivery of unparalleled patient care. Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation, and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package, including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 15/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced-rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Entry Level: Graduate of an accredited Nursing program through the Accreditation Commission for Education in Nursing (ACEN) or American Nursing Credentialing Center (ANCC). Intermediate Level: Graduate of an accredited Nursing program through the Accreditation Commission for Education in Nursing (ACEN) or American Nursing Credentialing Center (ANCC). Two (2) years of nursing experience. Senior Level: Graduate of an accredited Nursing program through the Accreditation Commission for Education in Nursing (ACEN) or American Nursing Credentialing Center (ANCC). Four (4) years of nursing experience. Substitution (All Levels): A combination of education and related technical/military/paraprofessional experience may be substituted for a bachelor’s degree on a year-for-year basis. Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Preferred Qualifications (All Levels): Bachelor of Science in Nursing (BSN). One to two (1-2) or more years of job-related/clinic experience. Bilingual, Spanish-speaking. Nursing certification (ANCC) in specialty area. Epic, Kronos, and HealthStream experience. Conditions of Employment (All Levels): Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without requiring sponsorship. We are unable to provide work visa sponsorship or employment authorization for this position now or in the future. Current Basic Life Support (BLS) for Healthcare Providers issued by the American Heart Association or the American Red Cross healthcare provider-level CPR certification. Registered Nurse (RN), State of Colorado. Maintains all required licensure and certifications for the position. Maintains all required continuing education requirements. Must be able to work in person. Must be able to travel to alternate locations as assigned. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities (All Levels): Strong organizational and communication skills. Ability to effectively communicate at all levels, including physicians, leadership, and staff within the various affiliate organizations (UCH, Children’s Colorado, CU Medicine, CU SOM). Ability to work within large, complex healthcare systems. Ability to analyze and interpret data. Ability to compile complex reports and develop presentations. Ability to compose letters and memorandums. Ability to deal calmly and courteously with people. Ability to deal with stressful situations. Ability to finish tasks in a timely manner. How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to the listed job qualifications and interest in the position Curriculum vitae / Resume Three to five professional references, including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Questions should be directed to: Emma Porter, Emma.Porter@cuanschutz.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Immediately and continues until the position is filled. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as (calculated for 0.8 FTE): Entry Level: $55,328 to $64,181 Intermediate Level: $ 59,478 to $68,994 Senior Level: $ 63,627 to $75,080 The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position may be eligible for overtime compensation, depending on the level. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans, and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@cuanschutz.edu . Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students, and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine-preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety-sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41283&lang=en": {
      "title": "Quality & Safety Specialist (Full- or Part-time)",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 1, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: CON-DEAN ADMINISTRATION Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Department: College of Nursing Job Title: Quality & Safety Specialist (Full- or Part-time) Position #: 00853678 – Requisition #: 41283 Job Summary: This position provides professional support for clinical operations, quality improvement, and program management activities. Functions include independently coordinating and implementing quality and performance improvement initiatives; supporting clinical programs and service delivery; monitoring and analyzing operational, quality, and patient care metrics; facilitating regulatory and accreditation compliance; developing and maintaining policies, procedures, and workflows; managing program implementation and evaluation; supporting clinical teams in achieving organizational goals; and coordinating training, communication, and continuous improvement efforts to enhance patient care, safety, efficiency, and outcomes. Positions may also serve as liaisons among clinical, administrative, academic, and community partners to advance strategic priorities and operational excellence. Examples of Duties Performed: Assist with and support the day-to-day operations of quality improvement and program implementation initiatives. Adhere to clinical practice standards, evidence-based practice, and established policies and procedures. Assist Team Leads, Supervisors, and/or management with creation and implementation of processes and procedures and quality improvement initiatives. Act as a project manager on multiple quality improvement/program implementation initiatives or grant-funded initiatives. Assist and train junior team members. Assist with identifying issues related to operational efficiency and share results with leadership. Support the Quality and Safety Program Administrator to coordinate quality improvement and performance improvement initiatives. Collect, analyze, and report clinical, operational, and quality performance data. Monitor, in collaboration with the leadership team, organizational quality metrics, benchmarks, and key performance indicators. Support program planning, implementation, evaluation, continuous improvement, and project implementation activities. Collaborate with colleagues to develop, revise, and implement policies, procedures, and standard operating workflows. Coordinate regulatory, accreditation, and compliance activities, including audit preparation and follow-up. Facilitate quality, safety, and program management committees and workgroups. Conduct chart reviews, workflow assessments, and process improvement analyses. Prepare reports, dashboards, presentations, and recommendations for leadership, governing boards, and external stakeholders. Support strategic planning, project management, and organizational change initiatives. Coordinate staff education, training, and competency-related activities to support quality and operational goals and grant deliverables. Collaborate with clinical, administrative, academic, and community partners to improve care delivery and patient outcomes. Support population health, patient experience, risk management, and care coordination initiatives. Contribute to reporting requirements as applicable. Monitor project timelines, deliverables, and outcomes to ensure achievement of organizational objectives. This description is a summary only and describes the general level of work being performed; it is not intended to be all-inclusive. The duties of this position may change from time to time and/or based on business need. We reserve the right to add or delete duties and responsibilities at the discretion of the supervisor and/or hiring authority. Work Location: Hybrid – this role is eligible for a hybrid schedule of three (3 ) days per week on campus and as needed for in-person meetings. Why Join Us: CU Nursing is an amazing place to be. We have the distinct advantage of being a part of a huge medical campus with three incredible hospitals – the VA, the nationally ranked University of Colorado Hospital, and the Children’s Hospital Colorado where our nursing students and faculty learn every day. From our beginning 125 years ago as part of the School of Medicine at CU Boulder to our current home at the Anschutz Medical Campus, the college has been a recognized leader in nursing education (ranked #10 in online MS graduate programs by U.S. News & World Report 2023). Our faculty, students, and staff have been instrumental in shaping the profession of nursing and teaching the next generation of nurses while treating patients in our own nurse-led clinics. Be a part of an innovative, dynamic, diverse, and exciting workplace -- helping make great things happen. Join us in our quest to boldly transform health together. Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation, and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package, including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 15/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced-rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree from an accredited institution. Substitution: A combination of education and related technical/paraprofessional experience may be substituted for the bachelor’s degree on a year-for-year basis. Two (2) years of experience leading quality improvement and/or program implementation projects in health care settings. Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Preferred Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree in science or health-related field. Experience with electronic data capture systems (e.g., EMR or EHR and data management systems such as RedCap and/or Atlas.ti ). Experience with EPIC EMR system. Six Sigma or Lean certifications. Certified Associate in Project Management (CAPM), Project Management Professional (PMP), or similar certification. Conditions of Employment: Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without requiring sponsorship. We are unable to provide work visa sponsorship or employment authorization for this position now or in the future. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Knowledge and understanding of evidence-based practice, quality improvement, and program implementation. Ability to communicate effectively, both in writing and orally. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with employees at all levels throughout the institution. Outstanding customer service skills. Knowledge of health care systems and medical terminology. Outstanding organizational skills and attention to detail. Ability to represent the University in a professional and positive manner. Ability to collaborate as a member of a team and to work highly independently to meet competing demands. Innovative problem-solving skills and ability to thrive on challenges encountered in a fluid, complex environment. Knowledge of institutional and governmental research administration policies and procedures and ability to strictly follow HIPAA regulations. Proficient use of computers and relevant software and database applications, including REDCap, OnCore, Microsoft Office, as well as the ability to master new software programs. Excellent project management, organizational, and time management skills. How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to the listed job qualifications and interest in the position Curriculum vitae / Resume Questions should be directed to : College of Nursing Human Resources at CON.HR@ucdenver.edu or 303.724.4447. Screening of Applications Begins: Applications will be accepted until finalists are identified, but preference will be given to complete applications received by two (2) weeks after the posting date. Those who do not apply by this date may or may not be considered. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as $47,533 to $55,614 (part-time, 0.8 FTE ) or $59,417 to $69,518 (full-time, 1.0 FTE ). The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position may be eligible for overtime compensation, depending on the level. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans, and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@cuanschutz.edu . Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students, and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine-preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety-sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41282&lang=en": {
      "title": "CAPE Education Technology Support Professional (0.8 FTE)",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 1, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: SOM-DEAN EO LL CAPE Schedule: Part-time University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus Department: Center For Advancing Professional Excellence Job Title: CAPE Education Technology Support Professional (0.8 FTE) Position #: 00803097 – Requisition #: 41282 Job Summary: This part-time (0.8 FTE) position is located at the University of Colorado School of Medicine, Center for Advancing Professional Excellence (CAPE). This position is regularly scheduled Tuesday through Friday, with occasional work on Mondays and Saturdays based on operational needs. This role may also require performing work at the Fort Collins, Colorado location as needed. CAPE provides modern medical simulation education that incorporates clinical scenarios, clinical instructors, mannequins of varying degrees of fidelity, and learners at any level of training into a robust teaching and learning environment. The CAPE is comprised of twelve (12) full-time team members and over 100 part-time standardized patients and teaching associates. This position will be based in a fast-paced, challenging, state-of-the-art clinical simulation environment. The person in this position will ensure all CAPE technologies are functioning properly and work to resolve any issues in collaboration with equipment vendors and university shared services. This person will also provide in-person support to ensure smooth session operations and utilization of CAPE space. Examples of Work Performed: Technology Suppor t (50%) Act as point of contact for desktop-related concerns from team members, learners, faculty, and clients. Monitor CAPE sessions to ensure paging, video, capture of metadata, and systems function correctly. Monitor and prioritize daily technology operations of the multidisciplinary simulation center and ensure communication of needs and issues to the appropriate project lead. Collaborate with the system vendors, A/V vendors, SOM Shared IT services, and/or OIT personnel to troubleshoot any system issues. Troubleshoot networks, servers, systems, and applications in order to identify and correct malfunctions and other operational difficulties. Interact with users to determine problems, analyze situations, identify the source of the problems, determine appropriate solutions, and take proper actions required to solve the problems. Perform a variety of maintenance, evaluation, and training tasks to ensure optimal technology performance and user experience. Create training materials pertaining to technology troubleshooting and usage. Serve as a technology resource to the team for use of technical platforms. Attend in-person and virtual meetings with the CAPE project lead and client to analyze, troubleshoot, and diagnose hardware and software problems. Technology Maintenance (20%) Act as point of contact for all desktop support needs at CAPE. Install, configure, and maintain staff and center computers, monitors, copiers, printers, etc. Work with the appropriate campus resources and vendors to resolve technical issues related to network interruptions. Track and resolve maintenance tasks and support tickets from the team. This includes maintaining a work log of support tickets and maintenance tasks. Maintain accurate and up-to-date documentation of technical procedures, system configurations, and issue resolutions. Maintain technology assets, software, and hardware for use and integration in simulation education modalities. This includes but is not limited to audio, video, learning management system, manikins, task trainers, computers, laptops, monitors, mobile technology carts, displays & TVs, copiers, printers, VR/AR equipment, etc. Other (10%) Utilize a project management application to organize and delegate project-specific tasks. Maintain technical expertise to effectively manage CAPE equipment and technologies and enforce proper usage and operation by authorized personnel. Attend briefings/debriefings/meetings with CAPE team members, clients, and project teams. Assist CAPE Director with the writing of technical and annual reports. Provide a conduit to the public and University communities about the Center. Assist CAPE Director with projects as needed. This may include items such as researching and reporting on the specs for new technology-related items and equipment, assisting with accreditations that fall within the scope of CAPE’s mission, etc. Perform other duties as required. Work Location: Onsite – this role is expected to work onsite and is located in Aurora, Colorado . Why Join Us: The CAPE is a national and international centerpiece of educational and assessment innovation, located at the Anschutz Medical Campus. At the core of the CAPE’s work is a dedication to and a passion for producing humanistic and scientifically grounded health professionals, using innovative methods to educate and assess the essential skills needed by these professionals to serve the citizens of Colorado and beyond. The CAPE also conducts research on the nature and quality of communication between health care professionals and patients, physical examination teaching and learning, high-fidelity simulation, and other topics. Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation, and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package, including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 15/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced-rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree in technology, computer science, educational field, or equivalent professional experience. Substitution: A combination of education and related technical/military/paraprofessional experience may be substituted for a bachelor’s degree on a year-for-year basis. At least one (1) year of experience supporting and troubleshooting technology-related programs. Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Preferred Qualifications: Direct project management experience or certification is preferred. Simulation technology experience including learning management systems, manikins, task trainers, etc. Previous experience with simulation center software platforms, EMS, B-Line, Laerdal, etc. Previous experience with VR, AR, and XR. At least two (2) years of experience in a higher education environment or technology support. Conditions of Employment: Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without requiring sponsorship. We are unable to provide work visa sponsorship or employment authorization for this position now or in the future. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Ability to gather and manipulate data in an efficient and organized manner. Ability to manage large-scale projects efficiently and effectively. Knowledge of the simulation field. Ability to work well with a variety of people, including members of the Center, Anschutz Medical Campus, clients from within and outside the institution, students, proctors, and teaching associates. Ability to communicate clearly and effectively. Ability to be well organized and work effectively on multiple tasks. Ability to work effectively as part of a team and independently. Capacity for flexibility and adaptability in different work situations. Computer skills, including ability to work with the following programs (SharePoint, Word, Excel, Access, Outlook). How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): Curriculum vitae / Resume Three to five professional references, including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Questions should be directed to: Melissa Giardina, melissa.giardina@cuanschutz.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Applications will be accepted until finalists are identified, but preference will be given to complete applications received by November 1, 2026 . Those who do not apply by this date may or may not be considered. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as $42,957 to $57,563 (calculated for 0.8 FTE). The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position may be eligible for overtime compensation, depending on the level. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans, and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@cuanschutz.edu . Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students, and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine-preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety-sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41281&lang=en": {
      "title": "Assistant Director of Marketing and Communications",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 1, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: SOP-Administration Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus Department: Skaggs School of Pharmacy and Pharmaceutical Sciences – Marketing & Communications Job Title: Assistant Director of Marketing and Communications Position #: 00853105 – Requisition #: 41281 Job Summary: This is an exciting opportunity for a collaborative and strategic marketing and communications leader to make a significant impact on the future of pharmacy education, research, and healthcare. Reporting directly to the Chief of Staff/Communications Director, the Assistant Director of Marketing and Communications will play a critical role in advancing the visibility, reputation, and strategic priorities of the Skaggs School of Pharmacy and Pharmaceutical Sciences. In this highly visible leadership role, the Assistant Director will oversee the daily operations of the Marketing and Communications Office and lead a talented multidisciplinary team responsible for content development, social media, web strategy, digital marketing, recruitment campaigns, CRM and email marketing, photography, video, and internal communications. The successful candidate will collaborate closely with faculty, academic program leaders, researchers, Student Services, and campus partners to develop and execute high-impact marketing and communications initiatives, strengthen the School's brand, improve operational effectiveness, and support emerging institutional priorities. This role offers a unique opportunity to influence strategic decision-making, mentor communications professionals, and drive meaningful engagement with prospective students, alumni, healthcare professionals, donors, and the broader community. Key Responsibilities: Develop, implement, and oversee integrated marketing and communications strategies that advance School priorities, increase visibility, strengthen brand awareness, and promote the School's educational programs, research, faculty expertise, and impact on healthcare and pharmacy practice. Partner with academic programs, Student Services, and School leadership to develop and execute recruitment marketing initiatives that support enrollment goals for Doctor of Pharmacy, Master's, PhD, certificate, and other academic programs. Oversee the day-to-day operations of the Marketing and Communications Office, including management of digital marketing, website, social media, content development, CRM and email marketing, and other communications platforms and technologies. Directly supervise, mentor, and develop a multidisciplinary team of marketing and communications professionals, fostering a collaborative, accountable, and high-performing work environment aligned with School priorities and objectives. Lead the planning, prioritization, and execution of multiple marketing and communications projects by establishing clear scopes, timelines, deliverables, workflows, and performance measures, while ensuring efficient use of staff and resources. Serve as the primary operational liaison for marketing and communications activities across the School, building effective partnerships with faculty, staff, students, academic leaders, research leaders, Student Services, campus partners, and external stakeholders. Collaborate closely with the Chief of Staff/Communications Director and School leadership to assess emerging opportunities and changing priorities, recommend strategic marketing and communications approaches, and adapt plans and resources to support the School's evolving goals and objectives. Work Location: Hybrid – this role is eligible for a hybrid schedule of 3 days per week on campus and as needed for in-person meetings. Why Join Us: The Skaggs School of Pharmacy and Pharmaceutical Sciences, located at the Anschutz Medical Campus, is an internationally renowned School of Pharmacy and a top-tier research school ranked in the top 10% of more than 140 schools in the country for research grant funding. At the Skaggs School of Pharmacy and Pharmaceutical Sciences, we are committed to excellence and innovation in professional, graduate, and post-graduate education; scholarship and research; patient-centered care; public health advocacy; and societal leadership and engagement. Together, our innovation, discoveries, and engagement with our communities improve the health and well-being of society. Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation, and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 15/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's degree in communications, public relations, marketing, or a closely related field from an accredited institution. Seven (7) years of progressively responsible professional experience in marketing, communications, public relations, recruitment marketing, or a related field. An advanced degree (Masters or Doctorate) may be substituted for experience on a year for year basis if the degree is in a field of study directly related to the work assignment. Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Preferred Qualifications: Master's degree in communications, public relations, marketing, journalism, or a related field. Marketing, student recruitment, communications, or public relations experience in a higher education setting. Experience supervising professional staff and managing multidisciplinary teams. Experience managing integrated marketing and communications campaigns across digital, web, social media, email, and traditional channels. Experience with CRM and marketing automation platforms, preferably Salesforce or similar systems. Experience using analytics and performance data to guide marketing and communications decisions. Experience managing budgets, vendors, consultants, and external agencies. Conditions of Employment: Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without requiring sponsorship. We are unable to provide work visa sponsorship or employment authorization for this position now or in the future. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Excellent written, verbal, interpersonal, and presentation communication skills. Strong organizational, project management, and prioritization skills with the ability to manage multiple complex initiatives simultaneously. Demonstrated ability to lead, supervise, mentor, and develop professional staff in a collaborative team environment. Ability to build partnerships, foster collaboration, and effectively engage diverse stakeholders across a matrixed organization. Strong problem-solving, analytical, and decision-making skills, including the ability to use data and metrics to inform recommendations. Adaptability and sound judgment to effectively manage changing priorities in a fast-paced, dynamic environment. Ability to translate complex and technical information into clear, compelling communications for diverse audiences. Knowledge of contemporary marketing and communications practices, including digital marketing, social media, web strategy, CRM platforms, email marketing, content strategy, and project management tools. Ability to coordinate cross-functional efforts, manage competing priorities, and ensure accountability for results. How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position. Curriculum vitae / Resume Three to five professional references, including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address. Questions should be directed to: Lori Westermann, LORI.WESTERMANN@CUANSCHUTZ.EDU Screening of Applications Begins: Screening begins 2 weeks after posting date . Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as $78,936 – $105,775 . The above salary range (or hiring range) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position may be eligible for overtime compensation, depending on the level. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@cuanschutz.edu . Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41278&lang=en": {
      "title": "Open Rank Clinical Research Coordinator (Entry – Senior)",
      "description": "Posted Date: Sep 30, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: SOM-MED-Endocrinology Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus Department: Medicine – Division of Endocrinology, Metabolism, and Diabetes Job Title: Open Rank Clinical Research Coordinator (Entry – Senior) Position #: 00853607 – Requisition #: 41278 Job Summary: Under the supervision of the Clinical Research Manager, the primary responsibility of the Entry or Intermediate Clinical Sciences Professional is to serve as a Clinical Research Coordinator in support of various research activities within Dr. Neda Rasouli’s Research Program at the University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus. Key Responsibilities: Trial Operations & Management: Assist with and oversee day-to-day operations for multiple clinical trials, acting as the Primary Coordinator to ensure all study activities align with the established protocol. Subject Recruitment & Screening: Participate and lead recruitment efforts by interviewing prospective subjects, reviewing medical histories against inclusion/exclusion criteria, and confirming final eligibility. Informed Consent Oversight: Execute and document the informed consent process, ensuring all participants are fully educated on study details and that legal documentation is filed per regulatory standards. Protocol Execution: Perform study-related procedures, assessments, and drug administrations as defined in the research protocol and in compliance with governing bodies. Subject Scheduling & Coordination: Manage the logistics of subject participation, including the coordination of clinic space and multidisciplinary support (Radiology, Pharmacy, Lab, and PIs). Clinical Assessments: Perform technical clinical tasks including phlebotomy (venipuncture), specimen processing/shipping, EKGs, and monitoring vital signs. Data Management: Abstract, code, and record patient data into Case Report Forms (CRFs) and clinical trial databases with a focus on accuracy and timely entry. Regulatory Compliance: Maintain meticulous study records to ensure strict adherence to FDA guidelines, Good Clinical Practice (GCP), and hospital Standard Operating Procedures (SOPs). Safety Reporting: Promptly alert Principal Investigators, sponsors, and the FDA regarding Serious Adverse Events (SAEs) to ensure patient safety and data integrity. Leadership & Quality Improvement: Assist in the creation of new clinical processes and quality initiatives while training junior staff members on study protocols. Work Location: Onsite – this role is expected to work onsite and is located in Aurora, Colorado. Why Join Us: The Division of Endocrinology, Metabolism and Diabetes on the state-the-art Anschutz Medical Campus. Our mission is to improve overall health and well-being by prevention, diagnosis, treatment and cure of Diabetes, Obesity, Metabolic disorders and Endocrine disorders through: Cutting-edge basic, translational and clinical research Nationally recognized consultative services in Endocrinology, Metabolism and Diabetes National leadership Training of future leaders in Academic Endocrinology To learn more about us, please visit: https://medschool.cuanschutz.edu/endocrinology Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation, and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 15/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Entry Level: Bachelor’s degree in science or health related field. Intermediate Level: Bachelor’s degree in science or health related field. One (1) year clinical research or related experience. Senior Level: Bachelor’s degree in science or health related field. Two (2) years clinical research or related experience . Substitution: A combination of education and related technical/military/paraprofessional experience may be substituted for a bachelor’s degree on a year for year basis. Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Preferred Qualifications: Three (3) years clinical research or related experience . Conditions of Employment: Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without requiring sponsorship. We are unable to provide work visa sponsorship or employment authorization for this position now or in the future. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Ability to communicate effectively, both in writing and orally. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with employees at all levels throughout the institution. Knowledge of basic human anatomy, physiology, and medical terminology. An understanding of genetics and molecular genetics. Ability to interpret and master complex research protocol information. Excellence with computer skills with Microsoft Office, including Word, Excel, PowerPoint and Outlook. Knowledge of the research process, e.g., research protocols, surveys. How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position. Curriculum vitae / Resume Three to five professional references, including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address. Questions should be directed to: Ellie Olthoff, eleanor.olthoff@cuanschutz.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Applications will be accepted until finalists are identified, but preference will be given to complete applications received by October 15 th , 2026 . Those who do not apply by this date may or may not be considered. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range (or hiring range) for this position has been established as: Entry Level: $49,899 – $63,472 Intermediate Level: $54,302 – $69,072 Senior Level: $58,705 - $74,673 The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position may be eligible for overtime compensation, depending on the level. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing non-discrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@cuanschutz.edu ​. Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students, and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=39258&lang=en": {
      "title": "Pediatric Psychologist in Physical Medicine & Rehabilitation- Open Rank Assistant Professor - Associate Professor",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 1, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: SOM-PM&R GENERAL OPERATIONS Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus Department: Physical Medicine and Rehabilitation Job Title: Open Rank: Assistant Professor to Associate Professor Working Title: Pediatric Psychologist in Physical Medicine & Rehabilitation Position #00759670: – Requisition #: 39258 Job Summary: The Pediatric Rehabilitation Psychology & Neuropsychology Program within the Department of Physical Medicine & Rehabilitation (PM&R) at the University of Colorado School of Medicine is seeking a full-time Pediatric (or Rehabilitation) Psychologist. This position involves direct clinical care, teaching, supervision, and program development, with a focus on providing integrated behavioral health services to children, adolescents, and their families seen in the Spina Bifida/Spinal Cord Injury multidisciplinary clinic, the Spina Bifida Teen Transition multidisciplinary clinic, and the Rehabilitation Psychology outpatient program. The position includes a faculty appointment at the University of Colorado School of Medicine, with academic rank commensurate with qualifications and experience. The successful candidate will be an integral member of an interdisciplinary medical team providing comprehensive, family-centered care to children and adolescents with spina bifida, spinal cord injury, and other rehabilitation-related conditions and will maintain an outpatient therapy caseload. Key Responsibilities: · Provide integrated behavioral health services in the Spina Bifida/Spinal Cord Injury clinic and Spina Bifida Teen Transition clinic, including psychosocial screening, brief intervention, and the development and implementation of behavioral health treatment plans. · Provide direct evidence-based interventions to youth with acute and chronic injuries or illnesses, including diagnostic evaluations and individual, family, and/or group therapy. Common patient conditions that are a focus of clinical work include spina bifida, acquired brain injuries (e.g., concussion, moderate to severe TBI), cerebral palsy, muscle disorders, spinal cord injury/disease, and functional neurologic disorders. · Consult with rehabilitation medicine teams to address behavioral health and environmental factors that impact child well-being, quality of life, injury recovery, and adjustment to chronic health conditions. Collaborate closely with psychosocial partners including social work, family navigators, and community health liaisons to deliver comprehensive, team-based care. · Collaborate and coordinate with internal and external providers involved in patient’s care. · Supervise, teach, and mentor psychology and neuropsychology trainees (externs, interns, fellows), as well as medical trainees. · Engage in research, scholarship, and/or quality improvement projects. · Serve on committees, task forces, and/or workgroups. Active pursuit and participation in research activities as well as mentoring residents and other faculty in research endeavors Work Location: Onsite - this role is expected to work onsite and is located in Aurora, Colorado. Why Join Us: Thank you for considering joining our team. The field of rehabilitation believes in using your whole body to improve your human performance. The department of Physical Medicine and Rehabilitation at the University of Colorado (which we affectionately call \"CU PM&R\") is at the forefront of using team science, regenerative medicine, and exercise treatments. It is uniquely situated in the state-of-the-art CU Anschutz Medical Campus, the first campus in the nation to be built from the ground up to bring research, education, and patient care into one visionary collaboration. Like the Rocky Mountains that provide a backdrop of our institutions, CU PM&R is on the rise! We combine the disciplines of rehabilitation medicine, physical therapy, psychology, speech/language therapy, and rehabilitation sciences into a singular department. The University of Colorado Department of Physical Medicine and Rehabilitation offers an exceptional learning and working environment. Our team of clinicians, researchers, educators, and administrative staff are dedicated to the advancement of physical medicine and rehabilitation and are committed to providing quality patient care. Our department is equipped with the latest technology and specialized equipment, enabling us to provide comprehensive care to our patients. Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year (based on percentage of time) Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 11/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Please be advised that this position is not eligible now or in the future for visa sponsorship. Assistant Professor: · PhD and/or PsyD from an APA-accredited program · 1-3 years of related clinical experience at rank or equivalent experience · Prior experience in a pediatric health psychology setting Associate Professor: · PhD and/or PsyD from an APA-accredited program · 4-7 years of related clinical experience at rank or equivalent experience · Prior experience in a pediatric health psychology setting Preferred Qualifications: · Experience working with pediatric populations with medical complexity, injuries, or chronic medical conditions. · Experience with supporting patients with community and school reintegration after injury or illness. · Ability to deliver services in Spanish is preferred. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: · Demonstrated skills in the use of developmentally and diagnostically appropriate screening and assessment tools. · Demonstrated skills using evidence-based treatment models including but not limited to motivational interviewing strategies, consultation models, behavior therapy, and flexible application of cognitive-behavioral therapies. · Ability to work collaboratively in a multidisciplinary team model and with physicians, psychosocial providers, trainees, and colleagues. · Experience and skill in consulting with professional colleagues and staff. · Ability to communicate effectively, both in writing and verbally · Ability to work effectively on multiple tasks and maintain a well-organized work environment. · Ability to work effectively as part of a team and independently. · Experience developing, training, and supervising psychology trainees. How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): 1. A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position 2. Curriculum vitae / Resume 3. Three to five professional references including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers . Questions should be directed to: Ann.Lantagne@childrenscolorado.org Screening of Applications Begins: Screening begins immediately and continues until position is filled. For best consideration, apply by February 1st, 2027. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as HIRING RANGE: Assistant Professor: $113,000 - $125,000 Associate Professor: $125,000 - $145,000 The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation unless it is non-exempt. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: The University of Colorado (CU) is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@ucdenver.edu ​. Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41280&lang=en": {
      "title": "Professional Research Assistant Level 2",
      "description": "Posted Date: Sep 30, 2026 Job category: Research Faculty Department: CSPH-CHWE Gen ops Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Department: Environmental and Occupational Health Job Title: Professional Research Assistant Level 2 Position #:00853624 – Requisition #: 41280 Job Summary: The Center for Health, Work, and Environment (CHWE) is seeking a part-time (50%FTE) Professional Research Assistant (PRA) – Level 2 position. This position will serve as an essential liaison and trusted bridge between the Mountain West Hub research team and local residents in Alamosa, CO. As part of a landmark clean air and health resilience study, the PRA is responsible for conducting community-based recruitment, securing informed consent, conducting structured home visits, placing indoor air filtration units, and collecting longitudinal health and environmental metrics across participating households. Community Outreach & Recruitment · Local Outreach & Engagement: Conduct direct outreach across Alamosa County to engage residents in the Clean Air Study. Represent the study at community meetings, local events, and public hubs to build awareness and trust. · Participant Recruitment Waves: Reach out to households identified through randomized address sampling and community sign-up lists, maintaining respectful, multi-modal contact attempts (phone, in-person, email). · Recruitment Tracking: Maintain accurate, real-time records of all participant contact attempts, eligibility screenings, and recruitment dispositions using REDCap and shared tracking logs. Informed Consent & Participant Onboarding · Study Explanation & Screening: Clearly explain study objectives, household eligibility criteria (year-round SLV residence, no existing air cleaner, adult 18+ household consent), and participation benefits ($200 incentive + free air filter). · Consent Administration: Guide participants through the informed consent process (via phone, Zoom link, or in person) and collect child assents during initial visits in accordance with IRB protocols. Home Visits & Environmental / Health Data Collection · In-Home Monitoring & Equipment Setup: Perform initial, quarterly/midpoint, and endpoint home visits to measure indoor air quality, record room dimensions, and set up DIY box-fan air cleaners (DIYacs) and UPAS air quality monitors. · Health Measurement Collection: Collect baseline and follow-up clinical and survey measures, including resting blood pressure, lung function testing (spirometry/PEF), survey responses, and urine sample coordination for designated sub-cohorts. · Equipment Maintenance & Inspection: Inspect air filter units and sensors during routine visits, ensuring proper placement in participant bedrooms or primary living areas and supplying replacement filters as needed. Acute Air Quality Event & Longitudinal Support · Poor Air Quality Event Follow-Up: Assist participants during text-alerted poor air quality events (wildfire smoke or dust events) by supporting short 3-day daily surveys and lung function measurements. · Ongoing Participant Support: Serve as the primary local point of contact for participating Alamosa households, delivering plain-language air quality/health results summaries and addressing participant questions. Training, Logistics & Compliance · Required Study Trainings: Complete mandatory pre-study onboarding, including CITI Human Subjects Training, REDCap data collection training, recruitment protocol review, and the 8-hour Full Study Training. · Team Meetings & Administrative Reporting: Participate in bi-weekly (and subsequent monthly) study team check-ins, coordinate with local couriers for sample/hardware handoffs, and submit monthly invoices and mileage logs to the CN Manager. Work Location: Remote – this role is eligible to work remotely, but the employee must be in the United States. Why Join Us: The Colorado School of Public Health is a collaborative endeavor involving the University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus (CU Anschutz), Colorado State University (CSU), and the University of Northern Colorado (UNC). The Colorado School of Public Health is the first and only accredited school of public health in the Rocky Mountain Region, attracting top-tier faculty and students from across the country and providing vital contributions towards ensuring our region’s health and well-being. Collaboratively formed in 2008 by CU Anschutz, CSU, and UNC, the Colorado School of Public Health provides education programs, including a Master’s concentration in global health, innovative research that places the School in the top 20 in NIH funding among Schools of Public Health, and community service that addresses public health issues including chronic disease, healthcare access, climate, and environmental threats, emerging infectious diseases, population mental health, ONE HEALTH and injuries for the Rocky Mountain region, nationally and globally. Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package including: · Medical: Multiple plan options · Dental: Multiple plan options · Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision · Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay · Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year (based on percentage of time) · Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) · Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) · Holiday Days: 11/year · Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses · ECO Pass: Reduced rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. · Must have Bachelor’s degree and 1+ year experience, community health, research coordination, or public service outreach, preferably in rural health initiatives · Bilingual in English and Spanish · Basic computer and mobile technology literacy (e.g., using smartphones, tablets, Zoom, Google Sheets, and web-based survey software like REDCap). · Interpersonal and Communication Skills Conditions of Employment Must be available to work year-round in Alamosa, CO, and have the ability to travel for local home visits across Alamosa County. Flexible work schedule requiring some evening and weekend hours to accommodate participant home visit availability. Preferred Qualifications: · Community Health / Outreach Experience: Prior experience working as a Community Health Worker (CHW), Promotora, patient navigator, research assistant, or community outreach worker in rural health or environmental health programs. · Established Local Networks: Established relationships with local community organizations, clinics, schools, agricultural groups, or public hubs in Alamosa and the San Luis Valley. · Field Data Collection Experience: Prior experience conducting structured home visits, administering surveys, or collecting basic health measurements (e.g., resting blood pressure or peak flow lung function) Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: · Community Dynamics: Deep familiarity with local geography, rural cultural norms, and community resources in Alamosa County and surrounding Valley communities. · Interpersonal & Cultural Responsiveness: Strong active listening and trust-building skills; ability to communicate warmly and respectfully with varied rural populations. · Technical & Equipment Handling: Practical aptitude to set up, demonstrate, and inspect household air cleaning hardware (DIY box-fan air cleaners / DIYacs) and air quality monitoring devices (UPAS units). · Digital & Survey Literacy: Proficiency in using smartphones, tablets, or computers for field data collection, including entering survey responses into REDCap, updating Google Sheets tracking logs, and participating in Zoom team check-ins. · Organizational & Outreach Management: Strong time management skills to schedule home visits, track up to 5 contact attempts per household, and maintain accurate activity logs. · Plain Language Communication: Ability to translate study procedures, health results, and air quality concepts into clear, accessible, jargon-free language. · Field Autonomy & Collaboration: Ability to work independently during local home visits while maintaining consistent communication with the research leadership. · Physical & Equipment Capability: Ability to carry, transport, and assemble light study hardware (such as box fans, filters, and monitors) into participant homes. · Adaptability & De-escalation: Ability to respond supportively during acute poor air quality alerts and handle participant questions or hesitations with empathy and patience. How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): 1. A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position 2. Curriculum vitae / Resume 3. Five professional references including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers . Questions should be directed to: Emily Ivanich, Emily.ivanich@cuanschutz.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Applications will be accepted until finalists are identified, but preference will be given to complete applications received by 11/5/2026 . Those who do not apply by this date may or may not be considered. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as HIRING RANGE: $26,266 – $34,516 for 0.50 FTE The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation unless it is non-exempt. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: The University of Colorado (CU) is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@ucdenver.edu ​. Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41273&lang=en": {
      "title": "CTRC Program Administrator",
      "description": "Posted Date: Sep 30, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: ADM VCR CCTSI Admin Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Department: The Colorado Clinical and Translational Sciences Institute (CCTSI) Job Title: CTRC Program Administrator Position #: 00853658 – Requisition #: 41273 Job Summary: The Colorado Clinical and Translational Sciences Institute (CCTSI), a clinical research institute located on the University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus, has an opening for a full-time Program Administrator. The Clinical Translational Research Center (CTRC) Program Administrator will provide program support to the CTRC in the areas of new research protocol receipt and routing, protocol lifecycle management (start-up, tracking of key metrics, protocol closeout), tracking and management of key financial metrics, and fee schedule management. This position does not supervise staff. Reporting to the CCTSI Director of Finance and Administration, the position will interact with multiple individuals throughout the CTRC to ensure the smooth flow of research from protocol receipt, through protocol review & approval, to project start-up, and project closeout. This position will also provide general administrative support to other programs of the CCTSI as needed. We are seeking a collaborative, well-organized individual, with an interest in contributing to human health in an academic environment. The successful candidate will be highly organized, communicate effectively, team oriented, and able to work independently as well as collaboratively. This position will be 100% in-person with the option to transition to partial remote work over time. Key Responsibilities: CTRC Research Protocol Management Receive all new protocols proposing to use the CTRC to conduct the research. This involves creating the electronic structure for the storage and management of protocol documents, ensuring all documents have been properly submitted, and communicating with other CTRC staff and Medical Directors regarding the status of the protocols. Utilize institutional applications (EPIC, OnCore, InfoEd, REDCap) to manage the research protocol lifecycle. Prepare messages to Investigators to communicate the status of protocols and provide formal approval to activate their protocols at the CTRC. Tracking key CTRC performance metrics. CTRC Financial Administration Assist CTRC investigators in the preparation of the protocol budget. Manage the CTRC fee schedule and coordinate the addition of new charge codes and fee changes. Resolve protocol billing errors. Track key financials Metrics. General CCTSI Administrative Support Assist CCTSI Managers with scheduling, graphing metrics (Excel), and other activities necessary to support their programs. General procurement of supplies & materials as needed. Participate in supporting CCTSI events. Other general administrative support as needed. Work Location: Onsite – this role is expected to work onsite and is located in Aurora, CO. Why Join Us: The CCTSI supports transformational clinical and translational research at the University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus and affiliated institutions. The CCTSI was created in 2008 with funding from the Clinical and Translational Science Award (CTSA) initiative of the National Institutes of Health (NIH) Because research conducted using CCTSI resources spans multiple institutions, this position acts as a liaison to other Information Technology departments. Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 15/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree in public health, public administration, social/behavioral sciences, physical sciences, nursing, healthcare, finance, accounting, business administration, business, or a directly related field from an accredited institution 3-5 years of professional experience in clinical research setting, academic administrative position, or in an environment that involves the core skills necessary to complete the job responsibilities (protocol review, protocol budget preparation and fee schedule management). A combination of education and related technical/military/paraprofessional experience may be substituted for a bachelor’s degree on a year for year basis. Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Preferred Qualifications: More than two years of professional experience in an academic medical center. Experience with Epic, OnCore, & REDCap Experience analyzing business operations or workflows, finding efficiencies, and implementing improvements Conditions of Employment: Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without requiring sponsorship. We are unable to provide work visa sponsorship or employment authorization for this position now or in the future. This position will be 100% in-person with the option to transition to partial remote work over time. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Ability to communicate effectively, both in writing and orally. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with employees at all levels throughout the institution. Outstanding customer service skills. Customer service orientation with excellent written and verbal communication skills in the English language. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with employees at all levels throughout the institution. Strong communication skills Highly organized individual Strong troubleshooting background. Team oriented. Able to work with minimal supervision; can independently research new processes and solutions to meet deadlines and expectations. Able to coordinate and prioritize several simultaneous tasks with potentially conflicting priorities Ability to adapt in a fast-paced work environment High proficiency in Microsoft Windows, Teams, Outlook, Word and Excel How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position Curriculum vitae / Resume Three to five professional references, including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Questions should be directed to: Tim Lockie, Tim.lockie@cuanschutz.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Immediately and continues until the position is filled. For best consideration, apply by October 16, 2026. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as HIRING RANGE $63,673 - $85,322 The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position may be eligible for overtime compensation, depending on the level. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@cuanschutz.edu ​. Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41046&lang=en": {
      "title": "Finance Program Manager",
      "description": "Posted Date: Sep 30, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: SOM-MED-Transplant GEN OPERATIONS Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus Department: Medicine – Division of Transplant Medicine Job Title: Finance Program Manager Position #: 00853028 – Requisition #: 41046 Job Summary: This is an excellent opportunity for a finance professional who enjoys using data, analysis, and partnership to support meaningful work in academic medicine. The Finance Program Manager will serve as the primary financial reporting and analysis resource for the Division of Transplant Medicine, the first division of its kind in the United States, while also providing financial reporting and analytical support for the Division of Hospital Medicine. In this role, the successful candidate will help translate complex financial and operational information into clear, actionable insights that support clinical operations, faculty planning, budgeting, forecasting, and long-term strategic decision-making. The position offers broad exposure to financial reporting, provider productivity, clinical revenue, business case development, and process improvement in a dynamic, mission-driven environment. Day to day, this individual will build and maintain financial models, monitor key performance trends, partner with division and department leaders, and identify opportunities to strengthen reporting workflows, improve revenue capture, and support responsible stewardship of divisional resources. For someone who is detail-oriented, collaborative, and interested in making a visible impact, this role provides the opportunity to contribute directly to the growth and success of an innovative clinical and academic enterprise. Key Responsibilities: Lead financial reporting and analysis for the Division of Transplant Medicine, including provider productivity, clinical activity, wRVU performance, cFTE targets, monthly financial results, and other key financial and operational metrics, while providing monthly financial reporting and related analytical support for the Division of Hospital Medicine. Monitor financial performance, identify trends and variances, and provide timely analyses and recommendations to support operational and strategic decision-making. Develop and maintain financial models to support budgeting, forecasting, business case development, faculty recruitment, compensation planning, clinical initiatives, and long-range planning. Support day-to-day management and oversight of divisional funds, including clinical, grant, gift, and other funding sources, ensuring appropriate use, documentation, reconciliation, and reporting. Partner with division leadership, the Department of Medicine finance team, CU Medicine, and other stakeholders to resolve financial questions, improve reporting workflows, and strengthen alignment with institutional requirements. Ensure CU Medicine sites of practice and related billing information are accurate, current, and aligned with division clinical operations and provider assignments. Provide guidance on procurement, reimbursement, payment activities, fund selection, and related compliance requirements to ensure transactions are accurate, allowable, properly documented, and aligned with applicable policies. Work Location: Hybrid – this role is eligible for a hybrid schedule of 3 days per week on campus and as needed for in-person meetings. Why Join Us: The CU Anschutz Division of Transplant Medicine is the newest division in the Department of Medicine, formed to bring together world-class experts dedicated to advancing patient care, groundbreaking research and educating future transplant leaders. The first division of its kind in the United States, we serve as a hub for interdisciplinary collaboration, driving new discoveries and improving outcomes for transplant recipients. Our faculty represent some of the nation’s leading transplant clinicians, scientists, and educators, united by a shared commitment to excellence and innovation. Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation, and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 15/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree in business administration, business, finance, accounting, or a directly related field from an accredited institution. A combination of education and related technical/paraprofessional experience may be substituted for the bachelor’s degree on a year-for-year basis. Four (4) years of professional experience in financial analysis, budgeting, accounting, or financial operations. Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Preferred Qualifications: Master’s degree in business administration, finance, accounting, or a related field from an accredited college or university. Experience in a healthcare or higher education institution. Experience with the University’s PeopleSoft finance system. Experience with Anaplan or similar financial planning system. Prior experience managing clinical revenues, productivity reporting, and financial modeling. Conditions of Employment: Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without requiring sponsorship. We are unable to provide work visa sponsorship or employment authorization for this position now or in the future. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Ability to communicate effectively, both in writing and orally. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with employees at all levels throughout the institution. Outstanding customer service skills. Demonstrated ability to successfully plan, organize, implement, and coordinate financial and administrative activities in a diverse and complicated system. Strong financial management skills to include comprehensive understanding of academic medical institution financial structure and operational standards. Advanced proficiency with Microsoft Excel, including financial modeling, data analysis, complex formulas, and reporting. How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position. Curriculum vitae / Resume Three to five professional references, including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address. Questions should be directed to: Fred Meisterplass, FRED.MEISTERPLASS@CUANSCHUTZ.EDU Screening of Applications Begins: Applications will be accepted until finalists are identified, but preference will be given to complete applications received by October 9 th , 2026 . Those who do not apply by this date may or may not be considered. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as $69,810 – $88,798 . The above salary range (or hiring range) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position may be eligible for overtime compensation, depending on the level. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@cuanschutz.edu . Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41267&lang=en": {
      "title": "Open Rank Administrative Assistant (Level I – Level III)",
      "description": "Posted Date: Sep 30, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: SOM-MED-Infectious Disease Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus Department: Medicine – Infectious Diseases Job Title: Open Rank Administrative Assistant (Level I – Level III) Position #: 00853619 – Requisition #: 41267 Job Summary: This position plays a key role in supporting the Division of Infectious Diseases within a dynamic academic medical center. The successful candidate will serve as a trusted partner to faculty and staff leaders, ensuring the efficient day-to-day operation of the office. In this highly visible role, the employee will collaborate with faculty and staff across the division to plan impactful programs and events, manage administrative and operational functions, and serve as a central resource for faculty and staff across the division. Key Responsibilities: Provide comprehensive administrative support to faculty and staff leaders, including calendar management, meeting scheduling, correspondence, and coordination of virtual and in-person meetings. Coordinate division meetings, programs, and events—including faculty meetings, orientations, retreats, wellness initiatives, and other activities—managing logistics, venues, catering, rentals, promotion, and on-site support in partnership with division leadership and the Faculty Wellbeing Director. Manage day-to-day office operations and shared spaces, including facilities requests, copier and conference room support, meeting technology, inventory and supply procurement, mail distribution, and coordination with IT and other campus service providers. Coordinate end-to-end logistics for faculty candidate interviews, including interview itineraries, travel and lodging, hosted meals, candidate job talks, on-site support, and travel and expense reimbursements. Lead new faculty onboarding, including orientation, workspace preparation, technology and equipment setup, badging, onboarding materials, and guidance on campus resources and administrative processes. Reconcile procurement, travel, and other divisional expenses in accordance with established policies. Coordinate division social media communications, including content planning, creation, scheduling, and posting. Provide backup coverage to ensure continuity of administrative and operational functions, while supporting special projects and performing additional duties as assigned. Work Location: Hybrid – This role is eligible for a hybrid schedule of 3 days per week on campus. Attendance on campus is required on the days of events the employee is coordinating or supporting, which may occur on any weekday and occasionally on weekends. Why Join Us: The Division of Infectious Diseases is dedicated to improving health through outstanding patient care, innovative research, and transformative education. We provide expert, compassionate, and collaborative infectious disease care, advance the field through scientific discovery, promote best practices in antimicrobial stewardship and infection prevention, and train the next generation of clinicians and physician-scientists. Our work extends across the Mountain-Plains region and beyond, with a commitment to advancing health equity, expanding knowledge, and improving the lives of the patients and communities we serve. Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation, and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 15/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Administrative Assistant I: One (1) year of professional experience in business operations support. A combination of related education and/or relevant experience in an occupation related to the work assigned equal to one (1) year. Administrative Assistant II: Two (2) years of professional experience in business operations support. A combination of related education and/or relevant experience in an occupation related to the work assigned equal to two (2) years. Administrative Assistant III: Three (3) years of professional experience in business operations support. A combination of related education and/or relevant experience in an occupation related to the work assigned equal to three (3) years. Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Preferred Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree from an accredited institution. Previous experience comprehensive administrative support, including calendar management, meeting coordination, scheduling, correspondence, and general office operations. Experience in academic medicine and/or higher education environments. Conditions of Employment: Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without requiring sponsorship. We are unable to provide work visa sponsorship or employment authorization for this position now or in the future. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Strong organizational and time management skills, with the ability to prioritize multiple responsibilities and meet deadlines in a fast-paced environment. Excellent verbal and written communication skills, with the ability to interact professionally and effectively with faculty, staff, students, visitors, and external partners. Ability to plan, coordinate, and execute meetings, events, and programs while effectively managing multiple logistical details and competing priorities. Strong attention to detail and accuracy in managing information, procurement and travel expenses, documentation, and administrative processes. Ability to exercise sound judgment, maintain confidentiality, work independently, and collaborate effectively within a team-oriented environment. Proficiency with Microsoft Office applications, including Outlook, Word, Excel, PowerPoint, and Teams, with the ability to learn and utilize institutional systems and technologies. How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position. Curriculum vitae / Resume Three to five professional references, including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address. Questions should be directed to: Eleanor Shields-Ramirez, eleanor.shields-ramirez@cuanschutz.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Immediately and continues until position is filled. For best consideration, apply by October 23 rd , 2026 . Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as: Administrative Assistant I: $39,520 – $45,996 Administrative Assistant II: $40,248 – $48,300 Administrative Assistant III: $51,360 – $61,632 The above salary range (or hiring range) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position may be eligible for overtime compensation, depending on the level. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@cuanschutz.edu . Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41265&lang=en": {
      "title": "Open Rank Medical Assistant - Oncology, Highlands Ranch",
      "description": "Posted Date: Sep 29, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: SOM-DEAN DO CPD - MEDICINE Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus Department: Community Practice Job Title: Open Rank Medical Assistant - Oncology, Highlands Ranch Position #: 00853632 – Requisition #: 41265 Job Summary: Calling all Medical Assistants and Certified Medical Assistants! Our busy clinics are recruiting for Medical Assistants! We need your training and skills to help our clinic run smoothly, providing our patients with top notch quality care. The Medical Assistant (MA) or Certified Medical Assistant (CMA) is responsible for providing patient care under the direction of a physician or another healthcare provider. The MA works to facilitate clinic workflow, assist patients, and ensure safe, seamless delivery of care for each patient. Key Responsibilities: Accurately rooms patients, obtains and records vital signs, patient history, and reason for seeking care. Accurately processes and records telephone messages in patient medical records and according to policy. Assists in preparing prescription refills for providers according to policy. Maintains patient confidentiality, written and verbal. Communicates effectively and in an attentive manner with every patient encounter. Verifies the patient’s understanding of the purpose of the visit. Accurately documents all care provided and procedures performed within the patient’s medical record. Work Location: Onsite – this role is expected to work onsite and is located in Highlands Ranch, CO . Why Join Us: Community Practice Medicine, housed within the School of Medicine at the University of Colorado, is seeking trained medical professionals to join our growing team. With clinics spanning from Longmont to Castle Rock, we offer a wide variety of opportunities. Specialty areas include, but are not limited to: Orthopedics, Vascular Surgery, OBGYN, Internal Medicine, Urology, Psychiatry, and many more! The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is a public education, clinical and research facility serving 4,500 students and a world-class medical destination at the forefront of life-changing science, medicine, and healthcare. CU Anschutz offers more than 42 highly rated degree programs through 6 schools and colleges and receives over $500 million in research awards each year. We are the single largest health professions education provider in Colorado, awarding nearly 1,450 degrees annually. Powered by our award-winning faculty, renowned researchers, and a reputation for academic excellence, the CU Anschutz Medical Campus drives innovation from the classroom to the laboratory to the delivery of unparalleled patient care. Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation, and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package, including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accrues over the year Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 15/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced-rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Medical Assistant: Completion of an accredited medical assistant program OR one year of medical assistant work experience. Certified Medical Assistant: Completion of an accredited medical assistant program. One year of medical assistant work experience. Current CMA certification (i.e., AAMA, NCCT). Substitution (All Levels): A combination of education and related technical/paraprofessional experience may be substituted on a year-for-year basis. Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Preferred Qualifications (All Levels): Experience with MS Office. Experience with EPIC. Experience with Kronos. Experience with HealthStream. Conditions of Employment (All Levels): Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without requiring sponsorship. We are unable to provide work visa sponsorship or employment authorization for this position now or in the future. Current Basic Life Support (BLS) for Healthcare Providers issued by the American Heart Association or the American Red Cross healthcare provider-level CPR certification. Maintains all required licensure and certifications for the position. Must be able to work in-person. Must be able to travel to alternate locations as assigned. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities (All Levels): Strong organizational and personal skills. Strong medical terminology knowledge and skills. Strong knowledge of CPT & ICD-10 procedures. Strong knowledge of value-based care and risk-based coding procedures in Primary Care. Strong knowledge of medication and injection procedures. Ability to safely administer a variety of treatments and medications as directed. Ability to use various types of equipment for examination and treatment procedures. Ability to accurately take and record vital signs. Ability to accurately reconcile patient medications. Ability to maintain quality control standards. Ability to identify problems and recommend solutions. How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position Curriculum vitae / Resume Three to five professional references, including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Questions should be directed to: Emma Porter, Emma.Porter@cuanschutz.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Immediately and continues until the position is filled. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as: Medical Assistant: $44,116 to $51,527 Certified Medical Assistant: $47,813 to $55,846 The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position may be eligible for overtime compensation, depending on the level. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans, and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@cuanschutz.edu . Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students, and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine-preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety-sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41264&lang=en": {
      "title": "Open Rank Medical Assistant - OBGYN, Family Planning, Lowry",
