    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41221&lang=en": {
      "title": "DOM Post Award Core Grants & Contract Program Manager",
      "description": "Posted Date: Sep 25, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: SOM-MED GENERAL OPERATIONS Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Department: Medicine Job Title: DOM Post Award Core Grants & Contract Program Manager Position #: 00729862 – Requisition #: 41221 Job Summary: The Department of Medicine (DOM) has an opening for a full-time Post-Award Core Grants and Contracts Program Manager. This position leads the Post-Award Core team, which provides comprehensive post-award support to Department of Medicine Faculty. This role sits within the DOM Research Office and works closely with research leadership, the Office of Grants and Contracts, divisions within the DOM, and research teams to ensure the effective administration and oversight of sponsored projects. Core hours are Monday through Friday, 8 AM - 5 PM. Under direction from Research leadership, this position provides day-to-day leadership, facilitates communication related to sponsored project administration, and ensures compliance with all federal, state, University, and sponsor regulations. A critical element of the role is to deliver timely and expert service and support to DOM faculty and administrators. The position is responsible for maintaining efficient and consistent grants management processes in a fast-paced, collaborative academic environment. Key Responsibilities: Supervision and Leadership Supervise a team of research services professionals (grant administrators) and assign workloads to team members, ensuring that team members have appropriate workloads. Create and maintain standard operating procedures and policies for the Post-Award Core. Ensure accuracy and timeliness of services provided. Serve as the Department’s content expert in post-award grants and contracts management. Post-Award Grants and Contracts Administration Perform journal entries, PETs, funding distributions, and other financial transactions involved in sponsored projects administration to complete financial tasks and tracking for NIH, VA, DOD, and private foundation grants and contracts. Implement university fiscal policies and procedures, and state, federal, and sponsor policies and standards applicable to business management of projects (personnel, accounting, auditing, etc.). Prepare budgets for federal, state, industry, university, and private sponsors for grants, fellowships, and contracts. Training and Reporting Responsible for training the team to provide team members with the necessary skills and knowledge to perform their duties effectively and accurately, including all tasks performed by post-award core, such as journal entries, PETs, funding distributions, projections, and other financial transactions involved in sponsored projects administration. Ensure all grant and contract team members stay up to date with the latest grant regulations, with a specific focus on NIH awards. Provide reports for DOM and division leadership as requested in a timely manner. Work Location: Hybrid – this role is eligible for a hybrid schedule with a minimum of three to four (3-4) days per week, 8 AM – 5 PM, on campus and as needed based on workload, in-person meetings, and CU Anschutz policies. Why Join Us: The Department of Medicine at the University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is the largest clinical department in the School of Medicine. With more than 1,000 faculty, 192 residents, and 200 fellows distributed in 14 divisions, our clinical, research, and academic programs attract the best providers, investigators, staff, and students from around the world who are transforming the future of health care. In addition to our exemplary performance, we continue to have strong standings in national rankings in all our academic missions. Our Department Chairperson remains committed to evolving the Department and meeting the ever-changing needs of healthcare and our patients. Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation, and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 15/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced-rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree in public administration, physical sciences, healthcare, finance, accounting, business administration, business, or a directly related field from an accredited institution Five (5) years of experience managing sponsored projects administration, including at least three (3) years of post-award administration.* Three (3) years of experience supervising professional employees.* *Experience may be obtained simultaneously. Substitution: A combination of education and related technical/military/paraprofessional experience may be substituted for a bachelor’s degree on a year-for-year basis. Substitution: An advanced degree (Master's or Doctorate) may be substituted for experience on a year-for-year basis if the degree is in a field of study directly related to the work assignment. Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire . Preferred Qualifications: Prior experience working in sponsored projects financial administration, with a focus on federal funders, in an academic environment. Previous experience managing a research administrator team. CRA certification. Experience with CU Anschutz information systems: InfoEd, CONCUR, CU Marketplace, PeopleSoft Finance, CU Data, and HCM. Conditions of Employment: Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without requiring sponsorship. We are unable to provide work visa sponsorship or employment authorization for this position now or in the future. Must be willing and able to walk approximately 0.5 miles between meeting sites. Must be able to work 8.00 AM - 5.00 PM Monday through Friday. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities (KSAs): Knowledge of federal, private, and industry grant and contract regulations and rules. Strong financial management skills. Ability to plan, organize, implement, and coordinate complex financial and administrative activities. Ability to work independently as well as part of a team. Superior communication skills to liaise effectively with medical, professional, administrative, and other personnel, and expertly present information both orally and in written form. Proactive in identifying and addressing issues in real time. Adaptability in an environment of frequent change. Ability to work efficiently in a fast-paced environment. Proven teamwork skills. Must be able to work independently following training. Ability to establish work priorities and handle multiple deadlines. Ability to handle sensitive and confidential information and documents and maintain strict confidentiality in all HR matters; using professionalism and discretion in all conversations, even those not directly related to HR actions. Strong organizational skills and attention to detail. Proficient in the use of Microsoft Office programs (Excel, Word, Outlook, PowerPoint) and advanced proficiency in creating and maintaining data/financial reports using Excel. How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position. Curriculum vitae / Resume Three to five professional references, including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address. Questions should be directed to: Jenny Kemp, JENNIFER.T.KEMP@CUANSCHUTZ.EDU Screening of Applications Begins: Applications will be accepted until finalists are identified, but preference will be given to complete applications received by October 15 th , 2026 . Those who do not apply by this date may or may not be considered. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as $70,814 – $90,937 . The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position may be eligible for overtime compensation, depending on the level. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans, and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@cuanschutz.edu . Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students, and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine-preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety-sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41220&lang=en": {
      "title": "Health Educator & Prevention Specialist (Part-time, 0.5 FTE)",
      "description": "Posted Date: Sep 26, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: SOM-PEDS Adolescent Med-GenOps Schedule: Part-time University of Colorado Anschutz Department: Department of Pediatrics, Section of Adolescent Medicine Job Title: Health Educator & Prevention Specialist (Part-time, 0.5 FTE) Position #: 00852077 – Requisition #: 41220 Job Summary: The part-time (0.5 FTE) Health Educator & Prevention Specialist will work with the Adolescent Family Planning Program (BC4U) and Aurora Public Schools, both of which are committed to offering comprehensive sexual health education to all youth throughout the State of Colorado. This is an exciting new role, and the final candidate will have the opportunity to lend an innovative lens to how it operates and works amongst the two organizations/programs. The Health Educator & Prevention Specialist will partner closely with BC4U’s Director of Program Development, Clinic Medical Director, and Program Manager to understand BC4U’s clinical services, outreach models, and in-clinic workflows to inform their work at Aurora Public Schools (APS) with an APS Teacher on Special Assignment focused on health. Key Responsibilities: Developing robust sexual health curriculum presentations for youth in Colorado alongside BC4U and Aurora Public Schools. Delivering sexual health education to middle-school and high-school students in Aurora Public Schools and various additional districts. Promote BC4U clinic services throughout APS and beyond. Partner with BC4U leadership’s Program Manager to ensure health education is embedded into BC4U’s and APS’ strategic plans. Develop and maintain BC4U’s Youth Advisory Board. Work Location: Onsite – this role is expected to work onsite and is located in Aurora, CO . Why Join Us: BC4U is known both throughout Colorado and nationally for offering comprehensive, free, confidential, and nonjudgmental sexual health care to youth in Colorado under the age of 25. BC4U partners with Aurora Public Schools to offer comprehensive sexual health education to all youth in their district. This partnership is supported by local foundations and has had a great impact on youth in Aurora and beyond. The BC4U program also works closely with the Adolescent Medicine Clinic, TRUE Center for Gender Diversity, the Young Mother’s Clinic, and Children’s Hospital’s HIV Prevention Program for youth and pregnant people. Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation, and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package, including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 15/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced-rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree in public/community health, social work, or a directly related field from an accredited university. Substitution: A combination of education and related technical/paraprofessional experience may be substituted for the bachelor’s degree on a year-for-year basis. Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Preferred Qualifications: At least one (1) year of experience working with young adults or adolescents. At least one (1) year of experience working in prevention or community health. Experience teaching sexual education to adolescents or young adults. Experience working in a clinical setting. Work experience in a middle school and/or high school setting. Demonstrated experience in community organizing and/or community engagement. Conditions of Employment: Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without requiring sponsorship. We are unable to provide work visa sponsorship or employment authorization for this position now or in the future. Must be willing and able to pass national criminal and sex offender background checks. Must successfully pass a 10-panel drug screen through Children’s Hospital Colorado. Willing to work flexible hours, including evenings and weekends. *For questions regarding Children’s Hospital drug testing requirements, please contact Children’s Human Resources at 720-777-8598. Some positions may require testing if access to Children’s Hospital or its systems is needed at any time during employment with the University. If drug testing is required, it will be listed in the job posting. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Ability to communicate effectively, both in writing and orally. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with employees at all levels throughout the institution. Outstanding customer service skills. Ability to interact in a compassionate and nonjudgmental manner with a diverse client population with a commitment to health equity. Excellent organizational and time management skills. Proficient in computer skills including Microsoft Word, Excel, Outlook, internet, and email. How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position Curriculum vitae / Resume Three to five professional references, including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Questions should be directed to: Andrea Loasby; andrea.speer@cuanschutz.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Immediately and continues until the position is filled. For best consideration, apply by October 1 st , 2026. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as $30,128.50 to $40,372 (calculated for 0.5 FTE). The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position may be eligible for overtime compensation, depending on the level. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans, and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@cuanschutz.edu . Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety-sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41217&lang=en": {
      "title": "Medical Education Learning Specialist",
      "description": "Posted Date: Sep 25, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: SOM-DEAN EO UME Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Department: Office of Medical Education Job Title: Medical Education Learning Specialist Position #: 00853476 – Requisition #:41217 Job Summary: As a dedicated subject matter expert and professional within the Office of Student Life, this role supports the planning, coordination, and implementation of initiatives that promote the academic and professional development success of medical students in all 4 years of their educational experience. This includes providing individualized student advising and coaching, overseeing tutoring services for MD students, and operating as a work lead for the 20+ student tutors staffed to provide support services. The Medical Education Learning Specialist will be responsible for developing, implementing and administering programs and workshops to support the academic success of students. This role works collaboratively with medical school faculty and staff to build knowledge about the science of learning and student support across the entire office of medical education. They will also provide one-on-one academic enrichment support for students with academic challenges. Key Responsibilities: Academic Advising – 70%: Provide individual academic assessment of medical students requesting help with learning and test taking skills. Act as a Department subject matter expert related to student advising, this includes developing individualized plans for learning success that is tailored to each student based on: what area/phase a student is struggling in specific recommendations for remediation, study planning and additional learning requirements, governed by Med School policies on Progress and Promotions Use expertise to establish services and a knowledge repository for students, including campus wide learning resources, medical student specific study aids and test taking aids, evidenced based study plans and learning tools, regular check in’s with students to adapt/adjust learning and remediation plans (in collaboration with progress and promotion committee policies and required learning steps for students). Possess knowledge of and effectively connect students with campus resources to include behavioral health, groups, library and other learning benefits afforded. Provide groups and workshops for students facing academic challenges in the pre-clinical medical school curriculum. Provide group and individual support and coaching for students taking medical boards exams. Teach and support faculty advisors with skills for supporting students through Step exam preparation. Facilitate institution wide academic success programming focused on study skills, time management, clinical efficiency, and board preparation strategies. Help set base line study and learning strategies specific to medical students and work alongside the faculty to ensure the students have been given ample resources and plans that will fit their specific academic needs for success. Maintain knowledge of best practices for academic support services and implement evidence-based strategies. Works independently and is able to make decisions on student academic advising and coaching needs. Administrative Oversight of Student Success – 20% Record and document student meetings to follow student progress. Participate in student success meetings with faculty members and students. Monitor and track student progress in pre-clinical and boards exam dashboards. Office of Student Life Executive Committee Meeting - Produce agendas, keeps Minutes, provides tech support, and procedural admin. Keep confidentiality of all private information. Tutoring Program Oversight – 5% Independently oversee the tutoring program for qualified MD students. Plan and execute tutor trainings and ensure training completion by newly onboarded tutors. Collaborate with HR to recruit student tutors. Oversee the on-boarding, training, and payment processing for student tutors. Oversee and manage the tutoring process for MD students by receiving student inquiries, matching students with prospective tutors, getting tutors access to student materials, and fielding any questions or concerns. Provide high-level committees with insight and data on tutoring efficacy and usage by struggling students. Manage the OSL library of donated books and educational resources for students to borrow within the Office of Student Life. Other Duties as Assigned – 5% Share in the duties of answering the phone and working with students who “drop in” with requests within the Office of Student Life. Establish and document best practices and standard operating procedures relevant to core work responsibilities. Contribute to program functions of the Office of Student Life; participate in event preparation (Orientation, Matriculation Ceremony, Match Day, Graduation, etc.), act as back up for admissions interviews, etc. Perform other duties as assigned by the Associate Dean of Student Affairs, the Assistant Dean of Student Success, the Student Affairs Assistant Deans, and the Manager of Admissions and Student Affairs. Work Location: Hybrid – this role is eligible for a hybrid schedule of 3 days per week on campus and as needed for in-person meetings. Why Join Us: Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 15/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: A Bachelor’s degree in education, psychology, learning science, or a related field. Substitution : A combination of education and related technical/military/paraprofessional experience may be substituted for a bachelor’s degree on a year for year basis. 3 or more years of professional experience working with medical students as an academic advisor/learning specialist. Substitution : An advanced degree (Masters or Doctorate) may be substituted for experience on a year for year basis if the degree is in a field of study directly related to the work assignment. Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Preferred Qualifications: A Master’s degree in education, psychology, learning science, or a related field. A EdD or PhD in education or psychology. 5 or more years of experience working at a medical school in student affairs as a learning specialist. Experience with curriculum development and assessment in higher education. Conditions of Employment: Ability to work a hybrid remote schedule with up to 3 days a week in the office. Additional on-site days may be required when sessions, on-site meetings, or events necessitate an additional on-site presence. Please see the campus-wide policy for additional information. May be required to work occasional nights and/or weekends. Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without requiring sponsorship. We are unable to provide work visa sponsorship or employment authorization for this position now or in the future. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Proven ability to work collaboratively with students, faculty and staff. Excellent organizational skills, capacity for empathy and independent work. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with individuals from varied backgrounds and organizational levels. Strong organizational skills and effective time management with the ability to manage multiple priorities and deadlines. Ability to work both independently and collaboratively within a team environment. Strong written and verbal communication skills. Demonstrated customer service and interpersonal skills. Ability to coordinate projects and events while maintaining attention to detail. Ability to interpret and apply university and departmental policies and procedures. Proficiency in Microsoft Office applications including Outlook, Word, Excel, and PowerPoint. Ability to analyze information, solve problems, and recommend practical solutions. How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position Curriculum vitae / Resume Three to five professional references, including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Questions should be directed to: Melanie Trinkwald at melanie.trinkwald@cuanschutz.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Immediately and continues until position is filled. For best consideration, apply by 2 weeks from posting date . Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as $60,905 - $81,613 The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position may be eligible for overtime compensation, depending on the level. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@cuanschutz.edu ​. Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41214&lang=en": {
      "title": "Clinical Science Program Manager, GN Trials",
      "description": "Posted Date: Sep 25, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: SOM-MED-REN GENERAL OPERATIONS Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus Department: School of Medicine, Department of Medicine, Division of Renal Diseases and Hypertension Job Title: Clinical Science Program Manager, GN Trials Position #: 00853550 – Requisition #: 41214 Job Summary: The Renal Division has a robust clinical trials program with its own dedicated space for administrative and clinical operations. This particular position offers the opportunity to lead and manage all aspects of approximately 8 trials (from interventional treatment to biobank) for rare inflammatory kidney disease (glomerulonephritis). Key Responsibilities: Independently manage the administrative, personnel, financial, and contracting functions for the GN trial group within the larger kidney disease renal research office. Oversee management of two clinical trial coordinators, including evaluations, troubleshooting, and advising, ensuring staff meet all requirements related to their assigned studies. Develop policies and procedures, as required. Maintain financial oversight of GN group research trials. Tasks include salary and expense allocations, invoicing, developing clinical trial budgets, negotiating contracts, and reconciling accounts. Maintain regulatory oversight in the startup, maintenance, and close-out of clinical research studies. Routinely interface with IRB, coordinators, investigators, sponsors, and monitors to ensure overall compliance with policies and procedures for conducting good clinical trials. Work Location: Hybrid – this role is eligible for a hybrid schedule of four to five (4-5) days per week on campus and as needed for in-person meetings. Why Join Us: Our dedicated research office faculty and staff make for a vibrant, supportive, and collaborative group to work with. Additionally, if you are someone who strives to grow and learn, you would be a proud part of the University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus, which is a world-class medical destination at the forefront of life-changing science, medicine, and healthcare. Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation, and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package, including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 15/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced-rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree in any field. Substitution: A combination of education and related technical/military/paraprofessional experience may be substituted for a bachelor’s degree on a year-for-year basis. Four (4) years of clinical research or related experience. Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Preferred Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree in science or health-related field. Five (5) years of clinical research or related experience. Prior experience providing program and/or project management duties in a clinical research setting. Experience with electronic data capture systems (e.g., EMR or EHR and data management systems). Conditions of Employment: Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without requiring sponsorship. We are unable to provide work visa sponsorship or employment authorization for this position now or in the future. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Strong project management skills and experience within a complex and diverse environment. Advanced knowledge and understanding of federal regulations and Good Clinical Practice (GCP). Demonstration of strong analytical and problem-solving skills. Demonstration of strong technological and Microsoft Suite skills. Ability to communicate effectively, both in writing and orally. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with employees at all levels throughout the institution. Outstanding customer service skills. Knowledge of basic human anatomy, physiology, and medical terminology. Ability to interpret and master complex research protocol information. How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position Curriculum vitae / Resume Three to five professional references, including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Questions should be directed to: Betsy Pike, Renal Division Human Resources, at betsy.pike@cuanschutz.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Applications will be accepted until finalists are identified, but preference will be given to complete applications received by October 15, 2026. Those who do not apply by this date may or may not be considered. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as $70,446 to $89,607. The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position may be eligible for overtime compensation, depending on the level. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans, and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@cuanschutz.edu . Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students, and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine-preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety-sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41212&lang=en": {
      "title": "Academic Services Professional (Open Rank: Intermediate-Principal)",
      "description": "Posted Date: Sep 25, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: SOM-NEUR GENERAL OPERATIONS Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus Department: Neurology Job Title: Academic Services Professional (Open Rank: Intermediate-Principal) Position # 00788668 – Requisition #41212 Job Summary: The Program Coordinator is responsible for supporting the administrative and operational functions of assigned non-ACGME fellowship programs, educational courses, conferences, and special events. This role provides coordination of fellowship activities, assists with the planning and execution of courses and events, supports day-to-day education operations, and collaborates with faculty and staff on educational initiatives and special projects. The ideal candidate possesses excellent organizational, interpersonal, and communication skills; demonstrates a high degree of attention-to-detail and professionalism; and has the ability to work both independently and collaboratively in support of educational programs and initiatives. Key Responsibilities: Instructor-Fellowship Program Coordination (75%) Manage the day-to-day operations for fellowship programs and fellows Assist the Program Director in developing and maintaining the educational quality of the training program & ensuring compliance with accreditation standards and regulatory requirements. Coordinates accreditation activities ‐ Special Reviews, Annual Program Evaluations, etc. Manages the Fellow recruitment and selection process Acts as an important liaison between fellows, fellowship directors, faculty, participating sites, and institutional and regulatory offices. Oversee content and design on fellowship webpages on both the department internet and intranet sites and collaborate with the department IT team to implement changes and updates accordingly Education Events & Operations Support (25%) Coordinate, develop, organize, and evaluate department education conferences and events and other assigned department educational conferences, including but not limited to: CME conferences, faculty educator development trainings, community education outreach initiatives, etc. Support the Vice Chair of Education and Academic Services Program Director with education strategic initiatives and special projects Manage and track all resident and fellow training verifications requests Maintain alumni database and assist with annual alumni newsletter Provide cross coverage for education teammates as needed Other duties as assigned Work Location: Hybrid – this role is eligible for a hybrid schedule of 3 days per week on campus and as needed for in-person meetings. Why Join Us: The University of Colorado Anschutz seeks individuals with demonstrated commitment to creating an inclusive learning and working environment. We value the ability to engage effectively with students, faculty and staff of diverse backgrounds. The Neurology non-ACGME Fellowship Coordinator, under the direction of the Education Program Director is responsible for managing various aspects of the department’s non-ACGME fellowship programs, educational courses, conferences, and events. This position coordinates the non-ACGME Fellowship programs with recruitment, accreditation efforts, course programming, database updates and reimbursements. This position will be expected to utilize knowledge, expertise and best practices in the design and successful operation of various educational experiences which support the department’s mission of providing high quality educational programs. Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 10/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Intermediate Professional Bachelor’s degree from an accredited college or university in communications, public relations, business administration, healthcare administration, or another related field. 1 year of professional level experience Senior Professional Bachelor’s degree from an accredited college or university in communications, public relations, business administration, healthcare administration, or another related field. 2 years of professional level experience Principal Professional Bachelor’s degree from an accredited college or university in communications, public relations, business administration, healthcare administration, or another related field. 3 years of professional level experience Substitution: A combination of education and related technical/paraprofessional experience may be substituted for the bachelor’s degree on a year for year basis. Preferred Qualifications: Experience working with Graduate Medical programs Experience organizing and working with CME conferences and event management. Experience coordinating meetings including providing concise written documentation Competencies Knowledge of current LCME, CUSOM, UME, AND CME policies to ensure all activities meet accreditation standards. Understanding of and competence in the use of the New Innovations program to build and maintain the evaluation and rotation database and schedules. Demonstrated motivation and capability of performing in a complex and fast-paced environment. Exceptional organizational skills and attention to detail, strong work ethic, positive problem-solving attitude, results oriented and able to work through projects independently. Effective communication and interpersonal skills with a high degree of professionalism and competence in dealing with a variety of individuals including physicians, program directors, university and hospital administrators, and industry representatives. Proficient knowledge and work experience in Microsoft Office Suite and ability to quickly learn new software programs. Strong time management skills, ability to meet multiple deadlines and manage interrelated and /or complex issues or transactions. Ability to represent departmental activities, issues, and concerns, and communicate committee decisions back to directors and education managers. How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position Curriculum vitae / Resume Three to five professional references, including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Questions should be directed to: neurology-hr@cuanschutz.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Applications will be accepted until finalists are identified, but preference will be given to complete applications received by October 16, 2026. Those who do not apply by this date may or may not be considered Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as: Intermediate Professional: $48,989 - $62,314 Senior Professional: $52,961 - $67,367 Principal Professional: $60,905 - $77,471 The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position may be eligible for overtime compensation, depending on the level. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@cuanschutz.edu ​. Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41211&lang=en": {
      "title": "PRN Registered Vascular Tech – Interventional Radiology, Highlands Ranch",
      "description": "Posted Date: Sep 24, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: SOM-DEAN DO CPD - RADIOLOGY Schedule: Part-time University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus Department: Community Practice Job Title: PRN Registered Vascular Tech – Interventional Radiology, Highlands Ranch Position #: 00853540 – Requisition #: 41211 Job Summary: The Registered Vascular Tech will perform advanced vascular imaging studies utilizing state-of-the-art ultrasound technology and physiologic imaging equipment for the diagnosis and treatment of vascular disease. This position is responsible for daily operations of the vascular laboratory, patient scheduling, equipment maintenance, and quality assessment at our Interventional Radiology location. Key Responsibilities: At the direction of a qualified physician or advanced practice provider, performs a variety of procedures requiring independent judgment and initiative in the utilization of ultrasonic equipment for the diagnosis of disease in humans. Performs high-quality vascular ultrasound examinations including, but not limited to, upper and lower extremity arterial duplex, upper and lower extremity venous duplex, aorto-iliac duplex, renal duplex, mesenteric duplex, dialysis access evaluation, and pre-operative/post-operative vein mapping. Performs high-quality physiologic studies including, but not limited to, ankle-brachial index (ABI), pulse volume recording (PVR), and photoplethysmogram (PPG). Reviews patient medical history and physician or advanced practice provider's orders in order to perform prescribed study. Works with the Medical Director to formulate or revise imaging protocols, policies, and procedures utilized in the production of images. Work Location: Onsite – this role is expected to work onsite and is located in Highlands Ranch, CO . Why Join Us: Community Practice Medicine, housed within the School of Medicine at the University of Colorado, is seeking trained medical professionals to join our growing team. With clinics spanning from Longmont to Castle Rock, we offer a wide variety of opportunities. Specialty areas include, but are not limited to; Orthopedics, Vascular Surgery, OBGYN, Internal Medicine, Urology, Psychiatry, and many more! The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is a public education, clinical and research facility serving 4,500 students and a world-class medical destination at the forefront of life-changing science, medicine, and healthcare. CU Anschutz offers more than 42 highly rated degree programs through 6 schools and colleges and receives over $500 million in research awards each year. We are the single largest health professions education provider in Colorado, awarding nearly 1,450 degrees annually. Powered by our award-winning faculty, renowned researchers, and a reputation for academic excellence, the CU Anschutz Medical Campus drives innovation from the classroom to the laboratory to the delivery of unparalleled patient care. Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation, and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package, including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 15/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced-rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: A High School Diploma or GED. Graduate of an accredited Ultrasound Technologist program or Diagnostic Medical Sonographer program. Two (2) years of experience working as an Ultrasound Technician. Substitution: A combination of education and related technical/military/paraprofessional experience may be substituted for a bachelor’s degree on a year-for-year basis. Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Preferred Qualifications: Three or more (3+) years of vascular experience. Experience working in vascular surgery or related practice. Experience setting up sterile and non-sterile procedure trays and medical procedure rooms. Experience and knowledge of medical chart preparation and setup. Experience with EPIC. Registered Phlebology Sonographer (RPhS). Bilingual, Spanish preferred. Conditions of Employment: Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without requiring sponsorship. We are unable to provide work visa sponsorship or employment authorization for this position now or in the future. Registered as a Vascular Technologist (RVT) through the American Registry for Diagnostic Medical Sonography (ARDMS). Registered as a Diagnostic Medical Sonographer (RDMS) by the American Registry for Diagnostic Medical Sonography. Current Basic Life Support (BLS) for Healthcare Providers issued by the American Heart Association or American Red Cross healthcare provider level CPR certification. Must be willing to work in person. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Ability to effectively communicate at all levels, to include physicians, leadership, and staff within the various affiliate organizations (UCH, Children’s Colorado, CU Medicine, CU SOM). Ability to work within large, complex healthcare systems. Ability to analyze and interpret data. Ability to compile complex reports and develop presentations. Ability to compose letters and memorandums. Ability to deal calmly and courteously with people. Ability to deal with stressful situations. How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position Curriculum vitae / Resume Three to five professional references, including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Questions should be directed to: Laurel Gebhard, Laurel.Gebhard@cuanschutz.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Immediately and continues until the position is filled. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as $40.70 to $48.19 per hour . The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position may be eligible for overtime compensation, depending on the level. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans, and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@cuanschutz.edu . Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students, and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine-preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety-sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
