    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41166&lang=en": {
      "title": "HR Senior Professional",
      "description": "Posted Date: Sep 21, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: SOM-PEDS GENERAL OPERATIONS Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus Department of Pediatrics Job Title: HR Senior Professional Position #: 00853403 – Requisition #: 41166 Job Summary: This is an exciting opportunity to join a human resources team in the University of Colorado School of Medicine – Department of Pediatrics at the Anschutz Medical Campus. The Anschutz Medical Campus fosters collaboration among students, researchers, and clinicians within one of the nation's largest academic health centers. Campus architecture and state-of-the-art technology bridge education and research with two world-class hospitals: University of Colorado Hospital and Children’s Hospital Colorado. The Department of Pediatrics includes 25 sections, 18 programs, and 3 affiliates with approximately 1,200 faculty and staff. The Department of Pediatrics is seeking applications for a Human Resources Business Partner. This full-time University Staff (non-classified) position will serve as a primary resource to sections within the department by providing support, guidance, and interpretation of Federal, State, University, and School of Medicine laws, rules, regulations, policies, and procedures, assuring compliance in a variety of human resources areas, which include recruitment, selection, onboarding, personnel management, and payroll. The person in this role will not only work closely with the Business Managers and Section Heads across all sections but will also collaborate with the School of Medicine Human Resources and Faculty Affairs departments, University Central HR, and Employee Services. The ideal candidate for this position will be an energetic individual who is ready to help create change and be part of a group of professionals dedicated to collaborative approaches, relationship building, outstanding customer service, and positive outcomes. Key Responsibilities: Independently complete the day-to-day recruitment activities for faculty and staff positions through the Human Capital Management (HCM) and CU Careers systems for a portfolio of Sections within the DOP. Assist sections as needed in recruiting new talent by sourcing candidates, writing job descriptions/announcements, screening applicants, performing job analysis, selecting/developing assessment devices, and consulting with subject matter experts. Participate in University Staff and Faculty searches. Draft letters of offer for faculty and staff appointments in coordination with CHCO Section Business Managers. Work with the DOP Immigration Coordinator to facilitate International Visa Administration requests, including J-1, H-1B, O, TN, OPT, and Permanent Resident applications for Faculty, Postdoctoral Fellows, Research Associate series, and students that require work authorization. Perform University onboarding processes for new employees, including gathering required documents, coordinating IT access, I-9 forms, and badging. Create transactions in the Human Capital Management (HCM) system related to compensation, position, and personnel management. Maintain accurate, timely, and complete records ensuring compliance with Federal, State, and University laws, regulations, policies, and procedures. Coordinate payroll entries for all employees within sections, including leave, additional pay, leave payouts, and time collection for hourly staff. Approve payroll entries for monthly and off-cycle payrolls. Work with the DOP Leave Coordinator to initiate and track FML, medical leave, and leave of absence requests. Update and maintain main page data for faculty and staff in the portfolio of sections. Process funding allocations and payroll expense transfers as needed to ensure proper funding for all employees. Assist supervisors with the performance management process to ensure the process complies with appropriate University and School of Medicine policies and procedures Serve as a resource on HR policies and procedures. In collaboration with HR leadership in the Department, assist in the development of standard operating procedures and implementation of process improvement initiatives. Assist with data collection and data entry for the semi-annual salary setting process. Manage Person of Interest records, Perform other duties, tasks, and projects as assigned. Work Location: Hybrid – this role is eligible for a hybrid schedule of two (2) days per week on campus and as needed for in-person meetings. Why Join Us: The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is a public education, clinical, and research facility serving 4,500 students and is a world-class medical destination at the forefront of life-changing science, medicine, and healthcare. CU Anschutz offers more than 42 highly rated degree programs through 6 schools and colleges and receives over $500 million in research awards each year. We are the single largest health professions education provider in Colorado, awarding nearly 1,450 degrees annually. Powered by our award-winning faculty, renowned researchers, and a reputation for academic excellence, the CU Anschutz Medical Campus drives innovation from the classroom to the laboratory to the delivery of unparalleled patient care. Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation, and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package, including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 15/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced-rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree in Human Resources, Business, Public Administration, Healthcare Administration, Communications, or related field from an accredited college or university. Substitution: A combination of education and related technical/military/paraprofessional experience may be substituted for a bachelor’s degree on a year-for-year basis. At least two (2) years of professional-level experience performing human resources duties and responsibilities. Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Preferred Qualifications: Experience working with PeopleSoft Human Capital Management and CU Careers. At least one (1) year of experience with financial transaction-level detail (for example, journal entries, payroll, account reconciliation, accounts payable, etc.). Experience working in an academic medical center. Conditions of Employment: Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without requiring sponsorship. We are unable to provide work visa sponsorship or employment authorization for this position now or in the future. Must be willing and able to pass national criminal and sex offender background checks. Must successfully pass a 10-panel drug screen through Children’s Hospital Colorado. *For questions regarding Children’s Hospital drug testing requirements, please contact Children’s Human Resources at 720-777-8598. Some positions may require testing if access to Children’s Hospital or its systems is needed at any time during employment with the University. If drug testing is required, it will be listed in the job posting. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Strong independent judgment and critical thinking skills. Self-directed. Strong attention to detail. Excellent communication and interpersonal skills. Ability to work collaboratively with people from all levels within an organization. Ability to independently establish work priorities, follow through, and meet established deadlines. Advanced Microsoft Office skills, including Word, Excel, and Outlook. Ability to maintain a high level of confidentiality while working with sensitive information. Strong analytical and problem-solving skills. Ability to actively listen and share relevant information, anticipate problems, and establish and maintain effective working relationships. Knowledge of professional standards, concepts, and practices related to human resources. Ability to analyze, interpret, and evaluate a broad range of laws, rules, and regulations to exercise good judgment in applying them to human resources challenges. Knowledge of applicable Federal and State laws and regulations. How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to the listed job qualifications and interest in the position Curriculum vitae / Resume Three to five professional references, including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Questions should be directed to: Kristy Elias, kristy.elias@cuanschutz.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Immediately and continues until the position is filled. For best consideration, apply within twenty (20) days after the posting date. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as $57,073 to $76,478 . The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position may be eligible for overtime compensation, depending on the level. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans, and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@cuanschutz.edu . Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students, and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine-preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety-sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41164&lang=en": {
      "title": "Research Service Professional (Open Rank: Entry – Intermediate)",
      "description": "Posted Date: Sep 18, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: SOM-AN Res General Operations Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus Department: Anesthesiology Job Title: Research Service Professional (Open Rank: Entry – Intermediate) Position #00853387 – Requisition #41164 Job Summary: The Basak and Calero Laboratories in the Department of Anesthesiology are interested in understanding the molecular mechanisms that mediate brain injury and recovery after a cardiac arrest. Our research uses translational animal models of cardiac arrest with cardiopulmonary resuscitation (CPR) across the lifespan to study the role of various molecular pathways in mediating neuronal cell death, synaptic loss, and cognitive dysfunction. We are currently seeking a Research Services Professional (RSP) to perform small-animal surgeries and neurobehavioral testing in support of these projects. The RSP will also be responsible for tissue collections and histological analyses related to projects. This position will work in a collaborative team environment and will assist with lab maintenance responsibilities, including regulatory compliance, maintenance of the mouse colony, and other experiments as determined by the supervisors. Selected candidates will have access to state-of-the-art equipment and resources to conduct their research. The RSP is expected to attend weekly lab meetings and departmental research seminars. The position offers an excellent opportunity to gain insights into the pathophysiology of brain injury in the setting of ischemia and support your professional development in a collaborative research environment. Duties Performed (Entry Professional) Perform rodent survival surgeries and post-operative care. Perform neurobehavioral testing to assess cognitive and motor outcomes. Manage animal colonies. Maintain thorough and accurate lab records. Collaborate with and support Principal Investigators (PI) and other stakeholders with laboratory and research functions Duties Performed (Intermediate Professional) Lab Management responsibilities including lab ordering and regulatory compliance. Support training of other lab members and collaborators. Train others on skills in which high proficiency has been gained. Learn and perform cardiac arrest and cardiopulmonary resuscitation in rodents. Monitor animals that have surgeries and provide support for animal husbandry, as needed. Learn and perform histology and immunohistochemistry brain tissue from animals. Work Location: Onsite – this role is expected to work onsite and is located in Aurora, CO. Why Join Us: The University of Colorado School of Medicine and the Department of Anesthesiology is a world-class medical destination at the forefront of transformative education, science, medicine, and healthcare. The Department of Anesthesiology has several clinical specialties and is a nationally recognized leader in anesthesiology and peri-operative medical education. We are dedicated to developing leaders in anesthesiology and perioperative medicine who demonstrate clinical excellence, professionalism, and a commitment to life-long learning. Our faculty have a resolve to create an exciting academic environment that will build upon what is already recognized as one of the finest residency programs in the country, and by advancing education within our specialty, we continue to improve the lives of learners and patients in a complex and evolving world of medicine. Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 15/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Entry Level: Bachelor’s degree in biology, molecular biology, chemistry, genetics or related field A combination of education and related technical/paraprofessional experience may be substituted for the bachelor’s degree on a year-for-year basis One (1) year professional level research experience// Intermediate Level: Bachelor’s degree in biology, molecular biology, chemistry, genetics or related field A combination of education and related technical/paraprofessional experience may be substituted for the bachelor’s degree on a year-for-year basis Two (2) years professional level research experience Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Preferred Qualifications: Master’s degree in biology, molecular biology, chemistry, genetics or related field 2-3 years of experience in an experimental or wet laboratory Prior experience with immunohistology and microscopy techniques. Prior experience with lab management responsibilities. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Knowledge or Proficient knowledge of basic laboratory techniques including safety procedures and techniques Ability to communicate effectively, both in writing and orally Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with employees at all levels throughout the institution Outstanding customer service skills Knowledge of basic human anatomy, physiology medical terminology Ability to interpret and master complex research protocol information How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position Curriculum vitae / Resume Three to five professional references, including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Questions should be directed to: Jessic Rocz, JESSICA.ROCZ@CUANSCHUTZ.EDU for position or application questions. Dr. Jacob Basak, JACOB.BASAK@CUANSCHUTZ.EDU for work related questions. Screening of Applications Begins: Immediately and continues until position is filled. For best consideration, apply by 10 days after the position has been posted . Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as: Entry Professional: $47,811 - $64,067 Intermediate Professional: $52,030 - $69,720 The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position may be eligible for overtime compensation, depending on the level. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@cuanschutz.edu ​. Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41160&lang=en": {
      "title": "Senior AI & Business Enablement Partner",
      "description": "Posted Date: Sep 18, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: ADM AVC VC Info Strategy&Svcs Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Department: Information Strategy and Services Job Title: Senior AI & Business Enablement Partner Position #: 00853247 – Requisition #: 41160 Job Summary: Are you passionate about improving how people work through AI, process innovation, and organizational change? Do you enjoy partnering with stakeholders to solve complex business challenges, identify opportunities for improvement, and deliver meaningful transformation? Join Information Strategy and Services (ISS) and help shape the future of administrative operations through AI-enabled innovation and business enablement. This is a unique opportunity to help define how AI and emerging technologies are applied across a world-class academic medical campus. You'll work at the intersection of people, processes, and technology, partnering with stakeholders to modernize operations, improve efficiency, and create lasting organizational impact. From research administration to financial services and beyond, you'll help shape the future of work at CU Anschutz. About the Role The Senior AI & Business Enablement Partner, will collaborate with campus partners to identify opportunities, lead initiatives, and implement solutions that improve business processes, enhance decision-making, and advance operational excellence. This unique role combines technical project leadership, business analysis, process improvement, and organizational change management to help drive AI adoption and business transformation across the CU Anschutz campus. You'll serve as a trusted partner who bridges business and technology teams to deliver meaningful, sustainable outcomes. What You'll Do Partner with business stakeholders to identify opportunities for AI-enabled process improvement, automation, and operational efficiency. Lead the planning, execution, and delivery of AI-enabled initiatives, including project planning, stakeholder communications, risk management, and progress tracking. Facilitate requirements gathering, stakeholder workshops, business process analysis, and future-state design to define solutions and drive organizational outcomes. Analyze current and future-state workflows to identify opportunities for optimization, automation, and operational improvement. Collaborate with technical and business teams to translate operational needs into technology-enabled solutions and actionable project outcomes. Assess organizational impacts and develop change management, communication, training, and adoption strategies that support successful implementation. Build strong partnerships with faculty, staff, vendors, and technology teams to advance transformational initiatives across campus. Promote the responsible and effective use of AI and emerging technologies to deliver measurable business value. What You'll Bring Strong relationship-building, stakeholder engagement, and partnership skills. Experience leading projects or initiatives that involve multiple stakeholders, competing priorities, and organizational change. The ability to analyze business challenges and develop practical, value-driven solutions. Strong facilitation, communication, and requirements-gathering skills. Experience supporting process improvement, workflow optimization, or business transformation efforts. Curiosity, adaptability, and a passion for innovation, emerging technologies, and continuous improvement. Join Us If you're excited about helping people work smarter, improving business processes, and unlocking the potential of AI and emerging technologies, we'd love to hear from you. Join ISS and help drive the future of business transformation at CU Anschutz. Work Location: Hybrid – This position is eligible for a hybrid work environment. AMC ISS strives for a high-flex work environment, meaning although this role may predominately be executed effectively with a remote schedule, there may be instances where in-person meetings and/or activities are needed. There is no minimum or prescribed in-person requirement. The work schedule will be based around core working hours in Colorado Mountain Time. Why Join Us: Information Strategy and Services (ISS) partners across the campus to deliver information technology services that empower teaching, learning, research, and patient care. ISS is organized into four core functions: Technology & Infrastructure, Security & Compliance, and Business Strategy. Together, we connect service and technology . Our work is guided by six shared principles that connect our teams and shape how we serve our customers: Curiosity- Explore beyond one’s own experience and environment. Compassion- Demonstrates empathy, understanding, and respect for all people. Collaboration- Partner well beyond our space and build partnerships to achieve organizational results. Commitment- Dedication and engagement one has to their job, team, organization and university. Competence- Know our craft and be committed to continuous improvement and learning. Confidence- Be empowered and assured to represent our customers and their needs. Active investment in our culture and our people is foundational in developing and delivering service excellence. ​To cultivate a people centric workplace, we do the following: Growth & Development : Our Workforce Development Program builds critical skills and supports career advancement. Empowered Managers : Leaders are trained in coaching and team effectiveness to drive success. Open Communication : Stay connected through monthly town halls and annual summits. Wellness Focus : We prioritize employee well-being with supportive wellness initiatives. Coaching Culture : Continuous learning and feedback are part of how we grow together. Flexible Work : We offer flexible arrangements whenever possible to support work-life balance. Click here to find out more about ISS’s Culture The University of Colorado offers a comprehensive benefits package that includes health insurance, life insurance, retirement plans, tuition benefits, ECO pass, paid time off – vacation, sick, and holidays and more. To see what benefits are available, please visit: https://www.cu.edu/employee-services/benefits-wellness . Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 15/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Education: Bachelor’s degree in Information Systems, Computer Science, Engineering, Business, Education, or a closely related field Substitution : 4 years of professional or high-level technical work experience may be substituted for the bachelor’s degree. An associate’s degree with two years of relevant work experience may be substituted for the bachelor’s degree Experience: 2+ years of experience leading projects and initiatives as a project manager, project lead, or similar role. 1-2 years of experience supporting business analysis efforts through requirements gathering, process mapping, stakeholder engagement, and workflow analysis. 1-2 years of experience working with or supporting AI technologies, workflow automation platforms, and digital solutions that enhance business processes and operational efficiency. Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Preferred Qualifications: Experience working in or supporting higher education, research administration, grants management, financial compliance, or technology-focused organizations. Experience leading complex projects involving business transformation, process improvement, organizational change, and technology implementation. Experience with business analysis techniques, including requirements gathering, process mapping, workflow analysis, and stakeholder engagement. Familiarity with AI/ML technologies, workflow automation platforms, enterprise applications, data governance, APIs, integration platforms, cloud services, and related technologies. Professional certification in project management, Agile methodologies, business analysis, or change management (e.g., PMP, CAPM, CSM, CSPO, CBAP, CCBA, Prosci). Conditions of Employment: Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without requiring sponsorship. We are unable to provide work visa sponsorship or employment authorization for this position now or in the future. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Demonstrated ability to establish and maintain positive working relationships with stakeholders at all levels of the organization, including faculty, administrators, and technical teams. Excellent interpersonal, collaborative, and written/verbal communication skills, with the ability to translate complex technical concepts into accessible language for non-technical audiences. Strong facilitation skills for leading meetings, workshops, and cross-functional working sessions. Strong critical thinking and problem-solving skills with a data-informed mindset. Proven ability to manage projects successfully under various constraints using established project management methodologies and tools. Ability to gather, analyze, and document business requirements and translate them into functional specifications, including current and future state process mapping. Knowledge of change management principles and the ability to develop and execute change plans that drive user adoption. Understanding of AI/ML concepts, automation technologies, and data architectures, with the ability to apply that knowledge to evaluating, scoping, and implementing AI-driven solutions for administrative business processes. How to Apply: We value the thoughts you put into a C over Letter and would like to see your Resume, and List of References . For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position Resume Three to five professional references, including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Questions should be directed to: ISS Human Resources iss-humanresources@cuanschutz.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Applications will be accepted until finalists are identified, but preference will be given to complete applications received by September 25, 2026. Those who do not apply by this date may or may not be considered. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as $95,000 - $120,000. The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position may be eligible for overtime compensation, depending on the level. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@cuanschutz.edu . Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41158&lang=en": {
      "title": "Senior AI Support Engineer",
      "description": "Posted Date: Sep 18, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: ADM AVC OIT Administration Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Department: Information Strategy and Services Job Title: Senior AI Support Engineer Position #: 00853246 – Requisition #: 41158 Job Summary: Does building intelligent AI agents excite you? Are you passionate about helping others transform business processes through AI-powered automation? Do you enjoy solving complex technical challenges, integrating systems, and developing innovative solutions that create measurable impact? Are you someone who can balance technical expertise with exceptional customer service and collaboration? If so, the AI Support Engineer role may be the perfect fit for you! Our work helps faculty, staff, students, researchers, and administrative teams achieve better outcomes through the responsible use of AI technologies. As part of the AI and Research Computing team, you will play a critical role in designing, developing, supporting, and optimizing AI agents, workflows, and integrations that enhance productivity, improve service delivery, and accelerate innovation across the University. Ongoing AI Agent & Automation Support Includes: Designing, configuring, and supporting AI agents using approved enterprise AI platforms. Assisting departments with identifying use cases and translating business requirements into agent-based solutions. Providing front-line and advanced support for AI agents, automations, and integrations. Monitoring agent performance, troubleshooting issues, and optimizing solutions for reliability and effectiveness. Supporting users with onboarding, adoption, best practices, and agent lifecycle management. Additional Responsibilities Include: Developing and maintaining AI agents, copilots, and conversational experiences using enterprise AI platforms. Building and supporting integrations between AI platforms and campus systems, applications, databases, and knowledge repositories. Designing and maintaining workflows that leverage AI to automate business processes and improve operational efficiency. Troubleshooting technical issues related to AI agents, APIs, integrations, authentication, data access, and workflow execution. Developing and maintaining standard operating procedures, knowledge base articles, technical documentation, and implementation guides. Evaluating new AI capabilities, platforms, and development frameworks to provide recommendations on future enhancements. Supporting AI platform administration, permissions, access controls, and agent deployment processes. Assisting with AI governance and exception review processes to ensure solutions align with institutional standards and policies. Partnering with Information Security, Compliance, Legal, and Privacy teams to assess risks associated with AI agents, automations, and integrations. Collaborating with business stakeholders to gather requirements, prioritize enhancements, and deliver scalable AI solutions. Participating in vendor engagements and platform roadmap discussions related to AI agent technologies. Delivering training, workshops, office hours, and user enablement activities that increase AI literacy and successful adoption. Helping evaluate the security, compliance, operational, and data governance impacts of AI-powered solutions. Identifying opportunities to automate support processes and improve user experiences through AI agents and workflow automation. What Success Looks Like: AI agents and automations are reliable, secure, scalable, and aligned with institutional policies. Faculty, staff, students, and researchers successfully leverage AI agents to improve productivity and service delivery. Agent implementations solve meaningful business challenges and demonstrate measurable value. Integrations between AI platforms and enterprise systems are maintained and operate efficiently. AI solutions are documented, supportable, and continuously improved. The University maintains a robust portfolio of AI-enabled services that advance innovation while managing risk responsibly. Work Location: Hybrid – This position is eligible for a hybrid work environment. AMC ISS strives for a high-flex work environment, meaning although this role may predominately be executed effectively with a remote schedule, there may be instances where in-person meetings and/or activities are needed. There is no minimum or prescribed in-person requirement. The work schedule will be based around core working hours in Colorado Mountain Time. Why Join Us: Information Strategy and Services (ISS) partners across the campus to deliver information technology services that empower teaching, learning, research, and patient care. ISS is organized into four core functions: Technology & Infrastructure, Security & Compliance, Information & Data Enablement and Business Services. Together, we connect service and technology . Our work is guided by six shared principles that connect our teams and shape how we serve our customers: Curiosity- Explore beyond one’s own experience and environment. Compassion- Demonstrates empathy, understanding, and respect for all people. Collaboration- Partner well beyond our space and build partnerships to achieve organizational results. Commitment- Dedication and engagement one has to their job, team, organization and university. Competence- Know our craft and be committed to continuous improvement and learning. Confidence- Be empowered and assured to represent our customers and their needs. Active investment in our culture and our people is foundational in developing and delivering service excellence. ​To cultivate a people centric workplace, we do the following: Growth & Development : Our Workforce Development Program builds critical skills and supports career advancement. Empowered Managers : Leaders are trained in coaching and team effectiveness to drive success. Open Communication : Stay connected through monthly town halls and annual summits. Wellness Focus : We prioritize employee well-being with supportive wellness initiatives. Coaching Culture : Continuous learning and feedback are part of how we grow together. Flexible Work : We offer flexible arrangements whenever possible to support work-life balance. Click here to find out more about ISS’s Culture The University of Colorado offers a comprehensive benefits package that includes health insurance, life insurance, retirement plans, tuition benefits, ECO pass, paid time off – vacation, sick, and holidays and more. To see what benefits are available, please visit: https://www.cu.edu/employee-services/benefits-wellness . Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 15/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: SENIOR Education: A bachelor’s degree in computer science, management/computer information systems, computer engineering, information technology, or a directly related field from an accredited institution. Substitution: A combination of education and related technical/military/paraprofessional experience may be substituted for the bachelor’s degree on a year-for-year basis. Experience: 2-4 years of professional-level experience designing, building, deploying AI agents and automated workflows that solve real business problems. Experience with python, REST APIs, JSON, OAuth, and SQL for application development, data integration, and automation. Experience integrating AI agents with enterprise systems using LLM APIs, tool/function calling, MCP, or similar agent connectivity frameworks. PRINCIPAL Education: A bachelor’s degree in computer science, management/computer information systems, computer engineering, information technology, or a directly related field from an accredited institution. Substitution: A combination of education and related technical/military/paraprofessional experience may be substituted for the bachelor’s degree on a year-for-year basis. Experience: 3-5 years of professional-level experience designing, building, deploying AI agents and automated workflows that solve real business problems. Experience with python, REST APIs, JSON, OAuth, and SQL for application development, data integration, and automation. Experience integrating AI agents with enterprise systems using LLM APIs, tool/function calling, MCP, or similar agent connectivity frameworks. Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Preferred Qualifications: Experience developing AI agents using Microsoft Copilot Studio, Azure AI, OpenAI, Gemini, Claude, or similar technologies. Experience with Power Automate, Logic Apps, Boomi, TeamDynamix, or similar workflow automation platforms. Experience developing integrations using REST APIs, JSON, OAuth, web services, connectors, and enterprise application platforms. Experience with Python, Git/GitHub, SQL, AI development frameworks, and cloud-based development environments. Experience working in higher education, healthcare, research, or other regulated environments. Conditions of Employment: Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without requiring sponsorship. We are unable to provide work visa sponsorship or employment authorization for this position now or in the future. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Knowledge of enterprise AI platforms, agent development environments, generative AI, large language models (LLMs), retrieval-augmented generation (RAG), prompt engineering, and Model Context Protocol (MCP). Knowledge of Microsoft 365, cloud technologies, identity management, software development lifecycle principles, and enterprise application architecture. Skill in AI agent development, workflow automation, solution design, and business process optimization. Skill in developing integrations using REST APIs, JSON, HTTP, OAuth, enterprise connectors, web services, and related technologies. Skill in Python development, API consumption, technical troubleshooting, debugging, root cause analysis, and performance optimization. Skill in designing, deploying, and supporting AI-enabled solutions that meet business, operational, and technical requirements. Skill in developing technical documentation, knowledge resources, implementation guides, and training materials. Strong communication, customer service, collaboration, stakeholder engagement, and relationship management skills. Ability to translate business requirements into scalable AI-enabled solutions and workflows. Ability to independently manage competing priorities, solve complex technical problems, and identify opportunities for automation and innovation. Ability to evaluate security, privacy, compliance, and data governance considerations when designing and implementing AI solutions. Demonstrated commitment to innovation, continuous learning, accountability, collaboration, critical thinking, technical curiosity, and service excellence. How to Apply: We value the thoughts you put into a C over Letter and would like to see your Resume, and List of References . For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position Resume Three to five professional references, including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Questions should be directed to: ISS Human Resources iss-humanresources@cuanschutz.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Applications will be accepted until finalists are identified, but preference will be given to complete applications received by September 25, 2026. Those who do not apply by this date may or may not be considered. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as Senior: $120,000 - $140,000 Principal: $135,000 - $160,000 The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position may be eligible for overtime compensation, depending on the level. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@cuanschutz.edu ​. Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
