    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41420&lang=en": {
      "title": "Post Award Manager",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 14, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: SOM-EM MED CLINICAL Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Department: Department of Emergency Medicine Job Title: Post Award Manager Position #: 00853962 – Requisition #: 41420 Job Summary: The Post Award Manager provides strategic leadership and operational oversight for post-award grant administration and financial management, ensuring compliance with sponsor requirements, regulatory standards, and organizational policies. This role directs the development, review, and delivery of accurate grant financial reporting, leads the resolution of complex financial discrepancies, and implements process improvements that strengthen internal controls and financial stewardship. The Senior Manager oversees the validation of General Ledger (GL) activity, grant-funded payroll allocations and transfers, budget modifications, and financial analyses to support informed decision-making and effective resource management. The Post Award Manager also serves as the supervisor to post award staff members, providing support and guidance. Partners with executive leadership, principal investigators, program leaders, and cross-functional stakeholders to optimize grant operations, maximize funding utilization, and mitigate financial and compliance risks. Leads operational planning and prioritization across a diverse portfolio of grants, balancing competing demands while ensuring timely execution of post-award activities. Serves as a trusted advisor on complex financial and operational matters, translating technical information into actionable insights and recommendations for audiences across all organizational levels. Fosters a culture of accountability, continuous improvement, and customer service excellence while driving operational effectiveness and long-term organizational success. Key Responsibilities: Operational and Administrative Management 50%: Provides leadership in the formulation and implementation of Emergency Medicine research policies and procedures and ensures these are in place and are reviewed on an annual basis and updated as needed. Oversee day-to-day administrative operations and resource allocation. Serve as a communication conduit across all levels of post award activities. Provide high-level administrative support to PIs, project leads, and co-investigators. Assist in strategic planning, communication and execution of major project functions. Act as a liaison between Emergency Medicine leadership, as well as all project stakeholders and project managers. Maintain documentation and reporting systems to support transparency and accountability. Partner with Human Resources to recruit, hire, onboard, and train new team members, ensuring a seamless integration and alignment with organizational goals Actively direct workload across all supervised positions. Meet regularly with PIs and post award staff to ensure objective attainment and correct process and procedure and being followed. Fiscal and Post Award Management (50%): Administer the awards and oversight of all post-award operations. Track program milestones, deliverables, and financial performance. Align financial resources with goals and programmatic priorities. Oversee the submissions of the annual Research Performance Progress Reports. Collaborate with PIs to develop and manage annual budgets. Work closely with the post award team on funding projections and spending. Monitor and review monthly expenditures to ensure fiscal responsibility. Approve purchases and expenditures when required, ensuring alignment with budgetary constraints. Manage invoicing processes and ensure timely payments and reimbursements. Assist in the preparation and submission of progress reports and financial summaries. Conduct regular financial forecasting, variance analysis, and scenario planning to support executive decision-making and long-term sustainability. Ensure all contractual obligations are fulfilled accurately and on time. Oversee all subcontract administration, including drafting, reviewing, and managing agreements and communicating with the subcontracted entities. Lead audit preparation and ensure adherence to internal controls, grant requirements, and regulatory standards. Review and monitor all research related procurement activities to ensure compliance with internal and external policies. Approve research purchase requests and ensure proper documentation is maintained. Monitor and approve high-value expenditures, maintain cost controls, and implement financial safeguards to ensure optimal use of funds. Work closely with internal teams and external partners to ensure transparency, accountability, and alignment across all financial activities. Serve as a liaison between finance, program staff, and leadership to support strategic goals. Work Location: Hybrid/Remote – In-State Candidates: this role is eligible for a hybrid schedule of 3 days per week on campus in Aurora, CO and as needed for in-person meetings. We will also consider fully remote applicants located within the United States. Why Join Us: The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is a public education, clinical and research facility serving 4,500 students, and a world-class medical destination at the forefront of life-changing science, medicine, and healthcare. CU Anschutz offers more than 42 highly rated degree programs through 6 schools and colleges, and receives over $500 million in research awards each year. We are the single largest health professions education provider in Colorado, awarding nearly 1,450 degrees annually. Powered by our award-winning faculty, renowned researchers and a reputation for academic excellence, the CU Anschutz Medical Campus drives innovation from the classroom to the laboratory to the delivery of unparalleled patient care. Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 15/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's degree from an accredited institution and 4-6 years of professional experience related to grants administration, fiscal oversight and administrative management. A combination of education and related technical/military/paraprofessional experience may be substituted for a bachelor’s degree on a year for year basis. An advanced degree (Masters or Doctorate) may be substituted for experience on a year for year basis if the degree is in a field of study directly related to the work assignment. Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Preferred Qualifications: Master’s degree in a related field. 6+ of years of high level experience in academic and research grants management administration. This position requires progressively responsible, diverse and extensive experience in contract management, grants management and financial management. Experience with complex federally-funded research projects. Experience with financial and research leadership. Experience supervising multiple FTEs. Experience with CU financial platforms (e.g. Concur, Marketplace, etc.). Experience with project and program management software (including Excel and Smartsheet). Certified Clinical Research Professional (CCRP) or Association of Clinical Research Professional (ACRP) certification. Conditions of Employment: Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without requiring sponsorship. We are unable to provide work visa sponsorship or employment authorization for this position now or in the future. Travel may be required. Maintain pre- and post-award university training requirements. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Demonstrate strong understanding of academic grant management, financial acumen and research administration. Strong knowledge of federally-funded research regulatory frameworks and compliance standards. Proven ability to manage complex projects and lead cross-functional teams. Proven ability to manage complex federal grants that have multiple subcontracts. Familiarity with academic research environments and collaborative science initiatives. Ability to navigate ambiguity and adapt to evolving priorities. Strong knowledge of research regulatory frameworks and compliance standards. Ability to communicate effectively, both in writing and orally. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with employees at all levels throughout the institution. Outstanding customer service skills. How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position Curriculum vitae / Resume Three to five professional references, including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Questions should be directed to: EMED Human Resources at emed.humanresources@cudenver.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Immediately and continues until position is filled. For best consideration, apply by October 30, 2026. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as $73,765 – $98,845. The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position may be eligible for overtime compensation, depending on the level. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@cuanschutz.edu ​. Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41409&lang=en": {
      "title": "Electronics Specialist I",
      "description": "Closing Date: 10/24/2026 Posted Date: Oct 14, 2026 Job category: Classified Staff Department: SDM-Dental Clinic Support Srvc Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Department: School of Dental Medicine — Dental Clinic Support Services Job Title: Electronics Specialist I Position: #00683505 — Requisition: #41409 Job Summary: The Electronics Specialist I installs, maintains, troubleshoots, tests, and repairs dental equipment used in the School of Dental Medicine’s patient clinics, simulation clinics, and laboratory/research areas. The position supports reliable equipment operation for patient care and clinical education, following manufacturer specifications, service manuals, and applicable requirements. The assignment also includes facility maintenance and repair support and monitoring of crash carts and emergency cabinets. Key Responsibilities Assemble, install, maintain, troubleshoot, and repair dental equipment in patient clinics, simulation clinics, and laboratory/research areas. Calibrate and safety-test dental equipment, working with a certified technician for x-ray and nitrous oxide systems. Monitor equipment for damage or malfunctions, monitor nitrous oxide/oxygen and other supply levels, and arrange manufacturer repairs as needed. Prioritize repair requests and communicate equipment status and repair timeframes to faculty, staff, and students. Support facility maintenance and repairs, address school personnel’s requests, and coordinate work beyond the position’s expertise with Campus Facilities or other appropriate departments. Check assigned crash carts and emergency cabinets, maintain inventories, monitor oxygen levels and equipment function, and report problems to responsible parties. Work Location: Onsite - this role is expected to work onsite in Aurora, Colorado. The requested schedule is four 10-hour days per week. Why Join Us: Join the School of Dental Medicine’s Support Services team and help keep the equipment and facilities used for patient care and clinical education operating reliably. This role combines hands-on dental equipment maintenance and repair with facility support and emergency equipment checks, working with faculty, staff, students, and service providers. Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement Plans: State pension (PERA Defined Benefit) or 401(a) - Employer contributes between 10% and 21.5% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year Vacation Days: Between 12/year and 24/year (maximum accrual between 192 hours and 384 hours) – specific amount depends on length of total State of Colorado service Sick Days: 10/year (360 hour maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 15/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Please make sure to include the following in your resume: job title, duties, months and years employed, and average hours worked per week as minimum experience is calculated on a 40 hour/week basis. Minimum Qualifications One (1) year of relevant mechanical and/or equipment repair experience. Substitution : A combination of related education and/or relevant experience in an occupation related to the work assigned equal to one (1) year. Colorado law requires that candidates for state government jobs be residents of Colorado at the time of application. Preferred Qualifications Experience working with dental or medical equipment. Experience working in facilities. Computer experience. Previous experience working in a dental education setting. Conditions of Employment Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without requiring sponsorship. We are unable to provide work visa sponsorship or employment authorization for this position now or in the future. Work onsite in Aurora, Colorado. Successfully complete the required criminal background and sex offender registry checks. Work a four-day, 10-hour-per-day schedule. Knowledge Skills and Abilities Outstanding interpersonal skills and ability to establish rapport with a wide variety of individuals. Ability to prioritize and multitask. Excellent time management skills. Ability to work independently and exercise judgment in decision making. Excellent customer service skills. Strong oral communication skills. How to Apply: Questions should be directed to: Oscar De Moya, oscar.demoya@cuanschutz.edu Application Materials Instructions: APPLICATION DEADLINE: This announcement is open until 10 days after posting. To apply, please submit the following materials to this posting: A cover letter and resume that specifically addresses the job requirements and outlines your qualifications. Special Instructions to Applicants Classified Staff positions have specific application requirements: Submit all required documents indicated in this posting and include a current email address and phone number. Please address minimum qualifications, competencies and preferred qualifications in your cover letter, as these along with previous work experience will be used in the assessment process. Click here to view Veteran and other General Information regarding Classified Staff positions: https://www.cu.edu/cu-careers/special-instructions-classified-staff-applicants For those who meet minimum qualifications, the comparative analysis process will include one or all of the following: Preferred Qualifications Application Review based on the preferred qualifications listed in the posting. Candidates will be evaluated and rated against the preferred qualifications based on information submitted within their application materials. Note: Candidates are not physically present for this portion of the comparative analysis. Interviews based on the job requirements, preferred qualifications and competencies listed in the posting. Candidates will be evaluated, scored and ranked based on oral responses Interviews may be over the phone, videoconference or in-person You will be notified via email if the comparative analysis process changes or includes additional assessment tools other than those listed above. Anticipated Pay Range: The proposed starting salary is $4,336 - $5,203 per month. This position is eligible for overtime compensation. The above hiring range represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. If you have prior state-classified service in the same class series as this position, your pay may be set at a higher amount per the state Step Pay Program implemented on July 1, 2024. For more information about the Step Pay Program, please visit the 2024 Step Pay Program for State of Colorado Employees | DHR . Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@cuanschutz.edu ​. Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students, and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41417&lang=en": {
      "title": "Open Rank (Entry – Senior) Research Services Clinical Science Professional",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 14, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: SOM-EM MED CLINICAL Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus Department: School of Medicine - Department of Emergency Medicine Job Title: Open Rank (Entry – Senior) Research Services Clinical Science Professional Position #: 00853955 – Requisition #: 41417 Job Summary: The Department of Emergency Medicine is seeking applications for a Open Rank (Entry – Senior) Research Services Clinical Science Professional . This is a full-time, University staff position to support ongoing grant-funded studies focused on mental health and firearm storage. The Clinical Science Professional will join a highly collaborative and exciting multi-disciplinary team (PI: Dr. Ian Stanley, PhD) that has an active research program domestically and internationally. The PI conducts research related to the prevention of psychological health conditions (e.g., suicide, posttraumatic stress disorder) across various populations (e.g., military service members, veterans, first responders, civilians). This research involves observational studies and interventional trials related to the understanding and prevention of psychological health morbidities. This position will focus on projects related to lethal means safety in veteran/military populations. This position requires familiarity and experience with clinical or public health research, preferably in psychological health and/or behavioral health. The ideal candidate will have experience within research (clinical or behavioral), collaborate effectively on multidisciplinary teams, and be highly detail oriented. Key Responsibilities: Clinical Trials Research Support (100%): Assist with and oversee the day to day operations of clinical trials and studies Review research protocol inclusion/exclusion criteria, and confirms eligibility of subject to participate in clinical trial Perform informed consent process or ensures that the informed consent process has occurred, is properly documented, and that informed consent form documents are filed as required Interview prospective subjects for a variety of research clinical trials. Educate potential subjects on the details of the studies through phone contacts and personal interviews Schedule subject participation in research clinical trial, coordinating availability of necessary space, and clinical research support (e.g., physician, nurse practitioner, laboratory, radiology, pharmacy) Collect, code, and analyze data obtained from research in an accurate and timely manner Adhere to research regulatory standards Maintain detailed records of studies to ensure compliance with requirements of the Food and Drug Administration (FDA), study protocols, department, hospital/clinical standard operating procedures and other regulatory guidelines Participate in subject recruitment efforts, including communicating with patients expressing an interest and all pre-screening/screening activities Intermediate Independently master study materials, including but not limited to protocols, informed consent forms, and all other essential study documents for assigned studies Independently perform study related processes, procedures, and assessments as defined in study protocol and in compliance with regulating bodies Assist Team Leads, Supervisors and/or management with creation and implementation of processes and procedures and quality improvement initiatives Act as a Primary Coordinator on multiple trials/studies Assist and train junior team members Senior Assist with developing or develops protocol-specific systems and documents including process flows, training manuals, Standard Operating Procedures (SOPs) and Case Report Forms (CRFs). Maintains subject level documentation and prepares documents, equipment and/or supplies Assist with identifying issues related to operational efficiency and shares results with leadership Collect information to determine feasibility, recruitment and retention strategies. Employ, evaluate and assist with the implementation of innovative solutions to maximize recruitment and retention Serve as a resource and participate in study initiation and close out duties Additional Duties & Responsibilities: Conduct qualitative interviews Design surveys This description is a summary only and is describing the general level of work being performed, it is not intended to be all-inclusive. The duties of this position may change from time to time and/or based on business need. We reserve the right to add or delete duties and responsibilities at the discretion of the supervisor and/or hiring authority. Work Location: Hybrid – this role is eligible for a hybrid schedule of 3 days per week on campus and as needed for in-person meetings. Why Join Us: The Department of Emergency Medicine at the University of Colorado School of Medicine is dedicated to delivering superlative patient care, providing an environment where training and education thrive and innovation and discovery are fostered. The Department of Emergency Medicine is based at the Anschutz Medical Campus in Aurora Colorado. The campus is a state of the art medical campus home to the University of Colorado Schools of Medicine, Nursing, Dentistry, Pharmacy, the Colorado School of Public Health; as well as the University of Colorado Hospital and Children's Hospital Colorado both of which serve as major training sites for the Denver Health Residency in Emergency Medicine. Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 10/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Entry: Bachelor’s degree in any field Intermediate Bachelor’s degree in any field One (1) year clinical research or related experience Senior Bachelor’s degree in any field Two (2) years clinical research or related experience Substitution: A combination of education and related technical/military/paraprofessional experience may be substituted for a bachelor’s degree on a year for year basis. An advanced degree (Masters or PhD) may be substituted for experience on a year for year basis if the degree is in a field of study directly related to the work assignment. Preferred Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in science or health related field Intermediate Two (2) years of clinical research or related experience Experience with electronic data capture systems (e.g. EMR or EHR and data management systems) Senior Three (3) years of clinical research or related experience Experience conducting qualitative interviews Experience with survey design Master’s degree in psychology, public health, behavioral health, or a research-related discipline Strong interest or previous experience working in psychological health, public health, or behavioral health Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Knowledge and understanding of federal regulations and Good Clinical Practice (GCP) Ability to communicate effectively, both in writing and orally Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with employees at all levels throughout the institution Outstanding customer service skills Knowledge of basic human anatomy, physiology medical terminology Ability to interpret and master complex research protocol information Excellent written and oral communication skills Excellent organizational and interpersonal skills Ability to think creatively, adapt quickly and work independently Excellent team player Self-starter with a desire to improve human health through research High Level Skills with Computer-Based Tools (Word, Outlook, PowerPoint, Etc.) Conditions of Employment: Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without requiring sponsorship. We are unable to provide work visa sponsorship or employment authorization for this position now or in the future. How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position Curriculum vitae / Resume Three to five professional references, including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Questions should be directed to: EMED Human Resources at emed.humanresources@ucdenver.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Immediately and continues until position is filled. For best consideration, apply by 11/15/26. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as HIRING RANGE: Entry: $49,899 – $66,865 Intermediate: $54,302 - $72,765 Senior: $58,705 – $78,665 The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position may be eligible for overtime compensation, depending on the level. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@cuanschutz.edu ​. Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41416&lang=en": {
      "title": "Senior Application & Infrastructure Engineer",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 14, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: ADM AVC OIT Administration Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Department: Information Strategy and Services Job Title: Senior Application & Infrastructure Engineer Position # 00678914: – Requisition #: 41416 Job Summary: Are you an experienced application and infrastructure engineer who enjoys solving complex technical problems and building reliable, secure enterprise platforms? Do you thrive at the intersection of applications, servers, cloud services, identity, integrations, databases, and automation? Join Information Strategy and Services (ISS) and help support the technology foundation that enables the University of Colorado Anschutz to advance education, research, healthcare, and service to our communities. About the Role The Senior Application & Infrastructure Engineer is a senior member of the IAM and Data Infrastructure (IDI) team responsible for designing, implementing, maintaining, and supporting highly available, secure, scalable, and resilient enterprise technology platforms. This role supports critical server, cloud, identity, integration, database, and application environments while helping improve reliability, security, performance, and operational efficiency. What You’ll Do This is a hands-on opportunity for an experienced engineer who enjoys troubleshooting complex systems, automating operational work, partnering across technical teams, and continuously improving enterprise services. The position also participates in periodic after-hours outage and patching support. Deploy, administer, maintain, and support enterprise application platforms and services, including single sign-on and multifactor authentication services. Administer application environments across on-premises and cloud-hosted platforms, including middleware, web services, databases, integrations, containers, and identity-enabled applications. Perform application upgrades, patches, configuration changes, migrations, release support, and lifecycle management activities. Monitor application availability, performance, logging, integrations, and service health, and diagnose complex disruptions in coordination with technical teams and vendors. Implement security controls, system hardening, vulnerability remediation, and monitoring practices that support university standards and regulatory requirements. Develop and maintain automation for application administration, deployment support, configuration management, monitoring, and operational workflows. Support backup, recovery, continuity, failover readiness, and restoration validation for critical application platforms. Create technical documentation, standard operating procedures, architectural diagrams, and support resources while providing guidance and knowledge sharing across the team. What You’ll Bring Strong analytical, troubleshooting, and problem-solving skills across complex, multi-tier enterprise systems. Experience administering Linux and/or Windows server environments, including configuration, patching, troubleshooting, performance tuning, automation, and shell scripting. Experience supporting cloud-based applications, virtualization technologies, container workloads, and enterprise infrastructure platforms. Knowledge of information security principles, standards, frameworks, and best practices. The ability to communicate complex technical information to technical and non-technical audiences and collaborate effectively across teams. Curiosity, initiative, sound judgment, and a commitment to continuous learning and service excellence. Work Location: Hybrid – This position is eligible for a hybrid work environment. AMC ISS strives for a high-flex work environment, meaning although this role may predominately be executed effectively with a remote schedule, there may be instances where in-person meetings and/or activities are needed. There is no minimum or prescribed in-person requirement. The work schedule will be based around core working hours in Colorado Mountain Time. Why Join Us: Information Strategy and Services (ISS) partners across the campus to deliver information technology services that empower teaching, learning, research, and patient care. ISS is organized into three core functions: Technology & Infrastructure, Security & Compliance, and Business Strategy. Together, we connect service and technology . Our work is guided by six shared principles that connect our teams and shape how we serve our customers: Curiosity- Explore beyond one’s own experience and environment. Compassion- Demonstrates empathy, understanding, and respect for all people. Collaboration- Partner well beyond our space and build partnerships to achieve organizational results. Commitment- Dedication and engagement one has to their job, team, organization and university. Competence- Know our craft and be committed to continuous improvement and learning. Confidence- Be empowered and assured to represent our customers and their needs. Active investment in our culture and our people is foundational in developing and delivering service excellence. ​To cultivate a people centric workplace, we do the following: Growth & Development : Our Workforce Development Program builds critical skills and supports career advancement. Empowered Managers : Leaders are trained in coaching and team effectiveness to drive success. Open Communication : Stay connected through monthly town halls and annual summits. Wellness Focus : We prioritize employee well-being with supportive wellness initiatives. Coaching Culture : Continuous learning and feedback are part of how we grow together. Flexible Work : We offer flexible arrangements whenever possible to support work-life balance. Click here to find out more about ISS’s Culture You will work across a broad enterprise technology ecosystem rather than within a single platform. The role combines application engineering, infrastructure operations, security, automation, service reliability, and technical leadership, providing an opportunity to make a visible impact on the stable and secure technology services that support the CU Anschutz mission. If you're excited to strengthen enterprise platforms, improve reliability through automation, and solve challenging technical problems with a collaborative team, we want to hear from you! The University of Colorado offers a comprehensive benefits package that includes health insurance, life insurance, retirement plans, tuition benefits, ECO pass, paid time off – vacation, sick, and holidays and more. To see what benefits are available, please visit: https://www.cu.edu/employee-services/benefits-wellness . Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 15/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Education: Bachelor’s degree in Information Systems, Computer Science, Information Technology, Engineering, Cybersecurity, or a closely related field. Substitution : 4 years of professional or high-level technical work experience may be substituted for the bachelor’s degree. An associate’s degree with two years of relevant work experience may be substituted for the bachelor’s degree Experience: 2 years of progressively responsible experience supporting applications in the enterprise environment, systems administration, cloud services, platform operations, or site reliability engineering functions. 2 years administering enterprise Linux and/or Windows server environments. Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Preferred Qualifications: 5 or more years of experience as a Systems Administrator, Infrastructure Engineer, Operations Engineer, or Site Reliability Engineer. Experience supporting public cloud platforms including Microsoft Azure or Oracle Cloud Infrastructure (OCI). Experience with infrastructure automation, configuration management, and Infrastructure as Code technologies. Experience with enterprise monitoring, alerting, logging, and observability platforms. Experience supporting common web technologies including Apache, NGINX, Node.js, PHP, Web Application Firewalls, and Load Balancers. Experience administering enterprise database platforms including Oracle, Microsoft SQL Server, MySQL/MariaDB, and PostgreSQL. Experience with CI/CD platforms and tools such as GitHub, Jenkins, or Azure DevOps. Experience supporting Integration Platform as a Service (iPaaS) technologies such as Boomi or MuleSoft. Familiarity with Identity and Access Management technologies including Active Directory, SAML, OAuth/OIDC, SCIM, Oracle Identity Governance, Oracle Unified Directory, Oracle Identity Domains, and Grouper. Experience working within higher education, healthcare, research, or other complex enterprise environments. Conditions of Employment: Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without requiring sponsorship. We are unable to provide work visa sponsorship or employment authorization for this position now or in the future. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Demonstrated curiosity, initiative, and commitment to continuous learning and professional growth. Strong analytical, troubleshooting, and problem-solving skills. Ability to prioritize competing demands and manage multiple tasks in a fast-paced environment. Ability to work independently while effectively collaborating within cross-functional teams. Excellent verbal, written, and interpersonal communication skills. Strong organizational, planning, and time management skills. Ability to communicate complex technical concepts to both technical and non-technical audiences. Knowledge of information security principles, standards, frameworks, and best practices. Experience administering Linux and Windows server environments. Experience with administering container workloads with technologies such as Docker, Podman or Kubernetes. Experience supporting virtualization technologies and enterprise infrastructure platforms. Experience supporting cloud-based applications and services. Ability to troubleshoot complex multi-tier systems spanning applications, containers, operating systems, databases, directories, networking, identity platforms, and cloud infrastructure. Proficiency in Linux administration including system configuration, patching, troubleshooting, performance tuning, automation, and shell scripting. Strong customer service orientation and commitment to service excellence. How to Apply: We value the thoughts you put into a C over Letter and would like to see your Resume, and List of References . For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position Resume Three to five professional references, including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Questions should be directed to: ISS Human Resources iss-humanresources@cuanschutz.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Immediately and continues until position is filled. For best consideration, apply by October 25, 2025. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as $78,051 - $93,143 The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position may be eligible for overtime compensation, depending on the level. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@cuanschutz.edu . Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41412&lang=en": {
      "title": "Assistant to the Assistant Dean of Communications",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 14, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: SOM-DEAN DO ADMINISTRATION Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Department: School of Medicine Office of the Dean Job Title: Assistant to the Assistant Dean of Communications Position #: 00 849889 – Requisition #: 41412 Job Summary: The School of Medicine (SOM) Dean’s Office seeks a full-time Assistant to the Assistant Dean of Communications who will work at the direction of the Assistant Dean of Communications for the CU School of Medicine Dean’s Office Administration. This person will work independently and as part of a team of five, coordinating projects, organizing activities, and providing administrative support to the Dean’s Office and the Assistant Dean. Key Responsibilities: (20%) Deliver high-quality customer service and operational support , including front office reception duties, collaboration with administrative staff, and maintaining professionalism and confidentiality in all interactions. (20%) Provide comprehensive administrative support to the Dean’s Office , including calendar management, meeting coordination, presentation preparation, and maintaining contact lists and shared resources. (20%) Manage executive-level meetings and events , including organizing Executive Committee meetings, preparing agendas and minutes, and ensuring all follow-up actions are completed. (20%) Oversee procurement and financial activities , such as handling purchasing, reconciling travel and procurement cards, and ensuring compliance with university policies. (10%) Coordinate communications operations by collecting content for the annual report, preparing materials, tracking project costs, and supporting the School of Medicine Communications team’s scheduling and logistics. (10%) Support leadership recruitment processes by coordinating search logistics, scheduling interviews, managing candidate communications, and ensuring required HR documentation and compliance. Work Location: Hybrid – this role is eligible for a hybrid schedule of four (4) days per week on campus and as needed for in-person meetings. Why Join Us: The University of Colorado Anschutz is a world-class academic medical campus leading transformative advances in science, medicine, education, and patient care. The campus includes the University of Colorado’s health professional schools, more than 60 centers and institutes, and two nationally ranked independent hospitals - UCHealth University of Colorado Hospital and Children's Hospital Colorado - which see nearly three million adult and pediatric patient visits each year. Innovative, interconnected, and highly collaborative, CU Anschutz delivers life-changing treatments, exceptional patient care, and top-tier professional training. The campus conducts world-renowned research supported by $890 million in funding, including $762 million in sponsored awards and $128 million in philanthropic gifts for research. Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation, and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 15/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced-rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Entry Level: Bachelor’s degree in communications or a related field. Substitution: A combination of education and related technical/military/paraprofessional experience may be substituted for a bachelor’s degree on a year-for-year basis. Intermediate Level: Bachelor’s degree in communications or a related field. Substitution: A combination of education and related technical/military/paraprofessional experience may be substituted for a bachelor’s degree on a year-for-year basis. One (1) year of professional experience providing support to leadership and managing projects. Senior Level: Bachelor’s degree in communications or a related field. Substitution: A combination of education and related technical/military/paraprofessional experience may be substituted for a bachelor’s degree on a year-for-year basis. Two (2) years of professional experience providing support to leadership and managing projects. Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Preferred Qualifications: Experience in higher education. Experience in editorial production. Conditions of Employment: Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without requiring sponsorship. We are unable to provide work visa sponsorship or employment authorization for this position now or in the future. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Ability to work independently as well as within a team. Advanced written, verbal, and professional interpersonal skills. Exceptional attention to detail. The ability to navigate a complex academic environment. Excellent organizational skills and the ability to effectively prioritize. Exercise judgment and independent initiative. Handle sensitive and confidential matters. Proven knowledge of Microsoft Office products, including Outlook, Word, Excel, and PowerPoint. How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position Curriculum vitae / Resume Three to five professional references, including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Questions should be directed to: Office of Communications, somcommunications@cuanschutz.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Immediately and continues until the position is filled. For best consideration, apply within fifteen (15) days of the posting date . Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as: Entry Level: $52,374 to $66,620 Intermediate Level: $56,995 to $72,498 Senior Level: $61,616 to $78,376 The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position may be eligible for overtime compensation, depending on the level. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans, and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@cuanschutz.edu . Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students, and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine-preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety-sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41411&lang=en": {
      "title": "Instructor/Fellow",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 14, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: SOM-PEDS Critical Care-GenOps Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Department: Pediatrics, Section of Critical Care Job Title: Instructor/ Fellow Position #:00853884 – Requisition #:41411 Job Summary: The Pediatric Advanced Practice Fellowship is a 12-month post-graduate program dedicated to enhancing the development of early-career Pediatric Nurse Practitioners and Physician Assistants or for those new to pediatric hospital-based medicine. Recognizing that PNPs and PAs are increasingly utilized in inpatient care models, our program’s mission is providing the knowledge, skills and attitudes necessary for a provider to succeed in the challenging world of pediatric inpatient medicine. Fellows will rotate through various sections within Children’s Hospital Colorado and will provide patient care under the direction of a supervising physician faculty member. Key Responsibilities: · Rotates through general ward pediatrics, pediatric intensive care unit, pulmonary, oncology, cardiology and electives. · Practices as a fully credentialed provider caring for pediatric patients under the supervision of an attending physician. · Gathers pertinent information systematically and skillfully from all sources: history, diagnostic tests, and comprehensive physical examinations, behavioral and developmental assessments. · Communicates verbally all pertinent patient information to the on call attending physician, nursing staff, and other relevant healthcare providers. · Rounds daily on patients based upon a rotating schedule and collaborates with the attending physician, other attending physicians from consulting services, and with the healthcare team to assess, diagnose, plan, set priorities and realistic outcomes, and evaluate the effectiveness and cost efficiency of patient care · Formulates management plans in conjunction · with the attending physician and evaluates patient physiologic and behavioral responses to these management plans. · Documents daily all relevant data including but not limited to results of diagnostic tests, laboratory results, patients’ condition, response to therapies/interventions, and follow-up interventions. · Communicates with the family regarding the changing health care needs of their child. · Accurately and appropriately performs routine diagnostic and therapeutic techniques according to established protocol and current pediatric critical care standards. · Initiates and performs measures necessary to resuscitate and stabilize a compromised pediatric patient according to current critical care and AHA standards. · Keeps knowledge base current by reading professional literature, attending educational programs, and reviewing changes in health legislation and relevant professional research. · Participates in interdisciplinary quality improvement and/or research activities. · Participates in documenting outcome measures. · Identifies potential areas for research. · Completes didactic work including attending lectures, completing online modules, outlined fellowship curriculum, simulations and case-studies. · Undergoes evaluation for successful completion of the fellowship program to include direct observation, written evaluation, and capstone project. Work Location: Onsite – this role is expected to work onsite and is located in Aurora, CO. Why Join Us: The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is a public education, clinical, and research facility serving 4,500 students and is a world-class medical destination at the forefront of life-changing science, medicine, and healthcare. CU Anschutz offers more than 42 highly rated degree programs through 6 schools and colleges and receives over $762 million in research awards each year. We are the single largest health professions education provider in Colorado, awarding nearly 1,450 degrees annually. Powered by our award-winning faculty, renowned researchers, and a reputation for academic excellence, the CU Anschutz Medical Campus drives innovation from the classroom to the laboratory to the delivery of unparalleled patient care. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Physician Assistant: Graduation from an APAP approved Physician Assistant Training Program. Certification from the National Commission on Certification of Physician Assistants. Colorado license will be required prior to start date. ACLS and PALS certification will be required prior to start date. Or Acute Care Pediatric Nurse Practitioner: Graduate of an accredited BSN program. APN licensure and a Masters from an accredited Nurse Practitioner program. ACLS and PALS certification will be required prior to start date. Pediatric Nursing Certification Board certificate or other comparable certification required. Acute Care Nurse Practitioner certification required. Ability to obtain Prescriptive Authority in the State of Colorado. Will need to qualify for and obtain prescriptive authority within one year of beginning position. Condition of Employment: · Must successfully pass a drug test through Children’s Hospital Colorado · Must be willing and able to pass a national criminal background check *For questions regarding Children’s Hospital drug testing requirements, please contact Children’s Human Resources at 720-777-8598. Some positions may require testing if access to Children’s Hospital or their systems is needed at any time during employment with the University. If drug testing is required, it will be listed in the job posting. Preferred Qualifications: · Previous experience in a pediatric clinical setting · Previous experience working in a multidisciplinary team · Previous experience working in a hospital setting Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: · Ability to communicate effectively; · Ability to handle stressful situations with professional composure; · Skill in prioritizing patient and system needs appropriately; · Knowledge and skill in customer service delivery; · Ability to work well both independently and aspart of a team; · Well organized and efficient in their work; · Knowledge of quality improvement, family-centered care, and evidence based practice. How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): 1. A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position 2. Curriculum vitae / Resume 3. Five professional references including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers . Questions should be directed to: appfellowship@childrenscolorado.org Screening of Applications Begins: This position may be seeking multiple candidates. Positions will remain open until filled. Applications will be reviewed as they are received, and candidates may be contacted for interviews throughout the posting period. Upon candidate(s) selection, the posting will be closed, and no further applications will be accepted. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary for this position has been established as: $80,470 The above salary represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the salary at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation unless it is non-exempt. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Equal Opportunity Statement: The University of Colorado (CU) is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@ucdenver.edu ​. Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41376&lang=en": {
      "title": "Lifecycle Grants & Contracts Professional (Open Rank)",
      "description": "Closing Date: 10/29/2026 Posted Date: Oct 14, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: CON-DEAN ADMINISTRATION Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Department: College of Nursing Job Title: Lifecycle Grants & Contracts Professional (Open Rank) Position #: 00604231 – Requisition #:41376 Job Summary: CU Nursing’s Office of Research and Scholarship is seeking an open-rank Lifecycle Grants & Contracts Professional (Entry Professional through Principal Professional) to support sponsored research administration. This position provides expertise across the research grant and contract lifecycle, with primary responsibility in either pre-award or post-award administration based on organizational needs and the candidate’s experience. Working closely with faculty, Principal Investigators (PIs), Research Service Professionals (RSPs), postdoctoral fellows, students, and administrative partners, the position supports the effective and compliant management of sponsored research. Responsibilities may include proposal preparation and submission, budget development and monitoring, award setup, financial management, reporting, procurement, subaward administration, project closeout, and other research administration activities. The position collaborates with the Lifecycle Grants and Contracts Program Manager and Office of Research and Scholarship staff to provide coordinated research administration services and contribute to training, knowledge sharing, and process improvement efforts. Successful candidates will demonstrate sound judgment, attention to detail, accountability, and the ability to identify and address issues proactively. Examples of Work Performed: The duties below apply across all ranks, with the complexity of work, size of the assigned portfolio, and level of independence scaled to the rank at hire. Duties listed under Advanced Responsibilities are expected of Senior and Principal Professionals. Pre-Award and Proposal Development (30%) Manage the pre-award lifecycle for an assigned portfolio of CU Nursing faculty, postdoc fellows, and students, including funding opportunity review, proposal planning, budget development, administrative compliance, internal routing, sponsor communication, and timely submission of proposals. Coordinate with the University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus Office of Grants and Contracts (OGC), CU Nursing Finance, and other University partners to obtain required approvals and documentation and facilitate timely proposal submission. Coordinate the transition from funded proposal to award, working with OGC and other University partners to facilitate award acceptance, account setup, subaward execution, requests for pre-award spending, Just in Time (JIT), and other post-submission activities. Post-Award Grant and Contract Management (30%) Manage post-award grants and contracts, including award setup, budget oversight, compliance, reporting, subawards, extensions, and closeout. Monitor expenditures, projections, and compliance; identify risks and advise PIs on award management. Coordinate with University offices to resolve award, financial, and administrative issues. Support sponsor reporting (RPPRs, NCEs, FFRs) and reconcile award, subaward, and financial records. Financial and Operational Management (20%) Support research financial activities, including funding distributions, effort management, HCM transactions, PETs, procurement, and gift card programs. Utilize University and sponsor systems, including HCM, InfoEd, CU Marketplace, Grants.gov, eRA Commons, and SAM.gov. Assist faculty with effort reporting, funding tracking, purchasing, invoicing, and compliance requirements. Manage procurement card reconciliation and research-funded incentive programs. Training and Collaboration (10%) Serve as a resource to faculty and research teams on research administration policies, systems, and sponsor requirements. Maintain expertise in research administration and communicate regulatory, policy, and process updates. Collaborate with Finance, HR, Academic Affairs, IT, and other University partners to support research operations and compliance. Process Improvement, Data, and Support (10%) Identify opportunities to improve processes within assigned areas and share recommendations with the Program Manager. Maintain accurate and accessible grant and contract documentation and contribute to the maintenance of CU Nursing research archives. Contribute to special projects and initiatives assigned by the Lifecycle Grants and Contracts Program Manager and the Associate Dean of Research & Scholarship, which may include the annual research symposium, research committee activities, hiring committees, intramural award administration, and other Office of Research and Scholarship initiatives. General Responsibilities Maintain a high level of professionalism, discretion, responsiveness, and accountability in interactions with faculty, staff, students, sponsors, and University partners. Take ownership of assigned portfolios, projects, and issues and follow them through to resolution. Communicate proactively regarding deadlines, potential risks, unresolved issues, and changes that may affect faculty or research projects. At the Entry level, duties are more limited in scope and are performed with guidance and direction from other professionals, and are performed in a training and development capacity. At the Intermediate level, duties may be limited in scope and are performed with guidance and direction from other professionals. At the Senior level, work is performed fully independently. At the Principal level, the role either leads work over others or is considered a subject matter expert in a particular area. In addition to the duties described above, positions at the Senior and Principal levels are responsible for: Advanced Responsibilities (Senior and Principal Professional): Serve as a lead research administration expert for pre- and post-award activities, advising faculty, students, postdoctoral fellows, and administrators on grants, contracts, compliance, proposal development, funding opportunities, and award management. Lead, train, and mentor research administration staff and stakeholders; provide guidance on award negotiations, contract setup, external agreements (JPA/IPA), and University research systems including InfoEd and NIH eRA Commons. Analyze and report grant data for institutional reporting and rankings, coordinate administrative support for research review committees, foster cross-institutional collaborations, and lead policy, process improvement, and compliance initiatives. Work Location: Hybrid – this role is eligible for a hybrid schedule of three (3) days per week on campus and as needed for in-person meetings. Why Join Us: CU Nursing is an amazing place to be. We have the distinct advantage of being a part of a huge medical campus with three incredible hospitals – the VA, the nationally ranked University of Colorado Hospital, and the Children’s Hospital Colorado where our nursing students and faculty learn every day. From our beginning 125 years ago as part of the School of Medicine at CU Boulder to our current home at the Anschutz Medical Campus, the college has been a recognized leader in nursing education (ranked #10 in online MS graduate programs by U.S. News & World Report 2023). Our faculty, students and staff have been instrumental in shaping the profession of nursing and teaching the next generation of nurses while treating patients in our own nurse-led clinics. Be a part of an innovative, dynamic, diverse, and exciting workplace -- helping make great things happen. Join us in our quest to boldly transform health together. Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation, and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package, including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 15/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced-rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Entry Level: Graduate with a bachelor’s degree in public health, public administration, social/behavioral sciences, physical sciences, nursing, healthcare, finance, accounting, business administration, business, or a directly related field from an accredited institution. Substitution : A combination of education and related technical/paraprofessional experience may be substituted for a bachelor’s degree on a year-for-year basis. Intermediate Level: Graduate with a bachelor’s degree in public health, public administration, social/behavioral sciences, physical sciences, nursing, healthcare, finance, accounting, business administration, business, or a directly related field from an accredited institution. Substitution: A combination of education and related technical/paraprofessional experience may be substituted for a bachelor’s degree on a year-for-year basis. One (1) year of professional-level experience. Senior Professional Level: Graduate with a bachelor’s degree in public health, public administration, social/behavioral sciences, physical sciences, nursing, healthcare, finance, accounting, business administration, business, or a directly related field from an accredited institution. Substitution: A combination of education and related technical/paraprofessional experience may be substituted for a bachelor’s degree on a year-for-year basis. Two (2) years of professional-level experience. Principal Professional Level: Graduate with a bachelor’s degree in public health, public administration, social/behavioral sciences, physical sciences, nursing, healthcare, finance, accounting, business administration, business, or a directly related field from an accredited institution. Substitution: A combination of education and related technical/paraprofessional experience may be substituted for a bachelor’s degree on a year-for-year basis. Three (3) years of professional-level experience. Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Preferred Qualifications: Experience working in a professional setting related to grants and contracts such as institutions of higher education and/or academic medical campuses. Experience interfacing with faculty in a professional research setting. For Senior and Principal Professional rank, experience in both pre-award and post-award research administration. For Principal Professional rank, experience serving as a work lead, trainer, or subject matter expert in research administration. Certified Research Administrator (CRA) or Certified Pre-Award Research Administrator (CPRA) credential. Conditions of Employment: Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without requiring sponsorship. We are unable to provide work visa sponsorship or employment authorization for this position now or in the future. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Excellent written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with faculty, staff, students, and other stakeholders. Strong customer service orientation, professionalism, and commitment to advancing the mission of the Office of Research and Scholarship within CU Nursing. Ability to manage competing priorities, meet deadlines, exercise sound judgment, and maintain composure in challenging situations. Proficiency with Microsoft Office Suite (Excel, Access, Word, Outlook, PowerPoint) and Adobe Acrobat. Knowledge of sponsored research administration, including grant application and award management processes, sponsor requirements, university policies and procedures, and applicable regulatory requirements (e.g., HIPAA and human subjects’ protections). Ability to analyze financial and administrative information, develop recommendations, and maintain accurate records and documentation related to grant submissions and post-award management. Ability to work independently at a level appropriate to the position rank, recognize when guidance or escalation is needed, and collaborate effectively within a team environment. For Senior and Principal Professional ranks, demonstrated ability to perform work independently with minimal supervision; Principal Professionals must also have the ability to lead, train, and mentor others. How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to the listed job qualifications and interest in the position Curriculum vitae / Resume Questions should be directed to: College of Nursing Human Resources at CON.HR@ucdenver.edu or 303.724.4447 . Screening of Applications Begins: Applications will be accepted until finalists are identified, but preference will be given to complete applications received 10/28/26. Those who do not apply by this date may or may not be considered. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as: Entry Level: $50,160 to $56,982 Intermediate Level: $54,586 to $62,010 Senior Level: $59,012 to $67,038 Principal Level: $67,864 to $77,093 The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position may be eligible for overtime compensation, depending on the level. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans, and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@cuanschutz.edu . Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students, and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine-preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety-sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41406&lang=en": {
      "title": "Post-Award Grant Specialist (Senior or Principal Professional)",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 14, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: SOM-OP GENERAL OPERATIONS Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Department: Ophthalmology Job Title: Post-Award Grant Specialist (Senior or Principal Professional) Position # 00853835 – Requisition # 41406 Job Summary: The Department of Ophthalmology is seeking a Post-Award Grant Specialist to support the financial and administrative management of its sponsored research portfolio, including federal, foundation, industry, and other externally funded projects. Reporting to the Program Manager of Research Finance and Administration, this position partners closely with Principal Investigators (PIs), research staff, and university offices to manage awards from award setup through closeout. The position is responsible for budget monitoring and forecasting, financial reconciliation, expenditure review, payroll, and funding transactions, subaward administration, sponsor invoicing and reporting support, award modifications, and maintaining accurate and compliant award records. Key Responsibilities: Senior Professional Manage a portfolio of sponsored projects from award setup through closeout in collaboration with the Program Manager and PIs. Monitor award budgets, expenditures, revenue, commitments, and projected balances; prepare financial reconciliations, forecasts, and budget variance analyses. Review expenditures for allowability, allocability, reasonableness, and compliance with sponsor requirements, University policies, and applicable federal regulations. Process and monitor financial transactions including funding distributions, Journal Entries (JEs), Payroll Expense Transfers (PETs), procurement, travel, invoices, and other award-related expenditures. Coordinate award actions including rebudgeting, carryforward, no-cost extensions, amendments, funding changes, and closeout activities. Maintain accurate, complete, and audit-ready award documentation. Provide responsive, solutions-oriented support to the Program Manager and research teams regarding sponsored project financial management. Extract, analyze, and validate financial and award information using institutional research administration and financial systems. Support Pre-Award and other research administration activities as needed, including troubleshooting SciENcv, Biosketch, Other Support, and Just-in-Time documentation, along with other submission requests. Principal Professional (including all of the above): Independently manage complex or higher-risk sponsored project portfolios and resolve financial and compliance issues with limited supervision. Provide advanced financial forecasting, budget analysis, and recommendations in consult with the Program Manager of Research Finance and Administration to PIs and research leadership. Interpret and apply complex sponsor, University, and federal requirements. Develop and improve procedures, reporting tools, and operational workflows. Serve as a resource and mentor to colleagues on research administration practices, financial management, compliance, and institutional systems. Work Location: Hybrid – this role is eligible for a hybrid schedule of 3 days per week on campus and as needed for in-person meetings. Consideration may be given to a fully remote arrangement for highly qualified candidates who reside more than 50 miles from campus. Why Join Us: Our department’s home in the UCHealth Sue Anschutz-Rodgers Eye Center on the Anschutz Medical Campus. This state-of-the-art facility is one of the largest eye centers in the country and serves patients not only in the Rocky Mountain region but also all over the world. The technological innovations conceived and developed by departmental faculty have changed the practice of eye care worldwide. Our educational programs train the next generation of leaders in ophthalmology. Our specialists have developed national and international reputations for excellence in routine and complex ophthalmic care. We have invested heavily in tracking our clinical outcomes, and we are proud that our clinicians perform at the highest levels in their respective fields. For all of you contemplating joining our Colorado organization, whether as a resident, fellow, clinical faculty, research faculty, or staff member, I welcome you to the website. It is a powerful tool to keep us connected to you. Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 15/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Senior Professional: Bachelor's degree in accounting, finance, business administration, public administration, healthcare administration, research administration, or a directly related field. Two (2) years of professional experience in finance, accounting, budgeting, business operations, grant/research administration, contract management, clinical trial finance, or a related field. Substitution: A combination of education and related technical, military, or paraprofessional experience may be substituted for the bachelor's degree on a year-for-year basis. Principal Professional: Bachelor's degree in accounting, finance, business administration, public administration, healthcare administration, research administration, or a directly related field. Three (3) years of professional experience in finance, accounting, budgeting, business operations, grant/research administration, contract management, clinical trial finance, or a related field. Substitution: A combination of education and related technical, military, or paraprofessional experience may be substituted for the bachelor's degree on a year-for-year basis. Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Preferred Qualifications: All Ranks Experience with post-award sponsored research administration in an academic, healthcare, or research environment. Experience managing federal grants, including NIH-funded awards. Experience with award setup, budget monitoring, financial reconciliation, forecasting, sponsor invoicing, progress reporting, award modifications, and closeout. Experience with subawards and subrecipient monitoring. Experience interpreting sponsor requirements and Uniform Guidance (2 CFR Part 200). Experience with University or comparable financial, reporting, and research administration systems such as InfoEd, CU Data/m-Fin, A2E, PeopleSoft Finance/HCM, CU Marketplace, Concur, ePERS, Power BI, or Smartsheet. Certified Research Administrator (CRA) credential, progress toward certification, or interest in pursuing certification. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Advanced Microsoft Excel skills, including the ability to independently analyze, reconcile, and validate complex financial data; build PivotTables; formulas such as XLOOKUP/VLOOKUP and SUMIFS; identify variances and discrepancies; and develop clear financial reports, projections, and tracking tools. Demonstrated ability to independently interpret financial, administrative, and regulatory requirements and manage multiple priorities and deadlines. Ability to communicate effectively, both in writing and orally. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with employees at all levels throughout the institution. Outstanding customer service skills. How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position Curriculum vitae / Resume Three to five professional references, including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Questions should be directed to: Erin Hegel erin.hegel@cuanschutz.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Applications will be accepted until finalists are identified, but preference will be given to complete applications received by October 23rd. Those who do not apply by this date may or may not be considered. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as: Senior Professional: $59,012 - $79,076 Principal Professional: $67,864 - $90,937 The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position may be eligible for overtime compensation, depending on the level. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@cuanschutz.edu ​. Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41405&lang=en": {
      "title": "HR, and Operations Professional (Open Rank: Intermediate and Senior)",
      "description": "Closing Date: 10/19/2026 Posted Date: Oct 14, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: SOM-SRG-GI Clinical Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Department: Surgery Job Title: HR, and Operations Professional (Open Rank: Intermediate and Senior) Position #:00842102 – Requisition #:41405 Job Summary: This full-time University Staff (non-classified) position will be responsible for leading all human resources and administrative operations for the Divisions of G.I., Trauma and Endocrine Surgery (GITES) and Surgical Oncology within the Department of Surgery, including Burn, Trauma and Acute Care Surgery (TACS), Surgical Trauma Intensive Care Unit (STICU), Colorectal, Bariatrics, Surgical Oncology Highlands Ranch Hospital, Surgical Oncology Anschutz Medical Campus. Under the supervision of the Division Administrative Director, the HR & Operations Professional will work collaboratively with the Human Resources Shared Services (HRSS) team to provide them with accurate and complete information when requesting positions, hires and transactions. This position will also manage the paid time off tracking process for faculty members within the divisions, as well as submission of additional shift pay for faculty through the system (CU Time). Lastly, this position will be the first point of contact for onboarding, additional pay, time collection, promotions, yearly increases, job posting, and office and laboratory moves for both faculty and staff employees. At the senior level, this role will independently oversee division responsibilities in relation to onboarding, human resources, and administrative operations. Key Responsibilities: Operations: Oversee faculty office and research lab space, ensuring proper allocation and usage. Coordinate updating Faculty Information Management System (FIMS) profiles and associated websites. Recommends changes, and initiates activity to improve and streamline internal processes and procedures to provide time savings, cost savings and facilitate effective operations. Provide day-to-day administrative program support to the Division of GI, Trauma, Endocrine Surgery and Division of Surgical Oncology and affiliate institutions. Makes recommendations for required resources, documents, personnel, and facilities for programs. Assist Admin IIIs with arranging candidate Skype and in-person interviews with faculty. Human Resources Support: Work with faculty and administrative staff to gather information for various HR transactions and coach on best course of action Effectively manage and request HR transactions, hiring requests, and position requests to the Surgery HR team. Assist with the requesting of volunteer clinical faculty, adjoint, adjunct, and post-doctoral positions acting as a liaison between the Division and the Surgery HR team. Develop and draft comprehensive job descriptions and letters of offer for new faculty Expertly handle and request faculty and staff terminations to the HR team Oversee and manage faculty and staff onboarding for the divisions to ensure onboarding moves along smoothly. Maintain accurate records for all personnel files for faculty and staff in the divisions. Process additional pay for faculty members with precision and accuracy. Provide HR guidance and counsel. Ensure compliance with HR policies and procedures in all HR transactions Manage faculty time off and leave submissions for multiple divisions. Coordinate with affiliate hospitals to ensure incoming faculty are onboarded. Fulfill additional duties and responsibilities as required, demonstrating a strong commitment to achieving departmental objectives. Work Location: Onsite – this role is expected to work onsite and is located in Aurora, CO. Hybrid – this role is potentially eligible for a hybrid schedule, 3 days per week on campus, 2 days a week remote. This position will be required to be in-person for the first several months and as needed for meetings. Approval for hybrid eligibility will be dependent on decision of the supervisor, department, and may be affected by return-to-campus policy updates. Why Join Us: Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 15/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Intermediate Professional: A bachelor’s degree from an accredited institution in business, business administration, social sciences, healthcare administration, or a directly related field. Substitution A combination of education and related technical/military/paraprofessional experience may be substituted for a bachelor’s degree on a year for year basis. 1 year of professional HR generalist experience. Senior Professional: A bachelor’s degree from an accredited institution in business, business administration, social sciences, healthcare administration, or a directly related field. Substitution A combination of education and related technical/military/paraprofessional experience may be substituted for a bachelor’s degree on a year for year basis. 2 years of professional HR generalist experience. Applicants for all levels must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Preferred Qualifications (All Levels): Related HR experience working in an academic medical center. Experience hiring and credentialing faculty. Prior experience working in SOM HR. Senior : 3-4 years of professional HR experience. Conditions of Employment Must be able to work on campus in Aurora, Colorado. Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without requiring sponsorship. We are unable to provide work visa sponsorship or employment authorization for this position now or in the future. Competencies: Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities (KSAs): Ability to communicate effectively, both in writing and orally, including public speaking. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with employees at all levels throughout the institution. Outstanding customer service skills. Ability to analyze, interpret, and evaluate a broad range of laws, rules, and regulations in order to exercise good judgment in applying them to human resource challenges. Knowledge of the professional standards, concepts, and practices of recruitment and selection, employee relations, or organizational development and human resource policy. Ability to maintain a high level of confidentiality while working with sensitive information. Attention to detail when dealing with complex processes. Accountability towards all deadlines. How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position ) Curriculum vitae / Resume Three to five professional references, including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Questions should be directed to: Marta O’Grady, marta.ogrady@cuanschutz.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Immediately and continues until five (5) days after requisition is posted. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as HIRING RANGE. Intermediate: $52,793 - $70,742 Senior: $57,073 - $76,478 The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position may be eligible for overtime compensation, depending on the level. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@cuanschutz.edu ​. Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
