    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=40871&lang=en": {
      "title": "Research Services Information Sciences Professional (Open Rank – Intermediate to Senior Qualitative Analyst)",
      "description": "Closing Date: 10/20/2026 Posted Date: Oct 12, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: SOM-COHO CTR GENERALOPERATIONS Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus Department: School of Medicine, ACCORDS Job Title: Research Services Information Sciences Professional (Open Rank – Intermediate to Senior Qualitative Analyst) Position #:00852401 – Requisition #:40871 Job Summary: The Adult and Child Center for Health Outcomes Research and Delivery Science (ACCORDS) has an opening for a full-time Research Services Information Science Professional who has experience with qualitative research methods. This Qualitative Analyst position is within the Qualitative and Mixed Methods Research Core (QM2) at ACCORDS. ACCORDS has a portfolio of research studies focused on health services research or implementation science that engage diverse patient populations, healthcare providers, and community stakeholders. This position will work on practice- and community-based research projects and will provide research support by assisting with qualitative data collection, coding, tool development, regulatory needs, analysis, and reporting. The position may also involve assisting with general project needs, such as staffing, budget management, and other duties as determined by study Principal Investigators. The ideal candidate will have experience and training in qualitative research data collection, coding and analysis, working on teams, and experience with developing and submitting institutional review board protocols for pragmatic trials or health services research studies. Key Responsibilities: Day-to-day activities related to the implementation of research protocols, including engaging with stakeholder groups, conducting and leading in-depth interviews or focus groups with various groups (patients, parents/family members, adolescents, providers, and community members) and coordinating and attending meetings with project investigators and staff Lead/manage tasks for qualitative data collection for basic methods (interviews and focus groups), such as recruitment, participant consenting and payment under frequent guidance of PI and Qualitative Methodologist Develop and maintain Institutional Review Board applications, amendments, and continuing review documents for qualitative aims on study projects Develop and maintain qualitative datasets, including entering, tracking, cleaning and preparing transcripts for analyses Co-leading with methodologist, managing, and conducting rigorous team-based coding efforts including coding of transcripts, and codebook development; these efforts may involve training coding team members Running queries and reports in qualitative data management software (Atlas.ti) and supporting qualitative analysis (ex. query summary planning, compiling query summaries/matrix summaries, etc.), under significant guidance of the PI and Qualitative Methodologist May develop, pilot, and employ a variety of data collection instruments and interview and focus group guides with the study team Additional Key Responsibilities for Senior Professionals: Assist and train junior Core team members May train early career investigators and fellows in qualitative data collection and analysis (SCORE fellowship and K awardees) May support methodologist/PI in development of study findings May support methodologist and PI in summarizing and presenting qualitative findings including drafting manuscript sections, abstracts, and presentations Lead/manage tasks for qualitative data collection for basic methods (interviews and focus groups), such as recruitment, participant consenting and payment under frequent guidance of PI and Qualitative Methodologist Co-lead (with methodologist), manage, and conduct rigorous team-based coding efforts including coding of transcripts, and codebook development; these efforts may involve training coding team members May lead/co-lead presentations at professional conferences Work Location: Hybrid – this role is eligible for a hybrid schedule of 1 day per month on campus and as needed for in-person meetings. Why Join Us: ACCORDS is a unique environment supporting innovative and interdisciplinary research across the University of Colorado Anschutz campus. ACCORDS brings together a large group of investigators from multiple disciplines, some who have their primary office at ACCORDS, and others who collaborate with ACCORDS personnel, programs and cores, while maintaining an off-site research home. Our methodologic cores provide support for the development of new projects, grant proposals for faculty, consultative support to investigators, as well as support our programmatic areas. Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 10/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Intermediate Professional Bachelor’s degree in Social Sciences, Public Health, or related field One (1) year of experience in data collection, coding, team-based coding and codebook development, and basic analysis of qualitative data using rigorous methods. Senior Professional Bachelor’s degree in Social Sciences, Public Health, or related field Two (2) years of experience in data collection, coding, team-based coding and codebook development, and basic analysis of qualitative data using rigorous methods. A combination of education and related technical/military/paraprofessional experience may be substituted for a bachelor’s degree on a year for year basis. An advanced degree (Masters or PhD) may be substituted for experience on a year for year basis if the degree is in a field of study directly related to the work assignment. A combination of education and related technical/military/paraprofessional experience may be substituted for a bachelor’s degree on a year for year basis. An advanced degree (Masters or Doctorate) may be substituted for experience on a year for year basis if the degree is in a field of study directly related to the work assignment. Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Preferred Qualifications: Intermediate Professional Master’s degree in Social Sciences, Public Health, or related field and two (2) years of qualitative data collection, coding, and analysis experience using rigorous methods Experience in public health or health services research Experience submitting protocols to an institutional review board (IRB) Experience with reference management software Experience with budget management Previous employment in a university environment Experience with electronic data capture systems (e.g. EMR or EHR and data management systems) Senior Professional Master’s degree in Social Sciences, Public Health, or related field and four (4) years of qualitative data collection, coding, and analysis experience using rigorous methods Experience with qualitative data management software, such as ATLAS.ti© Experience with co-moderating or moderating focus groups Experience in public health or health services research Experience submitting protocols to an institutional review board (IRB) Experience as a project manager and with budget management Experience with reference management software Previous employment in a university environment Experience with electronic data capture systems (e.g. EMR or EHR and data management systems) Conditions of Employment: Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without requiring sponsorship. We are unable to provide work visa sponsorship or employment authorization for this position now or in the future. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Experience with recruitment and enrollment of research participants Comfortable working with patients, caregivers/family members, providers, and community stakeholders Experience/Proficiency with qualitative research data collection, including leading focus groups and conducting interviews Proficiency co-developing qualitative data collection instruments Proficiency in coding and experience in leading codebook development Experience co-developing/developing analytic plan, leading query/matrix summaries, and involvement in additional analyses including thematic content analysis Experience running reports/queries Strong knowledge of basic qualitative methods in medical research Ability to analyze and solve complex problems and apply qualitative analytical approaches, including query and matrix summaries Experience summarizing and communicating study findings Demonstrated competency/proficiency in one or more data management programs (e.g., ATLAS.ti, NVivo, Maxqda,) and willingness to learn new data management software as necessary Familiarity/Experience with qualitative analytical concepts and methods Ability to communicate effectively, both in writing and orally Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with employees at all levels throughout the institution Outstanding customer service skills Excellent interpersonal skills Effective time management skills Ability to manage multiple concurrent assignments while meeting project deadlines and maintaining rigorous and detailed work Experience/Proficiency with Microsoft Office software (Word, Excel, Access, PowerPoint, and Outlook) Team-oriented, detail-oriented, self-motivated and able to work independently Demonstrated commitment and leadership ability to advance diversity and inclusion Ability to interpret and master complex research protocol information Experience/Proficiency with project management skills to support qualitative work such as managing gift card programs, transcription services, and agenda setting Advanced knowledge of basic qualitative methods in medical research Experience with variety of qualitative analytical concepts and methods How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position Curriculum vitae / Resume Three to five professional references, including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Questions should be directed to: ACCORDS HR, Accords-HR@CUAnschutz.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Immediately and continues until position is filled. Screening will begin on 10/20 Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as Intermediate Professional: $58,363 - $78,207 Senior Professional: $63,096 - $84,548 The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position may be eligible for overtime compensation, depending on the level. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@cuanschutz.edu ​. Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41517&lang=en": {
      "title": "Associate Director, Behavioral Health Clinical & Operational Excellence - Open Rank",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 26, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: SOM-PEDS DEV PEDS-GENOPS Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Department: Pediatrics Job Title: Associate Director, Behavioral Health Clinical & Operational Excellence Position #:00680704 – Requisition #:41517 Job Summary: The Department of Pediatrics seeks an accomplished and experienced professional to serve as Associate Director, Behavioral Health Clinical & Operational Excellence. The Associate Director will support department-wide leadership in the development and implementation of clinical practice strategies designed to improve practice efficiency, scope of practice standardization, revenue cycle optimization, and faculty well-being across amongst behavioral health clinicians. This role would receive 0.20 to 0.30 FTE (8-15 hours/week) of protected administrative time. Balance of FTE would be expected to comprise clinical/patient care activity in support of the Department’s clinical psychology services. Key Responsibilities: · Supports department-wide initiatives across the outpatient and inpatient clinical enterprise focused on behavioral health faculty practice optimization using QI/PI methodologies. · Acts as change agent for the successful implementation of practice optimization efforts including but not limited to influencing key stakeholders to ensure buy-in and engagement, removing significant project barriers and leading communication strategy impacting behavioral health faculty. · Proactively identify opportunities to improve behavioral health clinical practice models, including scope-of-practice alignment, scheduling and template design, access, productivity, clinical effort expectations, and revenue optimization. · Serve as an advocate and content expert for behavioral health clinical issues influencing department and hospital strategic conversations focused on practice scope, clinical time expectations, efficiencies, and well-being. · Serve as a key resource to the DOP clinical excellence team on project action plans and help define and implement project recommendations. · Participate in Children’s Hospital Colorado (CHCO), CU Medicine, and School of Medicine leadership committees as appropriate. · Support the development of behavioral health position requests (STAR) and workforce planning. · Provide support to the Vice Chair for Faculty Affairs when appropriate in performance or disciplinary matters pertaining to behavioral health faculty. · Serve as Departmental liaison to the School of Medicine Behavioral Health Executive Committee. · Support the development and sustainability of postdoctoral psychology training programs within the Department of Pediatrics. Work Location: Hybrid – this role is eligible for a hybrid schedule of 3 days per week on campus and as needed for in-person meetings. Why Join Us: The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is a world-class medical destination at the forefront of transformative science, medicine, education and patient care. The campus encompasses the University of Colorado health professional schools, more than 60 centers and institutes, and two nationally ranked independent hospitals - UCHealth University of Colorado Hospital and Children's Hospital Colorado - that treat more than two million adult and pediatric patients each year. Innovative, interconnected and highly collaborative, the University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus delivers life-changing treatments, patient care and professional training and conducts world-renowned research fueled by over $762 million in research grants. For more information, visit www.cuanschutz.edu . Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year (based on percentage of time) Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 11/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. This is an open rank position and could be categorized as Assistant Professor, Associate Professor or Professor based on experience and qualifications as indicated below: Assistant Professor: · PhD or PsyD degree from a program accredited by the American Psychological Association. · Three (3) years of experience practicing clinically in a Behavior Health related field in the Department of Pediatrics. · Currently licensed as a clinical psychologist and eligible for licensure in the State of Colorado. · Eligibility for School of Medicine faculty appointment at the rank of Assistant Professor or above. Associate Professor: · PhD or PsyD degree from a program accredited by the American Psychological Association. · Five (5) years of experience practicing clinically in a Behavior Health related field in the Department of Pediatrics. · Currently licensed as a clinical psychologist and eligible for licensure in the State of Colorado. · Eligibility for School of Medicine faculty appointment at the rank of Associate Professor or above. Professor: · PhD or PsyD degree from a program accredited by the American Psychological Association. · Ten (10) years of experience practicing clinically in a Behavior Health related field in the Department of Pediatrics. · Currently licensed as a clinical psychologist and eligible for licensure in the State of Colorado. · Eligibility for School of Medicine faculty appointment at the rank of Professor or above. Condition of Employment: · Must successfully pass a drug test through Children’s Hospital Colorado · Must be willing and able to pass a national criminal background check *For questions regarding Children’s Hospital drug testing requirements, please contact Children’s Human Resources at 720-777-8598. Some positions may require testing if access to Children’s Hospital or their systems is needed at any time during employment with the University. If drug testing is required, it will be listed in the job posting. Preferred Qualifications: · Five (5) plus years of experience practicing clinically in a Behavior Health related field in a Department of Pediatrics or similar Child Health focused practice. · Demonstrated experience managing and leading clinical psychology programs, work units or departments of sufficient scope and complexity required. · Process/Performance/Quality improvement experience and/or training (e.g., Lean certification, IHQSE) preferred. · Five (5) plus years of experience and familiarity with behavioral health billing, coding (CPT, ICD-10), and behavioral health documentation requirements preferred. · Leadership experience/training in team building. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: · Demonstrated strong communication and problem-solving skills. · Knowledge of clinic workflows, staff scheduling, multi-site management, and standardizing medical or clinical administration practices. · Understanding of state and federal healthcare mandates, HIPAA privacy laws, Medicaid/Medicare guidelines, and accreditation standards (e.g., Joint Commission, CARF, CMS). · Proficiency in Electronic Health Record (EHR) frameworks, clinical technology infrastructures, and data collection tools. · Knowledge of medical billing, auditing processes, resource allocation, and budget optimization within clinical environments. How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): 1. A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position 2. Curriculum vitae / Resume 3. Five professional references including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers . Questions should be directed to: Mike Jonen michael.jonen@childrenscolorado.org Screening of Applications Begins: Applications will be accepted until finalists are identified, but preference will be given to complete applications received by December 31, 2026. Those who do not apply by this date may or may not be considered. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as HIRING RANGE: Assistant Professor: $125,000 to $140,000 Associate Professor: $150,000 to $165,000 Professor: $175,000 to $200,000 The above hiring range represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation unless it is non-exempt. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: The University of Colorado (CU) is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@ucdenver.edu ​. Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41511&lang=en": {
      "title": "Event Manager",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 26, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: CSPH-Dean General Operation Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Colorado School of Public Health | Central Administration Event Manager Position #: 00854169 – Requisition #: 41511 Job Summary: Join the Colorado School of Public Health as an Event Manager. The Event Planner is a full ‑ cycle event professional responsible for planning, coordinating, and executing a wide range of school ‑ wide, administrative, and student ‑ focused events in support of both the Central Office and the Office of Academic and Student Affairs. Supporting both units equally, this role works independently, managing all logistics while ensuring seamless coordination with internal partners, campus liaisons, and external stakeholders. The position leads major institutional events such as orientations, convocations, and donor-sponsored lectures, maintains organized systems and documentation, and supports evaluation and continuous improvement efforts. Key Responsibilities: Plan, design, and execute a wide range of school-wide and central administration events, including lectures, donor gatherings, workshops, community events, and internal gatherings; develop event concepts and run-of-show plans that align with organizational goals and audience needs. Manage all logistics independently, including venue selection, catering, OIT coordination, décor, recruitment of volunteers for event support, scheduling, event registration, communications, attendee engagement strategies, and ensuring all room reservations/setup/configuration and necessary paperwork are completed in advance of all events. Serve as the primary point of contact for vendors, partners, sponsors, and internal stakeholders; attend weekly team meetings with central office staff and coordinate efforts with staff members such as the Office of Marketing and Communications for event promotion. Negotiate contracts, manage budgets, track expenses, and process payments to ensure cost-effective event delivery; ensure risk management and compliance with safety, accessibility, and organizational standards are met. Execute all on-site operations, including setup, troubleshooting, vendor coordination, and teardown; conduct post-event evaluations, prepare reports, recommend improvements for future events, and maintain an organized system for timelines, checklists, and documentation to ensure consistency and sustainability. Manage full event life-cycle for student-facing events, including New Student Orientations, ColoradoSPH Convocation, Fall Visit Day, Admitted Student Day, CU Anschutz Student Council events, Public Health Forum, National Public Health Week, and other recruitment and student engagement events; assist with event evaluations, coordinate with CSU and UNC partners, support occasional travel, and perform additional duties as assigned. This position reports to the Assistant Dean of Operations. Work Location: Hybrid – This position is located on the CU Anschutz Campus in Aurora, CO and is expected to work on site three days per week, with flexibility around event schedules. Why Join Us: The Colorado School of Public Health (ColoradoSPH) is a unique and collaborative graduate school that combines the collective expertise of three Colorado universities: the University of Colorado Anschutz (CU Anschutz) in Aurora, Colorado State University (CSU) in Fort Collins, and the University of Northern Colorado (UNC) in Greeley, Colorado. The Colorado School of Public Health is the only accredited school of public health in the Rocky Mountain Region, attracting top tier faculty and students from across the country, and providing a vital contribution towards ensuring our region’s health and wellbeing. The school’s faculty, staff, and students work together to share knowledge and conduct innovative research and community service to actively address public health issues including chronic disease, access to healthcare, environmental threats, emerging infectious diseases, costly injuries, and more. Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 15/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Requirements A bachelor’s degree in business, business administration, finance, accounting, education, social sciences, healthcare administration, public administration, communications, information systems or a directly related field from an accredited institution. 4-6 years of specified experience in event coordination and management. Substitution: A combination of education and related technical/military/paraprofessional experience may be substituted for a bachelor’s degree on a year for year basis Preferred Qualifications Experience in campus events, student life, student engagement Experience with event management software, registration software such as Qualtrics or Cvent, social media platforms Advanced understanding and knowledge of the field of public health Knowledge of higher education administration and student affairs Comfortable with public speaking Conditions of Employment Must be able to travel within the state and to several out-of-state events annually. Must be able to work flexible work schedules, including occasional evenings and weekends, to complete event timelines. Must have access to reliable transportation. Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without requiring sponsorship. We are unable to provide work visa sponsorship or employment authorization for this position now or in the future. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Professional written and verbal communication skills to effectively develop reports and communications for faculty and departmental administrators, staff, affiliates, and campus administration. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with employees at all levels throughout the institution. Outstanding customer service skills. Ability to manage a wide variety of tasks in a typical workday and to balance competing priorities Problem solving and decision-making ability Outstanding attention to detail Strong organizational and project management skills How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position Curriculum Vitae / Resume Three to five professional references including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Questions should be directed to: Megan Freije, Megan.Freije@cuanschutz.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Screening begins immediately and continues until November 6, 2026. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting target salary for this position has been established at $72,617 - $89,000 (100% FTE) The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position may be eligible for overtime compensation, depending on the level. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@cuanschutz.edu ​. Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41516&lang=en": {
      "title": "Post-Doctoral Fellow",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 26, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: SOM-PEDS Critical Care-GenOps Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Department: Pediatrics, Section of Critical Care Job Title: Postdoctoral Fellow Position #00691942: – Requisition #:41516 Job Summary: The Department of Pediatrics, Section of Pediatric Critical Care is seeking a full-time Postdoctoral Fellow to join a research program investigating the mechanistic drivers of pulmonary hypertension (PH) across the lifespan. This position offers the opportunity to work across in vivo mouse models, cell/tissue-based assays, and advanced molecular techniques (e.g., flow cytometry, spatial transcriptomics, single-cell sequencing) within a collaborative, translationally oriented lab environment. The successful candidate will be responsible for projects investigating how macrophage–extracellular matrix interactions govern vascular remodeling in PH, and maternal stress signaling pathways that predispose offspring to pulmonary vascular disease. Additional responsibilities include developing new lab protocols and teaching associated with the laboratory research. The ideal candidate is reliable, personable, highly motivated, and organized, with a demonstrated ability to work both independently and in a team. This is an excellent opportunity to join a fast-paced, diverse, and productive research group. The position is based in the Research Complex 2 building on the Anschutz Medical Campus. Key Responsibilities: · The post-doctoral fellow will plan, perform, analyze and oversee bench research. · Teaching activity will generally involve laboratory staff, students, or faculty collaborators. · The fellow is expected to take a leadership role in planning scientific activities; keep abreast of and share with the laboratory pertinent scientific literature; participate in lab meetings and Cardiovascular and Pulmonary Research Laboratory (CVP) seminars and attend relevant conferences. · write both grants and scientific publications. · The fellow will be afforded both time and resources to promote collaborative studies and develop new techniques. Work Location: Onsite – this role is expected to work onsite and is located in Aurora, CO. Why Join Us: The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is a public education, clinical, and research facility serving 4,500 students and is a world-class medical destination at the forefront of life-changing science, medicine, and healthcare. CU Anschutz offers more than 42 highly rated degree programs through 6 schools and colleges and receives over $762 million in research awards each year. We are the single largest health professions education provider in Colorado, awarding nearly 1,450 degrees annually. Powered by our award-winning faculty, renowned researchers, and a reputation for academic excellence, the CU Anschutz Medical Campus drives innovation from the classroom to the laboratory to the delivery of unparalleled patient care. Why work for the University? The University of Colorado offers a comprehensive benefits package. To see what benefits are available for Post-Doctoral Fellows, please visit: Payroll & Benefits Orientation for Post-Doctoral Fellows | University of Colorado (cu.edu) benefits guide cover-post-doc-2024 (cu.edu) Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. ● PhD, with interest in pulmonary hypertension and/or macrophage research. Condition of Employment: · Must successfully pass a drug test through Children’s Hospital Colorado · Must be willing and able to pass a national criminal background check *For questions regarding Children’s Hospital drug testing requirements, please contact Children’s Human Resources at 720-777-8598. Some positions may require testing if access to Children’s Hospital or their systems is needed at any time during employment with the University. If drug testing is required, it will be listed in the job posting. Preferred Qualifications: ● Experience with mouse models of human lung disease ● Proven experience and familiarity with immune cell profiling ● Proven experience and familiarity with extracellular matrix biology ● Proven experience and familiarity with molecular biology ● Experience in analyzing “omics” data sets, for example, metabolomics or single cell RNAseq How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): 1. A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position 2. Curriculum vitae / Resume 3. Five professional references including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers . Questions should be directed to: Caitlin Lewi s , CAITLIN.V.LEWIS@CUANSCHUTZ.EDU Screening of Applications Begins: Immediately and continues until position is filled. For best consideration, apply by November 30, 2026. Anticipated Pay Range: The hiring range for this position has been established at $63,480- $69,180. The above hiring range represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation unless it is non-exempt. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: The University of Colorado (CU) is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@ucdenver.edu ​. Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41514&lang=en": {
      "title": "Echocardiographer - Open Rank",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 26, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: SOM-PEDS Cardiology-GenOps Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Department: Pediatric Cardiology Job Title: Echocardiographer Position #: 00854082 – Requisition #:41514 Job Summary: Pediatric Cardiologist with sub-specialization in the performance and interpretation of transthoracic and transesophageal echocardiography. Key Responsibilities: Interprets diagnostic transthoracic echocardiograms (TTE) in the inpatient and outpatient setting on hearts with normal anatomy and complex congenital heart disease. Capable of performing transthoracic echocardiograms on patients with complex congenital heart disease. Performs and provides in-the-moment interpretations on diagnostic transesophageal echocardiograms (TEE) in the operating room, cardiac catheterization, and electrophysiology room settings on hearts with normal anatomy and complex congenital heart disease. Train and mentor pediatric categorical cardiology fellows, as well as pediatric advanced cardiac imaging 4 th year fellows. Help to train and mentor pediatic cardiac sonographers. Outpatient cardiology clinic at the Anschutz campus and possibly network of care. Work Location: Onsite – this role is expected to work onsite and is located in Aurora, Colorado. Why Join Us: As the largest pediatric heart program in the region, we have performed more than 675 heart surgeries and about 1,000 heart catheterization every year since 2017. Our highly specialized pediatric heart surgeons and interventional cardiologists take on the most complex congenital heart defects (CHDs) and childhood heart conditions and achieve some of the best results in the nation. The Society of Thoracic Surgery requires a hospital to perform at least 250 heart s urgeries per year to be considered a high-volume center. By far exceeding this, we gain more experience, which leads to better outcomes. The Heart Institute has 80 plus faculty members and continues to grow annually. Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year (based on percentage of time) Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 11/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. This is an open rank position and could be categorized as Assistant Professor, Associate Professor or Professor based on experience and qualifications as indicated below: Assistant Professor: Board Certified or Eligible in Pediatric Cardiology. Associate Professor: Board Certified or Eligible in Pediatric Cardiology. At least 5 years of experience Professor: Board Certified or Eligible in Pediatric Cardiology. At least 10 years of experience Condition of Employment: · Must successfully pass a drug test through Children’s Hospital Colorado · Must be willing and able to pass a national criminal background check *For questions regarding Children’s Hospital drug testing requirements, please contact Children’s Human Resources at 720-777-8598. Some positions may require testing if access to Children’s Hospital or their systems is needed at any time during employment with the University. If drug testing is required, it will be listed in the job posting. Preferred Qualifications: Minimum of at least one additional year of training in non-invasive cardiac imaging/echocardiography. Ability to perform and provide in-the-moment interpretations on diagnostic transesophageal echocardiograms (TEE) in the operating room, cardiac catheterization, and electrophysiology room settings on hearts with normal anatomy and complex congenital heart disease. At least a cursory understanding and comfort with performing 3D transesophageal echocardiography for the purposes of providing imaging guidance of procedures in the cardiac catheterization laboratory (e.g., transcatheter ASD closure, VSD closure, atrial septostomy, etc). Evaluate and manage general cardiology patients in the outpatient clinic Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Deep knowledge of congenital heart disease anatomy, physiology and clinical implications Strong communication skills Ability to work collaboratively with a large team, including echocardiographers, sonographers, cardiothoracic surgeons, interventional cardiologists, electrophysiologists, and critical care physicians. Desire to progress the clinical practice of pediatric cardiology and/or echocardiography through clinical investigation and research. Ability to teach medical students, residents, fellows, and sonographers the essentials of pediatric cardiology and echocardiography. How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): 1. A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position 2. Curriculum vitae / Resume 3. Five professional references, including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers . Questions should be directed to: Derek Young, DEREK.YOUNG@UCDENVER.EDU Screening of Applications Begins: Applications will be accepted until finalists are identified, but preference will be given to complete applications received by 12/15/2026 . Those who do not apply by this date may or may not be considered. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as HIRING RANGE: Assistant Professor: $240,000 to $254,886 Associate Professor: $293,814 to $314,752 Professor: $364,300 to $402,171 The above hiring range represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation unless it is non-exempt. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Perks & Benefits: https://advantage.cu.edu/search Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: The University of Colorado (CU) is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@ucdenver.edu ​. Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41510&lang=en": {
      "title": "Cancer Center Director of Finance and Administration",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 23, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: SOM-U of Colo Cancer Center Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Department: Cancer Center Job Title: Cancer Center Director of Finance and Administration Position #: 00613855 – Requisition #: 41510 Job Summary: The University of Colorado Cancer Center (Center) is seeking a Director of Finance & Administration. Located on the Anschutz Medical Campus, the Center is Colorado’s only National Cancer Institute (NCI)-designated comprehensive cancer center, a distinction recognizing its contributions to basic research, clinical trials, prevention, and cancer control research. The Center’s adult clinical partner, University of Colorado Hospital, is ranked among the nation’s top 15 hospitals by U.S. News & World Report, and Children’s Hospital Colorado is ranked eighth nationally in pediatric cancer care by the same organization. The Center is a member of the National Comprehensive Cancer Network (NCCN), an alliance of leading cancer centers that develops and advances evidence-based cancer care guidelines. It is also a member of the Oncology Research Information Exchange Network (ORIEN), a research partnership among leading North American cancer centers that integrates multiple data sources and helps match patients with targeted treatments. The Center is a consortium of approximately 260 researchers and physicians across three state universities and three clinical institutions, united by a vision to prevent and cure cancer while serving as a global model for patient care, interdisciplinary research, and training. The Director of Finance & Administration has primary responsibility for the Center’s administrative and financial functions. This includes developing and implementing the Center’s strategic plan, goals, performance outcomes, and budgets; developing and executing policies; and overseeing the NCI Cancer Center Support Grant (CCSG). As a member of the senior leadership team, the ADA/DFA acts on behalf of the Director when necessary. The DFA oversees the Center’s daily administrative and financial operations and provides leadership that advances collaboration with academic and healthcare partners. The Center employs approximately 280 technical and administrative staff, supports over 300 full and mentored faculty members, and provides partial financial support for approximately 30 faculty members who lead programs and manage resources across the Center. Key Responsibilities: Provide strategic oversight and leadership for the Center’s administrative and financial operations, including financial management; grants and contracts administration; human resources; clinical research operations, including OCRST and the Cancer Clinical Trials Office; internal information technology; space management; communications and public relations; and general administration. Lead and develop a management team with expertise in finance, research administration, clinical research, information technology, and communications. Oversee NCI CCSG activities, including preparation and submission of the application. Lead the Center’s strategic planning, including development, revision, implementation, and monitoring of the strategic plan. Oversee the management of Center Shared Resources, including prioritization, staffing, financial performance, and user satisfaction. Support the Center’s community outreach and engagement initiatives and its cancer research training and education efforts. Manage philanthropic funds and partner with the Advancement Office on fundraising, outreach, and donor relations. Represent the Center before institutional leaders, advisory bodies, state and federal government entities, external public and private organizations, fundraising organizations, and advocacy groups. Represent the Center on relevant boards and committees of member organizations, including ACCA, NCCN, ORIEN, and AACI. Facilitate collaboration within the Center, across partner institutions, and with external organizations. Participate, as appropriate or required, in School of Medicine and campus planning and operational management activities. Work Location: Hybrid – this role is eligible for a hybrid schedule of which can be negotiated with the Cancer Center Director once training for the position is complete. Why Join Us: At the University of Colorado Anschutz Cancer Center, patients and families receive compassionate, world-class cancer care in Colorado from nationally and internationally recognized experts. Our collaborative teams deliver the best possible outcomes through innovative treatments, groundbreaking cancer research, and access to leading-edge clinical trials. We are proud to be Colorado’s only National Cancer Institute (NCI) Designated Comprehensive Cancer Center - a distinction that reflects the highest standards in cancer research, prevention, and patient care. We are also a member of the National Comprehensive Cancer Network (NCCN), where our cancer experts help set the standard for cancer treatment nationwide. Our multidisciplinary approach unites specialists across fields to create comprehensive, individualized treatment plans, strengthened by our clinical partnerships with UCHealth, Children’s Hospital Colorado, and the Rocky Mountain Regional VA Medical Center. We not only treat and research cancer in humans but partner with the Colorado State University Flint Animal Cancer Center, the largest animal cancer center in the United States. Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 15/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree in education, psychology, business, public administration, healthcare , educational technology, social science, liberal arts, communications, accounting, finance, library science, or a directly related field from an accredited institution , Eight (8) years of progressively responsible professional experience in finance, business administration, operations, or a related field, including significant responsibility for financial management, budgeting, forecasting, and financial analysis. Four (4) years of management or supervisory experience, including responsibility for leading teams, managing complex administrative operations, and/or overseeing financial functions. Experience managing complex financial operations involving multiple funding sources, such as institutional funds, sponsored research, clinical revenue, philanthropy, gifts/endowments, and/or other restricted and unrestricted funds. Experience working in a complex healthcare, academic medical center, research, or similarly matrixed environment. An advanced degree (Masters or Doctorate) may be substituted for experience on a year for year basis if the degree is in a field of study directly related to the work assignment. Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Preferred Qualifications: Master’s degree in business administration, public administration, healthcare administration, cancer biology, or a related field from an accredited institution. Ten (10) years of relevant leadership experience in a large academic medical center, preferably within an NCI-designated cancer center, including experience with fund management, budgeting, and forecasting. Experience with oversight and management of an NCI-CCSG award, including experience with submitting a competitive renewal or initial submission. Experience leading organizational strategic planning initiatives. Experience supervising employees, including management-level staff. Experience providing administrative leadership in a grant-funded academic institution, with particular emphasis on federal awards. Conditions of Employment: Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without requiring sponsorship. We are unable to provide work visa sponsorship or employment authorization for this position now or in the future. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Demonstrated expertise in financial management, budgeting, and forecasting. Excellent written and verbal communication skills. Excellent interpersonal, collaboration, and relationship-management skills. Thorough knowledge of federal requirements governing NCI cancer center grants and related programs. How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position Curriculum vitae / Resume Three to five professional references, including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Questions should be directed to: Makeedra Keith at Makeedra.Keith@cuanschutz.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Immediately and continues until November 2, 2026. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as $160,000-$227,540 The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position may be eligible for overtime compensation, depending on the level. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@cuanschutz.edu ​. Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41512&lang=en": {
      "title": "Assistant Dean of Graduate Programs (Administrative Faculty Appointment); IRC-Instructional Faculty Appointment (Open Rank-Associate Professor/Professor)",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 23, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: CON-DEAN ADMINISTRATION Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Department: College of Nursing Job Title: Assistant Dean of Graduate Programs (Administrative Faculty Appointment); IRC-Instructional Faculty Appointment (Open Rank-Associate Professor/Professor) Position #:00729628 – Requisition #: 41512 Job Summary: The CU College of Nursing is seeking a strong faculty leader to serve as the Assistant Dean of Graduate Programs. The ideal candidate would be qualified to hold a faculty appointment within the IRC-Instructional Series at the rank of Associate Professor or Professor with dedicated release time to serve as the Assistant Dean of Graduate Programs (an administrative faculty appointment). Service and scholarship to the university and the college are expected of all faculty members. Also, faculty rank will depend on the candidate’s qualifications, experience, and scholarship. The Assistant Dean of Graduate Programs is responsible for the overall quality, effectiveness, and execution of the strategic direction of the College of Nursing's graduate programs, including master's, post-graduate certificate, and Doctor of Nursing Practice (DNP) programs. The Assistant Dean provides strategic, academic, and administrative leadership to ensure that graduate curricula, policies, and educational practices reflect academic excellence and meet national, state, accreditation, certification, and regulatory requirements within the framework of the Office of Academic Programs and the College of Nursing Strategic Priorities. The Assistant Dean reports directly to the Associate Dean of Academic Programs and is responsible for graduate program quality, growth, innovation, supporting accreditation, and long-range academic planning. This position works collaboratively with specialty directors, other academic leaders, faculty, staff, and college leadership to foster innovative educational experiences, support student success, monitor program outcomes, and advance the academic mission of the College. This position’s primary work location is the Anschutz Medical Campus, Aurora, Colorado, and will also have teaching responsibilities as needed on the Legacy Campus, in Lone Tree, Colorado. Examples of Work Performed · Academic Leadership and Strategic Planning o Provides leadership for master's, post-graduate certificate(s), and DNP programs. o Monitors and identifies emerging educational, professional, healthcare, and technological trends that may impact graduate nursing education and communicates implications for graduate programs. o Supports development of innovative curricula responsive to workforce, professional, and student needs. o Collaborates with faculty to operationalize strategic priorities for graduate education and align program initiatives with those priorities. o Supports implementation of the College's academic strategic plan by aligning graduate education initiatives and activities with established College priorities. · Curriculum Oversight and Quality o Ensures graduate curricula are consistent with accreditation, certification, regulatory, and professional standards. o Oversees systematic curriculum evaluation and continuous quality improvement. o Develops and monitors metrics related to curricular effectiveness, student learning outcomes, and program quality. o Collaborates with the Assistant Dean of Clinical Simulation Science and the Assistant Director of Interprofessional Education to ensure effective integration of simulation, technology-enhanced learning, and interprofessional education across graduate programs. o Reviews and provides direction on recommendations for curriculum revision and program development. o Demonstrates expertise in student-centered teaching and learning methodologies, including evidence-based online and technology-enhanced instructional strategies that support student success and learning outcomes. · Program Development, Growth, Innovation and Evaluation o Oversees collection and analysis of graduate program outcomes data to inform program improvement. o Ensures compliance with accreditation, certification, and regulatory requirements. o Leads graduate program reporting activities and accreditation preparation in collaboration with the Sr. Assistant Dean of Academic Operations. o Monitors graduate program performance and recommends quality improvement initiatives. · Program Leadership and Student Success o Provides leadership and support to any position that is supervised under this role. o Collaborates with Specialty Directors, Graduate Program operational staff, and any other relevant academic leaders in the college. Works with the Associate Dean for Academic Programs regarding contract faculty assignments and programmatic resource needs. o Collaborates with the Associate Dean of Academic Programs, Assistant Deans, Sr. Assistant Dean of Academic Operations and Division Chairs in planning course schedules and faculty workload assignments to support program delivery and resource needs. o Provides input into annual faculty evaluations of those that teach in the MS, PGC, and DNP program courses. o Ensures a student-centered educational environment and monitors student satisfaction to identify and address areas for improvement across graduate programs. o Reviews trends related to retention, progression, completion, certification outcomes, and graduate success to inform program improvement strategies. o Supports the escalation and resolution of graduate student concerns in collaboration as needed with the Sr. Director of Admissions and Student Affairs. · Collaboration, Resources, and Engagement o Participates in grant development and other strategic initiatives supporting graduate education. o Represents graduate programs within the College and externally to advance program priorities and partnerships, as appropriate. o Actively participates as a member of state, regional, and national professional organizations by attending meetings, and engaging in service activities. o Demonstrates effective, collaborative, and civil communication patterns with students, stakeholders, faculty, and staff. o Engages in other activities and responsibilities as delegated by the Associate Dean of Academic Programs. o Collaborates with the Associate Dean of Academic Programs regarding budgetary support for MS and DNP programmatic needs. o Collaborates with the Senior Assistant Dean of Academic Operations to support process improvement and systems integration to streamline graduate program operations and overall student experience. o Participates in teaching within the College of Nursing, serving as a role model for professional and educational excellence. This description is a summary only and describes the general level of work being performed; it is not intended to be all-inclusive. The duties of this position may change from time to time and/or based on business needs. We reserve the right to add or delete duties and responsibilities at the discretion of the supervisor and/or hiring authority. Work Location: Hybrid – this role is eligible for a hybrid schedule of 3 days per week on campus and as needed for in-person meetings. Why Join Us: CU Nursing is an amazing place to be. We have the distinct advantage of being a part of a huge medical campus with three incredible hospitals – the VA, the nationally ranked University of Colorado Hospital, and the Children’s Hospital Colorado where our nursing students and faculty learn every day. From our beginning 125 years ago as part of the School of Medicine at CU Boulder to our current home at the Anschutz Medical Campus, the college has been a recognized leader in nursing education (ranked #10 in online MS graduate programs by U.S. News & World Report 2023). Our faculty, students and staff have been instrumental in shaping the profession of nursing and teaching the next generation of nurses while treating patients in our own nurse-led clinics. Be a part of an innovative, dynamic, diverse, and exciting workplace -- helping make great things happen. Join us in our quest to boldly transform health together. Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation, and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package, including: · Medical: Multiple plan options · Dental: Multiple plan options · Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision · Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay · Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year · Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) · Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) · Holiday Days: 15/year · Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses · ECO Pass: Reduced-rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): 1. A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to the listed job qualifications and interest in the position 2. Curriculum vitae / Resume Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers . Questions should be directed to: College of Nursing Human Resources at CON.HR@ucdenver.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Applications will be accepted until finalists are identified, but preference will be given to complete applications received by November 6 th , 2026 . Those who do not apply by this date may or may not be considered. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as: Associate Teaching Professor: $115,000 to $130,000 annually at 1.0 FTE Teaching Professor : $130,000 to $150,000 annually at 1.0 FTE The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position may be eligible for overtime compensation, depending on the level. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans, and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@cuanschutz.edu . Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students, and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine-preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety-sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41506&lang=en": {
      "title": "Regulatory Coordinator (Open-Rank, Intermediate thru Senior)",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 23, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: SOM-OB/GYN CHAIR GENERAL OPS Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Department: Obstetrics and Gynecology Job Title: Regulatory Coordinator (Open-Rank, Intermediate thru Senior) Position #: 00854088 – Requisition #:41506 Job Summary: The Administrative Research Core (ARC) Regulatory Coordinator is a full-time position within the Department of Obstetrics and Gynecology at the University of Colorado School of Medicine. This role supports a diverse portfolio of clinical research studies by managing regulatory processes across the study lifecycle, including preparing and submitting regulatory applications, maintaining essential study documentation, tracking approvals and deadlines, and ensuring compliance with Institutional Review Board (IRB), U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA), Good Clinical Practice (GCP), and university requirements. The Coordinator will specialize in gynecologic oncology studies and manage regulatory documentation and submissions related to clinical research protocols including investigator-initiated trials (IITs), cooperative group studies (e.g., NRG Oncology), and Phase I–III industry trials. As an integral member of the Administrative Research Core, this position helps ensure the ethical and compliant conduct of human subjects research while providing an excellent opportunity for professional growth in clinical research regulatory affairs. Duties listed will phase in as this position is trained, receiving support from the Regulatory Manager. At the senior level, the Coordinator will independently manage regulatory documentation, submissions, and compliance for gynecologic oncology studies throughout the research lifecycle, ensuring adherence to IRB, FDA, GCP, and university requirements while supporting the ethical conduct of human subjects research. Key Responsibilities: Regulatory Oversight: 70% Prepares, submits, and tracks complete and accurate Gyn Onc clinical regulatory applications, amendments, continuing reviews, reportable events, and study closures to all required regulatory bodies for the conduct of clinical research at the University of Colorado. This may include, but is not limited to, the following: Colorado Multiple Institutional Review Board (COMIRB) Western Institutional Review Board (WIRB) NCI Central Institutional Review Board (CIRB/Advarra) Protocol Review and Monitoring System (PRMS) Completes and submits continuing reviews, amendments, and other protocol-specific documents. Develops clear and accurate informed consent documents, HIPAA authorizations, and participant-facing regulatory documents. Serves as a regulatory liaison interfacing between Gyn Onc/OB-GYN investigators, industry sponsors, CROs, and University review committees to resolve complex regulatory, ethical, or institutional approval bottlenecks. Collaborates with investigators, study teams, sponsors, and regulatory offices to facilitate efficient regulatory review and approval processes. Quality Assurance: 25% Maintains regulatory binders and electronic regulatory files and databases including OnCore to ensure complete, accurate, and audit-ready documentation. Leads internal quality assurance audits of shared study e-files and eReg binders across the Gyn Onc portfolio, developing corrective and preventive action (CAPA) recommendations for the Regulatory Manager. Monitors study approval periods and regulatory deadlines to ensure timely submissions and compliance. Assists the Regulatory Manager with FDA (IND/IDE) submissions, annual reports, safety reporting, and maintenance, as well as full ClinicalTrials.gov protocol registration, maintenance, and results reporting. Oversees and maintains OnCore protocol submissions, regulatory data integrity, and requirements for opening complex oncology studies to accrual. Reviews and interprets federal, state, local, and university regulations and guidelines, proactively advising Gyn Onc investigators, fellows, and research staff on regulatory impacts. Other Duties: 5% Assists the Research Program Director and Regulatory Manager with developing general research policies and procedures relating to clinical research. Senior Level: Independently responsible for development and maintenance of department SOPs relating to regulatory policies and procedures. Participates in cross-training and professional development opportunities related to grants and contracts to enhance skills and knowledge in this area including budgeting, proposal submissions, and subcontract setup and administration. Develops original content for Department research edition newsletter, including advising research personnel on changing regulations and policies/procedures. Networks with relevant University offices to build up the Department’s Best Practices. Cross trains with the other members of the team and provides service coverage when needed. Identifies and participates in training opportunities to enhance knowledge in all areas of responsibilities. Develops and presents original educational content to Department research faculty, fellows, and staff at quarterly research meetings, faculty meetings, and other relevant meetings as necessary. Perform other duties as assigned. Work Location: Hybrid – this role is eligible for a hybrid schedule of 3 days per week on campus and as needed for in-person meetings. Why Join Us: The Department of Obstetrics and Gynecology at the University of Colorado is a world-class research enterprise, ranked 25th in the nation by the Blue Ridge Institute for federal funding. The Department currently has over 130 active clinical an impressive research portfolio of $25M in existing federal and foundation grants and contracts through the lifetime of the projects, increasing in budget annually by $12M. Departmental faculty provide a full-spectrum of clinical care for women of all ages, participate in research, and provide education to students and residents. Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 15/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Intermediate Level: A bachelor’s degree in public health, public administration, social/behavioral sciences, physical sciences, nursing, healthcare, finance, accounting, business administration, business, or a directly related field from an accredited institution. Substitution : A combination of education and related technical/military/paraprofessional experience may be substituted for a bachelor’s degree on a year for year basis. One (1) year of professional experience coordinating clinical trials, clinical research administration, regulatory affairs, or healthcare compliance. Senior Level: A bachelor’s degree in public health, public administration, social/behavioral sciences, physical sciences, nursing, healthcare, finance, accounting, business administration, business, or a directly related field from an accredited institution. Substitution : A combination of education and related technical/military/paraprofessional experience may be substituted for a bachelor’s degree on a year for year basis. Two (2) years of professional experience coordinating clinical trials, clinical research administration, regulatory affairs, or healthcare compliance. Applicants for all levels must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Preferred Qualifications: Three or more years of professional medical, clinical and/or experience coordinating clinical research. Experience interpreting and applying policies from multiple levels of authority (federal, state, and institutional) and serving as a resource for others. Experience supporting IRB submissions and human subjects' research specifically for cancer research or women’s health research. Experience maintaining regulatory binders and essential regulatory documentation. Conditions of Employment: Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without requiring sponsorship. We are unable to provide work visa sponsorship or employment authorization for this position now or in the future. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Proficiency with Oncore, InfoEd, CU Data, Marketplace, and other relevant systems. Familiarity with FDA regulations, ICH-GCP guidelines, and human research protections. Demonstrated ability to work effectively with a diverse population of faculty, staff and students. Excellent knowledge regarding clinical research regulations and principals of ethical conduct. Ability to communicate effectively, both in writing and orally. Demonstrated ability to work effectively with a diverse population of faculty, staff and students. Effective communication/presentation skills and a proven track record of forming collaborative and effective working relationships with physicians and administrative leaders. Excellent knowledge regarding clinical research regulations and principles of ethical conduct related to human subjects research. Understanding of Good Clinical Practice (GCP) guidelines and regulatory compliance requirements. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with investigators, study teams, regulatory offices, and sponsors. Outstanding customer service skills. How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position Curriculum vitae / Resume Three to five professional references, including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Questions s hould be directed to: Naila Naushad, naila.naushad@cuanschutz.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Immediately and continues until position is filled. For best consideration, apply by November 30, 2026. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established at: Intermediate Level: $57,525 - $77,083 Senior Level: $62,189 - $83,333 The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position may be eligible for overtime compensation, depending on the level. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@cuanschutz.edu ​. Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41503&lang=en": {
      "title": "APP Instructor Fellow",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 23, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: SOM-NEUR GENERAL OPERATIONS Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Department: Neurology Job Title: APP Instructor Fellow Position #: 00853985 – Requisition #41503: Job Summary: The Department of Neurology is looking to fill a full-time Advanced Practice Provider Instructor/Fellow position. The APP Neurology Fellowship Position in the Department of Neurology at the University of Colorado School of Medicine will provide 12 months of training to qualified graduates of an advanced practice program (i.e., Nurse Practitioner, Advanced Practice Registered Nurse (APRN), or Physician Assistant (PA). A graduate of the APP Neurology Fellowship is expected to be able to conduct a neurology history and examination, determine the appropriate diagnostic evaluation, and formulate a management plan for patients with neurologic conditions within their scope of practice. We encourage graduates to apply for positions within our department upon completion of their training. The fellows will have an opportunity to rotate through various subspecialties, which can include Behavioral Neurology, Epilepsy, Epilepsy Monitoring Unit, General Neurology, Headache, Inpatient Consults, Movement Disorders, Multiple Sclerosis, Neuro-Infectious Disease, Neuromuscular Disorders, Neuro-Oncology, Neuro-Ophthalmology, Neuroradiology, Stroke. The program is recruiting APPs who would be willing to relocate to the Colorado area for future employment in the University of Colorado Neurology related practice. The University of Colorado offers competitive salaries. The program will accept two APP fellows each year who begin the program in the summer or immediately after graduation. We will accept new graduates as well as experienced APPs. We are seeking individuals who are collaborative, communicative, proactive, caring, detail-oriented, organized, able to think critically, focused on quality, and dedicated to personal growth. Key Responsibilities: · Design and implement a plan of care based on a patient’s history and exam · Adapt treatment based on patient response, and identify and manage complications of therapy · Incorporate evidence-based information and current guidelines into patient care · Perform procedures such as, but not limited to, lumbar punctures, occipital nerve blocks, baclofen pump refills · Utilize and interpret neurodiagnostic testing and imaging · Provide compassionate, sensitive care to patients, including vulnerable populations · Collaborate with a multidisciplinary team to make clinical decisions and to maintain patient safety Work Location: Hybrid – this role is eligible for a hybrid schedule. Why Join Us: The position is located at the University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus. The Anschutz Medical Campus is a public education, clinical and research facility serving 4,600 students, and a world-class medical destination at the forefront of life-changing science, medicine, and healthcare. CU Anschutz offers more than 42 highly rated degree programs through 6 schools and colleges and receives over $890 million in research awards each year. We are the single largest health professions education provider in Colorado, awarding nearly 1,450 degrees annually. Powered by our award-winning faculty, renowned researchers and a reputation for academic excellence, the CU Anschutz Medical Campus drives innovation from the classroom to the laboratory to the delivery of unparalleled patient care. Read CU Anschutz Quick Facts here. Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Voluntary tax deferred annuity savings option plans (401k, 403B, 457) Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. · Graduation in good standing from an accredited APRN or PA program no later than May 31 st , 2027, prior to the start of fellowship training on July 1st. · Have national board certification as an NP, CNS or PA. Preferred Qualifications: · Experience completing documentation and performing tasks routinely assigned in hospital settings using hospital record systems (e.g., Epic and Oncore) · Knowledge of University of Colorado Health Hospitals Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: · Outstanding interpersonal and communication skills with the ability to work independently and within diverse team structures · Being respectful of patient rights and putting patient safety first · Building patient rapport · A positive, motivated, engaged, and caring attitude · Great attention to detail and quality · Ability to work with colleagues and patients in a confidential and professional manner · Good documentation practices · Dedication to professional development and life-long learning · Ability to be adaptable, flexible, and think quickly on your feet · Experience with web-based tracking systems and Microsoft Office suite (e.g., Excel, Word, PowerPoint and Access) How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): 1. A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position 2. Curriculum vitae / Resume 3. Five professional references including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers . Questions should be directed to: Neurology Human Resources at Neurology-HR@cuanschutz.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Immediately and continues until December 31, 2026 Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as HIRING RANGE: $80,000 to $85,000 The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation unless it is non-exempt. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: The University of Colorado (CU) is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@ucdenver.edu ​. Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41502&lang=en": {
      "title": "Instructor – Behavioral Health Clinician",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 23, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: SOM-PEDS Adolescent Med-GenOps Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Department: Pediatrics, Section of Adolescent Medicine Job Title: Instructor – Behavioral Health Clinician Position #:00615081 – Requisition #:41502 Job Summary: In the Adolescent Medicine Primary Care Clinic, the Behavioral Health Clinician will be a part of the integrated behavioral health team and will provide clinical services, including individual and family therapy, and care coordination. Key Responsibilities: The duties and responsibilities of the position include, but are not limited to: Provide Behavioral Health services within the Adolescent Medicine Clinic. Conduct behavioral health assessments when clinically indicated, including assessment of patients’ strengths, needs, safety, and treatment goals. Provide consultation and brief intervention for behavioral health concerns identified during medical visits. Develop patient-centered treatment plans and provide individual or family therapy when appropriate, respecting adolescent confidentiality and involving families or caregivers as appropriate. Partner with medical providers and other team members in responding to concerns about suicide risk, suspected child abuse or neglect, and intimate partner or family violence. Partner with the clinical team as needed to provide further assessment, safety planning, patient support, referrals, and coordination of follow-up. Fulfill individual mandatory reporting obligations and follow hospital procedures for escalation and documentation. Coordinate transitions to longer-term therapy or a higher level of care when indicated. Collaborate with medical providers and other members of the integrated care team. · Work Location: Onsite – this role is expected to work onsite and is located in Aurora, CO Why Join Us: Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year (based on percentage of time) Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 11/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Instructor: ● MSW or equivalent from an accredited University ● DORA Licensure as a LCSW or LPC or LMFT in the state of Colorado or will obtain licensure before start date ● Training in CBT and Family Therapy ● 1-3 years of experience working with adolescent population Condition of Employment: ● Must successfully pass a drug test through Children’s Hospital Colorado ● Must be willing and able to pass a national criminal background check *For questions regarding Children’s Hospital drug testing requirements, please contact Children’s Human Resources at 720-777-8598. Some positions may require testing if access to Children’s Hospital or their systems is needed at any time during employment with the University. If drug testing is required, it will be listed in the job posting. Preferred Qualifications: · 2-3 years of experience working in a patient centered medical home/primary care practice · 2-3 years of experience working in an integrated behavioral health system · 2-3 years of experience working with gender diverse youth · Training trauma focused CBT Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: ● Excellent communication skills, both oral and written ● Understanding of the adolescent population ● Systems knowledge of the behavioral health landscape of the Metro Denver Area How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): 1. A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position 2. Curriculum vitae / Resume 3. Five professional references including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers . Questions should be directed to: Rebecca Barlow, Rebecca.barlow@childrenscolorado.org Screening of Applications Begins: Immediately and continues until position is filled. For best consideration, apply by 10/31/2026. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range (or hiring range) for this position has been established as HIRING RANGE: $75,000 – $90,000 The above salary range (or hiring range) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation unless it is non-exempt. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Equal Opportunity Statement: The University of Colorado (CU) is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@ucdenver.edu ​. Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41497&lang=en": {
      "title": "Advanced Practice Provider (APP) (PA/NP/APRN) Pediatric Orthopedic - Adjoint Instructor",
      "description": "Closing Date: 10/29/2026 Posted Date: Oct 23, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: SOM-ORTHO GENERAL OPERATIONS Schedule: Part-time University of Colorado Anschutz Department: Orthopedics Job Title: Adjoint Instructor – Pediatric Orthopedic PA/NP Position #:00854069 – Requisition #:41497 Job Summary: The Department of Orthopedics at the University of Colorado School of Medicine is seeking a part-time exempt, on-call Clinical Instructor-Physician Assistant/Nurse Practitioner in the area of Pediatric Orthopedics to practice at Children's Hospital Colorado-Colorado Springs and the CU Briargate Specialty Clinic for Children in Colorado Springs, Colorado. This position includes membership in the CU Briargate Center, a multispecialty pediatric clinic and CU School of Medicine cost center that includes faculty from multiple departments. The position is not eligible for benefits or tenure. Key Responsibilities: · Provide mid-level night and weekend call coverage for the Pediatric Orthopedic Colorado Springs provider group. · Provide fracture reductions in ER as needed. Perform joint aspirations and injections as needed. Duties will include consultation to CHCO colleagues and outside providers regarding care of orthopedic trauma patients. · Obtains detailed history and performs physical examinations on assigned patients; assesses and treats acute/chronic medical problems and provides direct patient care to a specified patient population. Write prescriptions for PT, OT, imaging studies, and DME as needed. Complete FMLA and other forms and school notes as needed (with assistance from office staff). Primary places of patient care are in a hospital operating room, hospital ward, hospital emergency department, and outpatient clinic. · Assists in providing pre-op, intra-op and post-op care; writes appropriate orders, including those for narcotics and other scheduled drugs. There will be some casting, splinting, and dressing required when the office MA/cast technician is overloaded but this will not be a primary duty. · Occasionally perform emergency lifesaving procedures in cases such as cardiac arrest, respiratory arrest, massive hemorrhage, or similar emergencies. · Notifies attending physician on call, house physician on call, or supervising physician regarding any unusual or unexpected events or problems requiring direct physician consultation. · Practices safety, environmental, and/or infection control methods. · Writes progress notes on patients' office and hospital charts indicating patient status and treatment procedures performed; maintains other records as required. · Provides health education to patients and families · Assist orthopedic surgeon in operating room setting. · Will share telephone, ER and hospital call coverage fairly with physicians. Telephone triage of urgent patients will be a critical function. Work Location: Onsite – this role is expected to work onsite and is located in Aurora, CO. Why Join Us: We are a department of nationally ranked Orthopedic surgeons with a mission to provide the highest quality patient care and advance the field of orthopedics through innovation in research and education. We place a high level of importance on achieving and maintaining a diverse environment that fosters excellence and rewarding opportunities. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. · State of Colorado Certified Physician's Assistant or Inclusion on the State of Colorado Advanced Practice Registry as an Advance Practice Nurse; Certification by the National Commission on Certification of Physician's Assistants or certification by the American Academy of Nurse Practitioners · CPR Certified Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: · Self-directed · Detail-oriented · Excellent communication and interpersonal skills How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): 1. A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position 2. Curriculum vitae / Resume 3. Five professional references including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers . Questions should be directed to: Lindsey Renn, lindsey.renn@cuanschutz.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Immediately and continues until position is filled. For best consideration, apply by October 28, 2026. Anticipated Pay Range: The pay rate for this position has been established as: $50/hour for unrestricted call coverage ($1,200 for 24-hour shift, prorated if less) $100/hour for restricted call coverage or ambulatory clinic coverage. The above pay rate represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation unless it is non-exempt. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: The University of Colorado (CU) is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@ucdenver.edu ​. Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41493&lang=en": {
      "title": "Senior Instructor – Orthopedic Athletic Trainer",
      "description": "Closing Date: 10/29/2026 Posted Date: Oct 23, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: SOM-ORTHO GENERAL OPERATIONS Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Department: School of Medicine – Department of Orthopedics Job Title: Senior Instructor – Orthopedic Athletic Trainer Position #: 00854102 – Requisition #:41493 Job Summary: This is a unique opportunity to work in an academic and clinical Adult Orthopedic Sports Medicine Surgery practice. The position will be a full-time exempt (non-hourly) Senior Instructor -Orthopedic Athletic Trainer position in the Department of Orthopedic Surgery. The position is not eligible for tenure. Key Responsibilities: · Provides daily clinical and operational support to surgeons to facilitate effective patient care and clinic and operating-room efficiency. · Obtains detailed history and performs physical examinations on patients; assesses and treats acute and chronic medical problems, with a focus on the musculoskeletal system, and provides direct patient care to a specified patient population within the scope of professional training, certification, and licensure. · Provides clinical assessment, triage, patient education, and follow-up care through in-person visits and telephone calls. · Participates in team-based care and avails self for emergent patient/staff calls. · Coordinates patient care with outside providers and other medical specialties including but not limited to physicians, physical therapists, Hematology and Pain Management, as needed to support comprehensive patient management and timely access to care. · Assists surgeons with clinic and operating-room preparation, patient care, case coordination, and other clinical needs to support efficient patient flow and operations. · Provides ongoing patient communication and clinical support to facilitate timely resolution of questions, concerns, and postoperative needs throughout the surgical care continuum. · Writes prescriptions for medications, PT, OT, imaging studies, and DME as permitted within applicable professional credentials, institutional policies, and scope of practice. · Writes progress notes on patients' office and hospital charts indicating patient status and treatment procedures performed; maintains other records as required. · Completes preoperative patient and caretaker education. · Completes FMLA and other forms, school and work notes, and other patient documentation as needed. · Provide surgical assistance in the operating room. · Enhances professional growth and development through participation in educational programs, current literature, in-service meetings, workshops, and professional certification opportunities. · Assists with community outreach events, including giving educational talks and assisting with organization, planning, and attendance. · Practices safety, environmental, and infection control methods. · Maintains proficiency in documentation and use of the current electronic medical record program. Additional Responsibilities: · Provides expanded care coordination for complex and out-of-town patients for preoperative and postoperative needs including travel, local accommodations and logistics, postoperative appointments, physical therapy, DME, imaging, procedures, and follow up care. · Provides direct support for care coordination of VIP patients, ensuring appropriate communication and continuity of care. · Assists with education and training of practice-specific workflows of orthopedic surgery fellows and other learners. · Assists with the development and implementation of educational materials, clinical protocols, and postoperative guidelines. · Participates in case discussions and multidisciplinary education with the physical therapy team to review processes, protocols and opportunities for improvement. · Maintains and improves clinical workflows and communication between surgeons, front-desk, clinical staff, radiology, physical therapists, and other members of the care team to facilitate appropriate scheduling, patient flow and coordination of patient care. · Participates in quality improvement and process-improvement initiatives related to patient care, surgical coordination, and clinical operations. · Assists with PRO collection and other research-related activities as needed. Work Location: Onsite - this role is expected to work onsite and is primarily located in Boulder, CO. Why Join Us: We are a department of nationally ranked orthopedic surgeons and our mission is to provide the highest quality, professional and innovative orthopedics care through the integration of comprehensive education and cutting-edge musculoskeletal research. We place a high level of importance on achieving and maintaining a diverse environment that fosters excellence and rewarding opportunities. Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year (based on percentage of time) Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 11/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. · Master’s Degree or equivalent experience · Certification by The Board of Certification for the Athletic Trainer · Licensure with the State of Colorado as an Athletic Trainer. · Current Basic Life Support (BLS) for Healthcare Providers issued by the American Heart Association or the American Red Cross CPR for the Professional Rescuer. · At least 5 years of experience as an Athletic Trainer Preferred Qualifications: · Experience working in conjunction with orthopedic/sports medicine physicians. · Orthopedic Technologist Certification (OTC) · Colorado Surgical Assist licensure. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: · Excellent written and verbal communication skills · Advanced knowledge of the field as it relates to sports medicine How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): 1. A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position 2. Curriculum vitae / Resume 3. Five professional references including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers . Questions should be directed to: Lindsey Renn; lindsey.renn@cuanschutz.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Applications will be accepted until finalists are identified, but preference will be given to complete applications received by October 28, 2026. Those who do not apply by this date may or may not be considered. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as HIRING RANGE: $85,000 - $105,000 The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation unless it is non-exempt. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: The University of Colorado (CU) is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@ucdenver.edu ​. Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41491&lang=en": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor",
      "description": "Closing Date: 10/29/2026 Posted Date: Oct 23, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: SOM-ORTHO GENERAL OPERATIONS Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Department: School of Medicine – Department of Orthopedics Job Title: Assistant Professor Position #: 00854152 – Requisition #: 41491 Job Summary: The position involves the development and sustained growth of an independent, externally funded research program focused on osteoarthritis, fracture healing, and the musculoskeletal implications of the gut microbiome. The successful candidate will establish and lead an innovative research laboratory within the Research Section of the Department of Orthopedics at the University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus. The candidate is expected to develop a nationally recognized research portfolio, secure extramural funding with an emphasis on NIH and other federal funding mechanisms, and foster multidisciplinary collaborations across basic, translational, and clinical science domains. Research activities should advance the understanding of musculoskeletal disease mechanisms and therapeutic strategies, with opportunities to leverage the extensive research infrastructure and collaborative environment of the Anschutz Medical Campus. The successful candidate will mentor graduate students, postdoctoral fellows, research staff, and trainees; contribute to the academic mission of the department; and participate in institutional initiatives that promote scientific innovation, team science, and translational impact. The candidate will be expected to disseminate research findings through high-impact peer reviewed publications and national and international scientific presentations, while building a sustainable program that enhances the department's reputation as a leader in musculoskeletal research. Key Responsibilities: · Develop, conduct, lead, and disseminate innovative research aligned with the Department of Orthopedics' research mission. This includes designing and executing independent research studies; establishing and leading a productive research program; presenting findings at local, national, and international scientific meetings; and publishing results in high-impact, peer-reviewed journals. Responsibilities also include developing competitive grant proposals and securing extramural funding from the NIH, other federal agencies, foundations, and industry partners to support a sustainable and growing research enterprise. · Provide education, mentorship, and training across the academic spectrum. This includes teaching and mentoring undergraduate students, medical students, graduate students, postdoctoral fellows, orthopedic residents, clinical fellows, and other trainees. The successful candidate will provide scientific expertise, supervision, constructive feedback, career development guidance, and leadership, while actively participating in and leading educational seminars, journal clubs, workshops, and community outreach activities. · Foster a culture of collaboration, teamwork, professionalism, and accountability within the Department of Orthopedics and the Research Section. This includes promoting interdisciplinary research initiatives, nurturing productive scientific relationships among faculty, trainees, and staff across all divisions of the department, and contributing to an inclusive and supportive research environment. The successful candidate will be expected to actively engage in collaborative team science efforts and help advance the department's strategic research goals. · Contribute to the growth and visibility of the Department's research enterprise. This includes participating in institutional and departmental committees, supporting strategic research initiatives, developing new collaborative opportunities across the University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus, and enhancing the national and international reputation of the Department of Orthopedics through scholarly achievement, leadership, and service. · Lead and manage an independent research laboratory. Responsibilities include recruiting, supervising, and mentoring research personnel; managing laboratory operations and budgets; ensuring compliance with institutional, regulatory, and funding agency requirements; and maintaining the highest standards of scientific rigor, reproducibility, and research integrity. Work Location: Onsite – this role is expected to work onsite and is located in Aurora, CO. Why Join Us: The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is one of the nation's leading academic health centers, bringing together nationally recognized programs in medicine, nursing, pharmacy, public health, dental medicine, and graduate biomedical sciences. The campus supports a robust community of researchers, clinicians, educators, and trainees engaged in collaborative discovery and translational science. The CU Anschutz School of Medicine recently ranked No. 8 among public medical schools and No. 21 overall nationally in NIH funding , its highest ranking in two decades, demonstrating the institution's strong commitment to research excellence and scientific innovation. The Department of Orthopedics is consistently ranked among the nation's leading orthopedic research programs, providing an exceptional environment for investigators pursuing impactful musculoskeletal research. The Anschutz Medical Campus is also recognized nationally for the strength of its educational and research programs. The School of Medicine is designated a Tier 1 Research Medical School by U.S. News & World Report and is part of a campus that includes numerous nationally ranked graduate and professional programs. The campus is home to extensive core facilities, research centers, clinical research infrastructure, and multidisciplinary collaborations that support investigators from basic discovery through clinical translation and implementation. Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year (based on percentage of time) Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 11/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced rate RTD Bus and light rail service Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. § MD and/or PhD Degree § At least 3 years of postdoctoral experience as a researcher in the musculoskeletal science field Preferred Qualifications: § More than 15 peer-reviewed publications as first or co-author § Active membership in the Orthopedic Research Society or American Society of Bone and Mineral Research § Previous success winning fellowship grants to support predoctoral or postdoctoral research activity § A scored NIH grant (K, R, P or U series) Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities § Experience in an academic laboratory setting performing bench research, data recording and analysis, and creation of figures § Excellent communication and writing skills § Experience participating in the assembly of grant applications § Experience mentoring junior lab staff How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): · A letter of interest describing interest in the position and summarizing the relevant experiences related to listed job qualifications · Current CV · Five professional references including name, title, physical work address, and email address Questions should be directed to: Lindsey Renn, lindsey.renn@cuanschutz.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Immediately and continues until position is filled. For best consideration, apply by October 28, 2026. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established. HIRING RANGE: $105,000 - $125,000 The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation unless it is non-exempt. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: The University of Colorado (CU) is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@ucdenver.edu . Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students, and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41490&lang=en": {
      "title": "Project Manager",
      "description": "Closing Date: 11/07/2026 Posted Date: Oct 23, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: CSPH-LEAD GEN OPS Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Colorado School of Public Health | Lifecourse Epidemiology of Adiposity & Diabetes Center Project Manager Position #: 00854154 – Requisition #: 41490 Job Summary: Join the Colorado School of Public Health as a Project Manager. This position is a key member of the school’s Lifecourse Epidemiology of Adiposity & Diabetes (LEAD) Center and will support a new NIH-funded pre-birth cohort study. This Denver-based cohort is part of a national consortium “Environmental influences on Child Health Outcomes” (ECHO) study. The goal of this project is to recruit and follow longitudinally a cohort of 810 pregnant people, their conceiving partners, and their offspring. This Project Manager will be responsible for the duties outlined below, including implementation of the ECHO research protocol as conducted by study investigators at t he LEAD Center of the Colorado School of Public Health. Key Responsibilities: Hire, train, and manage research assistants and other personnel who are responsible for conducting study visits and communicating with participants. Provide leadership across multiple NIH-funded, multi-site cohort studies with complex visit schedules, biospecimen collection protocols, and longitudinal participant follow-up Actively monitor recruitment and retention efforts to ensure goals are being met. Share key scientific findings and aggregate data with study partners and participants. Assist with developing and submitting progress reports to NIH and other ECHO components. Assist with data collection operations and maintaining data through REDCap Central. Oversee expenditure tracking and develop budget projections. Organize, lead, and record ECHO project meetings (budget meetings, visit implementation meetings, meetings with the Principal Investigators, etc.). This is a full-time position and reports directly to one of the Principal Investigators of the ECHO cohort. Work Location: Why Join Us: On Site – This role is expected to work onsite and is located at the CU Anschutz Campus in Aurora, CO. The Colorado School of Public Health (ColoradoSPH) is a unique and collaborative graduate school that combines the collective expertise of three Colorado universities: the University of Colorado Anschutz (CU Anschutz) in Aurora, Colorado State University (CSU) in Fort Collins, and the University of Northern Colorado (UNC) in Greeley, Colorado. The Colorado School of Public Health is the only accredited school of public health in the Rocky Mountain Region, attracting top tier faculty and students from across the country, and providing a vital contribution towards ensuring our region’s health and wellbeing. The school’s faculty, staff, and students work together to share knowledge and conduct innovative research and community service to actively address public health issues including chronic disease, access to healthcare, environmental threats, emerging infectious diseases, costly injuries, and more. Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 10/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Requirements A bachelor’s degree in public health, public administration, social/behavioral sciences, physical sciences, nursing, healthcare, finance, accounting, business administration, business , or a directly related field from an accredited institution. 4 years of e xtensive, diverse and progressively responsible experience, including direct responsibility for day-to-day operation of a clinical research study and direct staff supervision. Substitution : Option 2: An advanced degree (Masters or Doctorate) may be substituted for experience on a year for year basis if the degree is in a field of study directly related to the work assignment. Preferred Qualifications Experience managing complex longitudinal cohort studies and biospecimen collection workflows Experience with IRB submissions, regulatory coordination, and human subjects research oversight Experience with using research data systems, including REDCap or Epic (or similar electronic medical record systems), and using (non-statistical) data analysis to create reports and presentations and guide management decisions Experience working with pregnant women, children and families Experience working across multiple institutions, clinical sites, and research partners Conditions of Employment Applicants must be able to travel to annual study group meetings (2-3 day trips) given ample notification. Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without requiring sponsorship. We are unable to provide work visa sponsorship or employment authorization for this position now or in the future. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Ability to communicate effectively, both in writing and orally. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with employees at all levels throughout the institution. Outstanding customer service skills. Demonstrated experience in fostering a community that values a wide range of backgrounds, experiences, and perspectives. Outstanding interpersonal and communication skills with the ability to work independently and within diverse team structures Great attention to detail and quality Superior organizational and time management skills, with the ability to manage multiple projects and teams simultaneously. How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following documents: Curriculum Vitae / Resume A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position Three to five professional references including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address should be available upon request. Questions should be directed to: Megan Freije, Megan.Freije@cuanschutz.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Screening begins immediately and continues u ntil November 6, 2026. Anticipated Salary Range: The starting target salary for this position has been established as: $69,209 - $87,000 per year The above salary represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position may be eligible for overtime compensation depending on the level. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Equal Opportunity Statement: CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. As the School of Public Health located within the University of Colorado on the Anschutz Campus, we are committed to developing and sustaining a faculty, staff, and student body that reflects a broad range of backgrounds and perspectives. We advocate for and actively lead efforts and activities to build a community that treats people with dignity, respect, and compassion among the school’s students, staff, faculty, and external community partners. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@cuanschutz.edu ​. Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41489&lang=en": {
      "title": "HR Recruitment Specialist (Open Rank)",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 23, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: SOM-PSYCH GENERAL OPERATIONS Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Department: Psychiatry Job Title: HR Recruitment Specialist (Open Rank) Position #: 00854150 Requisition #: 41489 Job Summary: The Department of Psychiatry seeks an HR Recruitment Specialist at the Intermediate or Senior Level. The Specialist will focus on recruitment of faculty and staff within the department as part of a team to support major growth within the department. Key Responsibilities: Oversee recruitment through the entire recruitment process and Onboarding of new employees. Manage the posting of requisitions on various job boards and track efficacy of each site. Works with the HR Program Manager to manage the hire process for temporary staff and working retiree hires. Works with the HR Program Manager to manage the recruitment of internal administrative stipend process. Recruitment approval process for the Assistant Professor promotion process. Works with HR Program Manager on conflict resolution within the recruitment team Works with HR Program manager to strategize around how to improve the recruitment process. Work Location: Hybrid – this role is eligible for a hybrid schedule of 3 days per week on campus and as needed for in-person meetings. Why Join Us: The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is a world-class medical destination at the forefront of transformative science, medicine, education, and patient care. The campus encompasses the University of Colorado health professional schools, more than 60 centers and institutes, and two nationally ranked independent hospitals - UCHealth University of Colorado Hospital and Children's Hospital Colorado - that treat more than two million adult and pediatric patients each year. Innovative, interconnected and highly collaborative, the University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus delivers life-changing treatments, patient care and professional training and conducts world-renowned research fueled by over $650 million in research grants. For more information, visit www.cuanschutz.edu. The Department of Psychiatry is one of the largest units in the UCD-SOM and is comprised of 5 Divisions. The CU Department of Psychiatry sets the standard for Education and Training of leaders in psychiatry and mental health care, conducts ground-breaking Research that aims to eradicate suffering due to psychiatric and substance use disorders, provides ready access to state of-the-art mental health preventions and interventions across the continuum of care, and collaborates with the community and other key stakeholders to promote well-being among all Coloradans. We accomplish this vision in a manner that respects, values and advocates for the dignity and worth of each individual and family. The University of Colorado offers a comprehensive benefits package that includes health insurance, life insurance, retirement plans, tuition benefits, ECO pass, paid time off – vacation, sick, holidays and more. To see what benefits are available, please visit: https://www.cu.edu/employee-services/benefits-wellness . Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 15/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Intermediate Level: A bachelor’s degree in public administration, public policy, business, higher education administration, social sciences, behavioral sciences or a directly related field from an accredited institution. A combination of education and related technical/paraprofessional experience may be substituted for the bachelor’s degree on a year for year basis. One (1) year of professional level experience in Human Resources or Recruitment. Senior Level: A bachelor’s degree in public administration, public policy, business, higher education administration, social sciences, behavioral sciences or a directly related field from an accredited institution. A combination of education and related technical/paraprofessional experience may be substituted for the bachelor’s degree on a year for year basis. Two (2) years of professional level experience of Human Resources or Recruitment. Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Preferred Qualifications: Experience managing and handling sensitive and confidential information. Experience in project management. Experience with working in Smartsheet. Experience using CU programs (Smartsheet, HCM, FIMS, Salesforce, or similar programs). Experience working with students, staff, and faculty, within a higher education and/or academic medical environment. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Must be able to work independently. Strong and effective communication and writing skills, and a proven record of forming collaborative and effective working relationships. Ability to efficiently organize, multi-task, and prioritize duties and tasks. Ability to multi-task and maintain consistent high-level performance. Manages and enforces deadlines and schedules. Demonstrated ability to work effectively and harmoniously with supervisors, co-workers and various interested parties Ability to analyze, interpret, and evaluate a broad range of laws, rules, and regulations in order to exercise good judgment in applying them to human resource challenges. Knowledge of the professional standards, concepts, and practices of recruitment and selection, employee relations, or organizational development and human resource policy. Ability to communicate effectively, both in writing and orally, including public speaking. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with employees at all levels throughout the institution. Thorough knowledge of current management and leadership methods and best practices. Proficiency with Microsoft Office suite. Conditions of Employment: Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without requiring sponsorship. We are unable to provide work visa sponsorship or employment authorization for this position now or in the future. How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position Curriculum vitae / Resume Three to five professional references, including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Questions should be directed to: Brandon Fenner at brandon.fenner@cuanschutz.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Immediately and continues until position is filled. For best consideration, apply by November 20, 2026. Those who do not apply by this date may or may not be considered. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as Intermediate Professional: $52,793 - $67,152 Senior Professional: $57,073 - $72,597 The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position may be eligible for overtime compensation, depending on the level. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@cuanschutz.edu ​. Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41488&lang=en": {
      "title": "Research Services Clinical Sciences Professional (Open Rank: Entry to Intermediate)",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 23, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: SOM-EM MED CLINICAL Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus Department: Emergency Medicine Job Title: Research Services Clinical Sciences Professional (Open Rank: Entry to Intermediate) Position #00845108: – Requisition #: 41488 Job Summary: The Department of Emergency Medicine and the principal investigator, Dr. Elizabeth Goldberg, MD, ScM,, is seeking applications for a Clinical Sciences Professional (Open Rank: Entry-Intermediate) . This is a full-time University staff position to support ongoing grant-funded studies focused on geriatric emergency medicine, injury prevention, and digital health. Funding support comes from multi-year project grants from Health and Human Services and the National Institutes of Health. This research team focuses on observational studies and interventional trials related to emergency care. The candidate will assume the role of Clinical Sciences Professional within a highly collaborative and exciting multi-disciplinary team. The job is in-person and duties will be performed in the U.S. from office buildings on the University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus in Aurora, CO. This position will exercise building independence and work under the supervision of the PI and project coordinator to assist the team to conduct clinically relevant research. The Department of Emergency Medicine seeks motivated applicants for the position of Clinical Science Professional. This position requires familiarity and experience with clinical or epidemiological research, and an interest in geriatric to injury prevention. The ideal candidate will have experience within research (clinical or laboratory), collaborate effectively on multidisciplinary teams, and be highly detail oriented. Key Responsibilities Entry Professional: Primarily assist with and oversee the day-to-day operations of clinical trials and other studies Manage and conduct moderately complex research activities that are part of larger projects from initiation to close. Obtain participants’ medical history and current medication information, review research protocol inclusion/exclusion criteria, and confirm eligibility of participant to participate in clinical trials Perform informed consent process or ensures that the informed consent process has occurred, is properly documented, and that informed consent form documents are filed as required Interview prospective subjects for a variety of research clinical trials. Educate potential subjects on the details of the studies through phone contacts and personal interviews Schedule subject participation in research clinical trial, coordinating availability of necessary space, and clinical research support (e.g., physician, nurse practitioner, physical therapy, pharmacy) Identify, screen and consent potential study participants. Interact with clinical staff to confirm eligibility and implement study protocols. Extract relevant data from participant or medical records and enter it into online centralized databases or local data tools. Collect, code, and analyze data obtained from research in an accurate and timely manner Evaluate data sets for quality and completeness. Set up and or run statistical analyses. Analyze data, including statistical analyses and qualitative assessments of data and data quality. Identify and help solve gaps in data collection. Adhere to research regulatory standards Maintain detailed records of studies to ensure compliance with requirements, study protocols, department, hospital/clinical standard operating procedures and other regulatory guidelines Participate in subject recruitment efforts, including communicating with patients expressing an interest and all pre-screening/screening activities Ensure that the necessary supplies and equipment for studies are in stock and in working order Intermediate Professional, all of the above and: Independently master study materials, including but not limited to protocols, informed consent forms, and all other essential study documents for assigned studies Independently perform study related processes, procedures, and assessments as defined in study protocol and in compliance with regulating bodies Assist Team Leads, Supervisors and/or management with creation and implementation of processes and procedures and quality improvement initiatives Act as a Primary Coordinator on multiple trials/studies Assist and train junior team members Additional Duties & Responsibilities Manage and conduct moderately complex research activities that are part of larger project from initiation to close. Create complex data management and tracking tools (REDCap, ACCESS, Excel) to support tracking of project/recruitment activities. Oversee student worker(s) or junior research assistants as it relates to a specific project. Travel to study sites including fall prevention programs and referral partner sites (clinical offices and hospitals) Participate in instrument creation and/or analytical structures as appropriate to the project. Participate in tactical and strategic program/project development and planning. Collect study data via complex patient visits, surveys, observations or focus groups. Provide leadership in data collection to other research assistants and students. Carry out straightforward data analysis (e.g., summary data, histograms) and have basic skills in interpretation of descriptive statistics. Leverage creative problem-solving skills to ensure high data quality from a team of national data collectors Participate in audits, monitoring visits, and quality control checks of data collection, equipment maintenance, and study procedures. Help develop study findings for presentation to team and external audiences. May lead publication development (abstract/manuscript) Help with budget management/tracking (under direction of PM/PI) Lead manuscript preparation for publication or presentation in scientific forums. Work with members of the UCD and UCHealth community as needed to set up labs, participant visits, and access shared University resources. Manage study participant incentive program This description is a summary only and describes the general level of work being performed, it is not intended to be all-inclusive. The duties of this position may change from time to time and/or based on business need. We reserve the right to add or delete duties and responsibilities at the discretion of the supervisor and/or hiring authority. Work Location: Onsite – this role is expected to work onsite at the CU Anschutz Medical Campus . Why Join Us: The Department of Emergency Medicine conducts research into areas such as trauma, injury prevention, opioid misuse, critical care, mental health, pharmacogenomics, toxicology, global health, and healthcare policy. The Department values team members who are eager to pursue further training and growth as a researcher professional. The successful applicant will have a passion for research, enjoy and excel in the sharing of knowledge and life-long learning, and have a desire to work in a collaborative and driven pool of talented co-workers. Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 10/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Entry Professional: Bachelor’s degree in any field A combination of education and related technical/paraprofessional experience may be substituted for the bachelor’s degree on a year for year basis Intermediate Professional: Bachelor’s degree in any field A combination of education and related technical/paraprofessional experience may be substituted for the bachelor’s degree on a year for year basis One (1) year clinical research or related experience Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Preferred Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in science or health-related field Master’s degree in public health, or a research-related discipline Strong interest or previous experience working in geriatric emergency medicine, injury prevention, and/or digital health research Three (3) years of clinical research or related experience Experience with electronic data capture systems (e.g. EMR or EHR and data management systems) Conditions of Employment: Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without requiring sponsorship. We are unable to provide work visa sponsorship or employment authorization for this position now or in the future. Competencies/Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Knowledge and understanding of federal regulations and Good Clinical Practice (GCP) Ability to communicate effectively, both in writing and orally Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with employees at all levels throughout the institution Outstanding customer service skills Demonstrated commitment and leadership ability to advance diversity and inclusion Ability to interpret and master complex research protocol information Familiarity with medical/research terminology Excellent written and oral communication skills Ability to understand and interpret medical terminology and medical charts Excellent organizational, analytical and interpersonal skills Ability to think creatively, adapt quickly and work independently Excellent team player Enjoys working with human research subjects Self-starter with a desire to improve human health through research High Level Skills with Computer-Based Tools (Word, Outlook, PowerPoint, Etc.) How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position Curriculum vitae / Resume Three to five professional references, including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Questions should be directed to: EMED Human Resources at emed.humanresources@ucdenver.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Immediately and continues until position is filled. For best consideration, apply by October 30, 2026. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as Entry: $49,899 – $66,865 Intermediate: $54,302 - $72,765 The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position may be eligible for overtime compensation, depending on the level. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@cuanschutz.edu ​. Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41486&lang=en": {
      "title": "Research Services Professional Entry Level",
      "description": "Closing Date: 10/28/2026 Posted Date: Oct 22, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: SOM-OB/GYN RS GENERAL OPS Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus Department: Obstetrics & Gynecology Job Title: Research Services Professional Entry Level Position 00853994 – Requisition #:41486 Job Summary: The Department of Obstetrics and Gynecology has a full-time opening for a Research Services Entry Professional in the Division of Reproductive Sciences, whose principal investigator is a basic/translational research scientist. The selected individual will conduct research focused on placental physiology and function in humans and experimental animals and how changes in placental function causes pregnancy complications and programs the baby for disease later in life. This position has a particular focus on understanding the role of proteins secreted into the fetal circulation in preventing poor outcomes in prematurity. Key Responsibilities / Duties: Management of animal colonies: Daily check on mice and guinea-pig colonies (including weighing, checking plugs and status of vaginal membranes). Participate in animal surgery, experimentation and tissue collection Be responsible for maintenance of neonatal intensive care unit (NICU) for premature guinea-pigs. Performing laboratory analyses including immunoblotting, immunohistochemistry, RNA and DNA isolation, qPCRs, biochemical assays and ELISAs. Participating in general lab maintenance, including preparing standard buffers, maintaining accurate and detailed records of samples, chemicals and antibodies, doing dishes and general upkeep Handling procurement for lab supplies and services for the lab Comply with university policy on lab operations. Perform other duties as assigned. Work Location: Onsite – this role is expected to work onsite and is located in Aurora, CO. Why Join Us: The Department of Obstetrics and Gynecology at the University of Colorado is a world-class research enterprise, ranked 17th in the nation by the Blue Ridge Institute for federal funding. The Department currently has an impressive research portfolio of $32M in existing federal and foundation grants and contracts through the lifetime of the projects, increasing in budget annually by $9M. Departmental faculty provide a full-spectrum of clinical care for women of all ages, participate in research, and provide education to students and residents. Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 10/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in biology, molecular biology, chemistry, genetics or related field. Substitution : A combination of education and related technical/military/paraprofessional experience may be substituted for a bachelor’s degree on a year for year basis. Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Conditions of Employment: Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without requiring sponsorship. We are unable to provide work visa sponsorship or employment authorization for this position now or in the future. Preferred Qualifications Master’s degree in biology, molecular biology, chemistry, genetics or related field Prior experience or background within an experimental or wet lab Experience with animal experimentation Competencies, Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Knowledge of laboratory techniques including safety procedures and techniques Ability to communicate effectively, both in writing and orally Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with employees at all levels throughout the institution Outstanding customer service skills Demonstrated commitment and leadership ability to advance diversity and inclusion Knowledge of basic human anatomy, physiology medical terminology Ability to interpret and master complex research protocol information Flexibility with work hours How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position Curriculum vitae / Resume Three to five professional references, including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Questions should be directed to: Olivia Castillo, Olivia.castillo@cuanschutz.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Immediately. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as HIRING RANGE Entry Level: $47,811 - $ 64,067. The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position may be eligible for overtime compensation, depending on the level. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@cuanschutz.edu ​. Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41480&lang=en": {
      "title": "Women’s Health Psychologist Open Rank-Instructor, Sr. Instructor, Assistant Professor",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 22, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: SOM-PSYCH-OTHR CLIN SVS-GEN OP Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Department: Department of Psychiatry Job Title: Women’s Health Psychologist Open Rank-Instructor, Sr. Instructor, Assistant Professor Position #:00854021 – Requisition #:41480 Job Summary: The Women’s Behavioral Health and Wellness (WBHW) Service Line in the Department of Psychiatry (DOP) has an opening for a .8 Women’s Health Psychologist at the Instructor – Assistant Professor rank. This faculty member will provide direct patient services within a diverse set of WBHW clinical settings, which may include reproductive mental health specialty outpatient care and/or integrated services within Ob/Gyn or other women’s health specialty settings. The ideal candidate will be a skilled clinician with subspecialty training in psychology across the lifespan, an enthusiastic educator, and have a strong interest in service innovation, scholarship, and quality improvement. The WBHW clinical team provides patient-centered and evidence-based care aimed to promote wellness in women across the lifespan. Our dynamic interdisciplinary team of psychologists, psychiatrists, and social workers work collaboratively with primary care providers and specialists to offer consultative services and problem-focused care for women with behavioral health concerns related to periods of reproductive transition or medical conditions or treatment impacting reproductive hormones and well-being. We aim to maintain and expand access to services by implementing innovative models of clinical care, providing interdisciplinary clinical training, and deepening collaborative community and public partnerships. Key Responsibilities: · Provides direct patient care within WBHW clinical settings. · Supervision of medical trainees within WBHW. · Timely documentation of clinical interactions and adherence to clinic operations procedures Collaboration with WBHW faculty and staff, in addition to colleagues across the health system, to build professional relationships and provide patient-centered care. Work Location: Hybrid – this role is eligible for a hybrid schedule of 3 days per week on campus and as needed for in-person meetings. Why Join Us: The Department of Psychiatry is one of the largest units in the UCD-SOM and is comprised of 5 Divisions. The CU Department of Psychiatry sets the standard for Education and Training of leaders in psychiatry and mental health care, conducts ground-breaking Research that aims to eradicate suffering due to psychiatric and substance use disorders, provides ready access to state of-the-art mental health preventions and interventions across the continuum of care, and collaborates with the community and other key stakeholders to promote well-being among all Coloradans. We accomplish this vision in a manner that respects, values and advocates for the dignity and worth of each individual and family. Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year (based on percentage of time) Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 11/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. This is an open rank position and could be categorized as Instructor, Senior Instructor or Assistant Professor based on experience and qualifications as indicated below: SOM only (required language): Open Track: To support the growth of our faculty, selected candidates will be offered the opportunity to choose a track that corresponds to their area of excellence. Learn more about faculty tracks at the Office for Faculty Affairs . Open Rank: Rank at the time of appointment will be based on the candidate’s demonstrated contributions and experience in teaching, clinical, research, and/or service to the field. We welcome applicants with a range of backgrounds and accomplishments and encourage individuals to highlight the breadth and depth of their professional impact. Learn more about faculty tracks at the Office for Faculty Affairs . Instructor: ● 1-4 years of related clinical experience at rank or equivalent experience. ● Minimum degree qualifications: PhD/PsyD Senior Instructor: ● 1-4 years of related clinical experience at rank or equivalent experience. ● Minimum degree qualifications: PhD/PsyD Assistant Professor: ● 1-4 years of related clinical experience at rank or equivalent experience. ● Proven record of training, leadership, or publications ● Minimum degree qualifications: PhD/Psyd Preferred Qualifications: ● Experience with mental health care of sexual health. Certified in American Association of Sexuality Educators, Counselors and Therapists (AASECT) or similar certification or willing to become certified. ● Experience with mental health integration into primary care or ob/gyn settings. ● Expertise in the psychiatric care of perinatal persons as well as individuals who are receiving care for breast cancer, pelvic pain, menses-related mood disorders, infertility and/or symptoms of perimenopause. ● Interest in and experience with teaching medical trainees. ● Interest and experience in supporting the health and wellbeing of healthcare providers. ● Experience with EPIC. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: · Ability to communicate effectively, both orally and in writing, with faculty, staff, students, alumni, industry and the public. · Demonstrated commitment and leadership ability to advance equity, belonging, and fair opportunities for all. · Knows and applies best practices in promoting equity, fostering belonging, and understanding and respecting cultural differences. · Knowledge regarding clinical research regulations and principles of ethical conduct. · A demonstrated ability to organize and complete complex projects and to work under tight deadlines. · Must be comfortable working in high volume, fast paced office environment Conditions of Employment: ( Optional Statement) · Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without requiring sponsorship. We are unable to provide work visa sponsorship or employment authorization for this position now or in the future. How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): 1. A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position 2. Curriculum vitae / Resume 3. Five professional references including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers . Questions should be directed to: Anna Geiermann, anna.geiermann@cuanschutz.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Immediately and continues until position is filled. For best consideration, apply by 11/22/2026. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as HIRING RANGE: Instructor: $88,000 - $104,000 Based on 0.8 FTE Sr. Instructor: $88,000 - $104,000 Based on 0.8 FTE Assistant Professor: $88,000 - $104,000 Based on 0.8 FTE The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation unless it is non-exempt. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: The University of Colorado (CU) is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@ucdenver.edu ​. Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=40701&lang=en": {
      "title": "Behavioral Health Program Director",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 22, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: CON-DEAN ADMINISTRATION Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Behavioral Health Program Director Instructor / Senior Instructor / Assistant Professor of Clinical Practice (Open Rank College of Nursing Position Location: Sheridan Health Services (Southwest Denver) 3525 W. Oxford Avenue | Unit G1 Denver, CO 80236 Position #: 00611421 – Requisition #: 40701 Job Summary: The CU College of Nursing has an opening for a full-time (1.0 FTE) position as a Behavioral Health Program Director within its federally qualified health center (FQHC), Sheridan Health Services (SHS), located in southwest Denver, CO (zip code: 80236). This position is clinic based and includes dedicated 0.50 FTE effort for administrative duties. It is in the Clinical Practice Faculty Series and faculty rank is based on experience and qualifications. Health care provider positions at SHS, such as this one, qualify for federal and state loan repayment (more info at: https://tinyurl.com/pts4k4z2 ). The Behavioral Health Program Director is part of the SHS senior leadership team and will uphold the SHS mission by assuring the delivery of high-quality integrated care services and the fiscal soundness of the organization by meeting productivity standards. This position serves in an advisory capacity making recommendations about primary care and behavioral health integration to improve service delivery and achieve improved health outcomes. The position is responsible for the administrative and clinical management of psychiatric and behavioral health (BH) services. Clinic Description: Sheridan Health Services is a multi-site, nurse-managed FQHC, funded through the Health Resources and Services Administration Bureau of Primary Healthcare. The clinic serves community health needs primarily for residents of Arapahoe, Denver, and Jefferson counties, and is located in southwest Denver on the Fort Logan campus. It provides services to adults and children, 65% of whom identify as Latinx, and 42% of whom are best served in another language, with Spanish being the predominant second language. Services offered include primary care across the lifespan; prenatal and postpartum, women’s health, dentistry, pharmacy, behavioral health, and outpatient substance use treatment. SHS is a Patient-Centered Medical Home and upholds a model of care that places the patient at the center, incorporating the values and beliefs of the individual in all decision-making. https://nursing.cuanschutz.edu/patient-care/sheridan-health-services Program Management Core responsibilities of the Behavioral Health Program Director include programmatic oversight for creation, implementation and management of clinical programs within BH service line, oversite of fiscal expenditures, and supervision of BH providers and BH Patient Navigator. This position will ensure behavioral health programs operate within budgeted revenues and achieve productivity goals. This position shall be vigilant of potential new revenue streams and respond to these as appropriate (e.g., grants, contracts, managed care contracts, governmental relations, etc.). Clinical Care The Behavioral Health Program Director will provide a portion of total effort .5 FTE in direct care to patients from diverse backgrounds. · Provide brief behavioral health therapy and screenings in an integrated medical setting for patients across the lifespan (ages 0–99). · Deliver outpatient behavioral health services, including individual therapy, crisis intervention, care coordination, skill building, and psychoeducation. · Complete all documentation accurately, within established timelines, and in full compliance with clinic policies and professional standards, including timely completion of notes, referrals, follow ‑ up tasks, and any required paper records. Compliance Responsible for audit and compliance activities to ensure that behavioral health services and standards follow all state, federal, and CU regulations, in addition to contractual requirements associated with payers and funders, in collaboration with leadership team. Community Engagement Participate in community outreach for the purpose of increasing access to care, reducing barriers to treatment, and advancing the mission and vision of SHS. It will also be responsible for establishing and maintaining community partnerships. This description is a summary only and describes the general level of work being performed; it is not intended to be all-inclusive. The duties of this position may change from time to time and/or based on business need. We reserve the right to add or delete duties and responsibilities at the discretion of the supervisor and/or hiring authority. Work Location: Hybrid – this role is eligible for a hybrid schedule of 3 days per week on campus and as needed for in-person meetings. Why Join Us: CU Nursing is an amazing place to be. We have the distinct advantage of being a part of a huge medical campus with three incredible hospitals – the VA, the nationally ranked University of Colorado Hospital, and the Children’s Hospital Colorado where our nursing students and faculty learn every day. From our beginning 125 years ago as part of the School of Medicine at CU Boulder to our current home at the Anschutz Medical Campus, the college has been a recognized leader in nursing education (ranked #10 in online MS graduate programs by U.S. News & World Report 2023). Our faculty, students and staff have been instrumental in shaping the profession of nursing and teaching the next generation of nurses while treating patients in our own nurse-led clinics. Be a part of an innovative, dynamic, diverse, and exciting workplace -- helping make great things happen. Join us in our quest to boldly transform health together. Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation, and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package, including: · Medical: Multiple plan options · Dental: Multiple plan options · Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision · Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay · Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year · Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) · Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) · Holiday Days: 15/year · Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses · ECO Pass: Reduced-rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications Instructor: · Master’s degree from an accredited institution in one of the following disciplines: o Social work o Counseling o Marriage and family therapy o OR Doctorate degree in Psychology (PhD or PsyD) · Current licensure as a clinical social worker (LCSW), professional counselor (LPC), marriage and family therapist (LMFT), or psychologist (LP), in good standing o Must have CO licensures by date of hire. Could be working toward CO clinical licenses during application process and registered with DORA-Department of Regulatory Agencies. o Please review DORA’s Licensing Guides for detailed requirements: § Licensed Professional Counselor § Licensed Clinical Social Worker § Licensed Marriage & Family Therapist § Psychologist Four (4) years’ post-graduate experience providing direct patient care services One (1) year experience as a clinical supervisor Senior Instructor : Master’s degree from an accredited institution in one of the following disciplines: Social work Counseling Marriage and family therapy OR Doctorate degree in Psychology (PhD or PsyD) Current licensure as a clinical social worker (LCSW), professional counselor (LPC), marriage and family therapist (LMFT), or psychologist (LP), in good standing Must have CO licensures by date of hire. Could be working toward CO clinical licenses during application process and registered with DORA-Department of Regulatory Agencies. o Please review DORA’s Licensing Guides for detailed requirements: § Licensed Professional Counselor Licensed Clinical Social Worker Licensed Marriage & Family Therapist Psychologist Four (4) years’ post-graduate experience providing direct patient care services One (1) year experience as a clinical supervisor Demonstrated leadership in area of practice Demonstrated experience collaborating with academic colleagues and students in practice activities Assistant Professor : Doctorate degree from an accredited institution in one of the following disciplines: Social work Counseling Marriage and family therapy Psychology (PhD or PsyD) Current licensure as a clinical social worker (LCSW), professional counselor (LPC), marriage and family therapist (LMFT), or psychologist (LP), in good standing Must have CO licensures by date of hire. Could be working toward CO clinical licenses during application process and registered with DORA-Department of Regulatory Agencies. o Please review DORA’s Licensing Guides for detailed requirements: § Licensed Professional Counselor Licensed Clinical Social Worker Licensed Marriage & Family Therapist Psychologist Four (4) years’ post-graduate experience providing direct patient care services One (1) year experience as a clinical supervisor Demonstrated leadership in area of practice Demonstrated experience collaborating with academic colleagues and students in practice activities Applicants must meet minimum qualifications by time of hire. Conditions of employment: Obtain Colorado licenses by date of hire. Obtain valid NPI number by date of hire Obtain valid Colorado Medicaid Provider number within 30 days of hire date Complete CAQH by date of hire Remain credentialed by all necessary parties and ensure credentialing materials stay current. Obtain and maintain current BLS/CPR certification by date of hire. Willing and able to work in a normal patient care environment with some exposure to biological hazards and infectious diseases. Willing and able to work until 6pm on designated weeknights in rotation with other providers for Extended Hours. Preferred Qualifications: Experience working in a primary care or school-based health center setting using a brief model of service delivery Bilingual skills (Spanish/English) at a conversation level in a clinical setting Credentialed as a certified addiction specialist (CAS) or licensed addiction counselor (LAC) Experience as a preceptor/clinical supervisor of students and/or behavioral health trainees and interns · Experience successfully navigating program compliance and audits, as well as evidence of billing and reporting experience. Competencies : Leadership & Program Management Ability to establish program goals and objectives, evaluate progress, and manage multiple clinical program sites efficiently. Skill in providing both administrative and clinical supervision to behavioral health staff and trainees. Demonstrated ability to lead teams, foster collaboration, and build a cohesive, high ‑ functioning work environment. Clinical Expertise Expertise in clinical assessment and therapeutic interventions with individuals and groups; experience with family or couples therapy preferred. Demonstrated knowledge of primary care–behavioral health integration, including co ‑ located and fully integrated service models and population ‑ based interventions. Medical literacy, including familiarity with common medical terminology, first ‑ line psychiatric medications, and interdisciplinary treatment team dynamics. Cultural Responsiveness Knowledge of the cultural, social, and economic factors impacting the diverse populations served, and ability to apply culturally responsive practices. Demonstrated commitment to cultural responsiveness in clinical practice and leadership. Compliance, Quality, & Regulatory Knowledge Knowledge of regulatory requirements for clinical program oversight, billing, reporting, and compliance with state, federal, and payer standards. Ability to lead quality improvement activities and support staff in meeting quality and documentation standards. Skill in collecting, interpreting, and using data for reporting and program improvement. Communication & Interpersonal Skills Strong communication skills, including the ability to present information effectively, provide consultation, and navigate conflict resolution. Proven ability to build and sustain effective working relationships with patients, families, staff, faculty, and community partners. Technical & Documentation Skills Ability to document accurately and efficiently in an Electronic Health Record and use clinic software systems. Ability to provide services on virtual platforms and deliver telehealth care when required. Productivity & Organizational Skills Ability to set, maintain, and achieve productivity expectations for self and team. Strong initiative, independent work skills, and ability to address issues proactively to support desired outcomes. How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): 1. A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to the listed job qualifications and interest in the position 2. Curriculum vitae / Resume Questions should be directed to: College of Nursing Human Resources at CON.HR@ucdenver.edu or 303.724.4447. Screening of Applications Begins: Applications will be accepted until finalists are identified, but preference will be given to complete applications received by November 13 th , 2026 . Those who do not apply by this date may or may not be considered. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as HIRING RANGE: Instructor: $71,444 to $79,752 Sr. Instructor: $72,159 to $80,549 Assistant Professor: $72.873 to $81,347 The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation unless it is non-exempt. In addition to the annual salary for this position, an annual administrative stipend of $10,000/year will also be offered. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@cuanschutz.edu . Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students, and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine-preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety-sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41484&lang=en": {
      "title": "Open Rank OCD IOP Therapist - Instructor, Sr. Instructor",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 22, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: SOM-PSYCH-OTHR CLIN SVS-GEN OP Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Department: Department of Psychiatry Job Title: Open Rank OCD IOP Therapist - Instructor, Sr. Instructor Position #: 00854022 – Requisition #:41484 Job Summary: The Department of Psychiatry at the University of Colorado School of Medicine has an opening for a full (1.0 FTE) faculty position in the Obsessive Compulsive Disorder (OCD) Program. This position and will provide direct patient services in the Intensive Outpatient Program (IOP) as well as the Outpatient Clinic. The Intensive Outpatient Program (IOP) therapist at the University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus Obsessive Compulsive Disorder (OCD) Program will join a team of mental health providers treating community members with OCD requiring a higher level of care. The primary responsibilities of this clinician are to run groups in the IOP program (focusing on psychoeducation, skills development, and experiential), provide brief as-needed check-in appointments of 30 minutes or less, and complete exposures with IOP patients. A once-a-month group will be provided to support systems of individuals participating in the IOP program. In addition, the IOP therapist will be expected to hold a small caseload of patients at an outpatient level of care who have stepped down from IOP. The OCD program team members include psychiatrists, psychologists, and social workers. The team utilizes an Exposure and Response Prevention (ERP) modality for individuals presenting with OCD. The IOP Therapist must be willing to learn and implement an ERP approach, if not already trained in ERP. The IOP will run Monday, Tuesday, and Thursday from 8:30-11:30am. This clinician will also be expected to join and participate in team meetings prior to the start of the IOP day. Key Responsibilities: Provides multiculturally sensitive behavior health assessment, triage, case management, and individual and group psychotherapy. Collaborate with other mental health faculty and staff in the provision of mental health and wellness care. Manage details of insurance including authorization and peer to peer reviews for denials. Chart patient visits using an electronic medical record. Assist in discharge planning, including identifying community placement. Develop programmatic benchmarks and outcomes of effectiveness. Participate in quality and performance assessment projects. Participate in the development of and administration of group programs including skills development, ERP, experiential activities, and mindfulness. Participate in other programs and service development. · Other duties as assigned Work Location: Hybrid – this role is eligible for a hybrid schedule of 3 days per week on campus and as needed for in-person meetings. Why Join Us: The Department of Psychiatry is one of the largest units in the UCD-SOM and is comprised of 5 Divisions. The CU Department of Psychiatry sets the standard for Education and Training of leaders in psychiatry and mental health care, conducts ground-breaking Research that aims to eradicate suffering due to psychiatric and substance use disorders, provides ready access to state of-the-art mental health preventions and interventions across the continuum of care, and collaborates with the community and other key stakeholders to promote well-being among all Coloradans. We accomplish this vision in a manner that respects, values and advocates for the dignity and worth of each individual and family. Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year (based on percentage of time) Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 11/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. This is an open rank position and could be categorized as Instructor or Senior Instructor based on experience and qualifications as indicated below: Open Track: To support the growth of our faculty, selected candidates will be offered the opportunity to choose a track that corresponds to their area of excellence. Learn more about faculty tracks at the Office for Faculty Affairs . Open Rank: Rank at the time of appointment will be based on the candidate’s demonstrated contributions and experience in teaching, clinical, research, and/or service to the field. We welcome applicants with a range of backgrounds and accomplishments and encourage individuals to highlight the breadth and depth of their professional impact. Learn more about faculty tracks at the Office for Faculty Affairs . Instructor: ● 1-3 years of related clinical experience at rank or equivalent experience. ● Minimum degree qualifications: Master's Degree in Social Work or Counseling ● LCSW Senior Instructor: ● 1-3 years of related clinical experience at rank or equivalent experience. ● Minimum degree qualifications: Master's Degree in Social Work or Counseling ● LCSW Preferred Qualifications: ● LCSW, LPC or LMFT with active CO license ● Experience in program development and wellness ● Must have experience using Electronic Health Record and Patient Health Information management systems. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: ● Professional and personal qualities to work effectively with faculty, administrators, and patients. ● Must be willing to learn and implement treatment modalities relevant to OCD ● Knowledge of OCD comorbid mental health issues ● Demonstration of flexibility and problem-solving ● Knowledge of evidence-based treatments including: ERP, Cognitive Behavioral Therapy (CBT), Acceptance and Commitment Therapy (ACT), Dialectical Behavior Therapy (DBT), Cognitive Remediation Therapy (CRT), and Habit Reversal Training (HRT) ● Strong clinical judgement & leadership skills ● Excellent public speaking and interpersonal skills ● Must be knowledgeable OCD and comorbid mental health disorders including anxiety, depression, substance use, trauma, and eating disorders. ● Must have skills in risk assessment, including suicide and violence risk assessment. ● Must be comfortable with case management and coordination of care. ● Must be comfortable with a combination of individual and group therapy, as well as working with families. ● Must be efficient with time management with the ability to see many patients in a row if needed or to use time constructively for administrative or other work. ● Must develop knowledge about step-down processes and network with community providers. ● Must be able to work closely and collaboratively with the OCD program. ● Must be able to work cooperatively with all constituencies in the Department of Psychiatry including Departmental Chair, Program Directors, and administrative staff. ● Outstanding customer service skills. Conditions of Employment: ● Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without requiring sponsorship. We are unable to provide work visa sponsorship or employment authorization for this position now or in the future. How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): 1. A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position 2. Curriculum vitae / Resume 3. Five professional references including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers . Questions should be directed to: brandon.fenner@cuanschutz.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Immediately and continues until position is filled. For best consideration, apply by 11/22/2026. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as HIRING RANGE: Instructor: $ 72,000 to $80,000 Sr. Instructor: $ 72,000 to $80,000 The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation unless it is non-exempt. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: The University of Colorado (CU) is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@ucdenver.edu ​. Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41479&lang=en": {
      "title": "Open Rank Medical Assistant - Centerfield, Family Medicine",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 22, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: SOM-DEAN DO CPD - PRIM CARE Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus Department: Community Practice Job Title: Open Rank Medical Assistant - Centerfield, Family Medicine Position #: 00854097 – Requisition #: 41479 Job Summary: Calling all Medical Assistants and Certified Medical Assistants! Our busy clinics are recruiting for Medical Assistants! We need your training and skills to help our clinic run smoothly, providing our patients with top notch quality care. The Medical Assistant (MA) or Certified Medical Assistant (CMA) is responsible for providing patient care under the direction of a physician or another healthcare provider. The MA works to facilitate clinic workflow, assist patients, and ensure safe, seamless delivery of care for each patient. Key Responsibilities: Accurately rooms patients, obtains and records vital signs, patient history, and reason for seeking care. Accurately processes and records telephone messages in patient medical records and according to policy. Assists in preparing prescription refills for providers according to policy. Maintains patient confidentiality, written and verbal. Communicates effectively and in an attentive manner with every patient encounter. Verifies the patient’s understanding of the purpose of the visit. Accurately documents all care provided and procedures performed within the patient’s medical record. Work Location: Onsite – this role is expected to work onsite and is located in Centerfield, CO . Why Join Us: Community Practice Medicine, housed within the School of Medicine at the University of Colorado, is seeking trained medical professionals to join our growing team. With clinics spanning from Longmont to Castle Rock, we offer a wide variety of opportunities. Specialty areas include, but are not limited to: Orthopedics, Vascular Surgery, OBGYN, Internal Medicine, Urology, Psychiatry, and many more! The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is a public education, clinical and research facility serving 4,500 students and a world-class medical destination at the forefront of life-changing science, medicine, and healthcare. CU Anschutz offers more than 42 highly rated degree programs through 6 schools and colleges and receives over $500 million in research awards each year. We are the single largest health professions education provider in Colorado, awarding nearly 1,450 degrees annually. Powered by our award-winning faculty, renowned researchers, and a reputation for academic excellence, the CU Anschutz Medical Campus drives innovation from the classroom to the laboratory to the delivery of unparalleled patient care. Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation, and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package, including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accrues over the year Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 15/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced-rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Medical Assistant: Completion of an accredited medical assistant program OR one year of medical assistant work experience. Certified Medical Assistant: Completion of an accredited medical assistant program. One year of medical assistant work experience. Current CMA certification (i.e., AAMA, NCCT). Substitution (All Levels): A combination of education and related technical/paraprofessional experience may be substituted on a year-for-year basis. Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Preferred Qualifications (All Levels): Experience with MS Office. Experience with EPIC. Experience with Kronos. Experience with HealthStream. Conditions of Employment (All Levels): Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without requiring sponsorship. We are unable to provide work visa sponsorship or employment authorization for this position now or in the future. Current Basic Life Support (BLS) for Healthcare Providers issued by the American Heart Association or the American Red Cross healthcare provider-level CPR certification. Maintains all required licensure and certifications for the position. Must be able to work in-person. Must be able to travel to alternate locations as assigned. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities (All Levels): Strong organizational and personal skills. Strong medical terminology knowledge and skills. Strong knowledge of CPT & ICD-10 procedures. Strong knowledge of value-based care and risk-based coding procedures in Primary Care. Strong knowledge of medication and injection procedures. Ability to safely administer a variety of treatments and medications as directed. Ability to use various types of equipment for examination and treatment procedures. Ability to accurately take and record vital signs. Ability to accurately reconcile patient medications. Ability to maintain quality control standards. Ability to identify problems and recommend solutions. How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position Curriculum vitae / Resume Three to five professional references, including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Questions should be directed to: Megan Dohn, megan.dohn@cuanschutz.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Immediately and continues until the position is filled. For best consideration, please apply by 11/21/2026 . Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as: Medical Assistant: $44,116 to $51,527 Certified Medical Assistant: $47,813 to $55,846 The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position may be eligible for overtime compensation, depending on the level. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans, and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@cuanschutz.edu . Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students, and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine-preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety-sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41483&lang=en": {
      "title": "Research Associate",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 22, 2026 Job category: Research Faculty Department: SOM-OTO GENERAL OPERATIONS Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Department: Otolaryngology-Head and Neck Surgery Job Title: Research Associate Position #:00854049 – Requisition #:41483 Job Summary: The Lina lab investigates innovative therapeutics, biomaterials, and diagnostic tools to further our understanding of laryngotracheal stenosis, a group of disorders that result in airway obstruction . We use patient-derived clinical samples and in vivo surgical models to further our understanding of the pathophysiology of airway stenosis and laryngeal scar and develop treatment models with real-world clinical applications. General Description Will be part of a clinically driven translational research laboratory studying injury and wound healing in the larynx and trachea and developing tissue engineering strategies to treat the disease. Under the general supervision of a faculty investigator, this position is responsible for independently performing routine experiments in the research laboratory and contributing to general maintenance of the laboratory, equipment, supplies, and animal colonies. Work requires an advanced understanding of immunological methods, immunohistochemistry, experimental design, basic understanding of statistical methods, and techniques gained through previous training and experience. Examples of Duties Performed · Utilize in vivo animal models in experiments. Follows experimental protocols, monitors animal safety and maintains health in accordance with USDA and AALAC guidelines. Administrating anesthesia, sacrificing and dissecting animals as required. Prepares tissue for study utilizing biochemical and histochemical techniques. · Operates basic laboratory equipment such as centrifuge, analytical balance, incubator, spectrophotometer, flow cytometer, microscopy, and/or utilizes laminar flow hood. · Will keep accurate and up-to-date records of experiments performed. Expected to become familiar with computer ordering system. · Operates lab computers for data entry. Maintains accurate data records. · Prepare lab for daily operations, including stocking materials, equipment, safety, cleanliness, and related areas · Dispose of laboratory materials and samples using well-established guidelines and instructions · Review and implement lab support policies, practices, and programs to meet organizational, operations, and management needs · Assist Team Leads, Supervisors and/or management with creation and implementation of processes and procedures and quality improvement initiatives · Independently review, develop, and implement new or modified laboratory techniques required for research projects · Experiments will involve propagation of tissue culture, PCR, immunohistochemical staining of cells and tissue, and small animal husbandry. Expected to manage mouse census and care for animals according to protocols. Professional Development Opportunities Training in the Lina Lab supports postdocs and PhD scientists in pursuing academic or non-academic careers. Scholars will have access to tailored professional development, including: · Funding for annual attendance and presentation at a national conference. · Mentoring opportunities with graduate students · Opportunities to engage with clinicians Work Location: Onsite – this role is expected to work onsite and is located in Aurora, CO. Why Join Us: The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is a world-class medical destination at the forefront of transformative science, medicine, education, and patient care. The campus encompasses the University of Colorado health professional schools, more than 60 centers and institutes, and two nationally ranked independent hospitals - UCHealth University of Colorado Hospital and Children's Hospital Colorado - that treat more than two million adult and pediatric patients each year. Innovative, interconnected and highly collaborative, the University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus delivers life-changing treatments, patient care and professional training and conducts world-renowned research fueled by over $762 million in research grants. For more information, visit www.cuanschutz.edu . Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year (based on percentage of time) Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 11/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. · A PhD OR a graduate degree with extensive prior laboratory experience in biomedical engineering, physiology, or a related biomedical sciences field Preferred Qualifications: · Strong expertise in immunohistochemistry, single-cell transcriptomics, airway physiology, and tissue engineering Demonstrated skills in data analysis and scientific writing Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Excellent organizational and time management skills with the ability to multi-task, clearly establishing work priorities and handling multiple deadlines Ability to handle sensitive and confidential information and documents and maintain strict confidentiality in all HIPAA matters. Ability to communicate effectively, both in writing and orally across large, diverse academic and healthcare populations. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with employees at all levels throughout the institution, working independently as well as part of a team Ability to use various computer systems and software applications. Open Track: To support the growth of our faculty, selected candidates will be offered the opportunity to choose a track that corresponds to their area of excellence. Learn more about faculty tracks at the Office for Faculty Affairs . How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): 1. A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position 2. Curriculum vitae / Resume 3. Five professional references including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers . Questions should be directed to: Carly Moses, carly.moses@cuanschutz.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Immediately and continues until position is filled. For best consideration, apply by November 30, 2026. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as HIRING RANGE: $85,000 - $110,000 The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation unless it is non-exempt. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: The University of Colorado (CU) is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@ucdenver.edu ​. Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41478&lang=en": {
      "title": "Dental Assistant I–II (Open Rank)",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 21, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: CON-DEAN ADMINISTRATION Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Department: College of Nursing Job Title: Dental Assistant I–II (Open Rank) Position #: 00854056 – Requisition #: 41478 Job Summary: The University of Colorado, College of Nursing, is seeking a Dental Assistant I or II (open rank) for a full-time (1.0 FTE), benefits-eligible position at Sheridan Health Services (SHS), a Federally Qualified Health Center located in southwest Denver, CO (zip code: 80236). This position will provide quality oral health care to patients at the community clinic sites. Clinic Description: Sheridan Health Services is a multi-site, nurse-managed FQHC, funded through the Health Resources and Services Administration Bureau of Primary Healthcare. The clinic serves community health needs primarily for residents of Arapahoe, Denver, and Jefferson counties, and is located in southwest Denver on the Fort Logan campus. It provides services to adults and children, 65% of whom identify as Latinx, and 42% of whom are best served in another language, with Spanish being the predominant second language. Services offered include primary care across the lifespan; prenatal and postpartum, women’s health, dentistry, pharmacy, behavioral health, and outpatient substance use treatment. SHS is a Patient-Centered Medical Home and upholds a model of care that places the patient at the center, incorporating the values and beliefs of the individual in all decision-making. https://nursing.cuanschutz.edu/patient-care/sheridan-health-services Examples of Work Performed (All Levels): Rooms patients in the dental operatories. Collects/Records vitals (blood pressure, pulse, weight, height) and blood sugar as indicated. Assists dentists, hygienists, and other dental team members with patient preparation and positioning and clinical area preparation for the treatment of patients for a variety of treatment procedures. Bilingual in English and another language. Communicating clinical terminology to patients and colleagues. Assists faculty and dental students in all areas of four-handed dentistry including, but not limited to, surgical, periodontal, restorative, and all other related procedures. Prepares specialized instrument set-ups for faculty, dental students, and hygienists (as needed) to be used during dental patient treatment. Inspects instruments/tools to ensure they are in good condition/working order. Performs waterline shocking, spore testing, and deep cleaning of clinical equipment. Performs appropriate aseptic and sterilization techniques. Stocks/Maintains dental inventory/supplies in treatment rooms. Performs dental intraoral and extraoral radiographs and other images using appropriate technique, X-ray equipment, and safety equipment. Mounts and identifies radiographic films and other images. Transfers images into a patient’s chart as directed. Performs routine administrative work in support of the clinic such as: Electronic Health Record input, data reporting. Answers phone calls and schedules appointments for all clinic locations. Collects payments from patients for services provided and makes change where needed. Reconciles change bank daily and submits daily deposit and deposit reconciliation report. Obtains pre-authorizations for insurance companies. Aids with preparation of claims for insurance payers. Verifies financial coverage and coordinates payment plans. Prints and presents treatment plans to patients, and then builds and reviews treatment plan estimates with patients before the patient signs the estimate/treatment plan. Ensures strict compliance with University and professional policies/procedures. Cleans and sterilizes instruments/dental equipment. Cleans, disinfects, and maintains all clinical, laboratory, and other community workspaces. Communicates effectively with all team members and participates in meetings. Other duties as assigned. At the Dental Assistant I level, duties are performed within established and known systems, processes, and operations which permit little deviation. At the Dental Assistant II level , the type of duties is similar to those performed at the lower level, but the complexity of the job is different. In addition to the examples of work performed at both levels, the Dental Assistant II level: Makes temporary crowns. Trains new hires and externs. Places and removes retraction cords. Polishes teeth. Applies fluoride. Provides patients with pre-op and post-op instructions, as well as oral hygiene instructions. Charts existing restorations or conditions. Places and removes matrix bands. This description is a summary only and describes the general level of work being performed; it is not intended to be all-inclusive. The duties of this position may change from time to time and/or based on business need. We reserve the right to add or delete duties and responsibilities at the discretion of the supervisor and/or hiring authority. Work Location: Onsite – this role is expected to work onsite and is located at Sheridan Health Services - Southwest Denver, 3525 W. Oxford Avenue Unit G1, Denver, CO 80236 Why Join Us: CU Nursing is an amazing place to be. We have the distinct advantage of being a part of a huge medical campus with three incredible hospitals – the VA, the nationally ranked University of Colorado Hospital, and the Children’s Hospital Colorado, where our nursing students and faculty learn every day. From our beginning 125 years ago as part of the School of Medicine at CU Boulder to our current home at the Anschutz Medical Campus, the college has been a recognized leader in nursing education (ranked #10 in online MS graduate programs by U.S. News & World Report 2023). Our faculty, students, and staff have been instrumental in shaping the profession of nursing and teaching the next generation of nurses while treating patients in our own nurse-led clinics. Be a part of an innovative, dynamic, diverse, and exciting workplace -- helping make great things happen. Join us in our quest to boldly transform health together. Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation, and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package, including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 15/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced-rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Dental Assistant I: Graduate from an accredited dental assistant training program. Substitution: One (1) year of dental assistant experience may substitute for completion of an accredited program. Dental Assistant II: Graduate from an accredited dental assistant training program. Substitution: One (1) year of dental assistant experience may substitute for completion of an accredited program and is in addition to any required years of experience. One (1) year of experience as a dental assistant. Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Preferred Qualifications: Dental Assistant I: One (1) year of experience as a dental assistant. Experience utilizing one of the following languages, in addition to English, on a daily basis to communicate clinical terminology: Spanish, Dari, Farsi, Ukrainian, Russian, Arabic, or Swahili. Experience with or formal training in handling bloodborne pathogens. Experience with or formal training in complying with OSHA Biohazard Safety Standards. Experience as a dental assistant in a Federally Qualified Health Center, Patient-Centered Medical Home, and/or community health setting. Dental Assistant II: One (1) year of experience as a dental assistant in a Federally Qualified Health Center, Patient-Centered Medical Home, and/or community health setting. Experience utilizing one of the following languages, in addition to English, on a daily basis to communicate clinical terminology: Spanish, Dari, Farsi, Ukrainian, Russian, Arabic, or Swahili. Experience with or formal training in training dental assistant staff. Experience with or formal training in performing blood glucose checks. Experience with or formal training in cord placement. Experience with or formal training in placing provisional crowns, temp-bond use, and finish polishing. Experience with or formal training in occlusal adjustment. Experience with or formal training in pulp vitality testing. Conditions of Employment: Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without requiring sponsorship. We are unable to provide work visa sponsorship or employment authorization for this position now or in the future. Must be willing and able to obtain current BLS/CPR certification by the date of hire. Must be willing and able to remain credentialed and ensure credentialing materials stay current. Must be willing and able to work weekends as needed for promotional events. Must be willing and able to work in a patient care environment with some exposure to biological hazards and infectious diseases. Must be willing and able to provide quality oral health care to patients at Sheridan Health Services and other community clinic locations based on departmental need. Must be willing and able to work evening hours based on the needs of the department. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Exemplary patient care skills. Collaborative nature. Ability to work with children and adults. Analytical thinker. Strong social skills. Fundamental knowledge of dental materials, their use, maintenance, and storage. Digital competency. Familiarity with an Electronic Medical Record program. Exemplary organizational skills and ability to prioritize. Ability to function as a team member. Highly responsible and reliable. Welcoming and friendly attitude. Maintain sensitive & confidential client information according to HIPAA policy. Participates in quality improvement efforts for continued high-quality care. How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to the listed job qualifications and interest in the position Curriculum vitae / Resume Questions should be directed to: College of Nursing Human Resources at CON.HR@ucdenver.edu or 303.724.4447 Screening of Applications Begins: Applications will be accepted until finalists are identified, but preference will be given to complete applications received by November 3, 2026 . Those who do not apply by this date may or may not be considered. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as: Dental Assistant I: $42,156 to $45,528 Dental Assistant II: $44,256 to $47,798 The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position may be eligible for overtime compensation, depending on the level. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans, and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@cuanschutz.edu . Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students, and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine-preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety-sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41474&lang=en": {
      "title": "Accelerated 3-Year Pathways Curriculum Coordinator",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 21, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: SOM-DEAN EO UME Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Department: Office of Medical Education Job Title: Accelerated 3-Year Pathways Curriculum Coordinator Position #: 00853990 – Requisition #:41474 Job Summary: This position provides professional curriculum coordination support for the Accelerated Three-Year Pathways Program within the Office of Medical Education. The position will oversee assigned curriculum activities, including student scheduling, course material planning and auditing, learning session facilitation, project management, event planning, and administrative support for related program activities. The position works with faculty, staff, students, and community partners to support curriculum implementation and program activities, while ensuring compliance with all University of Colorado and School of Medicine policies, procedures, and accreditation requirements to assigned responsibilities. The position manages multiple assigned projects and competing priorities, reviews information to identify routine issues, coordinates appropriate follow-up, and develops and documents processes related to assigned responsibilities with guidance from program leadership. Key Responsibilities: Course Planning, Development, and Coordination – 40% Participates in curriculum planning sessions as a project coordinator and professional liaison. This includes: Documenting and translating meeting information into actionable project plans, deliverables and steps. Helps to set and manage roles, responsibilities, and expectations; follows up on assigned action items to support timely completion. Organizes curriculum resources. Builds relationships with stakeholders. Participates in the creation of reports, summaries and/or updates for faculty, staff and leadership. Helps track project performance at regular intervals to ensure that key milestones are met. Ensures curriculum is finalized on time and within scope, while ensuring compliance with all applicable accreditation and University rules, policies and regulations. Manages central curriculum email inboxes by responding to inquiries, coordinating requests, and routing matters to the appropriate resource as needed. Reviews curriculum sessions and student schedules to identify discrepancies and coordinates updates with faculty and program staff to maintain accurate schedules. Coordinates with other curriculum coordinators to upload and audit course materials in the Learning Management System (Canvas/OASIS), identifying missing or inaccurate materials and coordinating corrections as needed. Reviews curriculum materials for each session to ensure alignment with faculty specifications and are available to students in a timely and consistent manner. Communicates with faculty stakeholders regarding scheduled learning events, student attendance, and program requirements and follows up on assigned items as needed. Maintains accurate planning documents in Peak-to-Peak file systems. Coordinates the scheduling of rooms and event spaces for on-campus curriculum events based on established program requirements. Creates, sets up, and communicates online learning details for remote learning sessions. UME Administration – 30% Collaborates with faculty, staff, and other program partners to support cross-functional teamwork and work toward solutions to assigned program needs. Develops and documents best practices and standard operating procedures relevant to assigned responsibilities, applying established CU and SOM policies, procedures, and program requirements. Provide event coordination and planning support to Office of Medical Education events and curriculum sessions as needed. This includes: Planning and managing logistics for various curriculum activities or educational events. In conjunction with the Accelerated 3-Year Pathways Program Manager, plan event budgets to ensure event planning aligns with established budget restrictions. Providing key risk management support to ensure policies, codes and accessibility (ADA) are integrated into the planning process. Developing marketing and promotional strategies for individual events (over multiple mediums and for diverse audiences), as applicable. Directly contributing to event set-up and tear down logistics, using critical thinking and analysis to resolve last minutes issues. Generating surveys or leading debrief sessions to collect data on the effectiveness of the planning, marketing and execution of the event; analyze data/feedback to identify trends and specific areas of improvement (for future events). Applies University procurement processes and policies when supporting the purchase of supplies for UME curriculum activities. Live Session Set Up and Support – 20% Provides day-of support for curriculum sessions across the Trek curriculum and coordinates assigned logistical needs during session delivery. Collects, organizes and evaluates necessary resources, course printouts, and supplies to ensure each session is appropriately prepared for student learning. Greets guest faculty and assists with campus navigation and locating assigned rooms. Applies knowledge of common learning-space technology to troubleshoot routine issues for faculty and students and coordinates additional support when needed. Assists with capturing student attendance and reports results to faculty leadership as required. Attends live Zoom learning sessions and provides administrative and technical support for small-group breakouts, recordings, and functions such as screen sharing. Identifies and coordinates resolution of scheduling issues with faculty when an instructor or facilitator is unavailable. Other Duties as Assigned – 10% Performs other coordination duties as assigned by the Accelerated 3-Year Pathways Program Manager. Work Location: Hybrid – this role is eligible for a hybrid schedule of 2 days per week on campus and as needed for in-person meetings. Why Join Us: Join the Office of Medical Education (OME) at the University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus; a vibrant and growing hub supporting a diverse range of programs including the Offices of Undergraduate Medical Education, Medical Scientist Training Program (MD/PhD) , Graduate Medical Education , Research Education , Continuing Medical Education , and the Center for Advancing Professional Excellence (CAPE) . With over 350 faculty and more than 100 staff and student appointments, OME is dedicated to fostering lifelong learning for students and physicians across Colorado. This is an exciting time to join the team, as OME's growth is driving the expansion of the Business Services team, with an emphasis on collaboration and meaningful impact. Be part of a mission-driven environment committed to advancing medical education and making a difference in academic medicine. Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 15/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications A Bachelor’s degree in education, psychology, business, public administration, health care, educational technology, social science, liberal arts, communications, accounting, finance, library science, or a directly related field from an accredited institution. Substitution: A combination of education and related technical/military/paraprofessional experience may be substituted for a bachelor’s degree on a year for year basis. Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire Preferred Qualifications: One (1) year of experience working at a higher education institution. Prior experience working in an academic medical environment. Experience with curriculum management and coordination. Conditions of Employment This position will be a hybrid work environment with the expectation of at least 2 days on site per week. Additional on-site days may be required when sessions, on-site meetings, or events necessitate an additional on-site presence. Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without requiring sponsorship. We are unable to provide work visa sponsorship or employment authorization for this position now or in the future. Competencies: Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Proficiency with Microsoft Office software, especially Outlook and Excel. Knowledge of learning management systems (i.e. Blackboard, Canvas). Ability to align multiple, competing demands with established priorities, and enjoy the challenges of change. Displays analytical and critical thinking skills to assist in resolving complex problems. Effective and timely communications, with expectations of responses within two business days of email receipt. Exemplary organization skills with an ability to work with little supervision independently and as a member of a team. Excellent attention to detail with an emphasis on personal accountability. Strong customer service disposition; able to effectively de-escalate frustrated or upset stakeholders. Must be a quick learner who is able to grasp new concepts and then successfully implement them into core tasks. How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position Curriculum vitae / Resume Three to five professional references, including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Questions should be directed to: Emily Martin - emily.e2.martin@cuanschutz.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Immediately and continues until position is filled. For best consideration, apply by Two (2) weeks from posting date. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as $45,017 - $60,323 . The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position may be eligible for overtime compensation, depending on the level. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@cuanschutz.edu ​. Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41475&lang=en": {
      "title": "Temporary Administrative Assistant",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 21, 2026 Job category: Classified Staff Department: SDM-Dental Clinic Compreh Care Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Department: SDM-Dental Clinic Comprehensive Care Job Title: Temporary Administrative Assistant Position #:00807455 – Requisition #:41475 This is a Temporary position limited to no more than 9-months. Job Summary: The Dental Clinic Comprehensive Care team is seeking a temporary Administrative Assistant to support the clinic’s front desk administrative operations. The position exists to manage and operate the Information/Reception areas of the dental clinics. Triage and direct phone in/walk-in inquiries and facilitate efficient and professional patient, student, faculty interaction. Greet and register new patients in electronic health record system. Schedule appointments for students through electronic health record system. Screen new patients by having discussion of student providers and faculty supervision, time commitment, and financial responsibilities. Schedule appointments, confirm information, and accept payments. We are seeking professionals who are looking to develop their careers in clinical office administration and/or looking to gain experience and understanding of full-cycle dental patient life-cycles. We welcome applications from individuals who are collaborative, communicative, caring, detail oriented, organized, proactive, able to think critically, focused on quality, dedicated to personal growth, and highly. The position is located at the University of Colorado - Anschutz Medical Campus . Hours will be dependent on business need but typically will be Monday – Friday between the hours of 8:00am and 5:00 pm. Key Responsibilities: · Answer calls from patients to schedule, re-schedule, and cancel appointments · Call patients to schedule appointments as well as reminders for patients · Intake patients as they come into the clinic, coordinating their appointments with providers · Utilize Axium system to schedule and re-schedule appointments based on provider availability and patient procedure needs. · Collaborate with front desk staff and supervisor to ensure all appointments are done correctly and on time. · Help with billing and collection for appointments and procedures based on standard protocols of the clinics. · Assist and collaborate with other units as needed to provide backup and other administrative help. Work Location: Onsite - this role is expected to work onsite and is located in Aurora, CO. Why Join Us: At the School of Dental Medicine, University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus, you'll find an incredible opportunity to contribute to the field of dentistry while advancing your career. As part of our esteemed institution, you'll have access to cutting-edge research facilities, state-of-the-art equipment, and a collaborative and supportive environment. Join our team of dedicated professionals who are passionate about providing exceptional dental care, advancing oral health, and making a difference in patients' lives. With opportunities for growth, professional development, and meaningful impact, working with us offers a rewarding and fulfilling career in the dynamic field of dental medicine. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: · Two years of general clerical experience. o College or university course work, appropriate to the work assignment, may substitute for the experience on a year-for-year basis. Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Preferred Qualifications: · Experience working with faculty, staff, and students in a higher education environment · Experience working in a dental or medical office environment · Bilingual in English and Spanish Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: · Ability to think critically and make decisive judgements · Ability to identify problems and recommend solutions. · Ability to effectively communicate at all levels, including physicians, leadership, and staff. · Ability to work within large, complex healthcare systems. · Ability to work independently and with minimal supervision · Ability to maintain confidentiality and communicate in person, by phone, or in writing. · Ability to attest to computer proficiency and learn new computer applications. · Ability to keyboard/type, write legibly, and accurately record information. · Ability to analyze and interpret data. · Ability to organize workflow with particular focus on tracking patient care and improving patient flow. How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): 1. A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position 2. Curriculum vitae / Resume 3. Five professional references including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers . Questions should be directed to: Oscar De Moya, Oscar.demoya@cuanschutz.edu Screening of Applications Begins: This position will remain open until filled. Applications will be reviewed as they are received, and candidates may be contacted for interviews throughout the posting period. Upon candidate selection, the posting will be closed, and no further applications will be accepted. Anticipated Pay Range: The hiring range for this position has been established at: $25.00 to $30.00 / hour. The above hiring range represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty and training. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. Temporary employees are only eligible for sick leave benefits. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: The University of Colorado (CU) is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@ucdenver.edu ​. Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41473&lang=en": {
      "title": "Grants and Center Administrator",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 21, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: SOM-MED-PUL GENERAL OPERATIONS Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus Department: Medicine – Pulmonary, Allergy, and Critical Care Medicine Job Title: Grants and Center Administrator Position #: 00854079 – Requisition #: 41473 Job Summary: The Department of Medicine, Division of Pulmonary, Critical Care, and Sleep Medicine (PACCM) seeks a Grants and Center Administrator to join its team at the Anschutz Medical Campus in Aurora, Colorado. This position is responsible for overseeing both pre- and post-award research administration for divisional faculty while providing comprehensive administrative support for the Lung Fibrosis Center. The Grants and Center Administrator will provide end-to-end administrative and financial management of sponsored research activities, supporting the full grant lifecycle from proposal development and submission through award management, compliance, financial oversight, and closeout. In addition, this role will serve as a key operational partner to Center PACCM leadership, providing high-level administrative, financial, human resources, and research administration support. The position plays a critical role in ensuring the effective management of personnel, programs, resources, and sponsored research activities, contributing to the overall success and strategic goals of the Center. Key Responsibilities: Supporting full grant lifecycle from proposal development through award management, compliance, financial oversight, and closeout. Work with PIs and Office of Grants and Contracts as required for grants administration. Collaborate with the Division’s grants team on project administration, including transition of projects from pre-award to post-award and backing up team members as needed. Serve as primary administrative and operational parter to Center leadership, managing day-to-day operations and supporting the Center’s strategic, research and academic priorities. Work with Division’s HR Program Manager to manage human resources and personnel administration processes for the Center. Work with Division Administrator to administer Center finances, including budget monitoring, personnel funding allocations, salary distributions, funding changes and salary transfer transactions. Develop and implement administrative, financial, and operational processes that improve efficiency, support organizational growth, and ensure compliance with institution and sponsor requirements. Work Location: Hybrid – this role is eligible for a hybrid schedule of 2-3 days per week on campus and as needed for in-person meetings. Why Join Us: About the Division of Pulmonary, Allergy, and Critical Care Medicine Thank you for your interest in the Division of Pulmonary, Allergy, and Critical Care Medicine at the University of Colorado! Our over 150 faculty are located across four sites: the University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus, National Jewish Health, Denver Health, and the VA Eastern Colorado Health Care System. We are very proud of our long and illustrious history. Many seminal discoveries in pulmonary, allergy, critical care medicine occurred here in Denver, including advances in tuberculosis, interstitial lung disease, airway disease, cancer, and critical care. Many of our former trainees have taken leadership roles in academic medicine, including Division and Department Chairs, Deans, and American Thoracic Society Presidents. We continue to enhance all aspects of our division and training program, and as a result, we have seen tremendous and sustained growth. The clinical practice sites have built new hospitals, and there are multiple new research buildings across the campuses. We have been fortunate to recruit tremendous new faculty members while retaining many of our former trainees. About the University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is a world-class medical destination at the forefront of transformative science, medicine, education, and patient care. The campus encompasses the University of Colorado health professional schools, more than 60 centers and institutes, and two nationally ranked independent hospitals - UCHealth University of Colorado Hospital and Children's Hospital Colorado - that treat more than two million adult and pediatric patients each year. Innovative, interconnected and highly collaborative, the University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus delivers life-changing treatments, patient care and professional training and conducts world-renowned research fueled by over $700 million in research grants. For more information, visit www.cuanschutz.edu . Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation, and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 15/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree in public health, public administration, social/behavioral sciences, physical sciences, nursing, healthcare, finance, accounting, research, communications, marketing, business administration, business, or other closely related field. Substitution: A combination of education and related technical/military/paraprofessional experience may be substituted for a bachelor’s degree on a year for year basis. Three (3) years of professional experience with pre-award and post-award grant administration, including proposal development, award management, and sponsor reporting. Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Preferred Qualifications: Experience supporting an academic, healthcare, research, or higher education environment. Experience managing budgets, financial reporting, payroll funding, and salary distributions across multiple funding sources. Experience coordinating human resources activities, including recruitment, onboarding, personnel actions, and workforce planning. Conditions of Employment: Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without requiring sponsorship. We are unable to provide work visa sponsorship or employment authorization for this position now or in the future. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Ability to communicate effectively, both in writing and orally. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with employees at all levels throughout the institution. Outstanding customer service skills. Demonstrated ability to develop and improve administrative, financial, and operational processes in a complex organization. How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position. Curriculum vitae / Resume Three to five professional references, including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address. Questions should be directed to: Carissa Smith, carissa.smith@cuanschutz.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Immediately and continues until position is filled. For best consideration, apply by November 9 th , 2026 . Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as $67,864 – $90,937 . The above salary range (or hiring range) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position may be eligible for overtime compensation, depending on the level. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@cuanschutz.edu . Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=40731&lang=en": {
      "title": "Registered Nurse Diabetes Educator- Instructor of Clinical Practice",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 21, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: SOM-BDC Pediatric Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Department: Barbara Davis Center for Diabetes Job Title: Registered Nurse Diabetes Educator- Instructor of Clinical Practice Position #00851585 – Requisition #40731 Job Summary: The Barbara Davis Center for Diabetes at the University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is a multi-disciplinary diabetes center affiliated with Children’s Hospital Colorado as well as the University of Colorado School of Medicine. In the pediatric clinic the patient population is primarily children with type 1 diabetes. This position will provide diabetes care and education to pediatric patients with a new diagnosis of diabetes as well as for established patients. This diabetes educator will develop, implement, and evaluate care management plans for patients with complex health needs. This nurse educator will also work in the Barbara Davis Center Infusion Center, preparing and administering drugs via infusion to patients for early stage and newly diagnosed type 1 diabetes. In addition to the clinical program, the Barbara Davis Center has a large basic research program allowing many ongoing educational opportunities. This Instructor of Clinical Practice position is an at-will faculty appointment. This appointment will involve approximately 100% clinical work. The position serves as a Registered Nurse at the Instructor of Clinical Practice rank. Key Responsibilities : Clinical responsibilities (100%) Providing direct diabetes care and education to newly diagnosed and established children with diabetes. Educate and case manage children who have type 1 diabetes and other causes of hyperglycemia. This includes working with families to achieve age-appropriate diabetes management goals. Phone consultations with patients and their families, school nurses, advanced practice nurses, physician assistants and physicians in the community assisting with options in resolving complicated inquiries and/or issues related to diabetes management. Contribute to ongoing development and improvement of nursing/educator electronic medical record documentation/data entry programs. Participate as a presenter or collaborator in development of educational materials for conferences and classes conducted by the staff at the Barbara Davis Center related to diabetes management. Participate in professional development of the nursing/diabetes educator team through attending diabetes related conferences. Assisting in development of policies and procedures to maintain high standards of existing ADA Accredited Diabetes Program. Participate in Clinical Quality Improvement programs through individual and group work on annual clinical care goals. Participate in infusion protocol of teplizumab for stage 2 type 1 diabetes in the clinical infusion center. Why Join Us: The BDC Pediatric Diabetes Division provides families and patients with an understanding of type 1 diabetes and encourages their confidence in its day-to-day management. Present evidence strongly suggests that consistent blood sugar control greatly diminishes the chances of long-term eye and kidney complications. The Pediatric Clinic offers complete education and support for children and adolescents with type 1 diabetes. The expectation is that by the time patients are ready to leave home for college or the workforce, they will have the ability to manage their own blood sugars. The clinic is certified by the American Diabetes Association, and our nurses, dietitians, nurse practitioners, physician assistants and social workers are Certified Diabetes Educators. Our pediatric endocrinologists also participate in studies that strive to advance and improve glucose monitoring and closed-loop technology through observational studies and clinical trials at our Center. Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 11/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Master’s degree in Nursing or related field. Registered Nurse licensed to practice in Colorado Current Basic Life Support (BLS) and/or CPR certification, or willing to obtain prior to starting employment. A combination of education and related experience may be substituted for the master’s degree on a year for year basis. Preferred Qualifications: Priority will be given to someone with experience in childhood diabetes and with a Certificate in Diabetes Care and Education from the National Certification Board. Bilingual (English/Spanish) would be highly valued but not required. Phlebotomy and IV skills (peripheral and PICC) preferred but not required Current Pediatric Advanced Life Supports (PALS) certification or willingness to obtain preferred but not required. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Interpersonal and communication skills Ability to work in a team setting Ability to multitask Willingness to learn and comply with relevant laws, rules, regulations and policies. How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): 1. A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position 2. Curriculum vitae / Resume 3. Three professional references including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers . Questions should be directed to: Barbara Davis Center HR, BDCHR@cuanschutz.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Applications will be accepted until finalists are identified, but preference will be given to complete applications received by 11/30/2026 . Those who do not apply by this date may or may not be considered. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as HIRING RANGE: $65,000 – $88,000 The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation unless it is non-exempt. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@ucdenver.edu ​. Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases. If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41472&lang=en": {
      "title": "Assistant Director of Finance & Business Operations",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 21, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: SOM-DEAN DO ADMINISTRATION Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Department: School of Medicine, Office of the Dean Job Title: Assistant Director of Finance & Business Operations Position #: 00854025 – Requisition #: 41472 Job Summary: The Assistant Director of Finance & Business Operations serves as the senior operational finance leader for the School of Medicine (SOM) Dean's Office and is responsible for translating strategic priorities into operational execution. Reporting to the Business Affairs Director, this position provides executive-level leadership for the daily management of finance operations, financial planning and analysis (FP&A), budgeting, forecasting, financial reporting, resource planning, commitments, and operational business services. This position serves as the operational counterpart to the Business Affairs Director by ensuring that financial priorities are executed consistently, teams are effectively led, and operational objectives are achieved. The Assistant Director develops leaders, establishes accountability, improves operational effectiveness, and creates a culture focused on execution, continuous improvement, and exceptional customer service. The incumbent is expected to be both a highly credible finance professional and an experienced people leader capable of leading managers, mentoring emerging leaders, making complex operational decisions, and ensuring outstanding service delivery across the organization. Position Purpose: This position exists to: Lead day-to-day Finance, FP&A and Commitments operations. Build and develop a high-performing finance leadership team. Ensure operational excellence and accountability. Improve customer service across Business Affairs. Translate strategic priorities into operational execution. Strengthen financial stewardship across the organization. Develop scalable financial processes and internal controls. Serve as the operational leader for Business Affairs in the absence of the Business Affairs Director. Primary Responsibilities: Finance Operations Leadership (30%) Direct all daily financial operations. Oversee annual budgeting and forecasting. Lead labor planning and position budgeting. Oversee monthly and annual financial reporting. Review complex financial analyses. Monitor financial performance and emerging risks. Ensure compliance with University and School financial policies. Establish service standards and performance expectations. Resolve complex financial and operational issues. Ensure timely completion of operational deliverables. Leadership & Organizational Development (25%) Directly supervise finance leadership staff. Coach managers and supervisors. Build leadership capability throughout the organization. Establish accountability measures. Conduct performance management. Develop succession plans. Lead hiring and onboarding. Improve employee engagement. Develop training and mentoring programs. Foster a culture of ownership and accountability. Ensure managers effectively delegate work and develop staff rather than functioning as individual contributors. Financial Planning & Analysis (20%) Lead long-range financial planning. Develop financial forecasting models. Perform scenario planning. Evaluate financial performance trends. Recommend resource allocation strategies. Guide executive decision-making through sound financial analysis. Improve forecasting accuracy. Lead financial performance reviews with leadership. Operational Excellence & Continuous Improvement (15%) Standardize financial processes. Improve internal controls. Eliminate inefficiencies. Reduce turnaround times. Improve customer experience. Develop operational metrics. Lead process improvement initiatives. Improve communication between Finance, Procurement, HR, and other Dean's Office functions. Executive Partnership (10%) Translate strategic initiatives into implementation plans. Lead implementation of executive priorities. Represent Business Affairs on committees. Present financial recommendations to executive leadership. Coordinate cross-functional initiatives. Serve as acting leader during the Director's absence. Escalate strategic issues requiring executive attention while independently resolving operational matters. Work Location: Hybrid – this role is eligible for a hybrid schedule of four (4) days per week on campus and as needed for in-person meetings. Why Join Us: The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is a public education, clinical and research facility serving 4,500 students and a world-class medical destination at the forefront of life-changing science, medicine, and healthcare. CU Anschutz offers more than 42 highly rated degree programs through 6 schools and colleges and receives over $500 million in research awards each year. We are the single largest health professions education provider in Colorado, awarding nearly 1,450 degrees annually. Powered by our award-winning faculty, renowned researchers, and a reputation for academic excellence, the CU Anschutz Medical Campus drives innovation from the classroom to the laboratory to the delivery of unparalleled patient care. Read CU Anschutz Quick Facts here. Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation, and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package, including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 15/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced-rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's degree in Finance, Accounting, Business Administration, or a related field. Substitution: A combination of education and related technical/military/paraprofessional experience may be substituted for a bachelor’s degree on a year-for-year basis. Seven (7) years of progressively responsible finance leadership and supervision experience.* Three (3) years of experience leading budgeting, forecasting, financial planning, and organizational finance.* Three (3) years of experience leading organizational change and operational improvement initiatives.* *Experience may be obtained simultaneously. Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Preferred Qualifications: MBA, MPA, CPA, CMA, or similar graduate degree or certification. Academic medicine or higher education experience. Experience managing large, complex operating budgets. Experience leading multi-level management teams. Experience developing emerging leaders. Conditions of Employment: Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without requiring sponsorship. We are unable to provide work visa sponsorship or employment authorization for this position now or in the future. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Demonstrated knowledge of financial management principles and practices, including budgeting, forecasting, financial planning and analysis, financial modeling, labor planning, resource allocation, variance analysis, financial reporting, and internal controls. Demonstrated ability to translate strategic priorities into clear operational plans, assign responsibility, establish timelines, monitor progress, and ensure successful execution. Demonstrated ability to provide senior operational leadership for complex finance functions and ensure the accurate, timely, and consistent delivery of financial services and work products. Demonstrated ability to prepare and present high-quality financial analyses, forecasts, reports, recommendations, and executive-level presentations. Demonstrated ability to analyze complex financial and operational information, identify risks and trends, evaluate alternatives, and develop practical, data-informed recommendations. Demonstrated ability to manage multiple complex and competing priorities, adapt to changing organizational needs, and ensure deadlines and commitments are met. Demonstrated ability to communicate complex financial and operational information. Demonstrated ability to supervise and develop managers, supervisors, and professional staff through coaching, mentoring, feedback, performance management, and succession planning. Demonstrated ability to lead hiring, onboarding, training, and professional development efforts that strengthen technical capability, leadership effectiveness, and team performance. Demonstrated ability to foster a collaborative, service-oriented, and results-focused culture that promotes ownership, continuous improvement, professional development, and trust. How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position Curriculum vitae / Resume Three to five professional references, including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Questions should be directed to: Adam Kanallakan, ADAM.KANALLAKAN@CUANSCHUTZ.EDU Screening of Applications Begins: Immediately and continues until the position is filled. For best consideration, apply by November 3 rd , 2026 . Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as $89,208 to $128,638 . The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position may be eligible for overtime compensation, depending on the level. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans, and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@cuanschutz.edu . Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students, and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine-preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety-sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=39653&lang=en": {
      "title": "Specialty Director of the Psychiatric Mental Health Nurse Practitioner Programs/Instructional Series Faculty Appointment (Open Rank-Assistant Teaching Professor, Associate Teaching Professor, or Teaching Professor)",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 20, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: CON-DEAN ADMINISTRATION Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus Department: College of Nursing, Office of Faculty and Students Job Title: Specialty Director of the Psychiatric Mental Health Nurse Practitioner Programs/Instructional Series Faculty Appointment (Open Rank -Assistant Teaching Professor, Associate Teaching Professor, or Teaching Professor ) Position #: 0000644170 – Requisition #: 39653 Job Summary: The CU College of Nursing is seeking an energetic leader to serve as the Specialty Director of the Psychiatric Mental Health Nursing Practitioner Program. The ideal candidate would be qualified to hold a full-time (1.00 FTE) faculty appointment within the Instructional Faculty Series (rank will depend on the candidate’s qualifications and experience). This full-time faculty position includes dedicated time to serve as the Specialty Director in the Psychiatric Mental Health Nurse Practitioner Program. The successful candidate will have recent psychiatric mental health nurse practitioner practice experience and a track record of excellence in academic teaching. Responsibilities include participation in the teaching, practice, and service mission of the College of Nursing and the University of Colorado. Demonstration of academic leadership, such as curricular/program development, is preferred. Ideal candidates will have teaching and scholarship experience with the ability to teach across programs. Faculty rank will depend on the candidate’s qualifications and experience, and potential ranks include Assistant Teaching Professor, Associate Teaching Professor, or Teaching Professor within the Instructional Series. Successful candidates will have recent experience in the focus listed above and a track record of excellence in academic teaching. Responsibilities may include participation in the teaching, practice, and service mission of the College of Nursing and the University of Colorado. Demonstration of academic leadership, such as curricular/program development, is preferred. For APRN candidates, a portion of the position may be devoted to clinical practice depending on the candidate’s experience and expertise. While the primary focus for these positions resides in the teaching mission of the college, service and scholarship to the university and the college are expected of all faculty members. A successful candidate will help foster a community of belonging and will utilize a justice lens to effectively engage with all members of the CU Nursing community, specifically faculty, staff, students, and community partners with diverse identities. This faculty position involves didactic and clinical teaching responsibilities as well as administrative responsibility for the Psychiatric Mental Health Nurse Practitioner (PMHNP) Program including securing clinical placements for graduate students and the management of student program plans, progression monitoring and student support. Didactic courses are taught in the classroom, online, or in blended formats. Supervision of clinical courses includes clinical conferences using online conferencing, site visits, and close communication with clinical preceptors. Examples of Work Performed may include: Academic Advising & Student Support · Serve as the Academic Advisor for all PMHNP students. · Advise students, monitor progress and retention, and establish performance improvement plans as needed. · Support student growth in skills needed to succeed in a progressive teaching and learning environment that incorporates ongoing innovative strategies for competency development. · Evaluate student application of knowledge. · Promote accountability among students by implementing clear guidelines and expectations for preparation, engagement, and self-directed study and practice. · Lead the comprehensive examination process for PMHNP students, including evaluation of competencies and coordination of poster presentation activities. · Create and maintain formal Plans of Study, individualized to each student, to support expected progression and accurate administrative tracking across the program. Student Recruitment, Coordination & Alumni Engagement · Recruit and advise qualified students to the PMHNP program, including conducting interviews, portfolio reviews, and informational sessions. · Build and maintain relationships with alumni and constituents to monitor post-graduate outcomes, support preceptor recruitment, and strengthen alumni engagement. · Support recruitment of qualified faculty for the PMHNP program, as needed. Curriculum Development & Instruction · Serve as lead faculty for the PMHNP specialty, providing didactic and clinical instruction in classroom, online, and blended formats. · Instruct and facilitate meaningful learning aligned with course and program outcomes. · Provide learner-centered instruction that prepares graduates to meet evolving patient needs and workforce demands. · Encourage a culture of learning that values mutual responsibility, respect, lifelong learning, diversity, ethics, and professional development. · Participate in course, curricular, and program revision and development activities. · Evaluate and revise curriculum to ensure alignment with state and national certification standards and accreditation requirements and following faculty shared governance processes. · Introduce students to skills necessary for success in progressive learning environments that incorporate innovative strategies and competency-based development. · Integrate innovative teaching strategies and educational technologies to enhance learning and competency development. · Demonstrate proficiency in the use of educational technology tools. · Support student certification application processes and monitor program quality indicators, including certification pass rates and related benchmarks. · Collaborate to suggest teaching assignments within the PMHNP program and accept teaching assignments as determined by the Assistant/Associate Dean and/or Division Chair. Clinical Preceptor & Placement Coordination · Identify, recruit, and maintain relationships with clinical preceptors and practicum sites. · Ensure clinical placements are secured prior to each semester and provide required documentation to the Clinical Placement Office. · Monitor student clinical compliance, progression, and preceptor and site evaluations. · Leverage professional networks, organizations, and alumni relationships to expand and diversify the preceptor pool. Program Leadership & Administration · Participate in leadership teams administering the psychiatric-mental health nursing fellowship program, supporting students who complete supplemental research or evidence-based practice projects focused on mental health topics. · Participate in leadership teams administering the Tools of Engagement program, which provides foundational mental health skill development for nursing students across programs and specialties. · Plan and lead specialty faculty meetings, ensuring dissemination of key policies, procedures, and program updates. · Support development of new program opportunities, including initiatives that expand access to mental health education and workforce development. Communication & Collaboration · Maintain effective, collaborative communication with students, faculty, staff, preceptors, and external partners. · Serve on divisional, college, and university committees. · Demonstrate commitment to collaborative interprofessional teaching and scholarship. · Participate in activities that promote the reputation and stature of the academic programs and the College of Nursing while adhering to university and college policies and standards. Professional Engagement & Service · Engage in state, regional, and national professional organizations through meetings, service, and leadership activities. · Promote the mission and strategic priorities of the College of Nursing through active participation in professional and community initiatives. · Contribute to initiatives that support mental health education, professional development, and workforce advancement. This description is a summary only and is describing the general level of work being performed, it is not intended to be all-inclusive. The duties of this position may change from time to time and/or based on business need. We reserve the right to add or delete duties and responsibilities at the discretion of the supervisor and/or hiring authority. Work Location: This position’s primary work location is the Anschutz Medical Campus, Aurora, Colorado, and will also have teaching responsibilities as needed on the Legacy Campus, in Lone Tree, Colorado. Hybrid – this role is eligible for a hybrid schedule based on assigned teaching responsibilities. Why Join Us: CU Nursing is an amazing place to be. We have the distinct advantage of being a part of a huge medical campus with three incredible hospitals – the VA, the nationally ranked University of Colorado Hospital, and the Children’s Hospital Colorado where our nursing students and faculty learn every day. From our beginning 125 years ago as part of the School of Medicine at CU Boulder to our current home at the Anschutz Medical Campus, the college has been a recognized leader in nursing education (ranked #10 in online MS graduate programs by U.S. News & World Report 2023). Our faculty, students and staff have been instrumental in shaping the profession of nursing and teaching the next generation of nurses while treating patients in our own nurse-led clinics. Be a part of an innovative, dynamic, diverse, and exciting workplace -- helping make great things happen. Join us in our quest to boldly transform health together. Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation, and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package, including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 11/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced-rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): 1. A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position. 2. Curriculum vitae / Resume 3. Five professional references including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address 4. A copy of all relevant diplomas/certifications (i.e. confirmation of high school diploma) Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers . Questions should be directed to the College of Nursing Human Resources Team via CON.HR@ucdenver.edu or 303.724.4447. Screening of Applications Begins: Applications will be accepted until finalists are identified, but preference will be given to complete applications received by November 3rd, 2026 . Those who do not apply by this date may or may not be considered. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as HIRING RANGE: Assistant Teaching Professor: $98,000 to $115,000 annually at 1.0 FTE Associate Teaching Professor: $115,000 to $130,000 annually at 1.0 FTE Teaching Professor: $130,000 to $150,000 annually at 1.0 FTE The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation unless it is non-exempt. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: The University of Colorado (CU) is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@cuanschutz.edu . Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students, and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine-preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety-sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41471&lang=en": {
      "title": "Periodontics Program Coordinator (Entry and Intermediate)",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 20, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: SDM-Dept Surgical Dentistry Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Department: School of Dental Medicine, Department of Diagnostic Sciences & Surgical Dentistry, Division of Periodontics Job Title: Periodontics Program Coordinator (Entry and Intermediate) Position #: 00686073 – Requisition #:41471 Job Summary: The School of Dental Medicine Graduate Periodontics Residency Program is seeking an open-rank Academic Services professional to support the academic, clinical, and administrative operations of the Periodontics Residency Program. This position may be filled at the Entry or Intermediate Professional level based on the selected candidate’s qualifications and demonstrated experience. The Periodontics Program Coordinator supports clinical operations and patient care coordination, didactic curriculum and academic activities, residency recruitment and resident support, accreditation readiness, and program-related financial and administrative processes. Entry-level responsibilities are performed with greater guidance and in a training and development capacity. The Intermediate level performs the same functional work with greater discretion, complexity, and judgment within established program requirements. Key Responsibilities: Coordinate clinical operations, faculty coverage, and schedules supporting predoctoral and postgraduate periodontics education. Coordinate didactic courses, faculty teaching assignments, educational events, academic calendars, assessments, and instructional logistics. Coordinate residency recruitment and admissions, onboarding, resident records and credentials, meetings, leave requests, professional development activities, and graduation. Support resident clinical and academic tracking and maintain documentation required for program reporting. Support CODA and institutional accreditation readiness, including records, site visit preparation, deadlines, reports, and follow-up documentation. Coordinate patient prepayments and program-related purchasing, reimbursements, travel, and financial documentation. At the Intermediate level, exercise greater discretion in coordinating schedule and resource changes, addressing operational issues, recommending workflow improvements, and supporting accreditation readiness. Work Location: Onsite – this role is expected to work onsite and is located in Aurora, CO. Why Join Us: The University of Colorado School of Dental Medicine is nationally recognized for the quality of its educational programs, interdisciplinary research, and clinical care programs that contribute to the health and well-being of many of Colorado’s most underserved citizens. We are invested in creating career pathways, learning and development opportunities, and people-focused infrastructure to support our workforce. The Department of Diagnostic Sciences & Surgical Dentistry supports the School of Dental Medicine mission areas of education, research, patient care, and community engagement. The department includes the Divisions of Periodontics, Endodontics, Diagnostic Sciences, and Oral and Maxillofacial Surgery, and is committed to supporting student success, patient care, and the broader community. Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 15/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Academic Services Entry Professional: Bachelor’s degree in education, psychology, business, public administration, health care, educational technology, social science, liberal arts, communications, accounting, finance, library science, or a directly related field from an accredited institution. Substitution: A combination of education and related technical/military/paraprofessional experience may be substituted for a bachelor’s degree on a year for year basis. Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Academic Services Professional (Intermediate): Bachelor’s degree in education, psychology, business, public administration, health care, educational technology, social science, liberal arts, communications, accounting, finance, library science, or a directly related field from an accredited institution. One (1) year of professional experience in academic program administration, higher education, healthcare or clinical program operations, student or resident services, admissions or recruitment, or a directly related area. Substitution: A combination of education and related technical/military/paraprofessional experience may be substituted for a bachelor’s degree on a year for year basis. Substitution: An advanced degree (Master’s or Doctorate) may be substituted for experience on a year for year basis if the degree is in a field of study directly related to the work assignment. Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Preferred Qualifications: Conditions of Employment: Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without requiring sponsorship. We are unable to provide work visa sponsorship or employment authorization for this position now or in the future. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Ability to communicate effectively, both in writing and orally. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with employees, faculty, residents, students, applicants, and other stakeholders. Strong organizational and coordination skills with the ability to manage competing priorities in an academic and clinical environment. Analytical and problem-solving skills with the ability to identify operational issues and recommend process improvements. Ability to maintain a high level of confidentiality while working with sensitive information. Ability to learn and use business, academic, and clinical applications and technologies required to support program operations. Knowledge of or ability to develop knowledge of medical education, dental terminology, residency program administration, and clinic operations. How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position Curriculum vitae / Resume Three to five professional references, including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Questions should be directed to: Oscar De Moya, oscar.demoya@cuanschutz.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Applications will be accepted until finalists are identified, but preference will be given to complete applications received by 11/3/26. Those who do not apply by this date may or may not be considered. Hiring department will need to notify their Talent Acquisition Consultant when they want to have the advertisements removed for the posting. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range (or hiring range) for this open-rank position has been established as: Academic Services Entry Professional: $45,017 - $60,323 Academic Services Professional (Intermediate): $48,989 - $65,645 The above salary ranges represent the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. Overtime eligibility will be determined based on the level at which the position is filled. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@cuanschutz.edu ​. Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
