    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41462&lang=en": {
      "title": "Research Services Intermediate-Principal Professional – Regulatory Affairs Coordinator",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 20, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: SOM-OP GENERAL OPERATIONS Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus Department: Ophthalmology Job Title: Research Services Intermediate-Principal Professional – Regulatory Affairs Coordinator Position #00854020 – Requisition # 41462 Job Summary: The Department of Ophthalmology has an immediate opening for a full-time Research Services Intermediate-Principal Professional (open rank)-Regulatory Affairs Coordinator. The position will independently maintain and manage all IRB and regulatory processes for department research studies. Primary duties will include, but not be limited to: submissions to the Institutional Review Board (IRB) of record including amendments, unanticipated problems, continuing reviews, and study closures; maintenance of the investigator site file/regulatory binder and all essential documents including documentation of appropriate training and delegation for all personnel; submissions to internal University and Hospital research portals; acting as primary regulatory contact person for sponsors/Contract Research Organizations (CROs)/coordinating centers; maintaining research credentials, training documentation and licenses. The Regulatory Affairs Coordinator will work closely with the Regulatory Affairs Program Manager, Director of Clinical Research, other program managers, clinical research coordinators, and Investigators. Key Responsibilities: Prepare, submit, and manage regulatory documents for IRB submissions (COMIRB, Advarra, etc), including initial submissions, continuing reviews, amendments, reportable events, and study closures. Coordinate regulatory documentation for Investigator-Initiated Trials (IITs) and industry-sponsored clinical trials. Maintain complete and audit-ready regulatory binders in accordance with institutional, sponsor, and regulatory requirements. Ensure compliance with ICH-GCP, FDA regulations, institutional policies, and sponsor requirements. Track and maintain investigator qualifications, including CVs, medical licenses, training documentation, and financial disclosures. Assist with protocol and consent form development. Assist investigators and study teams with regulatory start-up activities, including feasibility documentation and site qualification materials. Maintain investigator site files (ISF) and ensure all required documents are current and complete. Prepare regulatory documentation for monitoring visits, sponsor audits, and regulatory inspections. Assist with regulatory reporting of adverse events, unanticipated problems, and protocol deviations as required by IRB and sponsors. Work closely with investigators and study teams to ensure regulatory compliance for specialized ophthalmology research protocols. Develop and maintain regulatory tracking systems for submissions, approvals, and expiration dates. Other tasks as assigned. Work Location: Hybrid – this role is eligible for a hybrid schedule of 3 days per week on campus and as needed for in-person meetings after onboarding/training period are complete. Why Join Us: The Department of Ophthalmology is housed in the Sue Anschutz-Rodgers Eye Center on the Anschutz Medical Campus. This state-of-the-art facility is one of the largest eye centers in the country and serves not only patients in the Rocky Mountain region but also patients all over the world. The technological innovations conceived and developed by departmental faculty have changed the practice of eye care throughout the world. Our educational programs train the next generation of leaders in ophthalmology. Our specialists have developed national and international reputations for excellence in routine and complex ophthalmic care. We have invested heavily in tracking our clinical outcomes and we are proud that our clinicians perform at the highest levels in their respective fields. The mission of the Department of Ophthalmology is to be a nationally recognized department of ophthalmology by providing exemplary patient care founded on educational leadership, innovative research, and high ethical standards. Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 15/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Intermediate Professional: Bachelor's degree from an accredited institution and 1 year of professional experience in public health, public administration, social/behavioral sciences, physical sciences, nursing, healthcare, or a directly related field from an accredited institution A combination of education and related mechnical/military/paraprofessional experience may be substituted for a bachelor’s degree on a year for year basis. Senior Professional: Bachelor's degree from an accredited institution and 2 years of professional experience in public health, public administration, social/behavioral sciences, physical sciences, nursing, healthcare, or a directly related field from an accredited institution A combination of education and related technical/military/paraprofessional experience may be substituted for a bachelor’s degree on a year for year basis. Principal Professional: Bachelor’s degree from an accredited institution and 3-5 years of professional experience public health, public administration, social/behavioral sciences, physical sciences, nursing, healthcare, or a directly related field from an accredited institution. A combination of education and related technical/military/paraprofessional experience may be substituted for a bachelor’s degree on a year for year basis. Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Preferred Qualifications: Master’s degree in in public health, public administration, social/behavioral sciences, physical sciences, nursing, healthcare, or a directly related field from an accredited institution Experience working with in ophthalmology and/or clinical research. Experience with eRegulatory software (Advarra, Veeva, Florence, CRIO) 1 year Project Management experience 3 years of regulatory experience IRB experience (COMIRB or central IRBs, such as WCG or Advarra) Experience drafting and editing study protocols and informed consent documents. Experience with University of Colorado/UCHealth systems (Colorado Multiple Institutional Review Board, UCHealth Research Administration, Oncore, RedCap and InfoED). Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Ability to communicate effectively, both in writing and orally. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with employees at all levels throughout the institution. Ability to maintain excellent organization across a variety of regulatory functions. Outstanding customer service skills. How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position Curriculum vitae / Resume Three to five professional references, including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Questions should be directed to: Ashley Woodhouse ashley.woodhouse@cuanschutz.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Immediately and continues until position is filled. For best consideration, apply by October 31, 2026 Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as: Intermediate Professional $57,525-$77,083 Senior Professional $62,189-$83,333 Principal Professional: $71,517-$95,833 The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position may be eligible for overtime compensation, depending on the level. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@cuanschutz.edu . Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41460&lang=en": {
      "title": "Research Associate / Senior Research Associate",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 20, 2026 Job category: Research Faculty Department: SOM-MED-BoneMarrow Transplant Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Department: SOM-MED-Bone Marrow Transplant – Pietras Lab Job Title: Research Associate / Senior Research Associate Position #00853845 - Requisition #41460 Job Summary: The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is a world-class medical destination at the forefront of transformative science, medicine, education and patient care. The campus encompasses the University of Colorado health professional schools, more than 60 centers and institutes, and two nationally ranked independent hospitals - UCHealth University of Colorado Hospital and Children's Hospital Colorado - that treat more than two million adult and pediatric patients each year. Innovative, interconnected and highly collaborative, the University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus delivers life-changing treatments, patient care and professional training and conducts world-renowned research fueled by over $762 million in research grants. For more information, visit www.cuanschutz.edu . The Division of Hematology at the University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus has an opening for a full-time Research Associate/ Senior Research Assocaite in the Pietras Laboratory. This position is expected to work independently under the guidance of the principal investigator. Projects will involve work with animal model and human patient sample experiments to investigate blood cancer and inflammation biology and candidate regimens, extensive development and use of cutting-edge flow cytometry, molecular biology, experimental therapeutics studies on novel agents, and cell biology assays on rare bone marrow-derived hematopoietic populations. Specific duties include: Key Responsibilities: · Development, Design and Performance of Research Experiments · Mechanism based discovery of cancer and inflammation therapeutics. · Characterization of metabolic processes of normal and leukemic cells. · Use of animal model systems to study leukemia pathogenesis. · Analysis and Publication of Research Data (20% of Time Spent) · Mentoring of students and technical staff (5% of Time Spent) · Prepare data and manuscripts for publication · Prepare grant proposals to obtain independent funding · Actively participate in and present data at group meetings, journal clubs and conferences · Work in conjunction with the PI and other lab staff to achieve programmatic goals, including trainee supervision. Other duties as assigned Work Location: Onsite – this role is expected to work onsite full time, in various sites on the Anschutz Medical Campus located in Aurora, CO. Why Join Us: The Department of Medicine, Hematology/Oncology/Bone Marrow Transplant Laboratories, at the University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus (CU), Denver is looking for a bright, creative and enthusiastic Research Associate in advancing their career in a new, high-impact laboratory headed by an energetic, established principal investigator, Dr. Eric Pietras. The lab is part of a richly collaborative interdisciplinary group of basic scientists and clinicians from immunology, hematology and molecular biology backgrounds with significant resources. Why work for the University? The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year (based on percentage of time) Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 11/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. · A doctoral level degree (PhD, MD, MD/PhD) in immunology, stem cell biology, experimental hematology, molecular biology, or equivalent from an accredited institution. · At least one first-author publication in an internationally recognized, peer-reviewed journal. Research Associate: One year experience Senior Research Associate: two years’ experience. Conditions of Employment: · Candidate must be able to work with laboratory animals, animal tissues, and human tissue specimens. · Candidate must meet eligibility requirements for career development fellowship and career transition awards. Preferred Qualifications: · Specific experience with leukemia or inflammation research. · Graduate training in a biomedical laboratory setting, studying immunology, molecular biology, hematology and/or stem cell biology. · Experience with the use of advanced flow cytometry equipment (including LSRII and FACSAria Fusion) for analysis and sorting of cells, and development of multicolor antibody staining panels. · Experience in mouse handling, husbandry and dissection. · Experience in experimental hematology and molecular biology assays and techniques, including HSC isolation and analysis, and high-throughput sequencing. · Candidates that have successfully obtained competitive, extramural funding during their doctoral studies are preferred. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Excellent written and verbal communication skills Ability to work independently and as a team member within a research environment. Ability to work efficiently and effectively with computer software including Microsoft Office. Skilled with the use of aseptic mammalian cell culture techniques. Skilled with common laboratory techniques and equipment consistent with PhD-level graduate training. Ability to commit to an independent scientific career in stem cell biology, immunology, or a related field, with a proven high degree of independence and self-motivation to achieve these ends. Ability to work a flexible schedule based on the needs of the project. How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): 1. Curriculum vitae / Resume Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers . Questions should be directed to: Daniel.Page@cuanschutz.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Applications will be accepted until finalists are identified, but preference will be given to complete applications received by 12/30/2026. Those who do not apply by this date may or may not be considered. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as HIRING RANGE: · Research Associate: $80,000 - $85,000 · Senior Research Associate: $85,000 - $90,000 The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation unless it is non-exempt. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: The University of Colorado (CU) is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@ucdenver.edu ​. Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41464&lang=en": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 20, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: SOM-MED-Geriatrics Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Department: DOM/Division of Geriatric Medicine Job Title: Assistant Professor Position #: 00853960 – Requisition #:41464 Job Summary: The Division of Geriatric Medicine in the School of Medicine at the University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus invites applications for a .75 - 1.0 FTE faculty clinician position at the rank of Assistant Professor. Successful candidates will join a collegial geriatrics division that includes physicians, nurse practitioners, and PhDs. This is a full-time position with varying/flexible work hours, including some evening and/or weekend coverage. The work site(s) may include (but may not be limited to) the University of Colorado Hospital (UCH) Seniors Clinics, and University of Colorado (UCD) Division of Geriatric Medicine’s administrative offices. Key Responsibilities: Examples of work performed may include: - Provide geriatric primary care to patients within UCHealth AMC Seniors or Lone Tree Seniors Clinic(s) - Work closely with a multidisciplinary team within a geriatric primary care clinic to include working with behavioral health, pharmacists, physical therapists, social work, nurse care manager, medical assistants, and nurses. - The incumbent will share responsibilities of night, weekend, and vacation coverage with other providers of the group practice and will participate in decisions regarding the practice operation. - Educational responsibilities may include: a) teaching in a primary care setting (students, residents, and fellows); b) participating in an active clinical residency program; c) participation in teaching lectures about geriatric principles to medical students, residents, and fellows. Work Location: Onsite – this role is expected to work onsite at either/both of our Seniors Clinics, located in Aurora and Lone Tree, Colorado. Why Join Us: The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is a world-class medical destination at the forefront of transformative science, medicine, education and patient care. The campus encompasses the University of Colorado health professional schools, more than 60 centers and institutes, and two nationally ranked independent hospitals - UCHealth University of Colorado Hospital and Children's Hospital Colorado - that treat more than two million adult and pediatric patients each year. Innovative, interconnected and highly collaborative, the University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus delivers life-changing treatments, patient care and professional training and conducts world-renowned research fueled by over $762 million in research grants. For more information, visit www.cuanschutz.edu . We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year (based on percentage of time) Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 11/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. · MD or DO · Board-certified or eligible in geriatrics and either family medicine or internal medicine ● Eligible to obtain an unrestricted Colorado Medical License, and an active and unrestricted DEA Registration Preferred Qualifications: ● Experience in adult education ● Have completed a fellowship in Geriatric Medicine Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: · Strong clinical knowledge and skills in the evaluation and management of complex older adults, including multimorbidity, geriatric syndromes, and polypharmacy. · Knowledge of and experience with team-based, interdisciplinary care in an ambulatory primary care setting. · Strong clinical teaching and precepting skills, with experience educating medical students, residents, and/or fellows. · Commitment to learner development, including providing effective feedback, mentorship, and role modeling in the clinical environment. · Excellent interpersonal and communication skills with patients, families, learners, colleagues, and interdisciplinary team members. · Demonstrated ability to collaborate effectively within multidisciplinary teams and contribute to a positive, collegial work environment. · Self-motivated and engaged, with the ability to work independently while contributing actively to shared clinical, educational, and divisional goals. · Demonstrates growth mindset, including openness to feedback, continuous learning, and professional development. · Commitment to academic medicine, with interest in contributing to the educational, clinical quality improvement, and/or scholarly missions of the division. · Demonstrates professionalism, reliability, adaptability, and accountability in clinical and academic responsibilities. · Commitment to being an engaged team member, including participation in division and clinic activities and efforts to improve clinical care and the workplace. How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): 1. A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position 2. Curriculum vitae / Resume 3. Five professional references including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers . Questions should be directed to: SABRINA FERGUSON, Sabrina.ferguson@cuanschutz.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Applications will be accepted until finalists are identified, but preference will be given to complete applications received by December 1, 2026. Those who do not apply by this date may or may not be considered. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as HIRING RANGE: $200,000 - $210,000 Based on 1.0 FTE This position is eligible for the division incentive plan, which is in addition to the base salary. The above salary range represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation unless it is non-exempt. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: The University of Colorado (CU) is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@ucdenver.edu ​. Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41461&lang=en": {
      "title": "Finance and Accounting Professional (Open Rank: Senior - Principal)",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 20, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: SOM-BioChem&Molecular Genetics Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Department: Biochemistry & Molecular Genetics Job Title: Finance and Accounting Professional (Open Rank: Senior - Principal) Position # 00823575 – Requisition #: 41461 Job Summary: This role offers a unique opportunity for individuals passionate about financial management within a vibrant academic and research environment. As a key financial strategist for the seven core facilities, you will play a pivotal role in forecasting costs, developing, and monitoring budgets, and ensuring financial sustainability. Your work will directly impact the advancement of groundbreaking research by providing essential support to core directors and the School of Medicine’s leadership. You'll engage in diverse and impactful projects, from managing complex budget reconciliations and financial reporting to coordinating construction funding for facility upgrades and implementing standardized invoicing systems. Day-to-day, you will collaborate with core facility managers, faculty, the Dean’s Office, and external entities, ensuring accurate financial tracking and compliance with university policies. You’ll also manage grant expenditures, perform financial analyses for research laboratories, and oversee payroll funding distributions. This role not only supports the financial health of the department but also enhances the university's mission of fostering innovative research. If you’re looking for a position where your financial acumen can make a tangible difference, this is an exciting and rewarding opportunity to contribute to the university's success and growth. Key Responsibilities: Forecast and reconcile complex program and project budgets for core facilities, including preparing annual cost studies and financial projections. Manage and coordinate construction and remodel funding processes for core facility expansions and upgrades. Develop and oversee a standardized invoicing system for all cores, ensuring accurate reporting and timely payment collection. Coordinate procurement support for large equipment and manage equipment inventories and depreciation schedules. Analyze grant notices, manage sponsored project expenditures, and prepare financial forecasts for laboratory budgets. Work closely with the Office of Grants and Contracts to ensure compliance with granting agency policies and regulations. Provide quarterly or monthly financial reports to facility directors, including budget recommendations and potential issue assessments. Work Location: Hybrid – this role is eligible for a hybrid schedule of # days per week on campus and as needed for in-person meetings. Why Join Us: Our department conducts research across a wide biological scale for fundamental scientific understanding with applications to many disease contexts. The overarching goal is to reach a level of molecular insight that helps develop therapeutic approaches to disease. As biochemists and molecular geneticists, we are amid an unprecedented time of discovery - our conception of the molecular biology of cells is going from the equivalent of grainy black-and-white to high-resolution technicolor. From deciphering the choreography of transcription complexes, chromosomes, and RNA molecules within cells to developing novel approaches to 3D molecular structure determination to understanding how viruses hijack a cell’s machinery and alter its metabolome, the researchers in Biochemistry and Molecular Genetics (BMG) are at the forefronts of their fields both conceptually and technologically. Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 15/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Senior Professional: Bachelor’s degree in business administration, business, finance, accounting, or a directly related field from an accredited institution and 2 years of professional experience, to include financial accounting, post-award grant and contract management. Experience with financial forecasting and budget analysis. Principal Professional: Bachelor’s degree in business administration, business, finance, accounting, or a directly related field from an accredited institution and 3-5 years of professional experience, to include financial accounting, post-award grant and contract management. Experience with financial forecasting and budget analysis. Substitution: A combination of education and related technical/military/paraprofessional experience may be substituted for a bachelor’s degree on a year for year basis. Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Preferred Qualifications: One (1) or more years of professional level experience with post-award grant and contract management, including direct responsibility for managing NIH grants. Core service center financial experience. Higher education experience. Experience working with HCM, Finance, CU Data, Concur, CU Marketplace, and InfoEd. Payroll experience. Experience in providing professional and technical assistance to faculty, staff, and students within a higher education and/or medical education environment. Experience with or knowledge of University policies and procedures as well as University payroll processes and procedures. Conditions of Employment: Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without requiring sponsorship. We are unable to provide work visa sponsorship or employment authorization for this position now or in the future. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Ability to communicate effectively, both in writing and orally. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with employees at all levels throughout the institution. Outstanding customer service skills. Demonstrated commitment and leadership ability to advance diversity and inclusion. Ability to find reasonable solutions to complex financial and personnel related issues. Strong technical skills, which include the ability to work with Microsoft software, programs, and applications (primarily Excel and Access); willingness to learn new systems is essential. Detail oriented and conscientious in the observance of deadlines. Ability to interpret and implement complex layers of policy. Ability to understand and interpret complex guidelines and regulations for salary caps, facilities and administrative cost calculations, and funding restrictions. How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position Curriculum vitae / Resume Three to five professional references, including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Questions should be directed to: Anthony Davis, Anthony.J.Davis@cuanschutz.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Applications will be accepted until finalists are identified, but preference will be given to complete applications received by 11/3/26. Those who do not apply by this date may or may not be considered. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as: Senior Professional: $58,175 - $68,064 Principal Professional: $66,901 - $78,274 The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position may be eligible for overtime compensation, depending on the level. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@cuanschutz.edu ​. Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41459&lang=en": {
      "title": "Open Rank Medical Assistant - Multi-Specialty Medicine, Highlands Ranch",
      "description": "Closing Date: 11/04/2026 Posted Date: Oct 20, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: SOM-DEAN DO CPD - ORTHOPEDICS Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus Department: Community Practice Job Title: Open Rank Medical Assistant - Multi-Specialty Medicine, Highlands Ranch Position #: 00854051 – Requisition #: 41459 Job Summary: Calling all Medical Assistants and Certified Medical Assistants! Our busy clinics are recruiting for Medical Assistants! We need your training and skills to help our clinic run smoothly, providing our patients with top notch quality care. The Medical Assistant (MA) or Certified Medical Assistant (CMA) is responsible for providing patient care under the direction of a physician or another healthcare provider. The MA works to facilitate clinic workflow, assist patients, and ensure safe, seamless delivery of care for each patient. Key Responsibilities: Accurately rooms patients, obtains and records vital signs, patient history, and reason for seeking care. Accurately processes and records telephone messages in patient medical records and according to policy. Assists in preparing prescription refills for providers according to policy. Maintains patient confidentiality, written and verbal. Communicates effectively and in an attentive manner with every patient encounter. Verifies the patient’s understanding of the purpose of the visit. Accurately documents all care provided and procedures performed within the patient’s medical record. Work Location: Onsite – this role is expected to work onsite and is located in Highlands Ranch, CO . Why Join Us: Community Practice Medicine, housed within the School of Medicine at the University of Colorado, is seeking trained medical professionals to join our growing team. With clinics spanning from Longmont to Castle Rock, we offer a wide variety of opportunities. Specialty areas include, but are not limited to: Orthopedics, Vascular Surgery, OBGYN, Internal Medicine, Urology, Psychiatry, and many more! The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is a public education, clinical and research facility serving 4,500 students and a world-class medical destination at the forefront of life-changing science, medicine, and healthcare. CU Anschutz offers more than 42 highly rated degree programs through 6 schools and colleges and receives over $500 million in research awards each year. We are the single largest health professions education provider in Colorado, awarding nearly 1,450 degrees annually. Powered by our award-winning faculty, renowned researchers, and a reputation for academic excellence, the CU Anschutz Medical Campus drives innovation from the classroom to the laboratory to the delivery of unparalleled patient care. Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation, and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package, including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accrues over the year Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 15/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced-rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Medical Assistant: Completion of an accredited medical assistant program OR one year of medical assistant work experience. Certified Medical Assistant: Completion of an accredited medical assistant program. One year of medical assistant work experience. Current CMA certification (i.e., AAMA, NCCT). Substitution (All Levels): A combination of education and related technical/paraprofessional experience may be substituted on a year-for-year basis. Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Preferred Qualifications (All Levels): Experience with MS Office. Experience with EPIC. Experience with Kronos. Experience with HealthStream. Conditions of Employment (All Levels): Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without requiring sponsorship. We are unable to provide work visa sponsorship or employment authorization for this position now or in the future. Current Basic Life Support (BLS) for Healthcare Providers issued by the American Heart Association or the American Red Cross healthcare provider-level CPR certification. Maintains all required licensure and certifications for the position. Must be able to work in-person. Must be able to travel to alternate locations as assigned. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities (All Levels): Strong organizational and personal skills. Strong medical terminology knowledge and skills. Strong knowledge of CPT & ICD-10 procedures. Strong knowledge of value-based care and risk-based coding procedures in Primary Care. Strong knowledge of medication and injection procedures. Ability to safely administer a variety of treatments and medications as directed. Ability to use various types of equipment for examination and treatment procedures. Ability to accurately take and record vital signs. Ability to accurately reconcile patient medications. Ability to maintain quality control standards. Ability to identify problems and recommend solutions. How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position Curriculum vitae / Resume Three to five professional references, including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Questions should be directed to: Nykol Jefferson, NYKOL.JEFFERSON@CUANSCHUTZ.EDU Screening of Applications Begins: Immediately and continues until the position is filled. For best consideration, please apply by November 3 rd , 2026 . Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as: Medical Assistant: $44,116 to $51,527 Certified Medical Assistant: $47,813 to $55,846 The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position may be eligible for overtime compensation, depending on the level. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans, and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@cuanschutz.edu . Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students, and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine-preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety-sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=40907&lang=en": {
      "title": "Director of Primary Care Faculty Practice",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 20, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: CON-DEAN ADMINISTRATION Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Department: College of Nursing Director of Primary Care Faculty Practice Assistant Professor of Clinical Practice Position Location: Community Health Clinic at CU Anschutz 1890 N Revere Ct Suite 5040, Aurora, CO 80045 Position #: 00007693 – Req #: 40907 Job Summary: Nature of Work The Director of Primary Care Faculty Practices provides strategic leadership and operational oversight for adult and pediatric primary care health services across the Colorado Front Range. This role is responsible for directing a team of clinical practice leads, fostering excellence in clinical care, and ensuring alignment with institutional goals and community needs. Key responsibilities include strategic planning, clinical service development, performance management, regulatory compliance, and cultivating a collaborative and inclusive clinical practice culture. The Director works in close partnership with the Office of Clinical and Community Affairs, contributing to programmatic and operational initiatives that advance clinical excellence and community engagement. This position reports to the Associate Dean for Clinical and Community Affairs and includes a balanced workload of 1.0 FTE, comprised of: · 0.5 FTE dedicated to administrative leadership and oversight of the practice lead team · 0.5 FTE allocated to clinical practice in adult primary care as an FNP at the Community Health Clinic at Anschutz Medical Campus Supervision Required This position is supervised by the Associate Dean for Clinical and Community Affairs. Supervision Exercised Supervises the primary care clinical practice leads. Supports a clinical practice faculty team who practice in primary care with the adult and pediatric population at a variety of sites including the Community Health Clinic at Anschutz Medical Campus, Children’s Hospital of Colorado, and the mobile pediatric practice in eastern Colorado. Work Performed · Serves as a strategic liaison between clinic staff and the Associate Dean of Clinical and Community Affairs to ensure alignment of clinical operations and patient care goals. · Partners with multidisciplinary teams to evaluate and apply key performance indicators, driving innovative, cost-effective improvements in clinical practice. · Contributes to programmatic development by formulating and implementing evidence-based health policies, protocols, and procedures. · Ensures adherence to safety, environmental, and infection control standards across clinical sites. · Leads continuous quality improvement initiatives focused on clinical excellence, operational efficiency, financial stewardship, and patient safety. · Coordinates and facilitates educational opportunities to support regulatory compliance and clinical competency. · Oversees clinical workflows and engages teams in performance improvement activities to enhance care delivery. · Supports and manages the clinical peer review process and annual evaluations in collaboration with CU Nursing teams. · Provides individualized mentorship, and support to clinical practice faculty. · Ensures compliance with University, College, and professional standards, policies, and procedures. · Participates in faculty and staff recruitment processes to support clinical growth and excellence. · Represents the clinic in leadership and governance meetings, advocating for operational and strategic priorities. · Acts as a liaison between the clinic and patients, collaborating providers, community stakeholders, and external partners. · Facilitates monthly faculty meetings to promote communication, collaboration, and shared decision-making. · Collaborates with the Medical Staff Office, College of Nursing Credentialing Committee, and CU Credentialing Committee to ensure provider credentialing and privileging. · Serves as a professional role model and thought leader, fostering a culture of excellence and innovation. · Manages clinical resources responsibly, aligning with institutional and practice-level fiscal goals. · Demonstrates expertise in patient documentation, compliance, and billing practices to support operational integrity. · Actively contributes to the advancement of the organization’s strategic plan and mission. Clinical : • Serves as primary care provider within team-based care model • Performs accurate physical examinations, evaluations, diagnoses, treatments, follow-up, and consultation • Supervises and/or coordinates the activities of patient care • Participates in after-hours call • Obtains patient history and develops comprehensive plan of care • Provides health education to patients, students, families, and/or community health practitioners and groups • Practices safety, environmental, and infection control methods • Functions as a clinical preceptor for health professions students • Identifies deviations from normal and consults as needed • Completes necessary documentation within established timeframes • Ensure strict compliance with University and professional policies/procedures • Adept at Electronic Health Record (EHR) use and EHR trouble shooting, improvement processes, and downtime procedures • Performs other duties, as assigned Work Location: Onsite – this role is expected to work onsite and is located in Aurora, Colorado. Why Join Us: CU Nursing is an amazing place to be. We have the distinct advantage of being a part of a huge medical campus with three incredible hospitals – the VA, the nationally ranked University of Colorado Hospital, and the Children’s Hospital Colorado where our nursing students and faculty learn every day. From our beginning 125 years ago as part of the School of Medicine at CU Boulder to our current home at the Anschutz Medical Campus, the college has been a recognized leader in nursing education (ranked #10 in online MS graduate programs by U.S. News & World Report 2023). Our faculty, students and staff have been instrumental in shaping the profession of nursing and teaching the next generation of nurses while treating patients in our own nurse-led clinics. Be a part of an innovative, dynamic, diverse, and exciting workplace -- helping make great things happen. Join us in our quest to boldly transform health together. Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package including: · Medical: Multiple plan options · Dental: Multiple plan options · Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision · Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay · Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year · Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) · Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) · Holiday Days: 10/year · Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses · ECO Pass: Reduced rate RTD Bus and light rail service To see what benefits are available, please visit: https://nursing.cuanschutz.edu/about/careers/benefits Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. · Doctoral degree in nursing from an accredited institution of higher education. · Current RN, APN and RxN licensures in good standing (Any State) · Could be working toward CO clinical licenses during application process and registered with DORA-Department of Regulatory Agencies. Must have Colorado licensures by date of hire. · Please review DORA’s Nursing Licensing Guide for detailed requirements: · https://drive.google.com/file/d/1XUWVoJSKm06kbhiH-WBNJ8OqolFRmXwD/view · Minimum of Five (5) years of full-scope primary care experience as an FNP · Four (4) years of progressive leadership experience in the primary care practice setting, including supervisory experience and experience with organizational finances. Conditions of employment: · Must be willing and able to obtain Colorado RN, APN, RxN licenses by date of hire. · Must be willing and able to obtain current DEA license within 90 days of hire. · Must be willing and able to obtain valid NPI number by date of hire · Must be willing and able to obtain valid Colorado Medicaid Provider number by date of hire · Must be willing and able to complete CAQH and all credentialing requirements prior to by date of hire. · Must be willing and able to obtain current BLS/CPR certification by date of hire. · Must be willing and able to actively participation in health plan contracts. · Must be willing and able to remain credentialed by the health plans and ensure credentialing materials stay current. · Must be willing and able to work in a normal patient care environment with some exposure to biological hazards and infectious diseases. · Must work standard clinic hours (Monday–Friday, 8:00 a.m.–5:00 p.m.) with rotating on-call coverage. Preferred Qualifications: · Experience in developing and implementing clinical protocols, policies, procedures, and patient consent to support high-quality, compliant care delivery. · Experience in clinical practice and program development, including strategic expansion and innovation in service offerings. · Experience managing large, interdisciplinary teams · Experience engaging in professional organizations and experience contributing to the advancement of clinical practice standards and advocacy efforts. · Experience in leading quality improvement initiatives or conducting program evaluations. Competencies : · Demonstrates independent judgment and the ability to prioritize work effectively in response to evolving healthcare trends and service line needs. · Builds and maintains strong working relationships with faculty, practice leadership, and interdisciplinary collaborators. · Exhibits clear, concise, and effective communication skills, both verbal and written, across diverse audiences. · Inspires and guides teams with a results-oriented leadership style that fosters engagement, accountability, and continuous improvement. · Committed to fostering professional growth through mentorship and collaborative leadership. · Applies strong organizational, time management, and analytical skills to manage complex workflows and solve problems proactively. · Works effectively across all levels of the organization to promote clinical and operational excellence through teamwork and shared goals. · Demonstrates a collaborative and supportive approach that values diverse perspectives and promotes a culture of inclusion. · Brings creativity and strategic insight to develop forward-thinking solutions that enhance clinical practice and operational performance. How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): 1. A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position 2. Curriculum vitae / Resume 3. Three to five professional references, including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Questions should be directed to: College of Nursing Human Resources at CON.HR@ucdenver.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Applications will be accepted until finalists are identified, but preference will be given to complete applications received by November 6 th , 2026 . Those who do not apply by this date may or may not be considered. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as $103,750-$115,278/year . The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position may be eligible for overtime compensation, depending on the level. In addition to the annual salary for this position, an annual administrative stipend of $10,000/year will also be offered . Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: The University of Colorado (CU) is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@ucdenver.edu ​. Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41458&lang=en": {
      "title": "Functional Reconstructive Urologist (FRU)- Open Rank",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 20, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: SOM-SRG-UR DIV Clinical Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Department: Surgery | Division of Urology Job Title: Open Rank-Assistant, Associate Working Title: Functional Reconstructive Urologist (FRU) Position #:00853896– Requisition #:41458 Job Summary: The Division of Urology, Department of Surgery, the University of Colorado School of Medicine is seeking a Functional - Reconstructive Urologist. Our robust urology service is provided by full-time faculty, fellows and mid-level providers. This position will address functional urologic conditions resulting in lower genitourinary tract dysfunction with a goal to improve bladder control, reduce pain, and restore sexual function, leading to a better quality of life. Designed to support regional growth, this role focuses on expanding clinical outreach in and around Metro Denver within established division productivity and coverage standards. The Functional Reconstructive Urologist will collaborate within the division and CU – Urology North to complement existing expertise, focusing on sub specialization across areas such as complex reconstruction, lower urinary tract dysfunction, neurogenic bladder, male prosthetics, and post-prostatectomy survivorship. The provider will utilize advanced, minimally invasive surgical techniques to optimize patient outcomes, reduce recovery time, and deliver high-quality, patient-centered care. Providing inclusive care for patients of all genders, the FRU provider will diagnose and treat complex functional disorders of the bladder, urethra, and ureter. Clinical management will emphasize a comprehensive approach that balances conservative, behavioral, and surgical options tailored to each patient's underlying disease process. Key Responsibilities: · Clinical Service & Regional Growth: Provide independent functional and reconstructive urology clinical services in inpatient and outpatient settings at University of Colorado Hospital, Metro Denver, which could include UCH Highlands Ranch, UCHealth Broomfield Hospital, and UCHealth Specialty Care - Baseline. Expand regional outreach and subspecialized volume while maintaining clinical productivity expectations (cRVUs) and shared call coverage aligned with division benchmarks. · Surgical & Perioperative Care: Perform complex inpatient and outpatient FRU surgeries, managing comprehensive pre- and post-operative care. · Cross-Disciplinary Collaboration: Work collaboratively with urology, urologic oncology, surgical oncology, burn surgery, orthopedic surgery colleagues to provide specialized reconstructive, prosthetic, and survivorship support for complex patient, ensuring multidisciplinary care. Work collaboratively with the integrated transgender program to provide comprehensive gender affirming surgical care. · Trainee & APP Supervision: Supervise advanced practice providers (APPs), fellows, residents, and medical students in ambulatory, inpatient, and operative settings to ensure clinical excellence and safety. · Fellowship & Academic Mentorship: Actively participate in the FRU Fellowship program by providing dedicated clinical teaching, surgical instruction, and career mentorship to the clinical fellow. · Education & Teaching: Engage directly in resident and medical student education, leading clinical teaching, surgical labs, and didactic training to foster academic development. · Research & Scholarly Activity: Collaborate with the FRU Research Program, supervising research activities alongside the Urology Research Team and the FRU Research Scholar. Work Location: Onsite – this role is expected to work onsite and is located in Aurora and Broomfield, CO. Why Join Us: We are driven to improve every life at the Department of Surgery with our commitment to innovative surgical care, curing through discovery, enlightening tomorrow’s leaders, and daring to be exceptional. Our focus on patient care, education, and research will lead to innovative discoveries and promote quality care and safety for our patients. Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year (based on percentage of time) Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 11/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. This is an open rank position and could be categorized as Assistant Professor or Associate Professor based on experience and qualifications as indicated below: Open Rank: Rank at the time of appointment will be based on the candidate’s demonstrated contributions and experience in teaching, clinical, research, and/or service to the field. We welcome applicants with a range of backgrounds and accomplishments and encourage individuals to highlight the breadth and depth of their professional impact. Learn more about faculty tracks at the Office for Faculty Affairs . Assistant Professor: Medical Degree from an accredited school of medicine Board certified or board eligible in urology Completion of a Functional and/or Reconstructive Urology fellowship Current or ability to obtain a license to practice as a physician in the state of Colorado with prescriptive privileges Demonstrated potential for excellence in clinical care, teaching, and research (e.g., through residency, fellowship, or early faculty work) Associate Professor: Medical Degree from an accredited school of medicine Board certified or board eligible in urology Completion of a Functional and/or Reconstructive Urology fellowship Current or ability to obtain a license to practice as a physician in the state of Colorado with prescriptive privileges Established record of clinical excellence, teaching, and independent scholarly work (peer-reviewed publications, presentations, or funded research) Minimum of 5 years of post-fellowship experience as an independent faculty member (or equivalent experience at another academic institution) Experience mentoring trainees, residents, or junior faculty. Preferred Qualifications: · Functional & Reconstructive Urology: Expertise in complex lower and upper urinary tract reconstruction, including robotic surgical approaches for urethral strictures, ureteral strictures, fistulas, and pubic osteomyelitis, complex genital reconstruction (ie concealed penis, hidradenitis, gender affirming surgery) · Prostate Cancer Survivorship & Men’s Health: Subspecialty focus on post-prostatectomy survivorship care—including male stress urinary incontinence (mSUI), anastomotic stenoses, erectile dysfunction, and Peyronie’s disease—offering cross-referral support for oncology and general urology practices. · Neurogenic Bladder & Voiding Dysfunction: Management of neurogenic lower urinary tract dysfunction, refractory overactive bladder (OAB), urinary retention, and complex voiding conditions. · Advanced Diagnostics & Neuromodulation: Proficiency in performing and interpreting complex video/wireless urodynamic testing, cystoscopy, sacral/tibial neuromodulation, and chemo-denervation (Botox). · Minimally Invasive Approaches: Demonstrated experience utilizing laparoscopic and robotic-assisted surgical techniques to reduce recovery times and improve clinical outcomes. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: · Diagnostic & Clinical Precision: Advanced proficiency in diagnosing and treating complex voiding dysfunction, urinary incontinence, and overactive bladder using comprehensive diagnostic modalities, including cystoscopy and video/wireless urodynamics. · Therapeutic & Procedural Expertise: Skill in advanced, minimally invasive treatments—including intravesical chemo-denervation (Botox), sacral and tibial neuromodulation, and anti-incontinence prosthetic procedures. · Complex Reconstruction: Demonstrated skill in complex open, endoscopic, and robotic surgical approaches to correct anatomical abnormalities, including urethral strictures, complex fistulas, and pubic osteomyelitis. · Comprehensive Care Model: Deep understanding of the interplay between neurological, behavioral, anatomical, and lifestyle factors in managing lower genitourinary tract dysfunction. · Academic Leadership: Strong interest in clinical care, resident and fellow education, and collaborative scholarly activity in functional and reconstructive urology. · Team & Division Collaboration: Strong interpersonal communication skills with a demonstrated commitment to working collaboratively across multidisciplinary teams and supporting division-wide referral networks. Conditions of Employment: ( Optional Statement) · Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without requiring sponsorship. We are unable to provide work visa sponsorship or employment authorization for this position now or in the future. How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): 1. A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position 2. Curriculum vitae / Resume 3. Five professional references including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers . Questions should be directed to: Jacky Bonds Jacky.Bonds@cuanschutz.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Applications will be accepted until finalists are identified, but preference will be given to complete applications received by December 30, 2026. Those who do not apply by this date may or may not be considered. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as HIRING RANGE: · Assistant Professor: $225,000 to $396,000 · Associate Professor: $261,761 to $450,000 The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation unless it is non-exempt. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: The University of Colorado (CU) is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@ucdenver.edu ​. Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=37634&lang=en": {
      "title": "Pediatric Cardiologist - Open Rank",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 20, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: SOM-PEDS Cardiology-GenOps Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus Department: Pediatrics - Cardiology Job Title: Pediatric Cardiologist Position #: 00670105 – Requisition:37634 Job Summary: The Cardiologist will perform general outpatient cardiology duties and may be expected to participate in inpatient cardiology care and consultation as well as Community education and networking. Key Responsibilities: · Outpatient cardiology clinic ~8 sessions per week in the NOC and outreach sites · 12 Saturday clinics per year (1 clinic session or 0.5 day clinic) · ~2 weeknights of cardiology call per month · Shared outpatient daytime call (City Team) Work Location: Onsite – this role is expected to work onsite and is located in Aurora, Colorado and NOC/regional locations. Why Join Us: As the largest pediatric heart program in the region, we have performed more than 675 heart surgeries and about 1,000 heart catheterization every year since 2017. Our highly specialized pediatric heart surgeons and interventional cardiologists take on the most complex congenital heart defects (CHDs) and childhood heart conditions and achieve some of the best results in the nation. The Society of Thoracic Surgery requires a hospital to perform at least 250 heart s urgeries per year to be considered a high-volume center. By far exceeding this, we gain more experience, which leads to better outcomes. The Heart Institute has 80 plus faculty members and continues to grow annually. Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 10/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. This is an open rank position and could be categorized as Assistant Professor, Associate Professor or Professor based on experience and qualifications as indicated below: Assistant Professor: ● Doctorate degree (MD or DO) ● Board Eligible in Pediatric Cardiology. ● Ability to obtain CO medical license ● DEA certificate ● 0-6 years of clinical experience, interest in pursuing academic promotion Associate Professor: ● Doctorate degree (MD or DO) ● Board Eligible in Pediatric Cardiology. ● Ability to obtain CO medical license ● DEA certificate ● 6 or more years of clinical experience ● Prior experience with program development, teaching or research ● Examples of scholarship Professor: ● Doctorate degree (MD or DO) ● Board Eligible in Pediatric Cardiology. ● Ability to obtain CO medical license ● DEA certificate ● 10 or more years of clinical experience ● Proven experience with program development, teaching or research ● Distinguished scholarship Condition of Employment: ● Must successfully pass a drug test through Children’s Hospital Colorado ● Must be willing and able to pass a national criminal background check *For questions regarding Children’s Hospital drug testing requirements, please contact Children’s Human Resources at 720-777-8598. Some positions may require testing if access to Children’s Hospital or their systems is needed at any time during employment with the University. If drug testing is required, it will be listed in the job posting. Preferred Qualifications: · Board certification in Pediatric Cardiology · Prior experience in outpatient cardiology including outreach Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: · Must be flexible · Good communication skills · Must be able to multitask How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): 1. A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position 2. Curriculum vitae / Resume 3. Five professional references, including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers . Questions should be directed to: Nicole Aviles, nicole.aviles@cuanschutz.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Immediately and continues until position is filled. For best consideration, apply by 12/30/2026. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as HIRING RANGE: Assistant Professor: $240,000-$254,886 Associate Professor: $293,814-314,752 Professor: $364,300-$391,436 The above hiring range represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation unless it is non-exempt. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Perks & Benefits: https://advantage.cu.edu/search Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: The University of Colorado (CU) is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@ucdenver.edu . Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41045&lang=en": {
      "title": "Assistant Director of Clinical Simulation",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 19, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: CON-DEAN ADMINISTRATION Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Department: College of Nursing, Office of Academic Programs Job Title: Assistant Director of Clinical Simulation (a faculty administrative appointment)/ Open Rank-Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, or Professor ) Position #: 00610603– Requisition #: 41045 Job Summary: The College of Nursing is seeking an energetic faculty leader to serve as the Assistant Director of Clinical Simulation, a faculty administrative appointment. The ideal candidate would be qualified to hold a faculty appointment within the IRC-Clinical Series, Clinical Teaching Track with dedicated time for the Assistant Director of Clinical Simulation role. This position is responsible for the operational leadership, management, and continuous improvement of the College of Nursing Clinical Simulation Program across multiple campuses. This position oversees the daily operations of simulation facilities, personnel, technology, resources, and educational support services to ensure the delivery of high-quality, innovative, and evidence-based simulation experiences that support undergraduate and graduate nursing education. Working under the general direction of the Assistant Dean of Clinical Simulation Science and in close operational collaboration with the Director of Clinical Simulation and Placements, the Assistant Director implements strategic initiatives, manages operational resources, supervises simulation personnel, supports faculty development, advances quality improvement efforts, and ensures compliance with national simulation standards, accreditation requirements, and university policies. The Assistant Director serves as an operational leader for the Clinical Simulation Program. simulation education resource, fostering innovation, operational excellence, and collaborative partnerships that advance the College's mission, vision, and strategic priorities for experiential learning. This position is responsible for developing efficient operational systems, monitoring program performance, supporting budget and resource management, maintaining state-of-the-art simulation facilities and technologies, and promoting a culture of excellence, continuous improvement, and exceptional service for faculty, students, staff, and external partners. This position reports directly to the Assistant Dean of Clinical Simulation Science within the College of Nursing, Office of Academic Programs. The Assistant Director works in close operational collaboration with the Director of Clinical Simulation and Placements, who provides day-to-day operational coordination and direction. This position directly supervises the Healthcare Simulation Assistants and serves as a member of the Clinical Education and Placements leadership team. Key responsibilities of the position include: Program Leadership & Operations · Provides operational leadership for the College of Nursing Clinical Simulation Program across multiple campuses. Oversees simulation operations, personnel, facilities, technology, and resources to ensure high-quality, efficient, and consistent simulation experiences that support undergraduate and graduate curricula. Develops standardized operational processes, monitors program performance, and collaborates with faculty and leadership to optimize resources and support the College's strategic priorities. · Direct the day-to-day operations of the Clinical Simulation Program, including scheduling, facilities, technology, and operational resources. · Develop and maintain standardized operational workflows, policies, and procedures to ensure consistent, high-quality simulation services. · Monitor simulation utilization, operational performance, and resource allocation; implement process improvements to enhance efficiency and effectiveness. · Collaborate with faculty and leadership to align simulation operations with curricular priorities and institutional goals. Personnel Leadership · Provides leadership and supervision of simulation personnel to foster a highly engaged, collaborative, and high-performing team. Oversees workforce planning, staff development, performance management, and employee engagement while promoting a culture of accountability, professionalism, and continuous learning. · Supervise Healthcare Simulation Assistants through recruitment, onboarding, scheduling, coaching, and performance evaluation. · Develop staffing plans and coordinate personnel assignments to ensure operational coverage across simulation locations. · Foster employee engagement, professional development, and a collaborative team environment. · Collaborate with leadership to anticipate workforce needs and support organizational growth. Quality, Accreditation & Regulatory Oversight · Promotes excellence in simulation-based education through evidence-based practices, continuous quality improvement, and adherence to national standards. Ensures simulation activities meet accreditation, regulatory, and professional standards while supporting faculty development and program evaluation. · Ensure compliance with the INACSL Healthcare Simulation Standards of Best Practice®, the Healthcare Simulationist Code of Ethics, accreditation standards, and regulatory requirements. · Develop and evaluate simulation policies, quality assurance processes, and continuous quality improvement initiatives. · Analyze learner, faculty, and program evaluation data to guide operational and educational improvements. · Support accreditation activities through documentation, reporting, and regulatory review processes. Faculty & Educational Partnerships · Collaborates with faculty to advance excellence in simulation-based education by providing consultation, mentorship, and educational support. Promotes evidence-based simulation methodologies while fostering faculty competency, innovation, and continuous professional development. · Mentor and consult with faculty on simulation design, facilitation, debriefing, and evaluation. · Develop faculty resources and lead professional development initiatives that enhance simulation competency. · Collaborate with academic leadership to integrate simulation strategically across undergraduate and graduate curricula. · Promote evidence-based simulation practices and educational innovation. Technology, Facilities & Innovation · Provides operational leadership for the management and advancement of simulation facilities, technologies, and equipment. Ensures simulation environments remain operationally ready, technologically current, and aligned with educational priorities. · O versee lifecycle management of simulation equipment, including inventory, maintenance, replacement planning, and capital equipment recommendations. · Collaborate with Information Technology, Facilities Management, vendors, and internal stakeholders to support simulation infrastructure. · Manage simulation facilities, technology systems, access permissions, and operational readiness across campuses. · Evaluate and implement emerging simulation technologies that enhance teaching, learning, and operational efficiency. Strategic Planning & Program Development · Collaborates with the Director of Clinical Simulation and Placements to implement operational priorities and strategic initiatives established by the Assistant Dean of Clinical Simulation Science. Supports program growth through operational planning, performance monitoring, and continuous process improvement. · Implement strategic initiatives and operational priorities that support the College's mission, vision, and strategic plan. · Monitor operational metrics, simulation utilization, and program outcomes; provide recommendations for continuous improvement. · Prepare operational reports and dashboards to support data-informed decision-making. · Participate in strategic planning, committee work, and implementation of new programs, technologies, and educational initiatives. Budget & Resource Stewardship · Provides stewardship of operational resources to ensure the sustainability, efficiency, and readiness of the Clinical Simulation Program. Collaborates with the Director to support budget planning, resource management, and fiscal accountability. · Assist in developing and monitoring annual operating and capital budgets for the Clinical Simulation Program. · Monitor expenditures and manage operational resources to ensure fiscal responsibility and efficient utilization. · Forecast equipment, technology, staffing, and supply needs to support current operations and future growth. · Recommend capital purchases and resource investments that support strategic priorities. Teaching & Educational Support · Provides instructional leadership to ensure continuity, quality, and innovation in simulation-based education. Maintains simulation teaching expertise and provides instructional support as needed to ensure operational continuity and advance evidence-based experiential learning. · Provide simulation instruction and faculty coverage as operational needs require. · Support implementation of new simulation curricula, educational initiatives, and pilot programs. · Model best practices in simulation facilitation, debriefing, and learner assessment. · Maintain clinical and simulation expertise through ongoing professional development and scholarly engagement. This description is a summary only and describes the general level of work being performed; it is not intended to be all-inclusive. The duties of this position may change from time to time and/or based on business need. We reserve the right to add or delete duties and responsibilities at the discretion of the supervisor and/or hiring authority. Work Location: Hybrid – This position carries significant leadership and operational responsibilities that necessitate regular in-person presence and engagement onsite. The successful candidate will be expected to work onsite a minimum of three (3) days per week, with the opportunity for remote work when duties, meetings, and business needs permit. Why Join Us: CU Nursing is an amazing place to be. We have the distinct advantage of being a part of a huge medical campus with three incredible hospitals – the VA, the nationally ranked University of Colorado Hospital, and the Children’s Hospital Colorado where our nursing students and faculty learn every day. From our beginning 125 years ago as part of the School of Medicine at CU Boulder to our current home at the Anschutz Medical Campus, the college has been a recognized leader in nursing education (ranked #10 in online MS graduate programs by U.S. News & World Report 2023). Our faculty, students and staff have been instrumental in shaping the profession of nursing and teaching the next generation of nurses while treating patients in our own nurse-led clinics. Be a part of an innovative, dynamic, diverse, and exciting workplace -- helping make great things happen. Join us in our quest to boldly transform health together. Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package including: · Medical: Multiple plan options · Dental: Multiple plan options · Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision · Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay · Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year (based on percentage of time) · Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) · Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) · Holiday Days: 11/year · Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses · ECO Pass: Reduced rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): 1. A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position 2. Curriculum vitae / Resume 3. Five professional references including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers . Questions should be directed to the College of Nursing Human Resources Team at con.hr@ucdenver.edu and 303-724-4447 Screening of Applications Begins: Applications will be accepted until finalists are identified, but preference will be given to complete applications received by October 31st, 2026 . Those who do not apply by this date may or may not be considered. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as HIRING RANGE: Assistant Professor of Clinical Teaching - $105,000 to $125,000 annually at 1.0 FTE Associate Professor of Clinical Teaching - $125,000 to $145,000 annually at 1.0 FTE Professor of Clinical Teaching - $145,000 to $165,000 annually at 1.0 FTE The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation unless it is non-exempt. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: The University of Colorado (CU) is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@ucdenver.edu ​. Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41455&lang=en": {
      "title": "Program Manager, Marketing & Growth",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 19, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: SOM-DEAN DO ADMINISTRATION Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Department: University of Colorado – School of Medicine – Dean’s Office – Institute for Healthcare Quality, Safety & Efficiency Job Title: Program Manager, Marketing & Growth Position #: 00854024 – Requisition #: 41455 Job Summary: The Program Manager, Marketing & Growth is responsible for developing and executing marketing initiatives that increase awareness, engagement, recruitment, participation, and growth across the Institute for Healthcare Quality, Safety & Efficiency. This position serves as the Institute's lead marketing strategist and marketing technology expert, overseeing campaign development, audience growth, marketing automation, customer acquisition, digital promotion, social media, and performance analytics. This role translates organizational priorities and communications content into measurable marketing outcomes that support program growth, brand awareness, and strategic objectives. Key Responsibilities: Marketing Strategy and Audience Growth (25%) Develop and implement annual marketing plans that support organizational and programmatic goals. Design recruitment and promotional strategies for educational programs, conferences, consulting services, and strategic initiatives. Identify opportunities to increase awareness, participation, and customer engagement. Conduct market research and competitive analysis to inform growth strategies. Campaign Development and Execution (25%) Develop and manage multi-channel marketing campaigns. Develop and manage customer pipeline. Lead promotion of educational programs, conferences, workshops, and organizational initiatives. Create audience-specific campaign strategies across email, social, web, and other digital platforms. Coordinate campaign schedules, timelines, and execution. Marketing Platforms and Automation (20%) Serve as primary administrator for marketing platforms, marketing automation tools, and email systems. Develop audience segmentation strategies and customer journey workflows. Maintain marketing databases and customer engagement systems. Digital Marketing and Social Media (15%) Manage the institute’s social media, including post creation, strategy, scheduling, and performance monitoring, maintaining alignment with stories and other content developed by the Communications, Brand & Design Program Manager. Oversee digital advertising and audience development efforts. Analytics & Measurement (10%) Develop dashboards and reports that measure marketing effectiveness. Monitor campaign performance, engagement, conversion rates, and audience growth. Use data and analytics to recommend improvements and optimization strategies. Communicate marketing performance to leadership and program teams. Leadership and Collaboration (5%) Partner closely with the Communications, Brand & Design Program Manager to transform content into effective marketing campaigns. Collaborate with program managers and institute leadership to align marketing efforts with organizational priorities. Support special initiatives and institutional growth opportunities. Work Location: Hybrid – this role is eligible for a hybrid schedule of three (3) days per week on campus and as needed for in-person meetings. Why Join Us: The Institute for Healthcare Quality, Safety and Efficiency’s (IHQSE) overarching goal is to fundamentally improve the care we provide our patients. Since our founding in 2012, we have experienced tremendous growth and expansion guided by our mission of transforming through discovery, improvement and spreading the people and processes that serve our patients. The core foundation of the IHQSE is our team. Comprised of dedicated and gifted faculty, our team not only teaches the fundamentals of leadership, how to initiate change, and how to improve healthcare outcomes, but also guides and inspires participants to become better leaders and more effective catalysts of sustainable change. Our formula for success combines expert training, intensive, tailored coaching, and a deep catalog of successful projects to tap into. Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation, and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 15/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced-rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree in marketing, journalism, public relations, communications, business administration, business, or a directly related field from an accredited institution. Substitution: A combination of education and related technical/military/paraprofessional experience may be substituted for a bachelor’s degree on a year-for-year basis. At least four (4) years of experience working in communications, public relations, social media, or marketing field(s). Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Preferred Qualifications: Professional experience in marketing, digital marketing, demand generation, audience development, or related fields. Experience with a CRM system, marketing automation, and email marketing platforms, specifically Salesforce and Marketing Cloud. Experience managing business social media accounts, including LinkedIn Ads. Experience developing and executing integrated marketing campaigns. Experience with analytics, reporting, and performance optimization. Experience in healthcare, higher education, nonprofit, or professional association environments. Basic graphic design skills and experience working in Canva. Conditions of Employment: Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without requiring sponsorship. We are unable to provide work visa sponsorship or employment authorization for this position now or in the future. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Well-developed professional skills in the areas of program planning, management, and data-driven decision-making. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with faculty, staff, fellows, residents, students, alumni, and administrative personnel at all levels, including outside organizations and the public. A demonstrated ability to independently manage and respond to support customer needs and requests in a professional, timely manner. Ability to work independently and as a member of a team, and handle a fast-paced environment. How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position Curriculum vitae / Resume Three to five professional references, including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Two samples of your marketing work, including but not limited to: marketing campaigns, promotional materials, social media posts, or other relevant content. Questions should be directed to: Anne Kercsmar ( anne.kercsmar@cuanschutz.edu ) Screening of Applications Begins: Immediately and continues until the position is filled. For best consideration, apply by November 5, 2026 . Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as $65,105 to $87,241 . The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position may be eligible for overtime compensation, depending on the level. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans, and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@cuanschutz.edu . Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students, and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety-sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41454&lang=en": {
      "title": "Program Manager, Communications, Brand & Design",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 19, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: SOM-DEAN DO ADMINISTRATION Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Department: University of Colorado – School of Medicine – Dean’s Office – Institute for Healthcare Quality, Safety & Efficiency Job Title: Program Manager, Communications, Brand & Design Position #: 00829325 – Requisition #: 41454 Job Summary: The Program Manager, Communications, Brand & Design is responsible for shaping and communicating the voice, identity, and impact of the Institute for Healthcare Quality, Safety & Efficiency (IHQSE) and its partnerships. This position serves as the Institute's lead storyteller, content strategist, and creative lead, transforming program outcomes, participant achievements, faculty accomplishments, and organizational priorities into compelling communications and visual experiences. Working closely with institute leadership, this position develops communication strategies that strengthen awareness, engagement, and reputation while ensuring consistency across organizational messaging, branding, and design. Key Responsibilities: Communications Strategy and Content Leadership (25%) Develop and implement integrated communications strategies that align with organizational goals and priorities. Create and manage annual communications and editorial calendars. Develop audience-specific messaging for participants, alumni, faculty, organizational partners, donors, and prospective customers. Ensure consistency of messaging, voice, and positioning across all communications materials. Provide communications guidance and consultation to institute leadership. Storytelling and Content Development (25%) Develop stories that highlight program outcomes, participant successes, faculty accomplishments, organizational achievements, and partnership impact. Conduct interviews and gather information from stakeholders, alumni, customers, faculty, and learners. Write feature stories, annual reports, newsletters, impact reports, case studies, and executive communications. Translate program outcomes and performance data into meaningful narratives that demonstrate organizational value. Support thought leadership initiatives and strategic communications efforts. Brand Management and Creative Direction (25%) Maintain and strengthen the IHQSE brand. Develop messaging frameworks and visual standards for organizational initiatives and programs. Ensure all communications materials align with established brand guidelines. Provide creative direction and execution for program materials, promotional materials, reports, presentations, and digital assets. Support multimedia production including photography, videos, and podcasts. Develop visual storytelling approaches that support organizational goals. Website and Content Management (15%) Lead website content strategy and user experience planning. Lead search engine optimization and artificial intelligence engine optimization. Design and organize website content to improve accessibility, engagement, and storytelling. Ensure website content remains accurate, current, and aligned with organizational priorities. Analytics & Measurement (5%) Develop dashboards and reports that measure communication effectiveness. Use data and analytics to recommend improvements and optimization strategies. Communicate performance to leadership and program teams. Leadership and Collaboration (5%) Collaborate with program leaders and institute leadership to identify content opportunities. Partner with the Program Manager, Impact & Strategic Initiatives to communicate customer successes and organizational impact. Work closely with the Marketing Strategy & Growth Program Manager to support coordinated campaign execution. Work Location: Hybrid – this role is eligible for a hybrid schedule of three (3) days per week on campus and as needed for in-person meetings. Why Join Us: The Institute for Healthcare Quality, Safety and Efficiency’s (IHQSE) overarching goal is to fundamentally improve the care we provide our patients. Since our founding in 2012, we have experienced tremendous growth and expansion guided by our mission of transforming through discovery, improvement and spreading the people and processes that serve our patients. The core foundation of the IHQSE is our team. Comprised of dedicated and gifted faculty, our team not only teaches the fundamentals of leadership, how to initiate change, and how to improve healthcare outcomes, but also guides and inspires participants to become better leaders and more effective catalysts of sustainable change. Our formula for success combines expert training, intensive, tailored coaching, and a deep catalog of successful projects to tap into. Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation, and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 15/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced-rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree in marketing, journalism, public relations, communications, business administration, business, or a directly related field from an accredited institution. Substitution: A combination of education and related technical/military/paraprofessional experience may be substituted for a bachelor’s degree on a year-for-year basis. At least four (4) years of experience working in communications, public relations, social media, or marketing field(s). Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Preferred Qualifications: Professional experience in communications, journalism, public relations, content strategy, marketing communications, or a related field. Experience developing organizational communications strategies. Demonstrated excellence in interviewing, writing, editing, and storytelling. Experience in graphic design and visual communications. Experience designing websites, digital experiences, and user-centered content (Sitefinity). Experience with graphic design software (such as Adobe Creative Suite). Experience working in healthcare, higher education, nonprofit, or professional association environments. Conditions of Employment: Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without requiring sponsorship. We are unable to provide work visa sponsorship or employment authorization for this position now or in the future. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Well-developed professional skills in the areas of program planning, management, and data-driven decision-making. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with faculty, staff, fellows, residents, students, alumni, and administrative personnel at all levels, including outside organizations and the public. A demonstrated ability to independently manage and respond to support customer needs and requests in a professional, timely manner. Ability to work independently and as a member of a team, and handle a fast-paced environment. How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position Curriculum vitae / Resume Three to five professional references, including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Two samples of your communications work, including but not limited to: feature stories, annual reports, newsletters, impact reports, infographics, blog posts, or other relevant content. Questions should be directed to: Anne Kercsmar (anne.kercsmar@cuanschutz.edu) . Screening of Applications Begins: Immediately and continues until the position is filled. For best consideration, apply by November 2 nd , 2026 . Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as $65,105 to $87,241 . The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position may be eligible for overtime compensation, depending on the level. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans, and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@cuanschutz.edu . Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students, and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety-sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41453&lang=en": {
      "title": "Dental Hygienist",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 19, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: CON-DEAN ADMINISTRATION Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Department: College of Nursing Job Title: Dental Hygienist Position #: 00854000 – Requisition #: 41453 Job Summary: Nature of Work: The CU College of Nursing is seeking a full-time (1.0 FTE), benefits-eligible Dental Hygienist within its Federally Qualified Health Center, Sheridan Health Services, located in southwest Denver, CO (zip code: 80236). This Dental Hygienist will provide quality oral health care to patients at the primary location and community settings. Sheridan Health Services (SHS) seeks a compassionate, skilled, and collaborative Registered Dental Hygienist to provide comprehensive preventive and therapeutic oral healthcare services for pediatric and adult patients. This position plays a vital role within an integrated healthcare environment that supports Behavioral Oral Health Integration (BOHI), Medical Dental Integration (MDI), Patient-Centered Medical Home (PCMH), and Culturally and Linguistically Appropriate Services (CLAS) models of care. This position serves as a clinical provider, educator, patient advocate, and collaborative member of the interdisciplinary healthcare team. The successful candidate will demonstrate excellence in patient care, documentation, quality improvement, community outreach, regulatory compliance, and student mentorship while supporting the mission, vision, and strategic goals of SHS and the University. Clinic Description Sheridan Health Services is a multi-site, nurse-managed federally qualified community health center, funded through the Health Resources and Services Administration Bureau of Primary Healthcare, and is a collaborative effort between the College of Nursing and the Sheridan School District. There are now two convenient locations to serve community health needs primarily for residents of Arapahoe, Denver, and Jefferson counties. Sheridan Health Services is located in southwest Denver on the Fort Logan campus and provides services to adults and children, 65% of whom identify as Latinx, and 42% of whom are best served in another language, with Spanish being the predominant second language. Services offered include primary care across the lifespan; prenatal and postpartum care, gynecology, dentistry, pharmacy, health, and outpatient substance abuse treatment. https://nursing.cuanschutz.edu/patient-care/sheridan-health-services Supervision Received Work is performed under the general direction and authority of the Sheridan Health Services Dental Director. Examples of Duties Performed: Assesses dental conditions and treatment needs utilizing patient screening procedures, including review of medical, dental, and behavioral health histories, medications, allergies, radiographs, and dental/periodontal charting to formulate a dental hygiene diagnosis. Delivers direct patient care and performs dental hygiene procedures in accordance with Colorado licensure and established standards of care. Performs preventive and periodontal procedures for patients of all ages, including prophylaxis, full mouth debridement, scaling in the presence of gingival inflammation, scaling and root planing, periodontal maintenance, polishing, and flossing. Obtains and documents vital signs, blood glucose levels, oral pH, salivary flow measurements, and other screenings as indicated by clinic policy and procedures. Maintains accurate, timely, and complete documentation in Epic and related electronic health record systems, including dental histories, treatment plans, procedures, referrals, consultations, prescriptions, and patient communications. Takes, processes, and evaluates dental radiographs; collaborates with the dentist regarding diagnostic findings and additional imaging needs. Refers patients to dentists or specialists for treatment beyond the scope of dental hygiene practice. Applies fluoride treatments, sealants, and caries-arresting medicaments as indicated. Takes impressions and prepares study models as needed. Demonstrates knowledge of documentation, coding, billing, and compliance best practices. Manages resources responsibly and supports fiscally sound clinical operations. Records and reports pertinent observations and patient reactions to dental staff. Documents laboratory procedures and follows up on results as appropriate. Educates patients and families regarding oral hygiene, caries prevention, periodontal disease prevention, and other oral health topics. Cleans, sterilizes, and maintains instruments and equipment in compliance with infection control standards. Participates in Behavioral Oral Health Integration (BOHI), Medical Dental Integration (MDI), Patient-Centered Medical Home (PCMH), and Culturally and Linguistically Appropriate Services (CLAS) initiatives. Collects and reports data for grant, quality improvement, and performance measurement activities. Participates in quality improvement initiatives, chart audits, regulatory compliance activities, and accreditation processes. Orients dental doctoral students, dental assistant students, and dental hygiene students as assigned. Assists with inventory management, ordering, and maintenance of dental equipment and supplies. Collaborates with the multidisciplinary team, utilizing key performance indicators to support innovative and cost-effective changes to practice. Ensures compliance with University, College, professional, HIPAA, OSHA, and other applicable regulatory requirements. Participates in provider and staff recruitment, credentialing activities, and departmental meetings as requested. Serves as a professional role model and supports the mission, vision, values, and strategic goals of Sheridan Health Services and the University of Colorado. This description is a summary only and describes the general level of work being performed; it is not intended to be all-inclusive. The duties of this position may change from time to time and/or based on business need. We reserve the right to add or delete duties and responsibilities at the discretion of the supervisor and/or hiring authority. Work Location: On-site - Sheridan Health Services , 3525 W. Oxford Avenue, Unit G1, Denver, CO 80236. This position provides care at the primary location and in community settings, with travel to community outreach locations as required. Why Join Us: CU Nursing is an amazing place to be. We have the distinct advantage of being a part of a huge medical campus with three incredible hospitals – the VA, the nationally ranked University of Colorado Hospital, and the Children’s Hospital Colorado where our nursing students and faculty learn every day. From our beginning 125 years ago as part of the School of Medicine at CU Boulder to our current home at the Anschutz Medical Campus, the college has been a recognized leader in nursing education (ranked #10 in online MS graduate programs by U.S. News & World Report 2023). Our faculty, students, and staff have been instrumental in shaping the profession of nursing and teaching the next generation of nurses while treating patients in our own nurse-led clinics. Be a part of an innovative, dynamic, diverse, and exciting workplace -- helping make great things happen. Join us in our quest to boldly transform health together. Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation, and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package, including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 15/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced-rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Graduate of an accredited Dental Hygiene program. Current, unrestricted Colorado Dental Hygienist license or eligibility to obtain licensure by date of hire. Current BLS/CPR certification or ability to obtain by date of hire. Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Preferred Qualifications: One (1) year of clinical dental hygiene experience. Experience in a community health center, public health, academic, or integrated healthcare setting. Experience with Epic Wisdom or similar electronic health record systems. Conversational Spanish/English bilingual proficiency in a clinical setting. Experience working with diverse and underserved populations. Experience teaching, precepting, or mentoring healthcare students. Conditions of Employment: Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without requiring sponsorship. We are unable to provide work visa sponsorship or employment authorization for this position now or in the future. Must participate in health plan credentialing and contracting activities as required. Must remain credentialed with health plans accepted by Sheridan Health Services. Must comply with University, College, SHS, and professional policies and procedures. Must be able to work in a clinical environment with exposure to biological hazards and infectious diseases. Must be willing and able to travel to community outreach locations as required. Must be willing and able to obtain and maintain a Colorado Dental Hygienist license by the date of hire. Must be willing and able to obtain and maintain a valid NPI number by the date of hire. Must be willing and able to obtain and maintain valid Colorado Medicaid Provider enrollment by the date of hire. Must be willing and able to complete and maintain CAQH credentialing by the date of hire. Must be willing and able to actively participate in health plan contracts. Must be willing and able to treat both adult and pediatric populations. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Ability to exercise sound clinical judgment and prioritize competing patient and organizational needs. Strong interpersonal, communication, and patient education skills. Ability to work effectively both independently and as part of an interdisciplinary healthcare team. Ability to manage schedules and maintain productivity expectations, including a full clinic schedule. Proficiency with electronic health record systems and related technologies. Strong organizational, analytical, problem-solving, and time-management skills. Demonstrated leadership, professionalism, reliability, and accountability. Commitment to HIPAA compliance, patient confidentiality, and ethical practice. Strong adherence to OSHA guidelines and dedication to safety in the workplace. Commitment to clinical excellence, operational effectiveness, and continuous quality improvement. Comprehensive knowledge of dental materials and equipment, their use, maintenance, and storage. Highly responsible, reliable, and courteous. How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to the listed job qualifications and interest in the position Curriculum vitae / Resume Questions should be directed to: College of Nursing Human Resources at CON.HR@ucdenver.edu or 303.724.4447 Screening of Applications Begins: Applications will be accepted until finalists are identified, but preference will be given to complete applications received within two (2) weeks of the posting date. Those who do not apply by this date may or may not be considered. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as $65,376 to $70,612.80 . The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position may be eligible for overtime compensation, depending on the level. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans, and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@cuanschutz.edu . Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students, and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine-preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety-sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41452&lang=en": {
      "title": "IT Data Analytics Manager",
      "description": "Closing Date: 10/31/2026 Posted Date: Oct 16, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: SOM-EM MED CLINICAL Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Department: Emergency Medicine Job Title: IT Data Analytics Manager Position #:00809331 – Requisition #: 41452 Job Summary: The IT Data Analytics Manager for the Department of Emergency Medicine is responsible for planning, organizing and managing business analytics, process improvement and project management activities while ensuring compliance with all internal and external policies and procedures of the department and UC Health. The It Data Analytics Manager is also responsible for the day-to-day operations of the data analytics team and supervising the professional and support staff of this departmental function. Working closely with the Associate Vice Chair of Clinical Operations and other clinical informatics leadership in the department and organization, this role will deliver information insights (dashboards, reports, etc.) that support clinical decision making, process improvement, strategic decisions and foster a “Data Driven” culture. Key Responsibilities: Data Analytics Strategy & Implementation – 50% Own and mature a Data Analytics Strategy that aligns to our Vision and Mission, and which drives the utilization of analytics throughout a variety of UCHealth and University of Colorado Emergency Department areas, including: Emergency Department Service Line Urgent Care Service Line Virtual Urgent Care Service Line University of Colorado Emergency Department Implement practices that maintain a high level of engagement between our stakeholders and analysts across Colorado. This includes maintaining a deep, and sometimes localized, understanding of clinical process flows and metrics. Lead or participate in initiatives that provide relevant and timely data, strengthen trust, and keep our services at the forefront of our stakeholder’s minds. Drive data governance best practices to assure our data is as relevant and as accurate as possible, including with AI practices. Ensure a high degree of data ownership and control for all related data. Data Analytics Team Supervision and Mentorship – 20% Directly manage, mentor, coach, and develop the talent of the Team. Partner with stakeholders to ensure analytics are relevant, timely and empower teams to make data-driven decisions. Responsible for the quality, direction and outcomes of the Team’s work. Project Management & Process Improvement – 30% Manage the Project Request Process and Project Delivery Framework to assure all work meets or exceeds expectations, is completed on time and with the highest quality. Maintain clear and frequent communications with all project stakeholders. Work directly with stakeholders on future projects. Continuously evaluate future trends in analytics to assure the best, most relevant advancements are evaluated and utilized. Utilize our EHR (Epic), as well as outside sources of information, to enrich the value and usefulness of our analytics. Work with various partners for best-in-class architecture, design and evolution of data needs. At times, you will be required to act in the role of an individual contributor in pulling reports, building dashboards, analyzing data and providing insights to stakeholders. Manage project implementation to achieve project goals while controlling risks, conflicts, timelines and costs. Provide administrative support, short and long term planning, program implementation, reporting and coordination of integration efforts. Assess new integration processes to enable business success. Recommend prioritization of projects and the project portfolio as they relate to the installation of integration efforts. Maintain records of all master agreements, operational business documents and system integration processes as requested/needed. Conduct needs assessment, planning, implementation, evaluation and sustainment of change to meet organizational business objectives. Work closely with key stakeholders to identify, evaluate and operationalize opportunities for process improvements and associated revenue cycle improvements and/or cost savings. Support and help to lead process improvement teams servicing primarily across UC Health – ED Service line. Focus on using AI to optimize workflow processes, and communication and partnership within teams. Monitor and improve patient flow processes, hand-offs, and care coordination. Manage process initiatives including, but not limited to process mapping, process design/re-design, and process improvement. Create and collaborate with teams to maintain dashboards, communication and strategy to increase effectiveness and sustainability of improvements. Work Location: Hybrid – this role is eligible for a hybrid schedule of 3 days per week on campus and as needed for in-person meetings. Remote – this role is eligible to work remotely, but the employee must be in the United States. Why Join Us: The Department of Emergency Medicine at the University of Colorado School of Medicine is dedicated to delivering superlative patient care, providing an environment where training and education thrive and innovation and discovery are fostered. The Department of Emergency Medicine is based at the Anschutz Medical Campus in Aurora Colorado. The campus is a state of the art medical campus home to the University of Colorado Schools of Medicine, Nursing, Dentistry, Pharmacy, the Colorado School of Public Health; as well as the University of Colorado Hospital and Children's Hospital Colorado both of which serve as major training sites for the Denver Health Residency in Emergency Medicine. Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 15/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree in computer science, management/computer information systems, computer engineering, information technology, or a directly related field from an accredited institution and 4-6 years of professional experience in IT analytics and management. A combination of education and related technical/military/paraprofessional experience may be substituted for a bachelor’s degree on a year for year basis. An advanced degree (Masters or Doctorate) may be substituted for experience on a year for year basis if the degree is in a field of study directly related to the work assignment. Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Preferred Qualifications: Master’s degree in information technology or data analytics. Progressive professional management and process improvement, process design and process mapping experience. Lean and project management experience and experience facilitating Lean events. Hands-on experience with well-established project management methodologies. Experience in patient care operations. Previous academic medical education institution experience. Ability to operate and manipulate MS Suite, Power BI and AI tools such as Co-Pilot and Chat GPT. Conditions of Employment: Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without requiring sponsorship. We are unable to provide work visa sponsorship or employment authorization for this position now or in the future. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Ability to communicate effectively, both in writing and orally. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with employees at all levels throughout the institution. Outstanding customer service skills. Critical thinking skills, decisive judgement and the ability to work with minimal supervision. Must be able to work in a fast-paced environment and take appropriate action. Strong commitment to teamwork and ability to optimize efforts through collaboration and partnerships. Demonstrate flexibility and responsiveness to change. Strong change management and facilitation skills. How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position (only use if a cover letter is necessary) Curriculum vitae / Resume Three to five professional references, including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Questions should be directed to: EMED Human Resources, emed.humanresources@ucdenver.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Immediately and continues until position is filled. For best consideration, apply by 10/30/26. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as $86,759 - $116,258 The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position may be eligible for overtime compensation, depending on the level. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@cuanschutz.edu ​. Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41451&lang=en": {
      "title": "Fellowship Coordinator",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 16, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: SOM-Pathology Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus Department: Department of Pathology Job Title: Fellowship Coordinator Position #00851492 – Requisition #: 41451 Job Summary: The Department of Pathology is seeking a Fellowship Coordinator who will be responsible for the day ‐ to ‐ day administration of five Fellowship training programs (3 ACGME-accredited, 2 unaccredited). Assist the Program Director in ensuring that the training programs are in full compliance with CUGME Office policies and procedures, as well as relevant institutional policies and procedures, ACGME program requirements and regulations, and relevant professional standards and criteria are met. Assist the Program Director in developing and maintaining the educational quality of the training programs. Key Responsibilities: Administer day‑to‑day operations for five pathology fellowship programs, ensuring compliance with ACGME, CUGME, and institutional policies. Coordinate onboarding, orientation, scheduling, and exit processes for fellows, residents, medical students, and visiting learners. Maintain program data and documentation, including MedHub records, evaluations, rotation schedules, and accreditation requirements. Support Program Directors in monitoring program quality, preparing accreditation materials, and maintaining continuous compliance. Manage fellowship recruitment cycles, including application review, interview scheduling, virtual interview facilitation, and ranking processes. Track fellowship budgets, process expenses, and coordinate with the Business Manager and Program Directors on funding allocations. Assist with planning and executing fellowship events, including graduation and other program activities throughout the year. Other duties as assigned Work Location: Onsite – this role is expected to work onsite and is located in Aurora, CO for initial training with the option to move to a hybrid schedule once the candidate becomes fully operational Why Join Us: Welcome to the Department of Pathology of the University of Colorado, Anschutz Medical Campus. The Department has grown substantially in the past 15 years, from 40 to 120 faculty in parallel with the remarkable growth of our hospital-based affiliates as well as the city and county of Denver. Our work is value driven and focused on scientific investigation, lifelong learning, and a balance of personal and professional values. In addition to a vibrant and highly competitive residency program with 25 positions, we offer 9 fellowships and participate in numerous graduate schools and the MD/PhD program of the CU School of Medicine. Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 15/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Intermediate Bachelor's degree from an accredited institution and 1 year of professional experience with residency and/or fellowship coordination Senior Bachelor's degree from an accredited institution and 2 year of professional experience with residency and/or fellowship program coordination A combination of education and related technical/military/paraprofessional experience may be substituted for a bachelor’s degree on a year for year basis. An advanced degree (Masters or Doctorate) may be substituted for experience on a year for year basis if the degree is in a field of study directly related to the work assignment. Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Preferred Qualifications: Previous experience in a graduate medical education environment and/or previous experience concurrently coordinating multiple Fellowship training programs. Competencies: Ability to communicate effectively, both in writing and orally. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with employees at all levels throughout the institution. Outstanding customer service skills. Conditions of Employment: Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without requiring sponsorship. We are unable to provide work visa sponsorship or employment authorization for this position now or in the future. How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): Curriculum vitae / Resume Three to five professional references, including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Questions should be directed to: Francina Jeelani at Francina.Jeelani@cuanschutz.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Applications will be accepted until finalists are identified, but preference will be given to complete applications received by November 5, 2026. Those who do not apply by this date may or may not be considered. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as: Intermediate : $48,989 to $65,645 Senior : $52,961 to $70,968 The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position may be eligible for overtime compensation, depending on the level. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@cuanschutz.edu ​. Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41450&lang=en": {
      "title": "Entry Laboratory Research Services Professional",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 16, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: SOM-EM MED CLINICAL Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus Department: Department of Emergency Medicine Job Title: Entry Laboratory Research Services Professional Position #:00829509 – Requisition #: 41450 Job Summary: The Department of Emergency Medicine has an opening for an Entry Laboratory Research Services Professional (RSP). This individual will be involved in conducting various research studies in a fast paced, translational neuroscience research laboratory setting in conjunction with multiple grants and contracts related to drug discovery and development aimed at treating ischemic and traumatic brain injury. We are currently seeking a Research Services Professional (RSP) to perform small-animal surgeries and neurobehavioral testing in support of these projects. Specific ongoing projects the applicant will participate in include the effect of age and gender on brain injury following experiment stroke, mild or moderate/severe TBI and the role of novel therapeutic interventions to enhance functional recovery. The candidate should have experience in neuroscience or related research field, and experience working with animal handling and surgeries would be advantageous. Experience with molecular, cellular and microscopy techniques is desirable, but not essential. In addition to experimental responsibilities, this position will have responsibilities that include general laboratory management, database and sample inventory management, assist in managing animal colonies, overseeing equipment maintenance, corresponding with internal and external collaborators, and conducting research. The successful candidate will be self-motivated, detail oriented and have the ability to work independently and collaboratively in a team environment. The position offers an excellent opportunity to gain insights into the pathophysiology of brain injury in the setting of ischemia and traumatic brain injury and support your professional development in a collaborative research environment. Key Responsibilities: 70% - Laboratory research activities Collaborate with and support Principal Investigators (PI) and other stakeholders with laboratory and research functions Perform small animal surgeries and post-operative care Perform molecular, histological and microscopy analyses. Perform behavioral assessments Maintain thorough and accurate lab records Manage animal colonies General lab maintenance duties Participate in all lab meetings Assist team members, Supervisors and/or management with creation and implementation of processes and procedures and quality improvement initiatives Assist with ensuring compliance with applicable laws, rules and regulations; receive guidance and direction or escalate when required 15% - Assay development/troubleshooting Serve as a resource to PIs and other stakeholders 15% - Data analysis and management Support analytical testing process using standard lab support knowledge in the collection and review of conditions, including preserving samples, completing sample preparation, documenting and communicating results Perform pre-analytical, analytical and post analytical test process and evaluate results produced This description is a summary only and is describing the general level of work being performed, it is not intended to be all-inclusive. The duties of this position may change from time to time and/or based on business need. We reserve the right to add or delete duties and responsibilities at the discretion of the supervisor and/or hiring authority. Work Location: Onsite – this role is expected to work onsite and is located in Aurora, Colorado. Why Join Us: The Department of Emergency Medicine at the University of Colorado School of Medicine is dedicated to delivering superlative patient care, providing an environment where training and education thrive and innovation and discovery are fostered. The Department of Emergency Medicine is based at the Anschutz Medical Campus in Aurora Colorado. The campus is a state of the art medical campus home to the University of Colorado Schools of Medicine, Nursing, Dentistry, Pharmacy, the Colorado School of Public Health; as well as the University of Colorado Hospital and Children's Hospital Colorado both of which serve as major training sites for the Denver Health Residency in Emergency Medicine. Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 10/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree in biology, molecular biology, chemistry, genetics or related field A combination of education and related technical/military/paraprofessional experience may be substituted for a bachelor’s degree on a year for year basis. Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Preferred Qualifications: Master’s degree in biology, molecular biology, chemistry, genetics or related field 2-3 years prior experience or background within an experimental or wet laboratory Prior experience with immunohistology and microscopy techniques. Prior experience with lab management responsibilities. Conditions of Employment: Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without requiring sponsorship. We are unable to provide work visa sponsorship or employment authorization for this position now or in the future. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Knowledge of basic laboratory techniques including safety procedures and techniques Ability to communicate effectively, both in writing and orally Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with employees at all levels throughout the institution Outstanding customer service skills Knowledge of basic human anatomy, physiology medical terminology Ability to interpret and master complex research protocol information How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position Curriculum vitae / Resume Three to five professional references, including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Questions should be directed to: EMED Human Resources emed.humanresources@ucdenver.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Immediately and continues until position is filled. For best consideration, apply by 10/30/26. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as HIRING RANGE $47,811 - $64,067 The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position may be eligible for overtime compensation, depending on the level. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@cuanschutz.edu ​. Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41197&lang=en": {
      "title": "Instructor – Nurse Practitioner/Physician Assistant",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 16, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: SOM-MED Hemo-Thrombosis Ctr Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Department: Hemophilia & Thrombosis Center Job Title: Instructor – Nurse Practitioner/Physician Assistant Position #: 00853048 – Requisition #:41197 Job Summary: The Hemophilia and Thrombosis Center is an interdisciplinary clinical and research program for children adults with bleeding or clotting disorders. The person in this position has primary responsibility to implement the clinical care, case management and program coordination for patients with bleeding and clotting disorders. The position is 1.0 FTE. Key Responsibilities: · Provide comprehensive clinical care to hemophilia, thrombosis, and stroke patients, including patient assessment, diagnosis, treatment planning, and follow-up. · Conduct patient evaluations , including medical histories, physical examinations, clinical trial assessments, and review of diagnostic laboratory tests and imaging. · Develop and manage individualized patient care plans based on clinical findings, medical history, and established clinical care guidelines. · Collaborate with multidisciplinary teams including physicians, pharmacists, physical therapists, social workers, and other specialists to coordinate and optimize patient care. · Provide patient and family education and support , including self-care instructions, phone triage, and education related to hemophilia, thrombosis, and thrombophilia. · Maintain accurate clinical documentation and patient data , including proficiency with EPIC and supporting data quality assurance and clinical program requirements. · Participate in HTC outreach and professional activities , including regional and national meetings, remote clinics, camps, education days, community events, and in-service training for healthcare staff and students. Work Location: Onsite – this role is expected to work onsite and is located in Aurora, CO Why Join Us: Joining the University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus offers the chance to work in a dynamic, innovative environment. Our campus is renowned for its cutting-edge research, state-of-the-art facilities, and commitment to advancing healthcare. As part of our team, you will enjoy opportunities for professional development, access to world-class resources, and a supportive, collaborative culture Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year (based on percentage of time) Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 11/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Current Certification as Nurse Practitioner or Physician Assistant Colorado License with prescriptive writing capability Preferred Qualifications: · Two (2) or more years of general clinical experience. · Two (2) or more years of hematology clinical experience. · Experience with clinical research. Familiar with point of care ultrasound Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: · Skills in working in a collaborative, multidisciplinary environment with a medical, psychosocial and administrative team to facilitate and develop patient treatment plans. · Experienced caring for both pediatric and adult populations. · Working knowledge of caring for patients with chronic conditions. · Professional demeanor and experience that demonstrates problem solving skills and the ability to manage multiple tasks and work independently with minimal supervision. · Excellent organizational, written and verbal communication skills with the ability to take direction. · Applicants will possess the qualities of being detail-oriented, self-motivated and a fast learner with good time management skills. · Proficient in electronic medical records systems. Conditions of Employment: · Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without requiring sponsorship. We are unable to provide work visa sponsorship or employment authorization for this position now or in the future. How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): 1. A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position 2. Curriculum vitae / Resume 3. Five professional references including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers . Questions should be directed to: julie.smith@cuanschutz.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Applications will be accepted until finalists are identified, but preference will be given to complete applications received by 11/16/2026 . Those who do not apply by this date may or may not be considered. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as HIRING RANGE: $97,000-112,000. The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation unless it is non-exempt. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: The University of Colorado (CU) is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@ucdenver.edu ​. Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41554&lang=en": {
      "title": "Bioinformaticist - Research Scientist",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 28, 2026 Job category: Research Faculty Department: SOM-OP GENERAL OPERATIONS Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Department: Ophthalmology Job Title: Research Scientist Position #00853944 – Requisition #41554 Job Summary: This Lead Bioinformatician will provide scientific and technical analysis for a growing translational biorepository focused on identifying biomarkers of disease subtype and treatment response. The position will lead the development and implementation of reproducible analytical workflows integrating high-dimensional immunologic, proteomic, genomic, and clinical datasets. Initial work will be heavily focused on the biorepository’s multi-omic data, including PhIP-Seq, high-dimensional cytometry, plasma proteomics, clinical phenotypes, and integration with whole-genome sequencing results generated by collaborating analysts. This role will help shape the analytical scope and long-term data strategy of the biorepository, establish reusable data and computational infrastructure, and support its continued growth in size and scientific scope. The position will also support additional collaborative projects involving single-cell RNA sequencing, spatial transcriptomics, and other emerging multi-omic technologies. The successful candidate will work closely with clinical investigators, laboratory scientists, statisticians, geneticists, and other computational collaborators to define research questions, develop analysis plans, interpret biological findings, and communicate results. The position will provide technical leadership, code review, training, and mentorship to approximately one to three analysts or trainees. Key Responsibilities : Multi-Omic Research and Analysis 65% Lead analysis and integration of PhIP-Seq, CYTOF, affinity-based and mass-spectrometry proteomics, clinical data, and externally analyzed WGS results. Develop analysis plans addressing biomarkers of disease subtype, prognosis, and treatment response. Apply and evaluate multi-omic methods including CCA, MOFA and related latent-factor models, WGCNA, pseudobulk analysis, cell-state and cell–cell communication analysis, and predictive modeling. Lead secondary projects involving single-cell RNA sequencing and spatial transcriptomics. Perform raw-data processing, quality assessment, normalization, statistical analysis, biological interpretation, and visualization. Work with investigators to refine research questions, assess feasibility, select appropriate methods, estimate timelines, and communicate analytical limitations. Prepare publication-quality figures and contribute to manuscripts, abstracts, presentations, and grant applications. Serve as a coauthor on collaborative work, with opportunities to lead analytically focused manuscripts. Data Infrastructure, Reproducibility, and Governance 25% Design a reusable analytical and data infrastructure that supports continued expansion of the biorepository. Develop, validate, document, and maintain reproducible computational pipelines using workflow-management systems Work in high-performance computing and cloud-computing environments. Develop and maintain data dictionaries, metadata standards, sample identifiers, provenance records, analysis documentation, and quality-control procedures. Harmonize clinical, laboratory, and multi-omic datasets across projects and collection periods. Establish standards for code quality, versioning, documentation, archiving, and reproducible reporting. Technical Leadership, Mentoring, and Collaboration 10% Provide technical guidance, code review, training, and mentorship to one to three junior analysts, trainees, or research staff. Teach best practices in bioinformatics, statistical analysis, reproducible research, data management, and scientific visualization. Promote consistent analytical standards across projects. Participate in project meetings and communicate findings to both computational and non-computational collaborators. Help prioritize analytical requests and support effective management of multiple concurrent projects. Approximately 90% of the roles’s initial work will support the biorepository , with the portfolio expected to broaden over the first two to three years. Work Location: Hybrid – this role is eligible for a hybrid schedule of 3 days per week on campus and as needed for in-person meetings. Why Join Us: Our department’s home to the Sue Anschutz Rodgers Eye Center on the Anschutz Medical Campus. This state-of-the-art facility is one of the largest eye centers in the country and serves not only patients in the Rocky Mountain region but also patients all over the world. The technological innovations conceived and developed by Departmental faculty have changed the practice of eye care throughout the world. Our educational programs train the next generation of leaders in ophthalmology. Our specialists have developed national and international reputations for excellence in routine and complex ophthalmic care. We have invested heavily in tracking our clinical outcomes and we are proud that our clinicians perform at the highest levels in their respective fields. Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year (based on percentage of time) Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 11/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Masters degree in bioinformatics, computational biology, biostatistics, or data science.. Four years of professional or research experience conducting bioinformatic or computational analyses, including substantial independent responsibility for study analysis and interpretation. Demonstrated experience with complex analyses involving multiple biological data modalities. Demonstrated proficiency in multiple coding languages, including R and Python. Experience developing reproducible bioinformatic workflows and using version control. Experience performing quality control, statistical analysis, visualization, and biological interpretation of high-dimensional biomedical data. Experience collaborating with both computational and non-computational investigators. Experience independently organizing work, managing timelines, and contributing to multiple concurrent research projects. Preferred Qualifications: Masters degree in bioinformatics, computational biology, biostatistics, or data science. Five or more years of relevant bioinformatics or computational research experience. Experience leading collaborative projects. Demonstrated experience integrating three or more omics or high-dimensional data types. Experience analyzing the following: single-cell RNA sequencing; spatial transcriptomics; affinity-based proteomics; mass-spectrometry proteomics; high-dimensional cytometry; PhIP-Seq or other serologic assays; germline genomic data; longitudinal clinical or treatment-response data. Experience with CCA, MOFA or related latent-factor methods, WGCNA, pseudobulk analysis, cell–cell communication analysis, and predictive modeling. Experience with Nextflow, Snakemake, or comparable workflow-management systems. Experience using containers such as Docker, Singularity, or Apptainer. Experience with HPC and/or cloud-computing environments. Experience designing metadata standards, harmonizing data across studies, or developing reusable research data infrastructure. Publication record demonstrating substantive contributions to biomedical data analysis. Experience contributing analytical sections to grant applications. Experience training or mentoring analysts, students, or research staff. Experience in immunology, translational research, autoimmune or inflammatory disease, ophthalmology, or biomarker discovery. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Advanced knowledge of statistical and computational principles relevant to multi-omic biomedical research. Ability to independently evaluate complex research questions and recommend rigorous analytical approaches. Ability to distinguish exploratory, confirmatory, and predictive analyses and communicate the limitations of each. Strong programming, data-management, troubleshooting, and scientific-visualization skills. Commitment to reproducibility, transparency, documentation, and code quality. Ability to translate complex analytical results for clinicians, laboratory scientists, trainees, and other stakeholders. Ability to work independently while contributing effectively within multidisciplinary teams. Strong organizational, project-management, and time-management skills. Ability to balance multiple projects, identify dependencies, communicate delays or risks, and establish realistic timelines. Ability to provide constructive technical feedback and mentorship without formal supervisory authority. Scientific curiosity and willingness to evaluate new analytical approaches as technologies and research questions evolve. How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): 1. A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position 2. Curriculum vitae / Resume 3. Five professional references including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers . Questions should be directed to: Ashley Woodhouse Ashley.woodhouse@cuanschutz.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Applications will be accepted until finalists are identified, but preference will be given to complete applications received by November 13, 2026 . Those who do not apply by this date may or may not be considered. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as HIRING RANGE: $90,000 - $105,000 The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation unless it is non-exempt. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: The University of Colorado (CU) is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@ucdenver.edu ​. Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
