    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41557&lang=en": {
      "title": "Advanced Practice Provider (APP) (PA/NP/APRN) Department of Surgery, Division of Urology - Instructor",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 28, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: SOM-SRG-UR DIV Clinical Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Department: Department of Surgery, Division of Urology Job Title: Advanced Practice Provider Position #:00854170 – Requisition #:41557 Job Summary: The Department of Surgery, Division of Urology is seeking applicants for a full-time (1.0) FTE Advanced Practice Provider (Nurse Practitioner or Physician Assistant) at the rank of Instructor to carry out duties related to patient care on the Urology Service. These duties include outpatient assessment, patient education, care coordination and disease management as well as the provision of urologic consultation to other services. Close collaboration with the surgeons, faculty across sites may be necessary. This position will serve as an integral part of the Urology South Denver team providing care to a general patient population while on the Urology Service and during all transitions of care. This position will primarily serve outpatient population but will be expected to serve the Urology inpatient population as needed. This position will be based at the University of Colorado - Highlands Ranch Medical Center. Key Responsibilities: Specific duties and responsibilities of the APP may include, but are not limited to the following: Evaluate and manage patients who are candidates for Urology care and/or surgery. This includes obtaining a thorough history and performing an appropriate physical examination and ordering appropriate testing as well as management of patients with post-operative complications. Monitoring overall care and providing education about the risks and benefits of the surgical procedures is also expected. See and evaluate patients in an outpatient setting, provide documentation, an assessment and care plan for outpatient. Evaluate and manage patients with urgent or emergent complaints in conjunction with the primary surgery. These duties will include outpatient such as patient assessment, patient education, care coordination and disease management. Triage patient telephone calls and emails and provide consultation. Provide monitoring and continuity of care for patients between physician visits. Attend required meetings and participate in committees as requested. Support and uphold established organizational policies, procedures, objective related to quality improvement, safety, environmental, and infection control. Provide urologic outpatient and inpatient consultation in collaboration with faculty member and residents. Participates in performance improvement activities; quality improvement and patient safety activities; assists in maintaining compliance with Joint Commission accreditation and other internal and external regulatory standards including the code of conduct. Work Location: Onsite – this role is expected to work onsite and is located in Highlands Ranch, Colorado. Why Join Us: We are driven to improve every life at the Department of Surgery with our commitment to innovative surgical care, curing through discovery, enlightening tomorrow’s leaders, and daring to be exceptional. Our focus on patient care, education, and research will lead to innovative discoveries and promote quality care and safety for our patients. Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year (based on percentage of time) Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 11/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Graduate of an accredited school of nursing with a Bachelor’s Degree in Nursing. Masters degree in Nursing required, or a graduate of an accredited Physician Assistant school. Current license to practice as an Advanced Practice Nurse/ Physician Assistant with prescriptive privileges. Meets and maintains the requirements of the Nursing Credential Review Board for the Advanced Practice Nurse/ Physician Assistant. Preferred Qualifications: One year prior experience in surgical subspecialty or outpatient care. Previous experience in urologic clinical setting. Demonstrated skill in outpatient surgical care. One year experience as an APP Conditions of Employment: · Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without requiring sponsorship. We are unable to provide work visa sponsorship or employment authorization for this position now or in the future. How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): 1. A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position 2. Curriculum vitae / Resume 3. Five professional references including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers . Questions should be directed to: Jacky Bonds, Jacky.bonds@cuanschutz.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Immediately and continues until position is filled. For best consideration, apply by November 12, 2026. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as HIRING RANGE: $111,010-$136,947 The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation unless it is non-exempt. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: The University of Colorado (CU) is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@ucdenver.edu ​. Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41556&lang=en": {
      "title": "Surgical Pathology Medical Records Specialist (Medical Records Technician I, II, III )",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 28, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: SOM-Pathology Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus Department: Pathology Surgical Pathology Medical Records Specialist ( Medical Records Technician I, II, III ) Position #: 00795567 – Requisition #: 41556 Job Summary: The CU Anschutz, Department of Pathology is excited to recruit two (2) Surgical Pathology Medical Records Specialists. This position will provide medical records services to the Surgical Pathology Laboratory, a CLIA and CAP approved clinical laboratory. The Surgical Pathology Laboratory is dedicated to providing complete gross and microscopic examinations for all specimens and tissues submitted by the physicians of University Hospital and Clinics. Surgical Pathology subspecialties include: Bone and Soft Tissue Pathology. Breast Pathology. Cardiovascular Pathology. Dermatopathology. Head and Neck (ENT) Gastrointestinal Pathology. Genitourinary Pathology. Gynecologic Pathology. Key Responsibilities: 30% Specimen referral coordination: Procures patient slides, blocks, reports and insurance information from outside institutions based on clinical orders for testing, including, but not limited to faxing requests for above materials and performing phone follow-up for timely receipt of specimens Procures patient slide and blocks from internal archives on clinical orders or research requests, using proper laboratory procedures for documentation Procures patient slide, blocks, reports and insurance information for release to internal and outside institutions based on clinical orders for testing, including, but not limited to preparing and releasing of above material via Fed Ex, UPS or other courier services. Optimization and improvements of workflow related material procurement for both clinical and research material. 30% Accession specimens Performs required training on, and demonstrated proficiency with SIMPL, CoPath and EPIC Performs routine specimen accessioning for the laboratory, which includes but not limited to entering patient information, insurance information, clinical and research testing information. 15% Provide customer service for the laboratory, including but not limited to: Answers phones to respond to queries regarding new testing, in progress testing, or previously performed testing E-mail based communication with clinicians, nurses, and others as needed Faxes final results 10% Data entry into clinical reports Performs manual entry of molecular results into SIMPL, CoPath and EPIC for pathologist review and sign out. Optimization and improvements of SOPs and workflow in regards to Molecular result entry into SIMPL, CoPath and EPIC. Performs required training on, and demonstrated proficiency with SIMPL, CoPath and EPIC 5% Obtain insurance pre-authorization Initiates pre-authorization procedures and will be responsible for contacting insurance companies to verify patient coverage, potential costs and if specific tests are covered by insurance; on behalf of individual patients 5% Administrative case finalization Will be involved in all necessary components of post-case administrative finalization, including initiating the return of all slides and blocks to originating institutions, completion of billing documentation for insurance coders and pathologist signature, scanning of final reports for archives 5% Filing of documentation and pathology materials in a timely matter. Work Location: Onsite – this role is expected to work onsite and is located in Aurora, CO. Why Join Us: Welcome to the Department of Pathology of the University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus. The Department has grown substantially in the past 15 years, from 40 to 120 faculty in parallel with the remarkable growth of our hospital-based affiliates as well as the city and county of Denver. Our work is value driven and focused on scientific investigation, lifelong learning and a balance of personal and professional values. In addition to a vibrant and highly competitive residency program with 25 positions, we offer 9 fellowships and participate in numerous graduate school and the MD/PhD program of the CU School of Medicine. The University of Colorado offers a comprehensive benefits package that includes health insurance, life insurance, retirement plans, tuition benefits, ECO pass, paid time off – vacation, sick, and holidays and more. To see what benefits are available, please visit: https://www.cu.edu/employee-services/benefits-wellness . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Medical Records Tech I A combination of related education, certification, and/or relevant experience in an occupation related to the work assigned equal to one (1) year Medical Records Tech II A combination of related education, certification, and/or relevant experience in an occupation related to the work assigned equal to two (2) years Medical Records Tech III A combination of related education, certification, and/or relevant experience in an occupation related to the work assigned equal to three (3) years Certification related to the work assigned to the position will substitute for 2 (two) years of the required experience Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Preferred Qualifications: Associates or Bachelor’s degree in business administration, accounting, finance, or related field Two (2) years’ of experience in an administrative role Experience calculating lab results and data using math and analytical skills Experience using MS Word and Excel. Preferred experience will include developing reports, spreadsheets, and databases using the mentioned software programs Experience entering data into an electronic system other than MS Office products Familiarity with medical terminology, human anatomy, and physiology Experience purchasing and maintaining lab supplies Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Ability to identify and then analyze problems, as well as possess the ability to interpret applied rules and regulations in order to develop and implement solutions to those issues. Work independently, and administer judgment and sensitivity to the business issues and campus culture. Strong interpersonal skills and the ability to establish rapport with persons of diverse backgrounds. Detail oriented, self-motivated, a fast learner and possess excellent organizational, written and verbal communication skills. Ability to communicate effectively with medical, professional, administrative and other personnel, to effectively present information both orally and in written form. How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): Curriculum vitae / Resume Three to five professional references, including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Questions should be directed to: PathHR at PathHR@cuanschutz.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Applications will be accepted until finalists are identified, but preference will be given to complete applications received by November 30, 2026. Those who do not apply by this date may or may not be considered. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as Medical Records Tech I : $39,520 - $45,996 Medical Records Tech II: $53,940 - $64,704 Medical Records Tech III: $59,460 - $71,352 The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position may be eligible for overtime compensation, depending on the level. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 ADA Statement: Equal Opportunity Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@cuanschutz.edu ​. CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41555&lang=en": {
      "title": "Instructor/ MST Expert",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 28, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: SOM-PEDS Kempe-GenOps Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Department: Pediatrics, Kempe Center Job Title: Instructor, MST Expert Position #: 00 688355 – Requisition #:41555 Job Summary: The Rocky Mountain Multisystemic Therapy (MST) Network at the Kempe Center is seeking a Multisystemic Therapy (MST) Expert to join our team and make a meaningful impact on the lives of youth and families. This exciting opportunity allows you to play a critical role in expanding access to evidence-based treatment by supporting community-based MST programs in delivering high-quality, effective services. As an MST Expert, you will work directly with an MST coach and MST Co-Director(s) to provide specialized training, consultation, and guidance to MST therapists, supervisors, and agency leadership, helping strengthen clinical practices, improve program outcomes, and support the successful implementation and sustainability of the MST model. In this role, you will collaborate with a dedicated team of MST professionals to support approximately 8–10 community-based MST programs through weekly consultation, ongoing training, and clinical and organizational guidance, partnering with community agencies to address organizational and systems-level challenges and strengthen program effectiveness. With opportunities to work remotely and travel as needed, this position may involve supporting MST partner sites in states such as Colorado, New Mexico, Arizona, Texas, and Washington. The role offers a unique combination of flexibility, professional growth, collaboration, and the opportunity to create lasting positive change for youth, families, and communities. Key Responsibilities: · Provide weekly clinical consultation for up to 10 MST teams, supporting therapists and supervisors in effectively implementing and maintaining fidelity to the MST treatment model. · Provide ongoing training, coaching, and professional development to MST therapists and supervisors, including facilitating portions of MST Orientation Trainings, Advanced Supervisor Workshops, and quarterly booster trainings. · Lead and participate in quality assurance and quality improvement activities, including Program Implementation Reviews (PIRs), to assess program performance, identify areas for improvement, and develop strategies to strengthen clinical outcomes and program effectiveness. · Collaborate with MST supervisors, agency leadership, and community stakeholders to identify and address organizational, clinical, and systems-level challenges that impact successful MST implementation and long-term program sustainability. · Assess ongoing training and development needs of MST teams, develop and document individualized development plans, and provide resources and guidance on research-supported interventions. · Work closely with MST Coach, MST Co-Directors, the Network Partner Director, and community agency partners to coordinate program support, share expertise, and provide consultation coverage for other MST Experts as needed. · Maintain expert knowledge of MST principles, practices, and quality standards through ongoing professional development and consultation. · Support MST programs through remote collaboration and travel approximately 35%–50% of work time, as required. Work Location: Remote – this role is eligible to work remotely, but the employee must be in the United States. Why Join Us: The Kempe Center was the first academic center in the U.S. to focus on the prevention and treatment of child maltreatment. For the past 50+ years, Kempe has promoted understanding, knowledge, and best practices to prevent and treat child abuse and neglect globally. Today we honor our legacy while looking ahead for ways to transform our field. It is our mission to improve the well-being of children and families. Through our work, we strengthen families, communities and the systems that serve them. We believe that abuse and neglect are preventable, and people are resilient. We are curious. We take a stand. We test assumptions. Our leadership in advocacy, research, education, and clinical work drives innovative strategies that transform the field. We are a catalyst, connecting people, information, and best practices to translate knowledge into action. Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year (based on percentage of time) Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 11/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. · Master's degree in psychology, social work, counseling, or related field · One (1) year of professional experience serving as an MST supervisor and/or MST Expert Condition of Employment: · Must be willing and able to pass a national criminal background check Preferred Qualifications: · 2 years of professional experience as an MST supervisor and/or MST Expert · 1 year of professional experience delivering trainings, workshops, or presentations to professional audiences · 5 years of experience providing home- and/or community-based clinical services using systemic approaches to treatment Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: · Clinical competence in family therapy, behavior therapy, and child development · The MST Expert will be expected to perform with self-disciplined independence in an environment of ongoing accountability · Strong leadership skills, approaches work with integrity and open to continuous learning · Familiarity with research literature on the causes, correlations, and treatments of delinquency desirable · Demonstrated knowledge and ability to effectively engage individuals and families from across varied cultural, socioeconomic, and geographic backgrounds · Excellent interpersonal skills as well as excellent verbal and written communication skills required · Ability to thrive in a team-based environment How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): 1. A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position 2. Curriculum vitae / Resume 3. Five professional references including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers . Questions should be directed to: Michele Bugos at michele.bugos@cuanschutz.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Immediately and continues until position is filled. For best consideration, apply by November 30, 2026. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range (or hiring range) for this position has been established as HIRING RANGE: $75,000 to $85,000 The above salary range (or hiring range) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation unless it is non-exempt. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Equal Opportunity Statement: The University of Colorado (CU) is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@ucdenver.edu ​. Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41553&lang=en": {
      "title": "Post-Doctoral Fellow",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 28, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: SOM-PHYS GENERAL OPERATIONS Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Department: Physiology and Biophysics Job Title: Post-Doctoral Fellow Position #00854142 – Requisition #41553 Job Summary: The Eissa lab is seeking to hire a postdoctoral fellow. The position will focus on the collection, analysis, and modeling of intracranial neural recordings from epilepsy patients performing cognitive tasks. The lab is located within the University of Colorado School of Medicine Department of Physiology & Biophysics and the Aurora/Denver Anschutz Medical campus. Postdoctoral fellows will benefit from a multidisciplinary, vibrant, open, and collegial department. The Eissa lab provides rich opportunities to interact with other biophysics and physiology laboratories within the department, also with an even larger collection of computational and translational neuroscience laboratories. Key Responsibilities: Develop pipeline for collecting and processing intracranial recordings across multiple institutions Run behavioral tasks with patients Data analysis and modeling Oral communication of preliminary results at lab meetings Oral and written communication of completed work at national or international meetings. Create figures and write papers Collaborate with and support Principal Investigators (PI) and other stakeholders with laboratory and research functions Independently and creatively identify laboratory solutions Independently review, develop and implement new or modified laboratory techniques required for research projects Provide laboratory science expertise and leadership in study design, study oversight, data management, data analysis and manuscript preparation to assist all levels of investigators, researchers and clinicians on new research activities across a wide range of disciplines Work Location: Onsite – this role is expected to work onsite and is located in Aurora, CO. Why Join Us: Dr. Tahra Eissa’s laboratory is part of the Department of Physiology and Biophysics at the University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus School of Medicine, which is known for its highly collaborative environment with many opportunities to interact with other sensory systems, behavior and decision making, and computational neuroscience groups. Why work for the University? The University of Colorado offers a comprehensive benefits package. To see what benefits are available for Post-Doctoral Fellows, please visit: · Payroll & Benefits Orientation for Post-Doctoral Fellows | University of Colorado (cu.edu) · benefits guide cover-post-doc-2024 (cu.edu) Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Ph.D. in neuroscience, computer science, or a closely related field A record of first-author publications in high-caliber field journal. Experience in the field of physiology, neuroscience, physics, computer science, or biology Preferred Qualifications: Two (2) – Three (3) years of prior experience in a computational neuroscience or systems neuroscience lab Experience in coding, electrophysiology (human intracranial preferred), behavioral quantification and modeling, Bayesian inference approaches, neural network modeling, signal, and grant or protocol application and management. Experience with research design, development of research hypotheses, collaborative multi-site research. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Advanced knowledge of laboratory techniques including safety procedures and techniques Ability to communicate effectively, both in writing and orally Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with employees at all levels throughout the institution Ability to interpret and master complex research protocol information Knowledge of computational and systems neuroscience How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): 1. A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position 2. Curriculum vitae / Resume 3. Three professional references, including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers . Questions should be directed to: Tahra Eissa, Tahra.Eissa@cuanschutz.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Applications will be accepted until finalists are identified, but preference will be given to complete applications received by December 1, 2026 . Those who do not apply by this date may or may not be considered. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as $65,000 - $70,000/year FT The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation unless it is non-exempt. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: The University of Colorado (CU) is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@ucdenver.edu ​. Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
