    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41550&lang=en": {
      "title": "Instructor, Instructor of Clinical Practice, PEM – Colorado Springs",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 28, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: SOM-PEDS EMERGENCY MED-GENOPS Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Department: Department of Pediatrics, Section of Emergency Medicine, School of Medicine Job Title: Instructor, Instructor of Clinical Practice, PEM – Colorado Springs Position #:00854068 – Requisition #:41550 Job Summary: Instructors are Clinical Faculty at the University of Colorado School of Medicine that will work in the Children's Hospital Colorado (CHCO) Network of Care (NOC) including Emergency Departments in Colorado. In this role, Instructors will provide medical care to acutely ill and injured pediatric patients age birth to 26 years. They will perform history taking, physical examinations, define and execute appropriate workup that leads to diagnosis with treatment and disposition plan. Key Responsibilities: 100% Clinical Effort You will be expected to maintain 1.0cFTE (clinical effort). Clinical Practitioners at 1.0 cFTE will be expected to provide coverage for 1,376 hours. All clinical hours obligations are negotiable with the Section Head at any time. This coverage will consist of Children's Hospital Colorado, Anschutz and Network of Care locations. Coverage will include: Pediatric emergency care Pediatric Observation Unit medicine Jeopardy shifts (an internal physician coverage system for unanticipated absence) Practitioner must maintain active medical staff privileges at all other facilities where ED or urgent care services are provided by the Children’s Hospital Colorado NOC unless a site is specifically excluded by mutual agreement by the practitioner and the medical director of the Children’s Hospital Colorado NOC. You will be expected to attend at least 75% of the monthly joint section and operational updates meetings of the Section of Emergency Medicine. It is recommended that you participate in Children’s Hospital Colorado Main OR with anesthesiology one time per year to maintain airway skills as well as other technical seminars as deemed by the section and/or practice site in conjunction with input from the medical director. · Clinical teaching of Medical Students, Family Practice Residents and Pediatric Residents · Clinical Supervision and support of onboarding for Advanced Practice Providers · Attendance and participation in required Section monthly meetings · Participation in Quality Improvement and development of Clinical Care Guidelines · Maintenance of skills required for provision of high quality, patient centered, safe urgent/emergent care of children. Annual requirements include but may not be limited to: o Two half-day Acute Care Education sessions put on by the Section per academic year o One high fidelity code simulation at the Simulation Center at CHCO and at least one code simulation at a local NOC site per academic year o Maintenance of PALS certification o Maintenance of CME relevant to clinical work o Attend other technical seminars as deemed mandatory by the section and/or practice site in conjunction with input from the Director Work Location: Onsite – this role is expected to work onsite and is located in Colorado Springs, CO. Why Join Us: With an abundance of sunshine and mountains nearby, the Colorado Front Range is the place to be! The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus ranks among the top 20 medical centers in the country. Living in Colorado is a great experience because of the natural environment, strong economic growth, and lots of recreational activities. The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus ranks among the top 20 medical centers in the country while the Department of Pediatrics was ranked No. 8 in the nation for “Best Medical Schools – Pediatrics” in U.S. News & World Report’s 2023 rankings. Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year (based on percentage of time) Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 11/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. · Doctor of Medicine or Doctor of Osteopathic Medicine Degree · Board certification and eligibility in Pediatric Emergency Medicine or Emergency Medicine. · Active certification in Pediatric Advanced Life Support · Active Colorado Medical License · Active Colorado State DEA license Preferred Qualifications: · Two or more years' experience in pediatric acute care environment · Experience teaching medical students and residents · Completion of fellowship training in Pediatric Emergency Medicine. · Experience with pediatric patient population; pediatric emergency, critical care or urgent care exposure ideal · POCUS trained Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Knowledge · Advanced understanding of pediatric disease and injury patterns · Understanding of and familiarity with resources to assist in making clinical decisions and diagnosis Skills · Use of electronic medical record (EPIC) · Teaching of medical learners · Effectively and respectfully field calls from referring physicians to facilitate referral to site appropriate for presenting problem/service requested and transport to site Technical skills · Interpretation of plain radiographs · Foreign body removal · Laceration repair, including vermillion border and nail bed repair (some advanced techniques can be learned on job) · Incision and drainage · Reduction of minor digit fractures or joint dislocations (can be learned on job) · Nerve blocks · Lumbar puncture · IV fluid management of electrolyte and endocrine derangements · Acute respiratory care · Intubation (ongoing yearly skills training mandatory) · Pediatric resuscitation (must maintain PALS certification and complete required annual mock resuscitations) · Procedural Sedation (do not need to hold previous credentials but must obtain credentialing at CHCO. Process in place for education and assisting with obtaining credentials.) Abilities · Work efficiently in a fast paced, acute care environment for 8-12 hours at a time · Promote teamwork amongst nurses, techs, learners, and colleagues · Strong communication and interpersonal skills · Work a mix of days, evening, overnights, weekend, and holiday shifts Conditions of Employment: · Must successfully pass a 10-panel drug test through Children’s Hospital Colorado · Must be willing and able to pass a national criminal and sex-offender background check Open Track: To support the growth of our faculty, selected candidates will be offered the opportunity to choose a track that corresponds to their area of excellence. Learn more about faculty tracks at the Office for Faculty Affairs . How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): 1. A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position 2. Curriculum vitae / Resume 3. Five professional references including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers . Questions should be directed to: Bernadette Johnson, Bernadette.Johnson@childrenscolorado.org Screening of Applications Begins: Applications will be accepted until finalists are identified, but preference will be given to complete applications received by November 30, 2026. Those who do not apply by this date may or may not be considered. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as HIRING RANGE: $225,000 to $245,000 The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation unless it is non-exempt. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: The University of Colorado (CU) is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@ucdenver.edu ​. Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41545&lang=en": {
      "title": "Research Services Senior Professional",
      "description": "Closing Date: 11/02/2026 Posted Date: Oct 27, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: SOM-PEDS EMERGENCY MED-GENOPS Schedule: Part-time University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus Department: Pediatrics - Emergency Medicine Job Title: Research Services Senior Professional Position #00828597 – Requisition #:41545 Job Summary: Join the Department of Pediatrics - Emergency Medicine at the University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus and play a vital role in advancing innovative pediatric emergency medicine research. This position serves as a senior clinical research professional responsible for the independent coordination and management of complex clinical studies involving pediatric patients and human subjects. Working closely with clinical teams, research partners, and families, the Research Services Senior Professional will support studies that improve outcomes for children through cutting-edge clinical research, and advancements in emergency care. Key Responsibilities: Act as a Primary Coordinator and point of contact on multiple trials/studies Develops protocol-specific systems and documents including process flows, training manuals, Standard Operating Procedures (SOPs) and Case Report Forms (CRFs). Maintains subject level documentation and prepares documents, equipment and/or supplies in compliance with regulations Assist and train junior team members Assist with identifying issues related to operational efficiency and shares results with leadership Collect information to determine feasibility, recruitment, and retention strategies. Employ, evaluate, and assist with the implementation of innovative solutions to maximize recruitment and retention Serve as a resource and participate in study initiation and close out duties Work Location: Hybrid – this role is eligible for a hybrid schedule of 3 days per week on campus and as needed for in-person meetings. In person requirements may be subject to change depending on study and departmental needs. Why Join Us: The Department of Pediatrics - Emergency Medicine is dedicated to improving the lives of children through innovative clinical research that directly informs and transforms emergency care. As a member of our research team, you will contribute to studies that address critical pediatric health challenges, collaborate with leading physicians and investigators, and help generate discoveries that improve outcomes for patients and families both locally and nationally. This role offers the opportunity to work in a collaborative, mission-driven environment at one of the nation's premier academic medical centers. You will gain exposure to diverse research programs, engage with multidisciplinary experts across Children's Hospital Colorado and the University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus, and make a meaningful impact on the future of pediatric emergency medicine while advancing your professional growth and clinical research expertise. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree in any field Two (2) years clinical research or related experience Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Preferred Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree in science or health related field Three (3) years of clinical research or related experience Experience with electronic data capture systems (e.g. EMR or EHR and data management systems) Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Knowledge and understanding of federal regulations and Good Clinical Practice (GCP) Ability to communicate effectively, both in writing and orally Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with employees at all levels throughout the institution Outstanding customer service skills Knowledge of basic human anatomy, physiology medical terminology Ability to interpret and master complex research protocol information How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position Curriculum vitae / Resume Three to five professional references, including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Questions should be directed to: Gonzalo Lerner, Gonzalo.Lerner@childrenscolorado.org Screening of Applications Begins: Immediately and continues until November 2 nd , 2026 . Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as $29,352 - $37,336 @ 0.50 FTE. The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position may be eligible for overtime compensation, depending on the level. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@cuanschutz.edu ​. Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41541&lang=en": {
      "title": "Open Rank CAMM Program Coordinator (Level I – Level II)",
      "description": "Closing Date: 11/02/2026 Posted Date: Oct 27, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: SOM-MED-PUL GENERAL OPERATIONS Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus Department: Medicine – Division of Pulmonary, Allergy, and Critical Care Medicine (PACCM) Job Title: Open Rank CAMM Program Coordinator (Level I – Level II) Position #: 00854198 – Requisition #: 41541 Job Summary: The Consortium for Applied Microbial Metrics, CAMM (microbialmetrics.org) at the University of Colorado’s Anschutz Medical Campus, is a multi-institutional collaboration of investigators with a shared goal: to develop new pharmacodynamic (PD) markers that will accelerate pre-clinical drug development and human trials in bacterial diseases. As a platform for cross-disciplinary collaborative innovation, the Consortium is developing practical new solutions to accelerate drug and regimen development for tuberculosis and other mycobacterial diseases while providing novel insights into disease pathogenesis. The Consortium is committed to the highest standards in research reproducibility and transparency. The Consortium is in a phase of rapid growth as key not-for-profit; federal and pharma stakeholders seek to utilize our novel drug-evaluation tools. The CAMM Program Coordinator will provide a wide spectrum of key administrative support to help ensure seamless operations of the CAMM research program through a variety of tasks. This position will provide comprehensive administrative support to the Associate Director and Director of the Consortium for Applied Microbial Metrics/ PI to help ensure the smooth and efficient operation of the program. This role includes providing support in the contract management process (MTAs, DTAs, and other agreements), tracking critical regulatory and institutional approvals and renewals, preparation of key regulatory and institutional documents and invoice tracking. Additional tasks include assisting with calendar management, meeting coordination, travel arrangements, and preparation of materials for meetings. The Program Coordinator will contribute to the development of standard operating procedures in collaboration with the CAMM leadership team. Comfort with data systems, financial tracking, and institutional compliance is essential. Key Responsibilities: Purchasing and finance support, including creating and submitting expense reports and reconciling procurement card charges, maintaining record of lab’s operating costs, service contracts, and equipment costs General administrative support and office operational duties Contracting and regulatory affairs, including working with PI and Lab Director to organize laboratory documents, supporting IRB submissions Responsible for exercising discretion, analytical skill, personal accountability, and responsibility in a wide range of areas including academic, administrative, and services functions Contributes to process improvement efforts as applicable to improve operational efficiency. Work Location: Hybrid – this role is eligible for a hybrid schedule of 3 days per week on campus and as needed for in-person meetings. Why Join Us: About the Division of Pulmonary, Allergy, and Critical Care Medicine Thank you for your interest in the Division of Pulmonary, Allergy, and Critical Care Medicine at the University of Colorado! Our over 150 faculty are located across four sites: the University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus, National Jewish Health, Denver Health, and the VA Eastern Colorado Health Care System. We are very proud of our long and illustrious history. Many seminal discoveries in pulmonary and critical care medicine occurred here in Denver, including advances in tuberculosis, interstitial lung disease, airway disease, cancer, and critical care. Many of our former trainees have taken leadership roles in academic medicine, including Division and Department Chairs, Deans, and American Thoracic Society Presidents. However, we do not rest on our laurels! We continue to enhance all aspects of our division and training program, and as a result, we have seen tremendous and sustained growth. The clinical practice sites have built new hospitals, and there are multiple new research buildings across the campuses. We have been fortunate to recruit tremendous new faculty members while retaining many of our former trainees. Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation, and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 15/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Level I: Four (4) years of experience in an administrative position that included procurement, fiscal management, vendor relations or related experience. A combination of related education and/or relevant experience in an occupation related to the work assigned equal to four (4) years. Level II: Five (5) years of experience in an administrative position that included procurement, fiscal management, vendor relations or related experience. A combination of related education and/or relevant experience in an occupation related to the work assigned equal to five (5) years. Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Preferred Qualifications: Bachelor’s in finance, accounting, economics, business administration, public health, or a closely related field. Three (3) years of experience in an administrative role. At least one (1) year of experience working in a regulated scientific, academic, manufacturing, or related environment Experience working in an academic research environment. Experience with financial management and expense systems finance systems. Experience creating expense reports to reconcile charges on procurement cards and submitting reimbursement requests. Experience using applications such as Smartsheet, procurement platforms, and other collaboration tools. Conditions of Employment: Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without requiring sponsorship. We are unable to provide work visa sponsorship or employment authorization for this position now or in the future. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Ability to communicate effectively, both in writing and orally. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with employees at all levels throughout the institution. Outstanding customer service skills. Ability to be flexible and maintain positive working relationships. Excellent organizational and time management skills. Ability to prioritize requests based on needs of the unit. Ability to proactively manage multiple competing deadlines and anticipate project needs. High attention to detail and accuracy of information. How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position. Curriculum vitae / Resume Three to five professional references, including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address. Questions should be directed to: Chantal Underkofler, chantal.underkofler@cuanschutz.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Immediately and continues until 11/1/26 Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as: Level I: $53,940 – $70,116 Level II: $59,460 – $77,304 The above salary range (or hiring range) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position may be eligible for overtime compensation, depending on the level. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@cuanschutz.edu . Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41544&lang=en": {
      "title": "Engagement Operations Professional",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 27, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: ADM-CHAN Anschutz Tech Transfe Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Department: CU Anschutz Innovations Job Title: Engagement Operations Professional Position #:00730768 – Requisition #: 41544 This is a Temporary position limited to no more than 9-months. Job Summary: The Engagement Operations Professional will support CU Anschutz Innovations in administering the post-execution billing and invoicing lifecycle for faculty and provider consulting engagements. They will help manage the CUI Consulting Billing shared inbox, which serves as a central communication pathway for reporting consulting hours, initiating customer billing, supporting vendor set-up, and responding to payment-status and process inquiries. This role combines high-volume communication, careful data management, workflow coordination, and process improvement. They will help ensure requests are acknowledged promptly, routed appropriately, documented consistently, and advanced through the billing and payment process. Key Responsibilities: · Monitor and organize the CUI Consulting Billing shared inbox during assigned working hours, using established procedures, templates, categories, and escalation pathways. · Review submissions from faculty, providers, and administrators reporting hours or services completed under executed consulting agreements; verify that required billing information is present and follow up on incomplete submissions. · Prepare, coordinate, or route billing requests to the appropriate team member, and maintain clear records of request status, outstanding information, next steps, and completion. · Respond to routine questions from providers, administrators, customers, and other partners regarding invoicing requirements, billing status, payment timing, and process expectations using approved communication templates and guidance. · Coordinate routine vendor setup communications with third-party organizations, including gathering and routing required forms or institutional information while escalating tax, legal, compliance, or nonstandard requests to the appropriate staff member. · Maintain accurate and complete records across the contracting and invoicing databases, including transferring executed agreements into the invoicing workflow and validating key fields such as parties, providers, rates, contract dates, billing contacts, payment terms, and engagement status. · Develop and maintain desk procedures, response templates, tracking tools, frequently asked questions, and other resources that support consistent service and operational continuity. · Analyze recurring questions, delays, handoff issues, and data-quality problems; recommend and help implement practical process improvements that reduce repetitive work and improve transparency for all parties. · Prepare basic activity summaries and operational metrics, such as inquiry volume, response timeliness, aging items, incomplete submissions, and recurring issue categories. Work Location: Hybrid – this role is eligible for a hybrid schedule, as needed for in-person meetings. Why Join Us: CU Anschutz Innovations is an integral part of The University of Colorado’s Anschutz Medical Campus, a top-tier academic medical institution, collaborating with pioneering researchers, clinicians, staff, and external partners at the University of Colorado, staff at UCHealth and Children’s Hospital Colorado. Together, we power innovation by imagining, discovering and commercializing advanced healthcare solutions, including treatments, medical devices, and cutting-edge technologies. Our mission at CU Anschutz Innovations is driven by the unique collaborative environment we operate in, and our guiding principle is to transform breakthrough discoveries and treatments into realities within an efficient ecosystem that accelerates their availability to patients. This approach not only empowers our partners to have an immediate and meaningful impact but also enhances the quality of life and outcomes for patients now and in the future, at both CU and beyond. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: · A bachelor’s or advanced degree from an accredited institution in business, finance, accounting, public administration, health administration, information systems, communications, or a related field. · Experience using Microsoft Outlook, Excel, Word, and shared electronic records or databases. · Demonstrated experience managing detailed tasks, written communications, or administrative workflows with accuracy and timely follow-through. Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Preferred Qualifications: · Experience with billing, invoicing, accounts receivable, vendor onboarding, contract administration, customer service, or professional-services operations. · Experience managing a shared inbox, ticket queue, customer relationship management system, or other high-volume request channel. · Experience improving a process, documenting a workflow, creating templates, or analyzing operational data. · Familiarity with university, healthcare, research, technology transfer, or consulting environments. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: · Exceptional written communication and customer-service skills, including the ability to provide clear, professional, and timely responses to varied stakeholders. · Strong attention to detail and commitment to accurate, complete, and well-documented records. · Ability to prioritize competing requests, monitor open items, meet deadlines, and escalate issues appropriately. · Ability to follow established procedures while exercising sound judgment when a request is incomplete, unusual, sensitive, or outside the Fellow’s authority. · Ability to work independently in a remote environment and collaborate effectively with finance, contracting, administrative, and program team members. · Strong organizational and analytical skills, including proficiency with Excel for tracking, reconciliation, quality review, and basic reporting. · Process-improvement mindset with the ability to identify repetitive work, communication gaps, and opportunities for standardization or automation. · Discretion in handling confidential information and a commitment to ethical conduct, accountability, and service. How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): 1. A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position 2. Curriculum vitae / Resume 3. Three professional references including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers . Questions should be directed to: Lindley Pagels, Lindley.pagels@cuanschutz.edu Screening of Applications Begins: This position will remain open until filled. Applications will be reviewed as they are received, and candidates may be contacted for interviews throughout the posting period. Upon candidate selection, the posting will be closed, and no further applications will be accepted. Anticipated Pay Range: The hiring range for this position has been established at: $25 to $30 / hour. The above hiring range represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty and training. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. Temporary employees are only eligible for sick leave benefits. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: The University of Colorado (CU) is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@ucdenver.edu ​. Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41540&lang=en": {
      "title": "Business Services Entry Professional",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 27, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: SOM-MED-PUL GENERAL OPERATIONS Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus Department: Medicine – Pulmonary, Allergy, and Critical Care Medicine Job Title: Business Services Entry Professional Position #: 00854076 – Requisition #: 41540 Job Summary: The Division of Pulmonary, Allergy, and Critical Care Medicine is searching for a Business Services Entry Professional to provide administrative and operational support for divisional faculty, staff, and leadership. This entry-level professional position coordinates business processes, purchasing activities, events, seminars, communications support, and routine financial transactions while working under guidance from the Business Operations Program Manager. Key Responsibilities: Provide support to faculty and divisional personnel, including but not limited to, scheduling and coordinating meetings, maintaining calendars, and performing conference registrations. Respond to routine inquires and provide customer service support. Coordination of Excellence Seminar, including maintaining logistics for guest speakers, schedules and event calendars, and assisting with communications and materials. Communications and website support for the Division, including website updates and maintenance, digital signage and communication displays, maintain email distribution lists and communication databases. Provide financial and purchasing support to include preparing purchasing requests and purchase orders, process reimbursements and procurement card reconciliations for faculty and Division. Work Location: Hybrid – this role is eligible for a hybrid schedule of 2-3 days per week on campus and as needed for in-person meetings. Why Join Us: About the Division of Pulmonary, Allergy, and Critical Care Medicine Thank you for your interest in the Division of Pulmonary, Allergy, and Critical Care Medicine at the University of Colorado! Our over 150 faculty are located across four sites: the University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus, National Jewish Health, Denver Health, and the VA Eastern Colorado Health Care System. We are very proud of our long and illustrious history. Many seminal discoveries in pulmonary, allergy, critical care medicine occurred here in Denver, including advances in tuberculosis, interstitial lung disease, airway disease, cancer, and critical care. Many of our former trainees have taken leadership roles in academic medicine, including Division and Department Chairs, Deans, and American Thoracic Society Presidents. We continue to enhance all aspects of our division and training program, and as a result, we have seen tremendous and sustained growth. The clinical practice sites have built new hospitals, and there are multiple new research buildings across the campuses. We have been fortunate to recruit tremendous new faculty members while retaining many of our former trainees. About the University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is a world-class medical destination at the forefront of transformative science, medicine, education, and patient care. The campus encompasses the University of Colorado health professional schools, more than 60 centers and institutes, and two nationally ranked independent hospitals - UCHealth University of Colorado Hospital and Children's Hospital Colorado - that treat more than two million adult and pediatric patients each year. Innovative, interconnected and highly collaborative, the University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus delivers life-changing treatments, patient care and professional training and conducts world-renowned research fueled by over $700 million in research grants. For more information, visit www.cuanschutz.edu . Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation, and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 15/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's degree from an accredited institution. Substitution: A combination of education and related technical/military/paraprofessional experience may be substituted for a bachelor’s degree on a year for year basis. Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Preferred Qualifications: Experience providing administrative support. Experience with event coordination and purchasing support. Experience with communications support and managing and designing websites. Experience working in higher education or healthcare environments. Conditions of Employment: Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without requiring sponsorship. We are unable to provide work visa sponsorship or employment authorization for this position now or in the future. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Ability to communicate effectively, both in writing and orally. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with employees at all levels throughout the institution. Outstanding customer service skills. Strong organizational skills and attention to detail. Ability to manage multiple priorities and deadlines. How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position. Curriculum vitae / Resume Three to five professional references, including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address. Questions should be directed to: Veronica Faiffer, veronica.faiffer@cuanschutz.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Immediately and continues until position is filled. For best consideration, apply by November 13 th , 2026 . Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as $50,224 – $67,300 . The above salary range (or hiring range) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position may be eligible for overtime compensation, depending on the level. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@cuanschutz.edu . Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41536&lang=en": {
      "title": "Executive Operations Professional",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 27, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: ADM AVC VC Info Strategy&Svcs Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Department: Information Strategy and Services Job Title: Executive Operations Professional Position #: 00729914 – Requisition #: 41536 Job Summary: Do you thrive behind the scenes, bringing structure to complex priorities and helping leaders and teams succeed? We are looking for an organized, resourceful professional who can anticipate needs, build trusted relationships and keep important work moving forward. About the Role Join Information Strategy and Services (ISS) as an Executive Operations Professional, providing high-level executive and administrative support to the CIO and coordinated operational support for the ISS Executive Leadership Team and Executive Director of AI Strategy. This role manages complex calendars and executive priorities, and coordinates department-wide events, meetings, materials, and routine business processes that help ISS operate effectively and support the university’s mission. This position sits at the center of leadership priorities and organizational activities across ISS. You will work with executives, senior leaders, campus partners, and teams across the organization while helping create consistent, well-coordinated experiences for employees and stakeholders. The role offers variety, visibility, and opportunities to improve how work gets done. What You’ll Do Provide executive and administrative support to the CIO and coordinated operational support to the ISS Executive Leadership Team and Executive Director of AI Strategy, including calendar management, executive priorities, scheduling, and related administrative activities. Coordinate executive and leadership meetings, including agendas, materials, logistics, stakeholder communications, and follow-up actions. Serve as a liaison among ISS leadership, staff, campus partners, vendors, and external stakeholders to support communication and operational coordination. Support cross-functional administrative and business processes, including interview scheduling, routine purchasing and procurement coordination, request tracking, and documentation. Coordinate logistics for department-wide meetings, events, and engagement activities, including ISS Town Halls, ISS Summits, IT and ISS Leaders Meetings, and other special initiatives. Responsibilities include scheduling, room reservations, catering, AV coordination, materials, and post-event follow-up. Create and maintain clear, audience-appropriate content and digital or print resources for ISS initiatives, programs, events, and organizational priorities. What Success Looks Like Build trusted relationships with leaders, staff, campus partners, and stakeholders. Demonstrate initiative and ownership while working independently. Approach challenges with curiosity, creativity, and a solutions-oriented mindset. Operate with professionalism, discretion, and sound judgment. Contribute positively to a collaborative, service-focused culture. Seek opportunities to improve processes, communications, and the overall employee experience. Ready to make an impact? If you enjoy bringing clarity to complex work, supporting leaders and teams and improving the way an organization operates, we want to hear from you. Work Location: Hybrid – This position is eligible for a hybrid work environment. AMC ISS strives to support flexibility while also recognizing the value of in-person collaboration. Employees in this role are generally expected to work on campus three days per week, with additional on-campus presence as needed based on business needs, meetings, activities, or other work requirements. The specific hybrid schedule will be determined in coordination with the supervisor. The work schedule will be based around core working hours in Colorado Mountain Time. Why Join Us: Information Strategy and Services (ISS) partners across the campus to deliver information technology services that empower teaching, learning, research, and patient care. ISS is organized into three core functions: Technology & Infrastructure, Security & Compliance, and Business Strategy. Together, we connect service and technology . Our work is guided by six shared principles that connect our teams and shape how we serve our customers: Curiosity- Explore beyond one’s own experience and environment. Compassion- Demonstrates empathy, understanding, and respect for all people. Collaboration- Partner well beyond our space and build partnerships to achieve organizational results. Commitment- Dedication and engagement one has to their job, team, organization and university. Competence- Know our craft and be committed to continuous improvement and learning. Confidence- Be empowered and assured to represent our customers and their needs. Active investment in our culture and our people is foundational in developing and delivering service excellence. ​To cultivate a people centric workplace, we do the following: Growth & Development : Our Workforce Development Program builds critical skills and supports career advancement. Empowered Managers : Leaders are trained in coaching and team effectiveness to drive success. Open Communication : Stay connected through monthly town halls and annual summits. Wellness Focus : We prioritize employee well-being with supportive wellness initiatives. Coaching Culture : Continuous learning and feedback are part of how we grow together. Flexible Work : We offer flexible arrangements whenever possible to support work-life balance. Click here to find out more about ISS’s Culture The University of Colorado offers a comprehensive benefits package that includes health insurance, life insurance, retirement plans, tuition benefits, ECO pass, paid time off – vacation, sick, and holidays and more. To see what benefits are available, please visit: https://www.cu.edu/employee-services/benefits-wellness . Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 15/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: PROFESSIONAL Education: A bachelor’s degree in business, education, human resources, organizational development or a directly related field from an accredited institution. Substitution: A combination of education and related professional experience may be substituted for the bachelor’s degree on a year-for-year basis. Experience: 1 year of professional level experience providing administrative or operational support to leaders, including responsibility for coordinating meetings and events, managing calendars, and handling confidential or sensitive information. SENIOR Education: A bachelor’s degree in business, education, human resources, organizational development or a directly related field from an accredited institution. Substitution: A combination of education and related professional experience may be substituted for the bachelor’s degree on a year-for-year basis. Experience: 2 years of professional level experience providing executive support to executive-level leaders, including responsibility for managing complex calendars, coordinating executive meetings and events, and handling confidential or sensitive information. Experience using Microsoft 365 tools, including Outlook, Teams, SharePoint, Word, Excel, and PowerPoint. Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Preferred Qualifications: Experience working in higher education, academic medicine, information technology, public sector, or a complex organizational environment. Experience developing communications, presentations, and other audience-facing materials across multiple channels and formats. Experience supporting human resources processes such as interview scheduling, candidate communications, and candidate visit logistics. Experience supporting procurement, basic vendor coordination, or routine business operations processes. Conditions of Employment: Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without requiring sponsorship. We are unable to provide work visa sponsorship or employment authorization for this position now or in the future. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Ability to interact professionally and effectively with senior leaders, executives, and external stakeholders. Ability to assess competing priorities and make sound decisions in fast-paced executive environment. Ability to manage multiple priorities while coordinating executive calendars, meetings, communications, materials and operational activities with strong attention to detail. Strong written and verbal communication skills, including ability to develop and maintain professional communications, presentations, meeting materials and digital content for diverse audiences. Proficiency with Microsoft 365 tools, including Outlook, Teams, Word, Excel, PowerPoint, and SharePoint. Ability to use modern productivity and AI-enabled tools to improve efficiency, communications and administrative processes. Ability to support basic purchasing and procurement by gathering information, tracking requests, coordinating with vendors and internal partners and maintaining accurate records. Ability to coordinate event logistics, including scheduling, room reservations, audiovisual support, catering materials and communications. Ability to document processes, maintain tracking tools and improve administrative workflows. Ability to work independently and contribute effectively within a collaborative team. How to Apply: We value the thoughts you put into a C over Letter and would like to see your Resume, and List of References . For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): 1. A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position 2. Resume 3. Three to five professional references, including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Questions should be directed to: ISS Human Resources iss-humanresources@cuanschutz.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Immediately and continues until position is filled. For best consideration, apply by 11/5/2026. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as: Professional: $56,995 - $66,000 Senior Professional: $61,616 - $72,000 The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position may be eligible for overtime compensation, depending on the level. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@cuanschutz.edu . Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41537&lang=en": {
      "title": "Advanced Practice Provider (APP)/(PA/NP/APRN)/Medicine/Endocrinology/Instructor, Senior Instructor, Assistant Professor of Clinical Practice",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 27, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: SOM-MED-Endocrinology Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Department: Department of Medicine, Division of Endocrinology, Diabetes and Metabolism Job Title: Advanced Practice Provider (APP)/(PA/NP/APRN)/Medicine/Endocrinology/ Instructor, Senior Instructor, Assistant Professor of Clinical Practice Position #00853986 – Requisition #41537 Job Summary: This position is a blend of inpatient and outpatient full-time clinical position. The primary responsibility is inpatient/consult care for patients with all types of endocrine and diabetes disorders as a member of the inpatient endocrinology consult service. Some effort will also be dedicated to outpatient clinic work, focusing on hospital follow ups and urgent consults. Also, could include some virtual patient care delivered onsite. This is a 1.0 FTE position at the University of Colorado Hospital (main campus) on weekdays (Monday – Friday) only and offers a flexible mix of inpatient and outpatient endocrinology care. The number of inpatient and outpatient sessions will vary based on the distribution of inpatient and outpatient care and the needs of the team. Successful candidates will be responsible for interfacing with other inpatient/consult teams and working as a collaborative team member on the Endocrinology Inpatient Team, which consists of a MD and Fellow, residents and medical students. This position will provide direct patient care, clinical follow-up, lab review and other duties primarily in the inpatient but also the outpatient environments. Experience in the evaluation and management of common endocrine disorders, including diabetes, thyroid disease, adrenal disease, pituitary disease, calcium disorders, and osteoporosis is preferred but is not required for this position. Duties will occur at the Anschutz Medical Campus University of Colorado Hospital. Key Responsibilities: Performs comprehensive health assessments, including health history, physical exams, preventive screening and identifies medical health risks and needs for patients on the inpatient endocrinology service Develops treatment plans and monitors response to therapy in collaboration with attending physicians and the interdisciplinary care team Participates in daily inpatient rounds, care coordination, and communication with referring teams, nursing staff, pharmacists, case managers, and other healthcare professionals Documents clinical encounters and treatment recommendations in the electronic medical record in a timely manner Facilitates safe discharge planning and coordinates follow-up care for patients with endocrine conditions Provides post-hospitalization follow-up care, including outpatient evaluation and management, patient education, medication adjustment, and ongoing disease monitoring Participates in self-directed continued learning Promotes evidence-based practice, quality improvement initiatives, and patient-centered care Collaborates with faculty physicians, advanced practice providers, trainees, and staff to support the clinical, educational, and academic missions of the division and endocrinology service. Performs, orders and/or interprets diagnostic studies within scope of practice and clinical area of practice. Develops diabetes care plan and reassesses and modifies plan as necessary. Serves as a clinical consultant to other clinical services in the hospital Collaborates with all members of the multidisciplinary services and units in the hospital to deliver excellent care Educates patients and families regarding management of health conditions outside the hospital setting Successful candidates are expected to participate in education and scholarly activity such as quality improvement and protocol development in addition to clinical responsibilities, as part of the academic faculty. Maintains CME credits as required for continued licensure. Work Location: This role is expected to work onsite and is located in Aurora, Colorado. Why Join Us: Join the Division of Endocrinology, Metabolism and Diabetes. Our mission is to improve overall health and well-being by prevention, diagnosis, treatment and cure of Diabetes, Obesity, Metabolic disorders and Endocrine disorders through: Cu​tting-edge basic, translational and clinical research Nationally-recognized consultative services in Endocrinology, Metabolism and Diabetes National leadership Training of future leaders in Academic Endocrinology​ Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year (based on percentage of time) Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 11/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. This is an open rank position and could be categorized as Instructor of Clinical Practice, Senior Instructor of Clinical Practice, Assistant Professor of Clinical Practice based on experience and qualifications as indicated below: Open Track: To support the growth of our faculty, selected candidates will be offered the opportunity to choose a track that corresponds to their area of excellence. Learn more about faculty tracks at the Office for Faculty Affairs . Open Rank: Rank at the time of appointment will be based on the candidate’s demonstrated contributions and experience in teaching, clinical, research, and/or service to the field. We welcome applicants with a range of backgrounds and accomplishments and encourage individuals to highlight the breadth and depth of their professional impact. Learn more about faculty tracks at the Office for Faculty Affairs Instructor of Clinical Practice Graduate of an accredited school of nursing with a master’s degree in advanced practice nursing or a graduate of an accredited program in Physician Assistant Studies. Current active license to practice in the state of Colorado as an Advanced Practice Nurse or Physician Assistant. Prescriptive authority is required. Certified as a Nurse Practitioner/or as a Physician Assistant by a national professional organization. Minimum of 0-4 years experience working in endocrinology Senior Instructor of Clinical Practice Graduate of an accredited school of nursing with a master’s degree in advanced practice nursing or a graduate of an accredited program in Physician Assistant Studies. Current active license to practice in the state of Colorado as an Advanced Practice Nurse or Physician Assistant. Prescriptive authority is required. Certified as a Nurse Practitioner/or as a Physician Assistant by a national professional organization. Minimum of 5 years experience working in endocrinology Assistant Professor of Clinical Practice Graduate of an accredited school of nursing with a master’s degree in advanced practice nursing or a graduate of an accredited program in Physician Assistant Studies. Current active license to practice in the state of Colorado as an Advanced Practice Nurse or Physician Assistant. Prescriptive authority is required. Certified as a Nurse Practitioner/or as a Physician Assistant by a national professional organization. Minimum of 10 years experience working in endocrinology Experience teaching and mentoring of advanced practice nursing or Physician Assistant students Clinical research or quality improvement research experience Preferred Qualifications: Applicants should be enthusiastic about a career in clinical Endocrinology with a strong interest in providing excellent clinical care in the inpatient and outpatient setting. There should be a desire for teaching and writing and an interest in opportunities in quality improvement and/or clinical research. How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): 1. A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position (only use if a cover letter is necessary) 2. Curriculum vitae / Resume 3. Three to five professional references, including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers . Questions should be directed to: Tyeise Edmond; EndoHR@cuanshcutz.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Applications will be accepted until finalists are identified, but preference will be given to complete applications received by 11/15/26 . Those who do not apply by this date may or may not be considered. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as HIRING RANGE: APP Instructor $109,000 - $123,000 APP Senior Instructor $115,000 - $128,000 Assistant Professor $125,000 - $140,000 The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position may be eligible for overtime compensation, depending on the level. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: The University of Colorado (CU) is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@ucdenver.edu ​. Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41535&lang=en": {
      "title": "Neuromodulation Section Manager",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 26, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: SOM-PSYCH GENERAL OPERATIONS Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Department: Psychiatry Job Title: Neuromodulation Section Manager Position #:00854202 – Requisition #: 41535 Job Summary: The Neuromodulation Section Manager provides administrative and operational leadership for the Neuromodulation Section within the Adult Psychiatry Division. In partnership with the Executive Director of Precision Neuromodulation in Psychiatry, Medical Director of Interventional Psychiatry, and the Adult Psychiatry Administrative Director, this role supports the section's research and clinical enterprise, with responsibility for day-to-day operations, people management, financial stewardship, grants and contracts, workforce funding and effort allocation, and section assets. The Section Manager works across CU Anschutz and affiliated partners to coordinate complex clinical and research workflows, manage multiple funding sources with distinct spending restrictions, support the full grant lifecycle, develop and execute contracts, and maintain sound fiscal and operational practices. The role also develops team capability in CU Anschutz administrative processes, supports faculty and staff effort and funding management, oversees section-owned physical and intangible assets, and helps package and communicate the section's accomplishments. Key Responsibilities: Provide section-level administrative and operational leadership in partnership with the Executive Director of Precision Neuromodulation in Psychiatry, the Medical Director of Interventional Psychiatry, and the Adult Psychiatry Administrative Director. Directly supervise the Program Manager and Finance Specialist, provide backup leadership for the Program Manager's team of more than 10 staff, supervise deep brain stimulation (DBS) coordinator, and support staff training and development. Partner with CU Medicine and industry stakeholders to achieve insurance billing for clinical and research workflows, such as fMRI-guided transcranial magnetic stimulation (TMS) Manage the section's portfolio of funding sources and their associated spending restrictions, including UCHealth funds, School of Medicine funds, CU Foundation gift funds, auxiliary speedtypes, startup packages, AEF and DEF speedtypes, and clinical revenue held through CU Medicine. Ensure expenditures and funding decisions align with applicable restrictions and University requirements. Lead grants and contracts administration in collaboration with principal investigators, Psychiatry Research Innovations, the Office of Grants and Contracts, CU Innovations, CU Medicine, and the Procurement Service Center. Support proposal submission, notices of award, award setup, post-award administration, grant transfers from prior institutions, revenue and expense agreements, and subcontracting. Manage staff and faculty effort allocation and funding within the section. Support personnel effort reporting; coordinate with the Senior Business Services Manager in Adult Psychiatry on FTE allocation for shared collaborator faculty, and work with the Finance Specialist on funding changes, payroll expense transfers (PETs), and journal entries (JEs). Coordinate clinical and research operations with the University of Colorado Hospital, CU Research Imaging Center, CU Brain Imaging Center, and other partners, with particular responsibility for clinical imaging workflows and related operational coordination. Maintain primary responsibility for section-owned physical and intangible assets, including TMS machines, coils, computing infrastructure, software, and other equipment. Track assets, warranties, and contracts, manage depreciation in alignment with CU accounting requirements, and report depreciation information to CU accounting teams. Develop the section team's knowledge and consistent use of CU Anschutz processes for fiscal management, procurement, grants management, personnel effort reporting, and FTE and funding management Support the continued growth and expansion of the Deep Brain Stimulation (DBS) Program, including coordination of clinical, operational, and program development activities. Develop and support outreach strategies to increase awareness of the DBS Program among patients, referring clinicians, and community partners, and facilitate appropriate patient recruitment and referral pathways. Support development of educational and informational materials related to DBS and other interventional psychiatry services. Provide administrative oversight and project management for the development and implementation of an Interventional Psychiatry Fellowship, including coordination of curriculum development, training requirements, recruitment, and institutional approval processes. Coordinate across Psychiatry, Neurosurgery, and other relevant clinical and administrative partners to support DBS and broader interventional psychiatry program initiatives. Support the Executive Director and Medical Director in packaging and communicating the accomplishments of the section to funders and other interested persons. Work Location: Hybrid - this role is eligible for a hybrid schedule of 3 days per week on campus and as needed for in-person meetings. Why Join Us: CU Department of Psychiatry sets the standard for education and training of leaders in psychiatry and mental health care, conducts ground-breaking research that aims to eradicate suffering due to psychiatric and substance use disorders, provides ready access to state of-the-art mental health preventions and interventions across the continuum of care, and collaborates with the community and other key stakeholders to promote well-being among all Coloradans. We accomplish this vision in a manner that respects, values and advocates for the dignity and worth of each individual and family. Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 15/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's degree in Psychology, Business Administration, Health Administration, Finance, or a related field. Four years of progressive professional experience in an academic setting including experience administering grants in an academic setting, experience managing research operations in an academic setting, and experience directly supervising three or more individual contributors A combination of education and related technical/military/paraprofessional experience may be substituted for a bachelor’s degree on a year for year basis. Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Preferred Qualifications: Master's degree in Business Administration, Finance, Health Administration, or a related field. Four or more years of experience managing a group of 10 or more people. One year of experience in managing a manager of individual contributors. Familiarity with University of Colorado systems such as Epic, CU Marketplace, MyBI, CU Data, A2E, HCM, FIN, and Smartsheet. Conditions of Employment: Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without requiring sponsorship. We are unable to provide work visa sponsorship or employment authorization for this position now or in the future. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Proficiency with the Microsoft Office suite, with an emphasis on Excel. Demonstrated leadership, staff supervision, coaching, and team-development skills, including the ability to provide leadership across both direct and indirect reporting relationships. Familiarity with neuromodulation and imaging concepts and modalities that will be applied in the section, such as EEG, TMS, (f)MRI, DTI, DBS. Knowledge of complex financial and fund management, including the ability to manage multiple funding sources with different spending restrictions and to apply sound fiscal controls. Knowledge of academic research administration, including pre-award and post-award grant processes, contract administration, subcontracting, and grant transfers. Ability to manage personnel effort, FTE, and funding allocations and to support personnel effort reporting, funding changes, payroll expense transfers, and journal entries. Strong analytical and organizational skills, with advanced ability to work in Microsoft Excel and manage detailed financial, operational, and workforce information. Strong written and verbal communication skills and the ability to collaborate effectively with faculty, staff, hospital partners, imaging centers, central administrative offices, and other internal and external stakeholders. Ability to manage physical and intangible assets throughout their lifecycle, including inventory tracking, warranties, contracts, depreciation, and related accounting coordination. How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): A cover letter describing relevant job experiences as they relate to the listed job qualifications and interest in the position Curriculum vitae / Resume Three to five professional references, including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Questions should be directed to: dophr@cuanschutz.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Immediately and continues until position is filled. For best consideration, apply by 11/16/26 . Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as $77,021 - $97,970 The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position may be eligible for overtime compensation, depending on the level. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@cuanschutz.edu ​. Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41523&lang=en": {
      "title": "Financial Aid Advisor",
      "description": "Closing Date: 11/01/2026 Posted Date: Oct 26, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: VCSSLS-AVCSESS-Financial Aid Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Department: Financial Aid & Scholarships Office Job Title: Financial Aid Advisor Position #: 00827939 – Requisition #:41523 Job Summary: As a part of the CU Anschutz Financial Aid & Scholarships team, the Intermediate Financial Aid Advisor provides guidance to health professions students and families on all aspects of educational funding. This position delivers comprehensive advising through in‑person, virtual, phone, and email interactions, helping students navigate application processes, meet documentation requirements, understand complex financial aid regulations, and make informed decisions about financing their education. In addition to advising, the position assists with processing tasks, participates in outreach and presentation efforts, and contributes to recruitment, retention, and financial wellness initiatives. The Intermediate Financial Aid Advisor also supports the College of Nursing by responding to routine questions, sharing updates, coordinating follow ‑ up tasks, and helping ensure consistent application of financial aid policies and procedures. This role requires strong communication skills, attention to detail, and the ability to work in a fast ‑ paced, student ‑ focused environment. Supervision Received: This position reports to the Associate Director of Financial Aid Advising. Supervision Exercised: This position does not supervise others. Examples of Work: Student Advising – 60% Conduct in-person, virtual, phone, and email advising sessions Provide guidance on FAFSA, verification, SAP, cost of attendance, loans, and aid options Respond to student inquiries within service-level expectations Maintain clear, empathetic, accurate communication using team-approved messaging Processing & Documentation Review – 5% Review verification documents, resolve conflicting information Process appeals (SAP, budget increases, dependency overrides), per training and delegation Track and follow up on incomplete files Process general requests (housing letters, NHSC, needs analysis) Assist with processing related projects as needed Outreach/Presentations - 10% Deliver presentations or outreach activities to internal and external audiences (e.g., students, community partners, or campus stakeholders) in alignment with departmental goals Coordinate logistics for outreach events or presentations (scheduling, materials, audience needs, follow up communication) Adapt presentation content and delivery style based on audience needs, feedback, and setting (in person, virtual, small group, large group) Report outreach activity (e.g., events completed, audiences reached, outcomes or follow up actions) as requested Training/Professional Development – 5% Participate in ongoing training to stay current with financial aid regulations, systems, and best practices Attend professional conferences, webinars, and workshops to enhance knowledge and skills Engage in cross-training opportunities to support office flexibility and coverage Maintain certifications and credentials relevant to financial aid advising Financial Literacy coordination – 10% Assist with delivering financial literacy presentations and workshops by preparing materials, presenting content, or supporting senior staff during sessions. Help maintain and update financial wellness resources, handouts, and web content to ensure information is clear and accessible for students Support outreach efforts by coordinating event logistics with internal and external stakeholders College of Nursing Support – 10% Serve as a support point of contact for the College of Nursing staff, responding to routine questions and escalating complex issues as needed Participate in meetings with program partners to take notes, share updates, and support follow ‑ up tasks as needed Help communicate program ‑ specific information and updates to internal team members under guidance from senior staff Work Location: Hybrid – this role is eligible for a hybrid schedule of 3 days per week on campus and as needed for in-person meetings. Why Join Us: The Financial Aid and Scholarships office, part of the Enrollment Operations division, is responsible for the administration of federal, state, and university financial aid and scholarship programs and for supporting students who have the potential to change the world through their practice and/or research. This team is dedicated to processing aid accurately and in a timely manner and to providing the best service possible to our busy students. The team also works collaboratively with other student services, schools and colleges, and the Denver campus in a dynamic and engaging work environment. Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 15/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: A bachelor’s degree from an accredited institution of higher education. Substitution : A combination of education and related technical/paraprofessional experience may be substituted for the bachelor’s degree on a year for year basis, but not for the specific experience. One year of professional level experience in financial aid, admissions, advising and/or scholarships office or related field that focuses on customer services in a financial context (ex. Banking, Advisory, Wealth Management, Insurance, University/College, TRIO/Upward Bound etc.). Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Preferred Qualifications: Experience working with graduate and professional students, especially those in health-related programs. Experience working with Oracle PeopleSoft Campus Solutions. Experience working with Federal and State aid regulations. Experience counseling student debt. Conditions of Employment: Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without requiring sponsorship. We are unable to provide work visa sponsorship or employment authorization for this position now or in the future. Standard campus hours are 8am – 5pm, with public-facing office hours of 9am – 4pm Employees are required to work on site a minimum of three (3) days per week, or more frequently as designated by campus policy, leadership direction, or operational needs. Occasional evening or weekend work may be required for events, outreach activities, or peak operating periods. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Comprehensive knowledge of federal, state, and institutional financial aid regulations, policies, and compliance requirements. Demonstrated commitment to high‑quality, student‑centered customer service. Strong public speaking, presentation, and facilitation skills across a variety of audiences and formats. Excellent interpersonal, conflict resolution, and relationship‑building skills. Strong analytical, research, critical‑thinking, and organizational abilities. Ability to exercise sound judgment and make independent decisions in complex situations. Proven ability to build and maintain effective working relationships with colleagues, campus partners, and external stakeholders. Ability to clearly communicate policies and procedures to diverse audiences and train staff or campus partners as needed. Ability to assess situations, identify challenges or opportunities, and provide practical, solution‑focused recommendations. How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position Curriculum vitae / Resume Three to five professional references, including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Questions should be directed to: Mercy Booth Mercy.Booth@cuanschutz.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Applications will be accepted until finalists are identified, but preference will be given to complete applications received by 10/31/2026. Those who do not apply by this date may or may not be considered. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as $48,989-$55,734. The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position may be eligible for overtime compensation, depending on the level. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@cuanschutz.edu ​. Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41529&lang=en": {
      "title": "Patient Intake and Scheduling Assistant (Administrative Assistant II)",
      "description": "Closing Date: 11/06/2026 Posted Date: Oct 26, 2026 Job category: Classified Staff Department: SDM-Dental Clinic Compreh Care Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Department: School of Dental Medicine Job Title: Patient Intake and Scheduling Assistant (Administrative Assistant II) Position: #00821022 — Requisition: 41529 Job Summary: The Patient Intake and Scheduling Assistant supports the CU Dental Team Care Clinic by assisting patients, students, faculty, and staff with reception, registration, appointment scheduling, payments, and patient records. The position explains clinic procedures and patient responsibilities, resolves routine administrative issues within established guidelines, and directs concerns to the appropriate clinic personnel. Key Responsibilities Greet and assist patients and respond to phone, virtual, and walk-in inquiries. Schedule and prioritize appointments for student providers and clinic patients through the electronic health record system. Register patients, update information and signatures, and support patient check-in and check-out. Explain clinic procedures, student-provider and faculty-supervision arrangements, time commitments, and financial responsibilities. Verify financial information, notify patients of amounts due, and accept payments. Maintain confidential patient records and facilitate records-release requests using established procedures. Work with faculty, students, coordinators, and staff to address scheduling or billing discrepancies and refer concerns when additional review is needed. Work Location: Onsite School of Dental Medicine Why Join Us: The clinical units at the School of Dental Medicine provide thorough and comprehensive dental care at significantly discounted rates. As a teaching facility, care is provided by dental students and residents under the supervision of highly skilled faculty who oversee all aspects of treatment. Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement Plans: State pension (PERA Defined Benefit) or 401(a) - Employer contributes between 10% and 21.5% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year Vacation Days: Between 12/year and 24/year (maximum accrual between 192 hours and 384 hours) – specific amount depends on length of total State of Colorado service Sick Days: 10/year (360 hour maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 15/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage. Qualifications: Please make sure to include the following in your resume: job title, duties, months and years employed, and average hours worked per week as minimum experience is calculated on a 40 hour/week basis. Minimum Qualifications: Two years of general clerical experience, which includes one year of experience working in a medical environment OR dental environment OR office environment. Substitution : Related c ollege or university course work may be substitute for the two years of general clerical experience on a year-for-year basis, but not for the one year of experience working in a medical/dental/office environment. Colorado law requires that candidates for state government jobs be residents of Colorado at the time of application. Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Preferred Qualifications Experience working with faculty, staff, and students in a higher education environment Experience working in a dental or medical office environment Bilingual in English and Spanish Conditions of Employment Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without requiring sponsorship. We are unable to provide work visa sponsorship or employment authorization for this position now or in the future. Successfully complete criminal background and sex offender registry checks. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Knowledge of administrative and clerical procedures and systems such as word processing, spreadsheets, managing files and records, designing forms, and other office procedures and terminology Knowledge of principles and processes for providing customer and personal services. Knowledge of electronic health record system. Knowledge of teleconferencing software (i.e. Zoom). Ability to efficiently organize, multi-task, and prioritize duties and tasks. Ability to work in a fast-paced, high volume environment. Excellent verbal and written communications skills. Excellent interpersonal skills Proficient computer skills. Ability to interpret and follow complex rules, regulations, policies, procedures, and guidelines. Ability to handle sensitive matters that require discretion and confidentiality. How to Apply: Questions should be directed to: Oscar De Moya, oscar.demoya@cuanschutz.edu Application Materials Instructions: To apply, please submit the following materials to this posting: A cover letter and resume that specifically addresses the job requirements and outlines your qualifications. Special Instructions to Applicants Classified Staff positions have specific application requirements: Submit all required documents indicated in this posting and include a current email address and phone number. Please address minimum qualifications, competencies and preferred qualifications in your cover letter, as these along with previous work experience will be used in the assessment process. Click here to view Veteran and other General Information regarding Classified Staff positions: https://www.cu.edu/cu-careers/special-instructions-classified-staff-applicants For those who meet minimum qualifications, the comparative analysis process will include one or all of the following: Preferred Qualifications Application Review based on the preferred qualifications listed in the posting. Candidates will be evaluated and rated against the preferred qualifications based on information submitted within their application materials. Note: Candidates are not physically present for this portion of the comparative analysis. Interviews based on the job requirements, preferred qualifications and competencies listed in the posting. Candidates will be evaluated, scored and ranked based on oral responses Interviews may be over the phone, videoconference or in-person You will be notified via email if the comparative analysis process changes or includes additional assessment tools other than those listed above. Anticipated Pay Range: The approved starting salary range: $ 3,355 –$ 4,024 per month ($40,251 - $48,298 per year). This position is eligible for overtime compensation. The above hiring range represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. If you have prior state-classified service in the same class series as this position, your pay may be set at a higher amount per the state Step Pay Program implemented on July 1, 2024. For more information about the Step Pay Program, please visit the 2024 Step Pay Program for State of Colorado Employees | DHR . Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@cuanschutz.edu ​. Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students, and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
