    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=39335&lang=en": {
      "title": "Women’s Health Nurse-Practitioner Open Rank- Instructor/ Senior Instructor / Assistant Professor of Clinical Practice",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 28, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: CON-DEAN ADMINISTRATION Schedule: Part-time University of Colorado Anschutz College of Nursing Women’s Health Nurse-Practitioner Open Rank- Instructor/ Senior Instructor / Assistant Professor of Clinical Practice Position #: 00828607 Req: 39335 Job Summary: The University of Colorado Denver l Anschutz Medical Campus seeks individuals with demonstrated commitment to creating an inclusive learning and working environment. We value the ability to engage effectively with students, faculty and staff of diverse backgrounds. The University of Colorado College of Nursing is seeking a Women’s Health Nurse Practitioner (WHNP) / Clinical Instructor / Senior Clinical Instructor / Assistant Professor Clinical (Open Rank) in the Clinical Practice Faculty Series for a 0.90 FTE position with our CU College of Nursing Women’s Health Faculty Practice at Anschutz Medical Campus. This is an ambulatory position including well-woman, reproductive health, menopause, and gynecological care across the lifespan. This position is clinically based as a health care provider and includes a Clinical Instructor / Senior Clinical Instructor / Assistant Professor Clinical (Open Rank) appointment within the College of Nursing. The University of Colorado, College of Nursing is the home of the Nurse Practitioner with a robust clinical practice division including primary care, pediatrics, and midwifery. The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is a world-class medical destination at the forefront of transformative science, medicine, education, and patient care. The campus encompasses the University of Colorado health professional schools, more than 60 centers and institutes, and two nationally ranked independent hospitals - UCHealth University of Colorado Hospital and Children's Hospital Colorado - that treat more than two million adult and pediatric patients each year. Innovative, interconnected and highly collaborative, the University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus delivers life-changing treatments, patient care and professional training and conducts world-renowned research fueled by over $650 million in research grants. For more information, visit www.cuanschutz.edu . Faculty Practice Description: The CU College of Nursing Women’s Health Clinic is an academic practice model that works collaboratively within the UCHealth and CU system. We offer patients a variety of services including individualized care through collaboration with our CU Nursing faculty practices, with referrals to provider groups within the system and community. The practice provides care to patients at the CU College of Nursing Women’s Health Faculty Practice at Anschutz Medical Campus. The WHNP is part of an academic clinical practice that has a long and successful history within the University of Colorado and UCHealth system. This position will join a team of WHNPs who practice across metro Denver. The WHNPs participate in practice expansion activities, practice promotion, and interdisciplinary committees within the UCHealth and CU system. Supervision Received: Work is performed independently under the direct supervision of the Director of Midwifery and Women’s Health. Supervision Exercised: Student supervision is required during clinical placements. Examples of Work Performed: · Provide full-scope care to patients across the lifespan including procedures driven by individual experience. · Provide care in the outpatient clinic setting. · Attend monthly practice meetings and participate in a minimum of one practice and/or College of Nursing committees. · Educate health care team students (APNs, medical students, residents) and actively participate in student evaluations. · Participate in practice development, promotion, and community outreach. · Active participation in health plan contracts. · Remain credentialed by the health plans and ensure credentialing materials stay current. · Performs other duties as assigned. Work Schedule: · Four clinics per week · Monthly practice meeting attendance · Protected administrative time Why Join Us: CU Nursing is an amazing place to be. We have the distinct advantage of being a part of a huge medical campus with three incredible hospitals – the VA, the nationally ranked University of Colorado Hospital, and the Children’s Hospital Colorado where our nursing students and faculty learn every day. From our beginning 125 years ago as part of the School of Medicine at CU Boulder to our current home at the Anschutz Medical Campus, the college has been a recognized leader in nursing education (ranked #10 in online MS graduate programs by U.S. News & World Report 2023). Our faculty, students and staff have been instrumental in shaping the profession of nursing and teaching the next generation of nurses while treating patients in our own nurse-led clinics. Be a part of an innovative, dynamic, diverse, and exciting workplace -- helping make great things happen. Join us in our quest to boldly transform health together. Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 11/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced rate RTD Bus and light rail service To see what benefits are available, please visit: https://nursing.cuanschutz.edu/about/careers/benefits Qualifications: Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Minimum Qualifications Instructor: · Master’s degree from an accredited school of nursing · Current NCC certification · Current RN, APN and RxN licensures in good standing (Any State) o Could be working toward CO clinical licenses during application process and registered with DORA-Department of Regulatory Agencies. Must have Colorado licensures by date of hire. Senior Instructor: · Master’s degree from an accredited school of nursing · Current NCC certification · Current RN, APN and RxN licensures in good standing (Any State) o Could be working toward CO clinical licenses during application process and registered with DORA-Department of Regulatory Agencies. Must have Colorado licensures by date of hire. · Demonstrated leadership in area of practice. · Demonstrated experience collaborating with academic colleagues and students in practice activities. Assistant Professor: · Doctoral degree from an accredited school of nursing · Current NCC certification · Current RN, APN and RxN licensures in good standing (Any State) o Could be working toward CO clinical licenses during application process and registered with DORA-Department of Regulatory Agencies. Must have Colorado licensures prior to date of hire. · Demonstrated leadership in area of practice. · Demonstrated experience collaborating with academic colleagues and students in practice activities. Conditions of Employment: · Must be willing and able to provide full scope contraceptive services and counseling on abortion services · Must be willing and able to obtain Colorado RN, APN, RxN licenses prior to date of hire · Must be willing and able to obtain current DEA license within 18 months of hire · Must be willing and able to obtain valid NPI number prior to date of hire · Must be willing and able to obtain valid Colorado Medicaid Provider number prior to date of hire · Must be willing and able to complete CAQH and all credentialing requirements prior to date of hire · Must be willing and able to obtain current BLS/CPR certification by date of hire · Must be willing and able to actively participation in health plan contracts · Must be willing and able to remain credentialed by the health plans and ensure credentialing materials stay current · Must be willing and able to work in a normal patient care environment with some exposure to biological hazards and infectious diseases Preferred Qualifications: · Current, active DEA licensure · Experience precepting advanced practice students Competencies : · Exceptional independent judgment to monitor and respond to changes in a · client’s condition · Interpersonal skills to work effectively with patients and other members of the · health care team · Skilled in the use of electronic medical health record · Excellent knowledge of and ability to perform clinical teaching · Ability to effectively develop and promote practice · Strong collaborative nature · Willingness and ability to actively participate in health plan contracts · Ability to remain credentialed by the health plans and ensure credentialing materials stay current · Ability to precept advanced practice students How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): 1. A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to the listed job qualifications and interest in the position 2. Curriculum vitae / Resume 3. Three to five professional references, including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Questions should be directed to: College of Nursing Human Resources at CON.HR@ucdenver.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Applications will be accepted until finalists are identified, but preference will be given to complete applications received by November 13th, 2026 . Those who do not apply by this date may or may not be considered. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as HIRING RANGE : · $81,372- $91,544 at Instructor of Clinical Practice/WHNP at 0.90 FTE · $82,186 - $92,459 at Sr. Instructor of Clinical Practice/WHNP at 0.90 FTE · $83,000 - $93,375 at Assistant Professor of Clinical Practice/WHNP at 0.90 FTE The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position may be eligible for overtime compensation, depending on the level. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans, and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@cuanschutz.edu . Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students, and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine-preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety-sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41565&lang=en": {
      "title": "Diabetes Educator Open Rank (Instructor– Senior Instructor)",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 28, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: SOM-OB/GYN MFM GENERAL OPS Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Department: SOM- Obstetrics and Gynecology- Maternal Fetal Medicine Job Title: Diabetes Educator Open Rank (Instructor– Senior Instructor) Position #: 00854173 – Requisition #: 41565 Job Summary: The Department of Obstetrics and Gynecology, Division of Maternal Fetal Medicine, at the University of Colorado has an opening for a full-time Diabetes Educator at the rank of Instructor 1.0 FTE. This position will provide support to the freestanding Maternal Fetal Medicine clinic, located in Downtown Denver, Littleton, Parker, and Fort Collins as well as the Children’s Hospital Colorado – North Campus location. Key Responsibilities: · Provide diabetes education and follow up to pregnant adults who have gestational diabetes and Type 2 diabetes. · Educate patients and families on: o Diabetes types and disease progression o Implications of diabetes in pregnancy o Blood glucose monitoring techniques o Insulin and non-insulin medications o Carbohydrate counting and meal planning o Exercise and lifestyle modifications o Management of hypo- and hyperglycemia o Use of diabetes technologies such as continuous glucose monitors (CGMs) · Propose insulin initiation and titration regimens, with authorization by MFM physician · Perform CGM placement and education · Interpret glycemic patterns from CGM or glucometer logs, and collaborate with MFM care team on therapeutic adjustments · Participate in diabetes program planning, delivery, and evaluation · Maintain accurate and up-to-date clinical notes in accordance with Maternal Fetal Medicine guidelines · Participate in team and staff meetings to support both service delivery and division goals · Work individually and collaboratively in the development and implementation of quality improvement initiatives and activities · Work in a manner that provides privacy and confidentiality · Practice independently · Demonstrate continuing education in diabetes management · Provide services via telehealth and in person · Bill for services accurately · Back up on communicating with pharmacies on supply and insulin orders as well as completing prior authorizations Work Location: Hybrid – this role is eligible for a hybrid schedule of 3 days per week on campus and as needed for in-person meetings. Why Join Us: Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package including: · Medical: Multiple plan options · Dental: Multiple plan options · Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision · Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay · Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year (based on percentage of time) · Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) · Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) · Holiday Days: 11/year · Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses · ECO Pass: Reduced rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. This is an open rank position and could be categorized as Clinical Instructor or Senior Clinical Instructor based on experience and qualifications as indicated below: Instructor: · Registered Dietitian · Master’s degree in nutrition or related field, and · Certified Diabetes Care and Education Specialist (CDCES) A combination of education and related technical/paraprofessional experience may be substituted for the master’s degree on a year for year basis. Senior Instructor: · Registered Dietitian · Master’s degree in nutrition or related field, and · Certified Diabetes Care and Education Specialist (CDCES) · 5+ years of experience working in diabetes care A combination of education and related technical/paraprofessional experience may be substituted for the master’s degree on a year for year basis. Preferred Qualifications: · Registered Dietitian · Certified Diabetes Care and Education Specialist (CDCES) · Experience working with the psychological and social aspects of living with diabetes. · Previous clinical and research experience · Knowledge of and experience working with Type 2 and gestational diabetes · Experience with independently assessing glucose patterns and making insulin initiation and titration recommendations, preferably in management of diabetes during pregnancy. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: · Excellent interpersonal and communication skills · Demonstrated ability to work under pressure · Ability to multitask · Willingness to learn and comply with relevant laws, rules, regulations, and policies Conditions of Employment: Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without requiring sponsorship. We are unable to provide work visa sponsorship or employment authorization for this position now or in the future. Open Track: To support the growth of our faculty, selected candidates will be offered the opportunity to choose a track that corresponds to their area of excellence. Learn more about faculty tracks at the Office for Faculty Affairs . How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): 1. A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position 2. Curriculum vitae / Resume 3. Five professional references including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers . Questions should be directed to: Joyce Fu, Joyce.Fu@cuanschutz.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Immediately and continues until position is filled. For best consideration, apply by November 30, 2026 Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as HIRING RANGE: Instructor: $79,000 – $87,000 Sr. Instructor: $87,000 – $95,000 The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation unless it is non-exempt. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: The University of Colorado (CU) is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@ucdenver.edu ​. Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41559&lang=en": {
      "title": "Clinical Psychologist – Senior Instructor",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 28, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: SOM-FM GENERAL OPERATIONS Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Department: Family Medicine Job Title: Clinical Psychologist – Senior Instructor Position # 00854209: – Requisition # 41559 : Job Summary: The Department of Family Medicine provides primary health care, educates medical and psychology students and graduates, conducts research and engages with communities. This position will provide therapeutic evaluation and treatment of patients with psychological disorders at Family Medicine clinic(s) coordinating with multi-disciplinary clinicians to provide team-based care in a patient-centered medical home setting committed to providing equitable care to a varied population. Ideal candidates will have experience with integrated team-based care, with additional expertise in motivational interviewing, evidence-based psychotherapies, and working with different populations. Clinical skill is required for conducting assessments, brief psychotherapy, health and behavior change interventions, substance use treatment, and triage to the appropriate level of care. Key Responsibilities: Clinical Care · Provide consultations and recommendations for behavioral health questions and presenting concerns to family medicine providers. · Assess, diagnose and treat behavioral, mental, and emotional conditions. · Facilitate group visits as needed. · Design and implement health promotion/disease prevention interventions. · Support goal setting and patient self-management skills. Teaching and Supervision · Directly supervise behavioral health trainees (graduate students, psychology interns, post-doctoral fellows, and pre-licensure psychologists). Interprofessional · Provide team-based care with multidisciplinary teams. · Coach physicians in communication skills and techniques of health behavior change. · Conduct hospital rounds as needed. · Facilitate referrals for more significant mental health conditions. · Participate in quality improvement and practice transformation initiatives, workflow modification, and the identification and deployment of new efficiencies. Administrative · Maintain eligibility for School of Medicine Faculty. · Keep well-informed of the latest developments in field, both academically and through applied skill. · May participate in clinical research projects (but not required to be a clinician-researcher unless pursuing traditional promotion path). Accept other responsibilities specifically assigned by the Director of Behavioral Health and Integrated Programs. · Attend and present at conferences, meetings and trainings in order to maintain certification and enhance professional skills; participate in faculty development activities. Work Location: Onsite – this role is expected to work onsite and is located Denver, Colorado. Why Join Us: The Department of Family Medicine (DFM) mission is “To heal, teach, discover, and connect. Together.\" by educating, nurturing, fostering, and enhancing those in family medicine and the communities we live in and serve. The Department of Family Medicine has four key aims, each with specific goals: · Patient Care – Providing outstanding Family Medicine to every patient. · Research – Create and disseminate new knowledge. · Training – Train a future integrated, Family Medicine workforce. · Community Engagement - Achieve health equality with community engagement and advocacy. Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package including: · Medical: Multiple plan options · Dental: Multiple plan options · Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision · Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay · Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year (based on percentage of time) · Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) · Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) · Holiday Days: 11/year · Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses · ECO Pass: Reduced rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. · Education: Doctoral degree in Psychology (PhD or PsyD) · Experience: Completion of an accredited postdoctoral program with enough clinical hours to be licensed as a clinical psychologist. · Special Skills: Ability to obtain Colorado state licensure as a psychologist. Ability to obtain and maintain credentialing through the University of Colorado Health system. Preferred Qualifications: · Experience with integrated team-based care, particularly in a primary care based setting that promotes an all-encompassing environment. · Expertise in motivational interviewing, and evidence-based psychotherapies. · E xperience with a variety of teaching methods and/or curricular perspectives. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: · Clinical skill is required for conducting brief and targeted assessments to provide short-term psychotherapy interventions, health and behavior change, substance use treatment, and triage for appropriate level of care. · Demonstrated skill in supervision of clinical staff and trainees. · Excellent written and verbal communication skills · Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with clinic faculty and staff. · Ability to maintain confidentiality. · Ability to work effectively as part of a team and independently. · Experience training and developing staff. Open Track: To support the growth of our faculty, selected candidates will be offered the opportunity to choose a track that corresponds to their area of excellence. Learn more about faculty tracks at the Office for Faculty Affairs . How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): 1. A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position 2. Curriculum vitae / Resume 3. Five professional references including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers . Questions should be directed to: Lydia Lyon, Lydia.lyon@cuanschutz.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Immediately and continues until 1/15/2027. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as HIRING RANGE: $92,000 to $140,000 The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation unless it is non-exempt. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: The University of Colorado (CU) is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@ucdenver.edu ​. Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41564&lang=en": {
      "title": "Research Associate",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 28, 2026 Job category: Research Faculty Department: SOM-Linda Crnic Inst Gen Ops Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Department: School of Medicine- Linda Crnic Institute for Down Syndrome Job Title: Research Associate Position #: 00854155 – Requisition #: 41564 Job Summary: The Linda Crnic Institute for Down Syndrome is seeking applicants for a full-time Research Associate to participate in the scientific management of various high-level internal and externally funded scientific projects. The Research Associate provides scientific leadership and operational oversight of multi-site, international research initiatives spanning the United States, Latin America, and Asia, coordinating cross-functional teams of investigators, clinicians, data managers, and research staff to ensure successful study implementation and alignment with program objectives. The position is responsible for translating scientific protocols into operational workflows, including the development and oversight of REDCap-based data systems, longitudinal data tracking frameworks, and data quality assurance processes. The role supports the design and implementation of clinical and translational research studies, including protocol development, site readiness, and coordination of regulatory requirements such as IRB approvals and international compliance considerations (including FDA and GDPR where applicable). The incumbent also facilitates data sharing agreements (MTAs/DTAs) and ensures compliant, efficient exchange of research data across collaborating institutions. Working closely with global partners and consortium members, this position supports study execution, data harmonization, and dissemination of findings across multi-institutional research networks. The role contributes to grant development, budgeting, and scientific reporting for large-scale federally funded initiatives, including the NIH INCLUDE Project. In addition, the Research Associate develops and maintains standard operating procedures (SOPs), reporting structures, and program monitoring tools to support research coordination, data integrity, and decision-making across sites. The incumbent also plays a key role in training and onboarding research staff and coordinators, supporting capacity building and standardization of research practices across international teams. The successful candidate will hold a Ph.D. in biomedical sciences, computational sciences, or a related field and bring experience in managing complex, multi-site research programs involving clinical and/or multi-dimensional biomedical data. The ideal candidate is a self-directed scientific leader and program manager with strong analytical, organizational, and collaborative skills, capable of operating independently in a highly interactive, global research environment. Key Responsibilities: 50% Project Management & Global Program Leadership · Lead multi-site international research initiatives, providing strategic oversight of cross-functional teams, timelines, deliverables, and stakeholder engagement. · Coordinate research activities across investigators, institutions, and global partners to ensure alignment with scientific objectives, funding requirements, and program milestones. · Oversee study implementation, site readiness, and operational workflows across multiple institutions. · Monitor project progress, identify operational challenges, and implement process improvements to support efficient and consistent study execution. 25% Research Infrastructure & Clinical Research Operations · Design, implement, and oversee data collection and management systems (e.g., REDCap), including longitudinal tracking, data quality assurance, and harmonization across sites. · Develop and maintain standardized data workflows, governance practices, SOPs, and reporting structures to support high-quality, reproducible research. · Support clinical and translational research implementation, including protocol development, regulatory compliance, and integration of clinical, biospecimen, and research data. · Coordinate regulatory and ethical requirements, including IRB, FDA, and GDPR considerations, to support compliance across participating institutions. 15% Consortium Collaboration, Grants & Strategic Planning · Collaborate with international investigators, clinicians, and research partners to coordinate study activities, facilitate data sharing (MTAs/DTAs), and strengthen collaborative networks. · Contribute to federal grant applications, budgets, progress reports, and strategic planning for large-scale NIH-funded initiatives, including the INCLUDE Project. · Track program milestones, deliverables, and outcomes to support sponsor reporting, program evaluation, and future funding opportunities. · Serve as a liaison between global research sites and central leadership to facilitate communication, resolve challenges, and support dissemination of research findings. 10% Training, Mentorship & Capacity Building · Lead onboarding and training of research staff and site coordinators to promote consistent protocol implementation, data collection, and regulatory compliance. · Provide ongoing mentorship and operational support to strengthen research capacity across international teams and institutions. · Develop training materials and resources to standardize practices, improve team coordination, and promote sustainability across research programs. Work Location: Hybrid – this role is eligible for a hybrid schedule of 4 days per week on campus and as needed for in-person meetings. Why Join Us: The Linda Crnic Institute for Down Syndrome is the largest academic home for Down syndrome research. The Crnic Institute collaborates with prominent scientists and leaders around the globe to enable precision medicine approaches to improve health outcomes in Down syndrome. Learn more at: https://medschool.cuanschutz.edu/linda-crnic-institute. The University of Colorado offers a comprehensive benefits package that includes health insurance, life insurance, retirement plans, tuition benefits, ECO pass, paid time off – vacation, sick, and holidays and more. To see what benefits are available, please visit: https://www.cu.edu/employee-services/benefits-wellness Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package including: · Medical: Multiple plan options · Dental: Multiple plan options · Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision · Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay · Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year (based on percentage of time) · Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) · Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) · Holiday Days: 11/year · Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses · ECO Pass: Reduced rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: · Ph.D. in Biomedical Sciences, Bioinformatics, Data Science, Molecular Biology, or related fields. · Minimum of 3 years of progressively responsible experience in biomedical or translational research, including demonstrated experience in managing complex, multi-component research programs or collaborations. Preferred Qualifications: · Demonstrated experience in biomedical or translational research, preferably within federally funded programs (e.g., NIH) and multidisciplinary research environments. · Experience coordinating multi-site, consortium-based, or international research initiatives, including collaboration with investigators, clinical teams, external partners, and vendors. · Experience with IRB-regulated human subjects research, including protocol development, regulatory submissions and amendments, and ongoing compliance. · Experience with research program management and implementation · Familiarity with research data management, including data curation, harmonization, quality assurance, and integration of longitudinal, clinical, biospecimen, or multi-omics datasets. · Experience contributing to grant applications, budget development, sponsor reporting, scientific manuscripts, and research publications. · Demonstrated ability to develop SOPs, operational workflows, and training materials, and to mentor colleagues and support consistent research practices across teams. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: To be successful in this position, candidates will demonstrate the following: · Ability to communicate complex scientific concepts effectively to diverse audiences, including researchers, clinicians, institutional leadership, and external stakeholders · Demonstrated ability to build and sustain collaborative relationships across multidisciplinary teams, institutions, and international partners · Proven ability to lead and contribute to scientific publications, including drafting, revising, and submitting manuscripts in peer-reviewed journals · Strong presentation skills, with experience delivering scientific findings at conferences, consortium meetings, and stakeholder briefings · Experience contributing to or leading the development of grant applications, budgets, and sponsor reports · Ability to initiate, develop, and manage scientific collaborations, including coordination across complex organizational structures · Expertise in data analysis, data stewardship, and management of complex biomedical datasets, including ensuring data quality and integrity · Demonstrated ability in research program coordination and team leadership, including managing competing priorities and timelines · Strong interpersonal skills with the ability to influence without direct authority and navigate complex team dynamics · Exceptional organizational and project management skills, with attention to detail and the ability to drive initiatives from concept through execution · Excellent written and verbal communication skills, including preparation of technical documents, SOPs, and strategic reports Conditions of Employment: Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without requiring sponsorship. We are unable to provide work visa sponsorship or employment authorization for this position now or in the future. Open Track: To support the growth of our faculty, selected candidates will be offered the opportunity to choose a track that corresponds to their area of excellence. Learn more about faculty tracks at the Office for Faculty Affairs . How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): 1. A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position 2. Curriculum vitae / Resume 3. Five professional references including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers . Questions should be directed to: Sydney Ashton, Sydney.ashton@cuanschutz.edu Screening of Applications Begins: This position may be seeking multiple candidates. Positions will remain open until filled. Applications will be reviewed as they are received, and candidates may be contacted for interviews throughout the posting period. Upon candidate(s) selection, the posting will be closed, and no further applications will be accepted. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as HIRING RANGE: $65,000 to $80,000 The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation unless it is non-exempt. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: The University of Colorado (CU) is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@ucdenver.edu ​. Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41558&lang=en": {
      "title": "Senior IT Application Developer",
      "description": "Closing Date: 11/03/2026 Posted Date: Oct 28, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: SOM-DEAN DO Shared Srvc-InfoTc Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Department: School of Medicine, Office of the Dean, IT Shared Services Job Title: Senior IT Application Developer Position #: 00854222 – Requisition #: 41558 Job Summary: The Senior IT Application Developer serves as a senior technical contributor responsible for the design, development, enhancement, integration, and ongoing support of School of Medicine applications, including those supporting faculty affairs, finance, and research administration. This position works across the full application lifecycle, from design and development through testing, deployment, and production support, including maintenance, modernization, and migration of existing applications. The role partners with the Data Team, project management, business stakeholders, security and compliance, and other developers to translate business needs into secure, maintainable solutions. The successful candidate will bring hands-on development experience, strong technical judgment, and the ability to independently investigate complex problems, make technical decisions, and own application work from design through production support. The work model for this position is hybrid, as determined by the School of Medicine Office of the Dean, Information Services department. Key Responsibilities: Application Design & Development (40%) Design, develop, and enhance School of Medicine applications, including front-end interfaces, application logic, services, and back-end components built with .NET/C# and JavaScript. Translate functional and technical requirements into application designs and make technical design and architecture decisions. Apply secure coding, accessibility, usability, performance, and maintainability standards and data-protection requirements such as HIPAA and FERPA throughout development. Application Maintenance, Enhancements & Technical Debt (25%) Maintain and enhance existing production applications, including legacy applications requiring modernization or migration. Evaluate existing code and architecture and perform refactoring and upgrades to reduce technical debt while maintaining continuity of critical business services. Balance new feature development with application lifecycle, maintenance, security, and sustainability requirements. Database, API & Systems Integration, Release Management (20%) Design and maintain SQL Server database components, queries, stored procedures, and data models, along with RESTful APIs and integrations with internal and external systems. Conduct peer code reviews, mentor other developers, and maintain code through approved version-control practices in GitHub. Follow established change, release-management, and CI/CD practices across development, testing/staging, and production environments, partnering with QA and project teams to validate acceptance criteria before deployment. Production Support (15%) Provide advanced troubleshooting and production support, resolving defects, performance issues, and integration failures. Maintain technical and release documentation, including architecture, integrations, dependencies, configuration, and support procedures, to reduce reliance on undocumented institutional knowledge. Collaborate with stakeholders to understand business requirements and explain technical options, constraints, risks, and trade-offs. This description is a summary of the general level of work and is not intended to be all-inclusive. Duties and responsibilities may evolve based on business need and the approved organizational design. We reserve the right to add or delete duties and responsibilities at the discretion of the supervisor and/or hiring authority. Work Location: Hybrid – this role is eligible for a hybrid schedule of three (3) days per week on campus and as needed for in-person meetings. Why Join Us: The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is a world-class medical destination at the forefront of transformative science, medicine, education, and patient care. The campus encompasses the University of Colorado health professional schools, more than 60 centers and institutes, and two nationally ranked independent hospitals - UCHealth University of Colorado Hospital and Children's Hospital Colorado - that treat more than two million adult and pediatric patients each year. For more information, visit www.cuanschutz.edu . The School of Medicine (SOM) Office of the Dean Information Services team supports digital, data, application, infrastructure, web, and end-user technology services for SOM departments. Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation, and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package, including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 15/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced-rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's degree in Computer Science, IT, Information Systems, or closely related field. Substitution: A combination of education and related technical/military/paraprofessional experience may be substituted for a bachelor’s degree on a year-for-year basis. Two (2) years of professional experience in software or web application development. Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Preferred Qualifications: Three (3) years of progressively responsible professional experience in software or web application development. Experience developing and maintaining full stack application using .NET/C#, REST APIs, and modern JavaScript or TypeScript frameworks. Experience working with relational databases, SQL, and Microsoft SQL Server. Experience with ASP.NET Core, Microsoft AZURE, cloud-based application development, and deployment. Experience troubleshooting application defects, performance issues, and system integrations. Conditions of Employment: Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without requiring sponsorship. We are unable to provide work visa sponsorship or employment authorization for this position now or in the future. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Advanced knowledge of modern software-development practices, with the ability to write clean, secure, testable, and maintainable code. Ability to independently analyze complex technical problems, weigh trade-offs such as maintainability, performance, security, and cost, and recommend practical solutions. Strong understanding of application architecture, APIs, relational databases, authentication/authorization, and system integrations. Strong organizational skills and ability to manage competing priorities. Strong communication and collaboration skills with technical and nontechnical stakeholders in a matrixed environment. Commitment to documentation, knowledge sharing, mentoring, quality, and continuous improvement. How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position Curriculum vitae / Resume Three to five professional references, including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Questions should be directed to: Melissa Roscosky, Melissa.Roscosky@cuanschutz.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Immediately and continues until November 3 rd , 2026. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as $78,051 to $99,281. The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position may be eligible for overtime compensation, depending on the level. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans, and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@cuanschutz.edu . Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students, and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine-preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety-sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41561&lang=en": {
      "title": "Non-Invasive Cardiologist: Assistant- Associate Professor",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 28, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: SOM-MED-Cardiology Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Department: Division of Cardiology – Non-Invasive Cardiologist Job Title: Assistant Professor – Associate Professor Position #:00851391 – Requisition #: 41561 Job Summary: The University of Colorado School of Medicine’s Division of Cardiology has an immediate opening for a non-invasive cardiologist to join our team as a clinician educator. This position will involve a range of general cardiology responsibilities split between the flagship University of Colorado Hospital on the Anschutz Medical Campus and one of its associated hospital-outpatient department ambulatory clinics in the Denver Metro area. The preferred candidate should be board certified/eligible in Cardiovascular Medicine by the ABIM. The candidate should also be trained and proficient in echocardiography services. There will be opportunity for academic work, including education, investigation, and administration within a large academic medical center. This is a terrific opportunity to join the region’s only comprehensive academic cardiology division dedicated to providing exceptional, cutting-edge clinical care to patients in the Denver Metro region, Colorado, and surrounding states. Key Responsibilities: · Approximately 50-75% patient care on the Anschutz Medical Campus split between ICU/inpatient rounding, clinic, and ancillary cardiology services at the University of Colorado Hospital Heart and Vascular Center · Approximately 25-50% ambulatory cardiac services at one of the outlying hospital-outpatient department clinics in the Denver Metro area. · Perform echocardiography +/- nuclear cardiology services · Education Work Location: Onsite – this role is expected to work onsite and is located in Aurora, CO. Why Join Us: We are the only full-service cardiology practice in Colorado, we practice out of the largest hospital in Colorado, and we are the only Division of Cardiology in the state servicing an allopathic medical school. Our mission is to provide the highest quality clinical care across the full spectrum of cardiovascular offerings, conduct cutting-edge research that improves our understanding of cardiovascular science and innovates care delivery, and train cardiovascular clinicians and researchers for future generations. We place a high level of importance on achieving and maintaining a diverse environment that fosters excellence and rewarding opportunities. Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package including: · Medical: Multiple plan options · Dental: Multiple plan options · Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision · Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay · Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year (based on percentage of time) · Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) · Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) · Holiday Days: 11/year · Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses · ECO Pass: Reduced rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Open Rank: Rank at the time of appointment will be based on the candidate’s demonstrated contributions and experience in teaching, clinical, research, and/or service to the field. We welcome applicants with a range of backgrounds and accomplishments and encourage individuals to highlight the breadth and depth of their professional impact. Learn more about faculty tracks at the Office for Faculty Affairs . Assistant Professor · MD · Board eligible/certified in Cardiovascular Medicine by ABIM Associate Professor · MD · Board eligible/certified in Cardiovascular Medicine by ABIM · 5 years experience Preferred Qualifications: · Articulate a vision for the future of academic and community cardiovascular care in the Colorado region · The candidate should also be trained and proficient in echocardiography; CT, MRI, and/or nuclear cardiology training is a plus. · Talented educator · Academically productive How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): 1. A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position 2. Curriculum vitae / Resume 3. Five professional references including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers . Questions should be directed to: Bobby Pinter, bobby.pinter@cuanschtuz.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Immediately and continues until position is filled. For best consideration, apply by January 31, 2027. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as HIRING RANGE: Assistant Professor $380,000 to $430,000 Associate Professor $410,000 - $450,000 The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation unless it is non-exempt. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: The University of Colorado (CU) is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@ucdenver.edu ​. Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41572&lang=en": {
      "title": "Patient Services Representative I-II – Orthopedics Longmont/Broomfield",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 30, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: SOM-DEAN DO CPD - ORTHOPEDICS Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus Department: Community Practice Job Title: Patient Services Representative I-II – Orthopedics Longmont/Broomfield Position #: 00854249 – Requisition #: 41572 Job Summary: Attention customer service experts with a passion for team-centric care coordination in an outpatient setting. We need your caring and compassionate expertise to continue providing our patients with top-notch quality care. The Patient Services Representative is responsible for providing efficient, effective, quality customer service through a variety of duties including, but not limited to, patient check-in, registration, scheduling, exam preparation, outbound calling, and some referral management. They comply with established company policies and procedures, HIPAA Privacy Rules, and the University of Colorado School of Medicine Confidentiality Policy. The Patient Services Representative ensures clear and timely communication, including patient appointment status, to clinical department(s). Key Responsibilities: Acknowledges and welcomes patients and visitors; sets the tone for a positive experience Checks patients in and out for appointments; schedules follow-up appointments at the time of discharge Verifies patient and insurance information, while accurately documenting necessary modifications in the Electronic Health Record (EPIC) Answers multiple phone lines to fulfill patient needs over the phone Monitors provider schedules daily to ensure that all open appointment slots are filled on the same day and schedules are free of roadblocks Reviews the Daily Appointment Report three to five days in advance for patient appointments to ensure referral accuracy Collects patient copays and balances the drawer daily Work Location: Onsite – this role is expected to work onsite and is located in Longmont/Broomfield, CO . Why Join Us: Community Practice Medicine, housed within the School of Medicine at the University of Colorado, is seeking trained medical professionals to join our growing team. With clinics spanning from Longmont to Castle Rock, we offer a wide variety of opportunities. Specialty areas include, but are not limited to: Orthopedics, Vascular Surgery, OBGYN, Internal Medicine, Urology, Psychiatry, and many more! The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is a public education, clinical, and research facility serving 4,500 students and a world-class medical destination at the forefront of life-changing science, medicine, and healthcare. CU Anschutz offers more than 42 highly rated degree programs through 6 schools and colleges and receives over $500 million in research awards each year. We are the single largest health professions education provider in Colorado, awarding nearly 1,450 degrees annually. Powered by our award-winning faculty, renowned researchers, and a reputation for academic excellence, the CU Anschutz Medical Campus drives innovation from the classroom to the laboratory to the delivery of unparalleled patient care. Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation, and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package, including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 15/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced-rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Patient Services Representative I: High school diploma or GED One or more (1+) years of patient/client-facing experience Patient Services Representative II: High school diploma or GED Two or more (2+) years of patient/client-facing experience Substitution (All Levels): A combination of education and related technical/military/paraprofessional experience may be substituted for a bachelor’s degree on a year-for-year basis. Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Preferred Qualifications (All Ranks): College graduate Medical office experience EPIC experience MS Office experience Bilingual, Spanish-speaking Conditions of Employment: Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without requiring sponsorship. We are unable to provide work visa sponsorship or employment authorization for this position now or in the future. Comply with the applicable University of Colorado School of Medicine, Community Practice mandatory education and training Must be able to work in person Must be able to travel to alternate locations as assigned Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Strong organizational and personal skills; must have strong work ethic Strong communication skills, both written and verbal Ability to maintain a positive attitude with clients, employees, and management Ability to work quickly – individually and as part of a team Ability to read, analyze, and interpret policies, documents, and regulations Must be detail-oriented and maintain excellent organizational skills Must be tech-savvy (ability to understand, apply, and benefit from technology) How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to the listed job qualifications and interest in the position Curriculum vitae / Resume Three to five professional references, including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Questions should be directed to: Jennifer Anderson, jennifer.4.anderson@cuanschutz.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Immediately and continues until the position is filled. For best consideration, apply by 11/29/2026. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as: Patient Services Representative I : $40,000 to $46,720 Patient Services Representative II : $43,700 to $51,042 The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position may be eligible for overtime compensation, depending on the level. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans, and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@cuanschutz.edu . Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students, and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine-preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety-sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41575&lang=en": {
      "title": "Instructor – Certified Athletic Trainer, Professional Sports Partnerships",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 30, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: SOM-ORTHO GENERAL OPERATIONS Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Department: Orthopedics Job Title: Instructor – Certified Athletic Trainer, Professional Sports Partnerships Position #00854153 – Requisition #41575 Job Summary: The University of Colorado Anschutz Department of Orthopedics is seeking an experienced Certified Athletic Trainer to serve as the central clinical and operational liaison between CU Sports Medicine, UCHealth, and our professional sports partners, including the Kroenke Sports & Entertainment (KSE) franchises (Colorado Avalanche, Denver Nuggets, Colorado Mammoth, and Colorado Rapids, including Rapids Academy) and the Colorado Rockies. This position serves as the primary point of contact for coordinating care, connecting players, coaches, and team personnel with orthopedic and primary care sports medicine team physicians, subspecialty providers, and UCHealth Executive Health. The role focuses on relationship management and care coordination rather than sideline coverage, including anticipating team needs, coordinating large-scale events such as team physicals, and developing workflows for a growing professional sports medicine program. This is not a traditional 9-to-5 position and requires flexibility to respond to urgent needs outside regular business hours. Key Responsibilities : Team Partnership and Relationship Management Serve as the primary operational contact for each team’s athletic trainers and medical staff, learning their workflows and checking in proactively to anticipate needs and resolve concerns. Build close relationships with team physicians (orthopedics and primary care sports medicine), their athletic trainers, and clinic personnel to streamline communication and care. Clinical Care Coordination and Executive Health Partnership Coordinate appointments, imaging, consultations, and testing for players, coaches, staff, and affiliates, with timely follow-through on urgent requests. Interface with subspecialty providers across CU and UCHealth (e.g., Cardiology, ENT, OB/GYN) to facilitate timely, appropriate care. Use Epic to pend orders that expedite care (no order sign-off authority). Coordinate care for team-affiliated workers’ compensation cases, particularly for Colorado Mammoth players and Rapids Academy athletes. Serve as the point of contact with UCHealth Executive Health for urgent needs of team-affiliated individuals and lead the transition of professional sports coordination into this role without disruption to service. Team Physicals and Large-Scale Events Plan and run preseason physicals, medical testing, and other large-scale team events, from scheduling and staffing to logistics and communication. Operations, Billing, and Process Improvement Coordinate billing, documentation, and administrative processes with Executive Health, physician practices, and finance; identify inefficiencies and build standardized workflows that continuously improve service and team satisfaction. Availability and Program Growth Respond to urgent team needs during evenings, weekends, and holidays, and take on new initiatives and responsibilities as team partnerships and the program grow. What Success Looks Like Success in this role will be reflected in strong working relationships with each team and physician group, timely and reliable coordination of clinical services, well-executed team physicals and events, and continued improvement in team satisfaction and operational efficiency. Work Location: Hybrid – this role is eligible for a hybrid schedule. # of days per week in person to be determined as the role evolves. Why Join Us: This position offers the opportunity to work alongside experienced orthopedic and sports medicine physicians at an academic medical center while partnering closely with the medical staff of Colorado’s professional sports teams. As a newly dedicated role, the individual will help establish the workflows, relationships, and standards that guide how CU Sports Medicine and UCHealth support these teams as the program grows. Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year (based on percentage of time) Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 11/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Master’s degree in Athletic Training, Exercise Science, Sports Medicine, or related field. Certification by the Board of Certification (BOC) for Athletic Trainers. Colorado Athletic Trainer licensure or eligibility for licensure. Current CPR/BLS certification. Condition of Employment: Willingness to work evenings, weekends, and holidays as needed. Preferred Qualifications: Experience in professional, elite, or collegiate sports medicine settings. Familiarity with the Epic electronic health record. Experience with workers’ compensation, billing, or team physicals. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Knowledge of sports medicine conditions sufficient to triage requests to the right provider. Proven ability to build trusted relationships with athletic trainers, physicians, and coaches. Excellent organization, communication, and problem-solving across multidisciplinary teams. Ability to independently manage competing, time-sensitive priorities. Professionalism and discretion when working with high-profile athletes. A process-improvement mindset and flexibility as the program evolves. How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): 1. A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position 2. Curriculum vitae / Resume 3. Five professional references including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers . Questions should be directed to: Lindsey Renn; lindsey.renn@cuanschutz.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Immediately and continues until position is filled. For best consideration, apply by November 30, 2026. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as HIRING RANGE: $60,000 - $90,000 The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation unless it is non-exempt. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: The University of Colorado (CU) is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@ucdenver.edu ​. Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41186&lang=en": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Fellow",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 30, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: SOM-OP GENERAL OPERATIONS Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Department: Ophthalmology Job Title: Postdoctoral Fellow Position #00853251 – Requisition #41186 Job Summary: The Department of Ophthalmology at the University of Colorado, Anschutz Medical Campus, seeks a full-time (1.0 FTE) Postdoctoral Fellow to work in the Quantitative Translational Imaging in Medicine Lab, located within the Division of Artificial Medical Intelligence of Department of Ophthalmology in the University of Colorado School of Medicine. We focus broadly on quantitative and machine learning techniques in multiple modalities of medical imaging (e.g. fundoscopy images, OCT scans, MRI, CT, X-ray and digital pathology). We bridge the gap between machine learning research and clinical practice through fruitful connections with our clinical collaborators. Our research has potential to revolutionize treatment paradigms and transform the care of patients. If you join us, you will become an integral part of an interdisciplinary team that values collaboration and teamwork above all else. We are seeking a motivated, proactive person who will be able to own their projects from their conceptualization to its completion, support faculty in grant writing, and mentor data scientists, PhD students and undergraduate and graduate interns. Key Responsibilities : Perform independent research: own a research project from conceptualization to publication Assist with grant writing and ideation Supervise PhD students, data scientists, and interns Work Location: Hybrid – this role is eligible for a hybrid schedule of 3 days per week on campus and as needed for in-person meetings. Why Join Us: The Department of Ophthalmology is housed in the Sue Anschutz-Rodgers Eye Center on the Anschutz Medical Campus. This state-of-the-art facility is one of the largest eye centers in the country and serves not only patients in the Rocky Mountain region but also patients all over the world. The technological innovations conceived and developed by departmental faculty have changed the practice of eye care throughout the world. Our educational programs train the next generation of leaders in ophthalmology. Our specialists have developed national and international reputations for excellence in routine and complex ophthalmic care. We have invested heavily in tracking our clinical outcomes and we are proud that our clinicians perform at the highest levels in their respective fields. The mission of the Department of Ophthalmology is to be a nationally recognized department of ophthalmology by providing exemplary patient care founded on educational leadership, innovative research, and high ethical standards. Why work for the University? The University of Colorado offers a comprehensive benefits package. To see what benefits are available for Post-Doctoral Fellows, please visit: Payroll & Benefits Orientation for Post-Doctoral Fellows | University of Colorado (cu.edu) benefits guide cover-post-doc-2024 (cu.edu) Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. PhD in computer science, data science, or related discipline Track record of publications in Artificial Intelligence and Deep Learning in peer-reviewed conferences and journals, specifically in Computer Vision and/or Natural Language Processing Proficiency in python and deep learning libraries (pytorch) Proficiency in git, Docker, python, and SQL Experience in Medical Computer Vision Experience with Large Language Models and Generative AI Experience working with real-world EHR and imaging data Experience working with PACS and the DICOM standard Preferred Qualifications: Experience in medical imaging for ophthalmology Track record of publications in Medical Imaging in top tier conferences (e.g., MICCAI) and journals (e.g., Nature, Medical Image Analysis, Transactions of Medical Imaging) Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Strong team player with excellent customer service and interpersonal skills and has the ability to work with a diverse group and competing interests. Strong verbal and written communication skills with the ability to effectively explain processes and procedures. Excellent time management and organizational skills with the ability to work independently, prioritize tasks, work under tight deadlines. Flexibility and the ability to adapt to various situations. Ability to take direction and use independent judgment to complete assigned tasks. Excellent attention to detail. Analytical and reasoning ability. Ability to represent the department and University in a professional manner with tact and diplomacy. How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): 1. A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position 2. Curriculum vitae / Resume 3. Five professional references including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers . Questions should be directed to: Ashley Woodhouse, ASHLEY.WOODHOUSE@CUANSCHUTZ.EDU Screening of Applications Begins: Applications will be accepted until finalists are identified, but preference will be given to complete applications received by November 15, 2026 . Those who do not apply by this date may or may not be considered. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as HIRING RANGE: Postdoc 0 $63,480 Postdoc 1 $63,900 Postdoc 2 $64,380 Postdoc 3 $66,948 Postdoc 4 $69,180 Postdoc 5 $71,748 Postdoc 6 $74,424 Postdoc 7 or more $77,076 The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation unless it is non-exempt. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: The University of Colorado (CU) is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@ucdenver.edu ​. Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41571&lang=en": {
      "title": "Senior Vulnerability Management Security Analyst",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 30, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: ADM AVCOIT SC Admin Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Department: Information Strategy and Services Job Title: Senior Vulnerability Management Security Analyst Position #: 00800716 – Requisition #: 41571 Job Summary: Does this describe you? Are you motivated by staying ahead of evolving threats and building smarter, more proactive security practices? Join Information Strategy and Services as our Senior Vulnerability Management Security Analyst, where you will lead and continuously improve the university’s enterprise vulnerability management program. In this role, you’ll apply threat intelligence, influence security-by-design, and lead initiatives that strengthen defenses across a dynamic, enterprise environment. You’ll join a collaborative Security Operations team focused on proactively reducing risk and strengthening the university’s security posture through partnership, innovation, and continuous improvement. This role offers the opportunity to influence enterprise-wide security practices, work across diverse teams, and help protect critical systems that support education, research, and patient care. If you’re passionate about staying ahead of cyber threats and making a meaningful impact, we encourage you to apply! Key Responsibilities: Lead and oversee the enterprise threat and vulnerability management program, ensuring effective risk reduction across environments. Evaluate and interpret threat data to assess risk and communicate recommended actions to stakeholders. Drive remediation efforts by collaborating with IT teams, developers, and system owners. Design and implement a vulnerability management strategy across on-prem and cloud environments and track program metrics and outcomes. Collaborate with incident response, vendors, and stakeholders to identify and address emerging threats and vulnerabilities. Demonstrates a high degree of integrity and ethical conduct and consistently applies secure, responsible practices in professional activities, decision-making, and the use of information and technology. What You'll Bring: Expert-level proficiency in a variety of vulnerability management technologies and principles. Knowledge of regulatory requirements related to security, privacy, and data protection. Excellent written and verbal communication skills. Strong analytical and problem-solving skills, including interpersonal problem resolution. Exhibits intellectual curiosity and a commitment to continuous professional development. Values collaboration and recognizes the importance of building strong professional relationships. Work Location: Hybrid – This position is eligible for a hybrid work environment. AMC ISS strives for a high-flex work environment, meaning although this role may predominately be executed effectively with a remote schedule, there may be instances where in-person meetings and/or activities are needed. There is no minimum or prescribed in-person requirement. The work schedule will be based around core working hours in Colorado Mountain Time. Why Join Us: Information Strategy and Services (ISS) partners across the campus to deliver information technology services that empower teaching, learning, research, and patient care. ISS brings together expertise across four key areas: Technology & Infrastructure, Security & Compliance, Information & Data Enablement, and Business Strategy. Together, we connect service and technology . Our work is guided by six shared principles that connect our teams and shape how we serve our customers: Curiosity- Explore beyond one’s own experience and environment. Compassion- Demonstrates empathy, understanding, and respect for all people. Collaboration- Partner well beyond our space and build partnerships to achieve organizational results. Commitment- Dedication and engagement one has to their job, team, organization and university. Competence- Know our craft and be committed to continuous improvement and learning. Confidence- Be empowered and assured to represent our customers and their needs. Active investment in our culture and our people is foundational in developing and delivering service excellence. ​To cultivate a people centric workplace, we do the following: Growth & Development : Our Workforce Development Program builds critical skills and supports career advancement. Empowered Managers : Leaders are trained in coaching and team effectiveness to drive success. Open Communication : Stay connected through monthly town halls and annual summits. Wellness Focus : We prioritize employee well-being with supportive wellness initiatives. Coaching Culture : Continuous learning and feedback are part of how we grow together. Flexible Work : We offer flexible arrangements whenever possible to support work-life balance. Click here to find out more about ISS’s Culture The University of Colorado offers a comprehensive benefits package that includes health insurance, life insurance, retirement plans, tuition benefits, ECO pass, paid time off – vacation, sick, and holidays and more. To see what benefits are available, please visit: https://www.cu.edu/employee-services/benefits-wellness . Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 15/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Education: Bachelor’s degree in Information Systems, Computer Science, Engineering, Business, Education, or a closely related field Substitution : 4 years of professional or high-level technical work experience may be substituted for the bachelor’s degree. An associate’s degree with two years of relevant work experience may be substituted for the bachelor’s degree Experience: 2-4 years of relevant experience configuring and administering enterprise security vulnerability management tools and conducting cyber threat intelligence. Experience must include: Overseeing security threat and vulnerability management programs. Monitoring IT controls for regulatory and compliance requirements such as: NIST, CIS, SOX, HIPAA, HITRUST, SSAE 16 - SOC 1 & SOC 2, PCI compliance - PCI DSS / PA-DSS. Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Preferred Qualifications: Experience deploying, integrating, and managing Rapid7 InsightVM. Advanced degree in Computer Science, Information Security, or related field. CISSP, GIAC (GSEC, GCIH, GCIA, GPEN) or other technical security certifications. Penetration testing experience Conditions of Employment: Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without requiring sponsorship. We are unable to provide work visa sponsorship or employment authorization for this position now or in the future. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Expert-level proficiency in a variety of vulnerability management technologies and principles. Knowledge of regulatory requirements related to security, privacy, and data protection. Excellent written and verbal communication skills. Strong analytical and problem-solving skills, including interpersonal problem resolution. Exhibits intellectual curiosity and a commitment to continuous professional development. Values collaboration and recognizes the importance of building strong professional relationships. Demonstrates initiative and a proactive approach to workload management. Works collaboratively with stakeholders to develop solutions that meet defined requirements and desired outcomes. Curiosity, motivation, and a desire for continuous learning. A belief that strong relationships are key to success. A self-starter with a can-do attitude. An effective servant leader and manager of people who begins interactions by listening. A collaborator with a focus on providing solutions based on the requirements and necessary outcomes of those whom we serve. Demonstrates a high degree of integrity and ethical conduct and consistently applies secure, responsible practices in professional activities, decision-making, and the use of information and technology. How to Apply: We value the thoughts you put into a C over Letter and would like to see your Resume, and List of References . For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): 1. A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position 2. Resume 3. Three to five professional references, including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Questions should be directed to: ISS Human Resources iss-humanresources@cuanschutz.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Immediately and continues until position is filled. For best consideration, apply by 11/15/2026. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as $81,050 - $90,000 . The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position may be eligible for overtime compensation, depending on the level. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@cuanschutz.edu . Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41569&lang=en": {
      "title": "Open Rank - Research Scientist or Senior Research Scientist",
      "description": "Closing Date: 11/04/2026 Posted Date: Oct 29, 2026 Job category: Research Faculty Department: CSPH-EOH General Op Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Department: Environmental & Occupational Health, Centers for Health, Work & Environment Job Title: Open Rank - Research Scientist or Senior Research Scientist Position #: 00854230 – Requisition #41569: Job Summary: This is a full-time open-rank position at either the Research Scientist or Senior Research Scientist level, depending on the candidate’s qualifications and experience. The position is based at t he Colorado School of Public Health (ColoradoSPH), Centers for Health, Work & Environment (CHWE) . The Centers for Health, Work & Environment (CHWE) at the Colorado School of Public Health conducts research, offers education and training, and implements community-based public health projects with the mission of improving the health, safety and well-being of workers, their families, and communities both domestically and internationally. We invite applicants who are eager to become part of a vibrant academic center. We are seeking a highly motivated and versatile Research Scientist (or Senior Research Scientist) to serve in the role of an Industrial Hygienist, conducting occupational and environmental research that is especially applicable to the understanding and preventing the impacts of climate and other environmental hazards on worker health and safety. Competitive candidates will have a track record of conducting and publishing rigorous research in the field of industrial hygiene and exposure by health effects related to workforces in low and middle income countries. Candidates will have a great opportunity to join a community of researchers and public health practitioners who conduct cutting-edge research in a setting that takes pride in its supportive culture. This position will have opportunities to engage with faculty, staff, and students conducting international and domestic research on impacts of climate on working populations experiencing vulnerability, implementation research in Occupational Health and Safety, and Total Worker Health®. The Center is home to two NIOSH-funded Centers: the Mountain and Plains Education and Research Center (MAP ERC) and the Center for Health Work & Environment, a NIOSH Total Worker Health Center of Excellence. Key Responsibilities: This person will spend 85 to 100% of their time conducting research, with the possibility of contributing 10-15% of their effort to the teaching mission of the Centers, Department of Environmental and Occupational Health, and Colorado School of Public Health. · Conduct research-grade workplace exposure assessments for chemical, physical, and biological hazards such as solvents, particulate matter, dust, noise, heat, radiation, mold, or infectious agents · Participate in international research that requires travel to Latin America for one- to two-week periods multiple times per year based on research protocol needs · Participate on (or for Senior Research Scientist, lead) exposure assessment teams as part of the CHWE international research team · Develop and maintain the CHWE industrial hygiene program, including management of essential equipment and supplies to support grant-funded research protocols. · Establish SOPs and protocols including meticulous attention to data collection, recordkeeping, and integration into data systems in a team science environment. · Contribute to the design, writing, submission, and publication of peer-reviewed research manuscripts and grants regarding exposures and health effects. In the case of Senior Research Scientist, this may include leadership in the preparation of manuscripts, presentations and grant applications. · Present research at regional, national, and international meetings · Optional: Teach exposure science/industrial hygiene/safety courses and content in the Colorado School of Public Health Work Location: Hybrid – this role is eligible for a hybrid schedule of a minimum of 3 days per week on campus and as needed for in-person meetings. M ust be willing and able to travel off-campus, including availability to work internationally (especially Latin America) for periods of 1-2 weeks at a time, multiple times a year based on research needs. Why Join Us: The Colorado School of Public Health is a collaborative endeavor involving the University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus (CU Anschutz), Colorado State University (CSU), and the University of Northern Colorado (UNC). The Colorado School of Public Health is the first and only accredited school of public health in the Rocky Mountain Region, attracting top-tier faculty and students from across the country and providing vital contributions towards ensuring our region’s health and well-being. Collaboratively formed in 2008 by CU Anschutz, CSU, and UNC, the Colorado School of Public Health provides education programs, including a Master’s concentration in global health, innovative research that places the School in the top 20 in NIH funding among Schools of Public Health, and community service that addresses public health issues including chronic disease, healthcare access, climate, and environmental threats, emerging infectious diseases, population mental health, ONE HEALTH and injuries for the Rocky Mountain region, nationally and globally. Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year (based on percentage of time) Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 11/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. This is an open rank position and could be classified as Research Scientist or Senior Research Scientist based on experience and qualifications as indicated below: Research Scientist: · A Master’s degree in Industrial Hygiene, or another closely related field/concentration such as occupational or environmental health, exposure science, or engineering. · A minimum of 2 years of professional experience. · Experience in participating in conduct of international research assessing environmental exposures and hazards. Senior Research Scientist: · A PhD in Industrial Hygiene or another closely related field/concentration such as occupational or environmental health sciences, exposure science, or engineering. · Experience in leading teams in the performance of industrial hygiene research or services/practice. · A minimum of 2 years of professional experience. · Experience in participating in conduct of international research assessing environmental exposures and hazards. Preferred Qualifications: · Certification in Industrial Hygiene (CIH) · Spanish language proficiency at a conversational level · Proficiency with data collection and analysis software such as RedCAP, R, SAS, STATA, Excel Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Knowledge · Technical knowledge of the principles of industrial hygiene, exposure science, occupational health and safety, toxicology as well as the ability to convey that knowledge to others · Scientific knowledge: how to identify and understand gaps in research and the principles of study design, methods, data collection, data analysis, interpretation. · Familiarity with applicable workplace health and safety regulations and recognized exposure guidelines. Skills Skills include proficient manual and verbal manipulation of industrial hygiene instruments and management and manipulation of data, including: Technical: · Hazard recognition, sampling strategy, instrument use, exposure assessment, control selection, and understanding of toxicology, occupational health, and personal protective equipment Analytic: · Interpreting measurements and laboratory results, identifying trends, summarizing results and drawing conclusions based on quantitative and qualitative data · Applying AI and machine learning technologies as appropriate · Calibration and maintenance of industrial hygiene/exposure assessment equipment and supplies. Problem-solving: · Tailoring sampling strategies, field methods, and recommended changes to work practices and research protocols by balancing health protection, research rigor, feasibility, and operational needs Collaboration: · Working effectively with employers, workers, research study subjects, and research collaborators · Mentoring graduate students and junior faculty members Communication: · Writing concise reports and explaining technical details clearly to collaborators · Contributing to the writing of research manuscripts and grant applications · Actively participating on interdisciplinary research and public health practice teams · Teaching students at the graduate level, residents, and postgraduate level trainees Professional practice: · Attention to detail, ensuring data integrity and completeness, quality assurance, ethical conduct · Demonstrating consideration and empathy for study participants, collaborators and other stakeholders Abilities · Establish and maintain an exposure science unit in CHWE, including identifying essential equipment and supplies for research studies and assessing equipment performance, calibration, and maintenance. · Execute exposure assessment/industrial hygiene protocols in field settings including in rural/agricultural communities and businesses in Latin America and U.S. · Serve as an exposure science/industrial hygiene consultant to collaborators, industries, companies · Analyze research data, prepare necessary graphs and tables, and collaborate writing rigorous research publications and grant applications · Prepare and deliver community-facing presentations for different audiences ranging from scientific conferences to meetings with employers, workers, and other stakeholders · For Senior Research Scientists, demonstrated ability to lead a team in the performance of complex, field based research protocols both domestically and internationally. How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): 1. A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position 2. Curriculum vitae / Resume 3. Five professional references including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers . Questions should be directed to: Lyndsay Krisher, Lyndsay.krisher@cuanschutz.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Immediately and continues until 11/3/2026. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as HIRING RANGE: Research Scientist: $80,000 to $95,000 Senior Research Scientist: $100,000 to $110,000 The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation unless it is non-exempt. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: The University of Colorado (CU) is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@ucdenver.edu ​. Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    }
  },
